o the parent frame (overridden by a followed trajectory). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: position (3) parent frame's coordinates procedure, public :: set_x_label private  subroutine set_x_label (self, text) The text of the x-axis label (default 'X'). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: text procedure, public :: set_y_label private  subroutine set_y_label (self, text) The text of the y-axis label (default 'Y'). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: text procedure, public :: set_z_label private  subroutine set_z_label (self, text) The text of the z-axis label (default 'Z'). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: text procedure, public :: show_axes private  subroutine show_axes (self, axes) Which axes vectors to show: NO_AXES, or X_AXIS, Y_AXIS, Z_AXIS combined with ior. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: axes procedure, public :: show_axes_labels private  subroutine show_axes_labels (self, labels) Which axes labels to show (as show_axes ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: labels procedure, public :: show_contents private  subroutine show_contents (self, show) Show or hide what the frame draws (its sphere, model, ...), but not its\naxes, labels or children. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: show procedure, public :: show_decorations private  subroutine show_decorations (self, show) Show (true) or hide all the frame's decorations at once: its axes,\ntheir labels and its name label (show_axes, show_axes_labels,\nshow_name_label). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: show true: all axes, axes labels and the name label procedure, public :: show_name_label private  subroutine show_name_label (self, show) Show or hide the name label (at the frame's origin; default shown). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: show (true: shown) procedure, public :: sync private recursive subroutine sync (self) Copy the positions and attitudes of this frame and its descendants to\ntheir transform nodes (only those that changed since the last sync). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self procedure, public :: unfollow private  subroutine unfollow (self) Stop following trajectories (the frame keeps its last position and attitude). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self procedure, public :: units_per_meter private pure function units_per_meter (self) Scene units per meter the body is drawn at. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TerrainBody ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) procedure, public :: update => terrain_update private recursive subroutine terrain_update (self, t) Each frame: if the map's window has closed (the map was released with\nit), the map again for a window still open (compiled for the windows\nrunning), then the frame's update. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TerrainBody ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t simulation time (s) procedure, public :: world_matrix private recursive function world_matrix (self) result(m) The transform from this frame to the root of its tree, through the first\nparent at each level. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (4,4) Source Code type , extends ( ReferenceFrame ), public :: TerrainBody private character ( len = :), allocatable :: profile_ !! Rocky's tiling profile ('': the Earth) real ( wp ) :: units_per_meter_ = 1.0e-3_wp !! scene units per meter logical :: lighting_ = . true . !! lit by the scene's lights type ( MapLayer ), allocatable :: layers (:) !! (capacity): the layers, in the order added integer :: n_layers = 0 !! number of layers type ( c_ptr ) :: map = c_null_ptr !! Rocky's map node (null: not made) type ( c_ptr ) :: map_group = c_null_ptr !! the group the map is in (once shown) contains procedure :: add_image_layer , add_elevation_layer , num_layers procedure :: set_lighting , lighting procedure :: profile , units_per_meter , body_radius , elevation procedure :: frame_info => terrain_frame_info procedure :: bound => terrain_bound procedure :: pick => terrain_pick procedure :: build_contents => terrain_build_contents procedure :: update => terrain_update end type TerrainBody","tags":"","url":"type/terrainbody.html"},{"title":"ArtistPointer – vkframes ","text":"type, private :: ArtistPointer One of a DrawableTrajectory's artists: a pointer to it (Fortran has no\narrays of pointers) and the node it is drawn under. Inherits type~~artistpointer~~InheritsGraph type~artistpointer ArtistPointer c_ptr c_ptr type~artistpointer->c_ptr group type~trajectoryartist TrajectoryArtist type~artistpointer->type~trajectoryartist p type~trajectory Trajectory type~trajectoryartist->type~trajectory traj Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Inherited by type~~artistpointer~~InheritedByGraph type~artistpointer ArtistPointer type~drawabletrajectory DrawableTrajectory type~drawabletrajectory->type~artistpointer artists Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type(c_ptr), public :: group = c_null_ptr the artist's node (null until built) class( TrajectoryArtist ), public, pointer :: p => null() the artist (not owned) Source Code type :: ArtistPointer class ( TrajectoryArtist ), pointer :: p => null () !! the artist (not owned) type ( c_ptr ) :: group = c_null_ptr !! the artist's node (null until built) end type ArtistPointer","tags":"","url":"type/artistpointer.html"},{"title":"ChainArtist – vkframes ","text":"type, private, abstract, extends( TrajectoryArtist ) :: ChainArtist The base of the artists drawing a trajectory's points through one chain\nof buffers (CurveArtist: a line, a chain point per trajectory point;\nRibbonArtist: a surface, a pair of chain points per trajectory point):\nthe chain and how much of it is written and drawn, the trace tail, the\ntrajectory's colors, and the update (chain_update: the points written\nas they change, then drawn all or, in trace mode, those passed and the\ntail to the point at the current time). Each extension says what its\nchain is (chain_kind), how many points it draws (points), its tail's\nnode (new_tail), its style (apply_style), how its points are written\n(write_points) and its tail drawn (draw_tail). Inherits type~~chainartist~~InheritsGraph type~chainartist ChainArtist c_ptr c_ptr type~chainartist->c_ptr group, tail type~linechain LineChain type~chainartist->type~linechain chain type~trajectoryartist TrajectoryArtist type~chainartist->type~trajectoryartist type~linechain->c_ptr group, image type~linechunk LineChunk type~linecha