inter solid line); length (scene units, for the whole\npattern: the other patterns, a trail's future's and the arrows', in\nproportion), else the pattern's length on screen where the line is\nfirst drawn. DASH_SCREEN and DASH_FIXED cost projecting the points\ndrawn on the CPU, per view and frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: mode DASH_SCENE, DASH_SCREEN or DASH_FIXED real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: length (DASH_FIXED) the pattern's length, scene units procedure, public :: set_highlight => curve_set_highlight private  subroutine curve_set_highlight (self, mode, color, arrow_spacing, arrow_speed, band_width, pulse_period) Highlight the curve (see the module documentation): mode a sum of\nHIGHLIGHT_PULSE and HIGHLIGHT_ARROWS (HIGHLIGHT_NONE: not highlighted),\nin color ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]; default white). The other\nsettings are kept when not given. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: mode HIGHLIGHT_* (added) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: color (:) [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: arrow_spacing between arrows (window units; default 40) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: arrow_speed (window units per second; default 50) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: band_width of the arrows' band (window units; default 12) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: pulse_period (s; default 1.5) procedure, public :: set_level_of_detail private  subroutine set_level_of_detail (self, enabled) Level of detail (default on): seen from far away, the curve is drawn\nfrom every 2nd, 4th, ... point (and its last), as many as can be\nskipped while staying within half a pixel of all of them, chosen per\nview and per chunk of points. Off: every point is drawn. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: enabled procedure, public :: set_pattern => curve_set_pattern private  subroutine curve_set_pattern (self, factor, pattern) A dash pattern, as OpenGL's line stipple (OpenFrames' setPattern): each\nbit of the 16-bit pattern (bit 0 first; z'FFFF', the default, is\nsolid) covers factor window units, along the whole curve (the dashes\nrun on across its points). The dashes' length on screen is kept within\n0.7 to 1.4 times the pattern's (see shaders/line.vert). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: factor integer, intent(in) :: pattern procedure, public :: set_pickable => artist_set_pickable private  subroutine artist_set_pickable (self, pickable) Whether pick tests what this artist draws (default true; e.g. false for\na spacecraft's marker beside its orbit's curve). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryArtist ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: pickable procedure, public :: set_point_colors private  subroutine set_point_colors (self, enabled) Whether a trajectory with colors is drawn in them (default true); points\nwithout a color yet (colors arriving after positions) in the artist's\ncolor. A curve: each segment blended from its first point's color to its\nsecond's (with level of detail, a color lasting fewer points than are\nskipped may not show from far away); a surface: each point's pair in its\ncolor, times the artist's alpha. False: all in the artist's color. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ChainArtist ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: enabled true: the trajectory's colors procedure, public :: set_trace_mode private  subroutine set_trace_mode (self, enabled) Draw only the part up to the current time (see the module documentation). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryArtist ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: enabled procedure, public :: set_trail private  subroutine set_trail (self, past, future, fade) A trail (see the module documentation): only the part within past before the current time and future after it (s, >= 0; 0: none of\nit; huge(1.0_wp): no limit), each fading out over the last fade (0\nto 1, default 0.25) of its window toward its cutoff. Replaces trace\nmode while set. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: past s before and after the current time real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: future s before and after the current time real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: fade of each part's window (default 0.25) procedure, public :: set_trail_style private  subroutine set_trail_style (self, which, color, opacity, factor, pattern) The style of a trail's part, which TRAIL_PAST or TRAIL_FUTURE: color ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]: drawn in it instead of the line's\ncolors), opacity (its alpha multiplied by it: translucency, default\n1), a dash pattern ( factor and 16 pattern bits, as set_pattern;\ndefault solid). Settings not given are kept. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: which TRAIL_PAST or TRAIL_FUTURE real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: color (:) [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: opacity 0 to 1 integer, intent(in), optional :: factor window units per bit (>= 1), 16 bits integer, intent(in), optional :: pattern window units per bit (>= 1), 16 bits procedure, public :: set_trajectory => curve_set_trajectory private  subroutine curve_set_trajectory (self, traj) Draw traj ; with the default data sources, its positions (per its DOF). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self type( Trajectory ), intent(in), target :: traj procedure, public :: set_width => curve_set_width private  subroutine curve_set_width (self, width) The line's width in window units (logical pixels). Arguments Type Intent 