rows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( ArtistPointer ), private, allocatable :: artists (:) the artists (1:n_artists; not owned) type(c_ptr), private :: contents_group = c_null_ptr the artists' group (null until built) integer, private :: n_artists = 0 number of artists logical, private :: shown = .false. built for a window (artists added later are compiled) Constructor public        interface DrawableTrajectory The DrawableTrajectory constructor: DrawableTrajectory(...) makes one (see new_drawable_trajectory for its\narguments). private  function new_drawable_trajectory (name, color) result(d) A drawable trajectory frame named name (decorations of color color ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: color (:) Return Value type( DrawableTrajectory ) Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: add_artist private  subroutine add_artist (self, a) Add an artist (it must stay alive while added). Artists added after the\nframe is shown are built and compiled at the next update. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DrawableTrajectory ), intent(inout) :: self class( TrajectoryArtist ), intent(in), target :: a procedure, public :: add_child private  function add_child (self, child) result(ok) Add child to this frame's children. Returns false (and does nothing)\nfor this frame itself or an ancestor of it; true if it is already a child. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout), target :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout), target :: child Return Value logical procedure, public :: artist private  function artist (self, i) result(a) Artist i (1 to num_artists). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DrawableTrajectory ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i Return Value class( TrajectoryArtist ), pointer procedure, public :: attitude private pure function attitude (self) result(q) Attitude relative to the parent frame, a quaternion [x, y, z, w]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (4) procedure, public :: axes_labels_shown private pure function axes_labels_shown (self) Which axes labels are shown (as axes_shown ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: axes_shown private pure function axes_shown (self) Which axes vectors are shown (NO_AXES, or X_AXIS, Y_AXIS, Z_AXIS combined). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: axis_label private  function axis_label (self, axis) result(text) The label text of axis X_AXIS, Y_AXIS or Z_AXIS. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: axis Return Value character(len=:), allocatable procedure, public :: bound private  subroutine bound (self, center, radius) The bounding sphere of what the frame draws, in its own coordinates\n(radius 0 if it draws nothing; extensions override it). Views use it for\ntheir default distance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: center (3) frame's coordinates real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: radius frame's coordinates procedure, public :: build_contents => drawable_build_contents private  subroutine drawable_build_contents (self, viewer, group) Build the artists' nodes under group ( viewer , may be null: those made\nlater are compiled if not null). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DrawableTrajectory ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: group procedure, public :: child private  function child (self, i) result(c) Child i (1 to num_children). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i Return Value class( ReferenceFrame ), pointer procedure, public :: child_index private  function child_index (self, frame) Index of frame among the children, or 0. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), target :: frame Return Value integer procedure, public :: color private pure function color (self) result(c) The color of the frame's decorations, [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (4) procedure, public :: contents_shown private pure function contents_shown (self) Whether what the frame draws is shown ( show_contents ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: detach private  subroutine detach (self) Remove this frame from all its parents and children (before it goes out\nof scope or is deallocated while in a tree). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout), target :: self procedure, public :: follow private  subroutine follow (self, traj, data, mode, add) Follow traj (in addition to trajectories already followed, if add is true), with what to follow ( data : FOLLOW_POSITION and/or\nFOLLOW_ATTITUDE; default both) and how ( mode : FOLLOW_LOOP, the\ndefault, or FOLLOW_LIMIT). traj must stay alive while followed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self type( Trajectory ), intent(in), target :: traj the trajectory to follow (not owned) integer, intent(in), optional :: data FOLLOW_POSITION/FOLLOW_ATTITUDE; FOLLOW_LOOP/FOLLOW_LIMIT