pe procedure :: set_marker_image , marker_image_file procedure :: set_auto_attenuate , auto_attenuate procedure :: set_point_colors => marker_set_point_colors , point_colors => marker_point_colors procedure :: drawn_color => marker_drawn_color procedure :: set_intermediate_type , intermediate_type procedure :: set_intermediate_spacing , intermediate_spacing procedure :: set_intermediate_direction , intermediate_direction procedure :: build => marker_build procedure :: update => marker_update procedure :: release => marker_release procedure :: num_intermediate , drawn_marker end type MarkerArtist","tags":"","url":"type/markerartist.html"},{"title":"RibbonArtist – vkframes ","text":"type, public, extends( ChainArtist ) :: RibbonArtist Draws a translucent surface swept between two points at each point of\na trajectory (not in OpenFrames): from the point given by the start data\nsources to the one given by the end data sources, with a quad between\neach point's pair and the next's. Default: from the frame's origin to the\npositions, sweeping out an orbit's plane (a fan, as the radius vectors of\na SegmentArtist would fill it); other sources give e.g. a curtain from\nthe positions down to a ground track stored as an optional. Unlit, seen\nfrom both sides, depth tested but writing no depth (as the equatorial\nplane of a RadialPlane), drawn to double precision as the curves (its\nedge on a CurveArtist's line through the same points). Trace mode draws the surface up to the current time: the quads passed\n(a draw range, no upload) and one from the last point passed to the\npoint interpolated at the time. Point colors: a trajectory with colors\ncolors the surface, each point's pair in its color, with the artist's\nopacity (its alpha times theirs); see set_point_colors. A trajectory\ngoing round several times covers the surface again each time, so it\ngets more opaque: trace one revolution, or lower the alpha. Inherits type~~ribbonartist~~InheritsGraph type~ribbonartist Ribbon