tent(in) :: self Return Value type( Trajectory ), pointer procedure, public :: pickable => artist_pickable private pure function artist_pickable (self) Whether pick tests what this artist draws. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryArtist ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: release => artist_release private  subroutine artist_release (self) Forget the render nodes (after the artist's group was removed from the\nscene): build starts again. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryArtist ), intent(inout) :: self procedure, public :: set_pickable => artist_set_pickable private  subroutine artist_set_pickable (self, pickable) Whether pick tests what this artist draws (default true; e.g. false for\na spacecraft's marker beside its orbit's curve). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryArtist ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: pickable procedure, public :: set_trace_mode private  subroutine set_trace_mode (self, enabled) Draw only the part up to the current time (see the module documentation). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryArtist ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: enabled procedure, public :: set_trajectory private  subroutine set_trajectory (self, traj) Draw traj (it must stay alive while drawn). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryArtist ), intent(inout) :: self type( Trajectory ), intent(in), target :: traj procedure, public :: trace_mode private pure function trace_mode (self) Whether only the part up to the current time is drawn. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryArtist ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure( artist_update ), public, deferred :: update subroutine artist_update(self, t) Prototype Bring the drawing up to date with the trajectory at simulation time t . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryArtist ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t Source Code type , abstract , public :: TrajectoryArtist private type ( Trajectory ), pointer :: traj => null () !! the trajectory drawn (not owned; null if none) logical :: trace = . false . !! trace mode: drawn up to the current time logical :: pickable_ = . true . !! picked (WindowProxy%pick) ! what was drawn integer :: seen_generation = - 1 , seen_revision = - 1 !! trajectory generation and revision drawn (-1: none) contains procedure :: set_trajectory , get_trajectory procedure :: set_trace_mode , trace_mode procedure :: set_pickable => artist_set_pickable , pickable => artist_pickable procedure :: release => artist_release procedure ( artist_build ), deferred :: build procedure ( artist_update ), deferred :: update end type TrajectoryArtist","tags":"","url":"type/trajectoryartist.html"},{"title":"CustomLineSegments – vkframes ","text":"type, public, extends( ReferenceFrame ) :: CustomLineSegments Line segments with a color per endpoint (see the module documentation). Inherits type~~customlinesegments~~InheritsGraph type~customlinesegments CustomLineSegments type~linechain LineChain type~customlinesegments->type~linechain chain type~linesegmentscallback LineSegmentsCallback type~customlinesegments->type~linesegmentscallback callback type~referenceframe ReferenceFrame type~customlinesegments->type~referenceframe c_ptr c_ptr type~linechain->c_ptr group, image type~linechunk LineChunk type~linechain->type~linechunk chunks type~referenceframe->c_ptr light_node, light_switch, node_, contents_node, axis_node, axis_label_node, axis_arrow, axis_text, name_label_node, name_text type~framepointer FramePointer type~referenceframe->type~framepointer children, parents type~trajectoryfollower TrajectoryFollower type~referenceframe->type~trajectoryfollower follower_ type~framepointer->type~referenceframe p type~linechunk->c_ptr line type~lodlevel LodLevel type~linechunk->type~lodlevel lod type~datasource DataSource type~trajectoryfollower->type~datasource sources_ type~trajectorypointer TrajectoryPointer type~trajectoryfollower->type~trajectorypointer trajs type~trajectory Trajectory type~trajectorypointer->type~trajectory p Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: a (:,:) (3, n): their endpoints (frame coordinates) real(kind=wp), private, allocatable :: b (:,:) (3, n): their endpoints (frame coordinates) class( LineSegmentsCallback ), private, pointer :: callback => null() computes the segments each frame (not owned) type( LineChain ), private :: chain draws the segments (separate, colored) logical, private :: changed = .true. to write and upload at the next update real(kind=c_float), private, allocatable :: color_a (:,:) (4, n), or not allocated: the frame's color real(kind=c_float), private, allocatable :: color_b (:,:) (4, n), or not allocated: the frame's color integer, private :: n = 0 segments integer, private :: n_drawn = 0 segments written to the chain (drawn) integer, private :: pattern_ = int(z'FFFF') 16-bit dash pattern (z'FFFF': solid) integer, private :: pattern_factor = 1 window units per bit of the dash pattern real(kind=wp), private :: width_ = 1.0_wp line width (window units) Constructor public        interface CustomLineSegments The CustomLineSegments constructor: CustomLineSegments(...) makes one (see new_custom_line_segments for its\narguments). private  function new_custom_line_segments (name, color, width) result(s) Line segments named name , of color (for segments set without\ncolors; default white) and width (window units; default 1). Arguments Type Intent Optional Att