Graph type~windoweventhandler WindowEventHandler type~windowproxy WindowProxy type~windowproxy->type~windoweventhandler handler Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: before_draw => handler_before_draw private  subroutine handler_before_draw (self, window, t) Called each frame just before drawing, the scene at time t and the\ncamera placed (see the module documentation): e.g. to move HUD text\nnext to a moving object. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowEventHandler ), intent(inout) :: self class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: window real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t simulation time procedure, public :: button_press => handler_button_press private  subroutine handler_button_press (self, window, x, y, button) A mouse button (MOUSE_LEFT, MOUSE_MIDDLE, MOUSE_RIGHT) was pressed at\n(x, y) (see mouse_motion ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowEventHandler ), intent(inout) :: self class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: window real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: y integer, intent(in) :: button MOUSE_LEFT, MOUSE_MIDDLE or MOUSE_RIGHT procedure, public :: button_release => handler_button_release private  subroutine handler_button_release (self, window, x, y, button) A mouse button was released at (x, y) (see button_press ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowEventHandler ), intent(inout) :: self class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: window real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: y integer, intent(in) :: button as button_press's procedure, public :: handle_drag => handler_handle_drag private  subroutine handler_handle_drag (self, window, handle, stage) A handle (vkf_handles) was grabbed (DRAG_START), dragged (DRAG_MOVE:\nit has moved) or released (DRAG_END) with the mouse: e.g. compute\nagain what depends on it (see the module documentation). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowEventHandler ), intent(inout) :: self class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: window the window the handle is dragged in class( DragHandle ), intent(inout), target :: handle the handle (select type for its kind) integer, intent(in) :: stage DRAG_START, DRAG_MOVE or DRAG_END procedure, public :: key_press => handler_key_press private  subroutine handler_key_press (self, window, key, modifiers, handled) A key was pressed: key (a character's code, iachar('v'), or KEY_ ),\nwith the modifier keys held (MOD_ bits). Set handled (false on entry)\nto skip the built-in key's action. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowEventHandler ), intent(inout) :: self class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: window the window of the event integer, intent(in) :: key a character code or KEY_ ; MOD_ bits integer, intent(in) :: modifiers a character code or KEY_ ; MOD_ bits logical, intent(inout) :: handled (true: skip the built-in key) procedure, public :: key_release => handler_key_release private  subroutine handler_key_release (self, window, key, modifiers) A key was released (see key_press ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowEventHandler ), intent(inout) :: self class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: window integer, intent(in) :: key as key_press's integer, intent(in) :: modifiers as key_press's procedure, public :: mouse_motion => handler_mouse_motion private  subroutine handler_mouse_motion (self, window, x, y, buttons) The mouse moved to (x, y) (-1 to 1 across the window, y up), with the\nbuttons held (left, middle, right): moving (none held, OpenFrames' mouse\nmotion) or dragging. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowEventHandler ), intent(inout) :: self class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: window real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x -1 to 1 across the window, y up real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: y -1 to 1 across the window, y up logical, intent(in) :: buttons (3) (held: left, middle, right) Source Code type , public :: WindowEventHandler contains procedure :: key_press => handler_key_press procedure :: key_release => handler_key_release procedure :: mouse_motion => handler_mouse_motion procedure :: button_press => handler_button_press procedure :: button_release => handler_button_release procedure :: before_draw => handler_before_draw procedure :: handle_drag => handler_handle_drag end type WindowEventHandler","tags":"","url":"type/windoweventhandler.html"},{"title":"WindowProxy – vkframes ","text":"type, public :: WindowProxy A window showing a scene (see the module documentation). Inherits type~~windowproxy~~InheritsGraph type~windowproxy WindowProxy c_ptr c_ptr type~windowproxy->c_ptr viewer_ type~cameraflight CameraFlight type~windowproxy->type~cameraflight flight type~draghandle DragHandle type~windowproxy->type~draghandle hovered_handle, dragged_handle type~framemanager FrameManager type~windowproxy->type~framemanager scene type~hudentry HUDEntry type~windowproxy->type~hudentry huds type~simulationclock SimulationClock type~windowproxy->type~simulationclock clock_ type~skysphere SkySphere type~windowproxy->type~skysphere sky_ type~view View type~windowproxy->type~view default_view, shown type~viewpointer ViewPointer type~windowproxy->type~viewpointer views type~windoweventhandler WindowEventHandler type~windowproxy->type~windoweventhandler handler type~cameraflight->type~view from, to type~referenceframe ReferenceFrame type~draghandle->type~referenceframe type~framemanager->type~referenceframe root type~hudentry->c_ptr node type~hudtext HUDText type~hudentry->type~hudtext p type~simulationclock->type~simulationclock sync type~skysphere->c_ptr image, root, texture_switch, star_switch, texture_node, star_node, name_node, line_switch, line_node type~constellation Constellation type~skysphere->type~constellation groups type~starname StarName type~skysphere->type~starname names type~view->type~referenceframe root, frame, lookat type~viewpointer->type~view p type~referenceframe->c_ptr light_node, light_switch, node_, contents_node, axis_node, axis_label_node, axis_arrow, axis_text, name_label_node, name_text type~framepointer FramePointer type~referenceframe->type~framepointer children, parents type~trajectoryfollower TrajectoryFollower type~referenceframe->type~trajectoryfollower follower_ type~framepointer->type~referenceframe p type~datasource DataSource type~trajectoryfollower->type~datasource sources_ type~trajectorypointer TrajectoryPointer type~trajectoryfollower->type~trajectorypointer trajs type~trajectory Trajectory type~trajectorypointer->type~trajectory p Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: background (3) = [0.0_wp, 0.0_wp, 0.0_wp] background color [r, g, b] (0 to 1) logical, private :: camera_throw_ = .true. the camera keeps moving after a drag released while moving type( SimulationClock ), private :: clock_ the window's simulation clock integer, private :: current = 0 number of views; the current one (0: none) logical, private :: default_keys_ = .true. the built-in keys on type( View ), private :: default_view used when there are no views class( DragHandle ), private, pointer :: dragged_handle => null() the handle grabbed (not owned) type( CameraFlight ), private :: flight the camera flight (when active) real(kind=wp), private :: fps_ = 0.0_wp frames per second (the last count's) real(kind=wp), private :: frame_ms_ = 0.0_wp milliseconds between frames (the last count's) class( WindowEventHandler ), private, pointer :: handler => null() the program's event handler (not owned) integer, private :: height_ = 1 logical size (for the views' aspect ratio) logical, private :: hosted = .false. in a host's window (its size from resize ) class( DragHandle ), private, pointer :: hovered_handle => null() the handle under the cursor (not owned) type( HUDEntry ), private, allocatable :: huds (:) the HUD texts shown (first n_huds used) real(kind=wp), private :: last_frame_ms = 0.0_wp the last frame()'s duration (ms) real(kind=wp), private :: light_ambient_ (3) = 0.2_wp [r, g, b] real(kind=wp), private :: light_diffuse_ (3) = 1.0_wp [r, g, b] logical, private :: light_on = .true. the window's light enabled (no frame's light source) real(kind=wp), private :: light_position_ (4) = [0.0_wp, 0.0_wp, 1.0_wp, 0.0_wp] eye coordinates (w 0: directional) real(kind=wp), private :: light_specular_ (3) = 0.0_wp [r, g, b] integer, private :: n_huds = 0 number of HUD texts integer, private :: n_views = 0 number of views; the current one (0: none) real(kind=wp), private :: pixel_ratio_ = 1.0_wp framebuffer pixels per window unit (a host's window) integer, private :: rate_frames = 0 frames since then real(kind=wp), private :: rate_start = -1.0_wp the wall time the frames are counted from (s; -1: none) real(kind=wp), private :: record_fps = 30.0_wp the video's frames per second integer(kind=int64), private :: record_frames = 0_int64 frames drawn while recording real(kind=wp), private :: record_wall = 0.0_wp the wall time at the start (s) logical, private :: recording_ = .false. recording (start_recording) logical, private :: running = .false. open, and not closed by the user type( FrameManager ), private, pointer :: scene => null() the scene shown (not owned) logical, private :: scene_added = .false. scene, sky, HUD texts given to the viewer integer, private :: scene_seen = -1 the scene's updates at this window's last frame type( View ), private, pointer :: shown => null() the view whose camera is in the renderer type( SkySphere ), private, pointer :: sky_ => null() the background sky real(kind=wp), private :: switch_duration = -1.0_wp s, for the next view change (< 0: transition_) real(kind=wp), private :: transition_ = 0.0_wp s, for view changes and resets type(c_ptr), private :: viewer_ = c_null_ptr the rendering layer's viewer (null while closed) type( ViewPointer ), private, allocatable :: views (:) not owned (first n_views used) integer, private :: width_ = 1 logical size (for the views' aspect ratio) real(kind=wp), private :: zoom_speed_ = 1.0_wp the trackball's zoom per scroll step and drag (1: VSG's) Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: add_hud_text private  subroutine add_hud_text (self, h) Show h in the window, on top of the scene (it must stay alive while\nshown), from the next frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self type( HUDText ), intent(in), target :: h procedure, public :: add_view private  subroutine add_view (self, v) Add v to the end of the window's views (it must stay alive while added). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self type( View ), intent(in), target :: v procedure, public :: background_color private pure function background_color (self) result(rgb) The background color [r, g, b]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: camera_throw private pure function camera_throw (self) Whether the camera keeps moving after a released drag (set_camera_throw). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: capture private  function capture (self, file) result(ok) Save the last frame as an image (format from the file extension, e.g.\n.png). Returns false on failure. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: file image file name (e.g. .png) Return Value logical procedure, public :: clear_event_handler private  subroutine clear_event_handler (self) Give the events to no handler (the built-in keys remain). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self procedure, public :: clock private  function clock (self) result(c) The window's simulation clock (e.g. to synchronize it with another window's). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in), target :: self Return Value type( SimulationClock ), pointer procedure, public :: close private  subroutine close (self) Close the window (waiting for the GPU). The scene is kept, and can be\nshown again in another window. So are the window's settings (views,\nHUD texts, sky, handler, time): open again (e.g. on a host's new\nnative window, after Qt destroyed the old one) shows them as before. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self procedure, public :: current_view private  function current_view (self) result(v) The view shown (the default view of the scene's root if none were added). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in), target :: self Return Value type( View ), pointer procedure, public :: cursor_ray private  function cursor_ray (self, x, y, origin, direction) result(ok) The ray from the eye through point (x, y) of the window (-1 to 1 across\nit, y up: as the event handler's positions), in the root frame, as at\nthe last frame: its origin (the eye; in an orthographic view, on the\neye's plane) and its direction (a unit vector). False before the first\nframe. E.g. where the cursor points on a plane: vkf_pick's ray_plane. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x -1 to 1 across the window, y up real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: y -1 to 1 across the window, y up real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: origin (3) root frame (direction: a unit vector) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: direction (3) root frame (direction: a unit vector) Return Value logical procedure, public :: default_keys private pure function default_keys (self) Whether the built-in keys are on ( set_default_keys ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: device_info private  function device_info (self) result(info) The window's Vulkan device and driver (see vkf_diagnostics); '' while it\nisn't open. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value type( DeviceInfo ) procedure, public :: event_handler private  function event_handler (self) result(handler) The event handler (null if none). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value class( WindowEventHandler ), pointer procedure, public :: frame private  function frame (self) result(running) Render one frame: advance the clock, update the frames and draw. Returns\nfalse once the window has been closed (or on failure). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: get_camera private  subroutine get_camera (self, eye, center, up, in_root) The camera of the view shown (from the last frame): eye, center and up\nin the view frame's coordinates (OpenFrames' trackball\ngetTransformation), or in its root frame's if in_root . Zero before\nthe window's first frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: eye (3) view frame's coordinates (or root's) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: center (3) view frame's coordinates (or root's) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: up (3) view frame's coordinates (or root's) logical, intent(in), optional :: in_root procedure, public :: gui => window_gui private  function window_gui (self, font, size) result(g) The window's GUI panels (vkf_gui), made on first use: with font (a\nfont file name or path, as labels'; default DejaVu Sans) of size window units (default 15), which apply then. Not valid unless open. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: font file name or path (default DejaVu Sans) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: size window units (default 15) Return Value type( Gui ) procedure, public :: in_transition private pure function in_transition (self) True while the camera is flying (a transition). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: is_open private pure function is_open (self) Whether the window is open (not closed, by the program or the user). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: is_recording private pure function is_recording (self) Whether the window is recording a video. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: is_time_paused private  function is_time_paused (self) Whether the simulation time is paused. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: key private  subroutine key (self, pressed, symbol, modified_symbol, modifier) A key press (pressed true) or release, as VSG key symbols and modifiers\n(ASCII for printable keys; vsg/ui/KeyEvent.h). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: pressed integer, intent(in) :: symbol the key without modifiers (VSG's keyBase) integer, intent(in) :: modified_symbol the key with the modifiers (VSG's keyModified, e.g. 'A') integer, intent(in) :: modifier the modifier keys held (MOD_* bits) procedure, public :: light_ambient private pure function light_ambient (self) result(rgb) The ambient color of the window's light [r, g, b]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: light_diffuse private pure function light_diffuse (self) result(rgb) The diffuse color of the window's light [r, g, b]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: light_position private pure function light_position (self) result(p) The position of the window's light (see set_light_position ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (4) procedure, public :: light_specular private pure function light_specular (self) result(rgb) The specular color of the window's light [r, g, b]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: mouse private  subroutine mouse (self, kind, x, y, mask, button) A mouse event: kind MOUSE_MOVE, MOUSE_PRESS or MOUSE_RELEASE. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: kind MOUSE_MOVE, MOUSE_PRESS or MOUSE_RELEASE integer, intent(in) :: x framebuffer pixels from the top left integer, intent(in) :: y framebuffer pixels from the top left integer, intent(in) :: mask buttons held (ior: 256 left, 512 middle, 1024 right) integer, intent(in) :: button button pressed or released (1 left, 2 middle, 3 right) procedure, public :: next_view private  subroutine next_view (self, duration) Show the next view (wrapping around); duration as select_view's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: duration procedure, public :: num_views private pure function num_views (self) Number of views added. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: open private  function open (self, width, height, title, native_window, pixel_ratio, vsync) result(ok) Open the window: width x height (logical pixels) titled title , or,\nwith native_window (a host window's native handle) and its pixel_ratio , render into that window. vsync (default true): frames\nare presented at the display's refresh; false: as soon as they are ready\n(where the driver allows it), e.g. to measure frame times. Returns false\non failure. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: width window units (logical pixels) integer, intent(in) :: height window units (logical pixels) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: title default 'vkframes' integer(kind=c_long_long), intent(in), optional :: native_window host window's handle (0: own window) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: pixel_ratio framebuffer pixels per window unit (default 1) logical, intent(in), optional :: vsync Return Value logical procedure, public :: pause_time private  subroutine pause_time (self, paused) Pause (true) or resume (false) the simulation time. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: paused procedure, public :: pick => window_pick private  subroutine window_pick (self, x, y, hits, tolerance, kinds, nearest) What is under point (x, y) of the window (-1 to 1 across it, y up: as\nthe event handler's positions), nearest first (see the module\ndocumentation): none before the first frame. tolerance : how close\nlines, markers and frames' origins must be, in window units (logical\npixels; default 4), beyond half a line's width or a marker's size. kinds : only hits of these kinds (PICK_*; the others aren't tested). nearest : only the nearest hit (cheaper: what is deeper than a hit\nfound is skipped, e.g. to pick on every mouse move). Frames and\nartists can be left out ( set_pickable(.false.) ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in), target :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: x -1 to 1 across the window, y up real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: y -1 to 1 across the window, y up type( PickHit ), intent(out), allocatable :: hits (:) what is there, nearest first real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: tolerance window units (default 4) integer, intent(in), optional :: kinds (:) PICK_* (default: all) logical, intent(in), optional :: nearest default false procedure, public :: pixel_ratio private pure function pixel_ratio (self) Framebuffer pixels per window unit of a host's window (as given to open or resize ; 1 for a window of its own). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) procedure, public :: previous_view private  subroutine previous_view (self, duration) Show the previous view (wrapping around); duration as select_view's. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: duration procedure, public :: recorded_frames private pure function recorded_frames (self) Frames recorded since recording started (the video's length: frames / fps). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer(kind=int64) procedure, public :: remove_all_views private  subroutine remove_all_views (self) Remove all the window's views (the default view is then used). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self procedure, public :: remove_hud_text private  subroutine remove_hud_text (self, h) Stop showing h in the window. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self type( HUDText ), intent(in), target :: h procedure, public :: remove_view private  subroutine remove_view (self, v) Remove all instances of v from the window's views. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self type( View ), intent(in), target :: v procedure, public :: render_stats private  function render_stats (self) result(stats) The window's frame rate and frame times (see vkf_diagnostics); zeros\nwhile it isn't open. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value type( RenderStats ) procedure, public :: resize private  subroutine resize (self, width, height, pixel_ratio) The host window was resized (framebuffer pixels), and pixel_ratio : its\nframebuffer pixels per window unit (Qt's devicePixelRatio), if it may\nhave changed (the window moved to a screen of another scale, or the\ndisplay's scaling changed: sizes in window units, such as line widths,\nmarkers and labels, are scaled by it). Once the scene is shown, a frame\nof the new size is rendered at once (call this from the host's resize\nevent), so that the window isn't shown stretched or blank while it is\nresized. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: width framebuffer pixels integer, intent(in) :: height framebuffer pixels real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: pixel_ratio framebuffer pixels per window unit procedure, public :: run private  subroutine run (self, max_frames) Render frames until the window is closed (or for max_frames frames). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in), optional :: max_frames procedure, public :: scene_counts private  function scene_counts (self) result(counts) The size of the window's scene graph (see vkf_diagnostics): traverses\nit all, for an occasional update, not every frame. Zeros while it isn't\nopen. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value type( SceneCounts ) procedure, public :: screen_position private  function screen_position (self, p, position) result(visible) Where point p (root frame) is in the window, as HUD text positions:\n(x, y) from 0 to 1, left to right and bottom to top (as at the last\nframe). False if it is behind the eye (or before the first frame).\nE.g. to keep HUD text next to a moving object, each frame: a callout. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: p (3) root frame real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: position (2) (x, y), 0 to 1 from the bottom left Return Value logical procedure, public :: scroll private  subroutine scroll (self, dy) The scroll wheel: dy > 0 away from the user. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dy wheel steps (> 0: away from the user; fractions\nfor a trackpad's small steps: Qt's angleDelta / 120) procedure, public :: select_view private  subroutine select_view (self, i, duration) Show view i (1 to num_views), flying there over duration s (default:\nthe view transition, set_view_transition ; 0: a cut). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: duration procedure, public :: set_background_color private  subroutine set_background_color (self, rgb) The background color [r, g, b] (0 to 1; default black). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rgb (3) procedure, public :: set_camera private  subroutine set_camera (self, eye, center, up, duration, in_root) Set the camera of the current view: eye, center and up in the view\nframe's coordinates (OpenFrames' trackball setTransformation), or in its\nroot frame's if in_root (as the frames are now). With duration (s),\nfly there from the camera shown. Before the view is shown, it is its\ncamera when it is (View%set_camera). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout), target :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eye (3) view frame's coordinates (or root's) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: center (3) view frame's coordinates (or root's) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: up (3) view frame's coordinates (or root's) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: duration s (default: at once) logical, intent(in), optional :: in_root procedure, public :: set_camera_throw private  subroutine set_camera_throw (self, enabled) Whether the camera keeps moving (turning, zooming, panning) after a drag\nis released while the mouse moves (default true, VSG's and OSG's throw);\nfalse: it stops where it is released. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: enabled procedure, public :: set_default_keys private  subroutine set_default_keys (self, on) The built-in keys (default on): v the next view, V the previous\none, the space bar resets the view. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: on procedure, public :: set_event_handler private  subroutine set_event_handler (self, handler) Give the window's keyboard and mouse events to handler (not owned: it\nmust stay alive while set), in place of any handler set before. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self class( WindowEventHandler ), intent(in), target :: handler not owned procedure, public :: set_light_ambient private  subroutine set_light_ambient (self, rgb) The ambient, diffuse and specular colors ([r, g, b], 0 to 1) of the\nwindow's light (OpenFrames' defaults: 0.2 gray, white, none). The\nwindow's light is used while no frame of the scene has a light source\n(ReferenceFrame%set_light_source_enabled). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rgb (3) procedure, public :: set_light_diffuse private  subroutine set_light_diffuse (self, rgb) The diffuse color of the window's light (see set_light_ambient ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rgb (3) procedure, public :: set_light_position private  subroutine set_light_position (self, position) The light's position in eye coordinates (x right, y up, z toward the\nviewer): [x, y, z, 0] for a directional light from direction (x, y, z),\n[x, y, z, 1] for a point light (OpenFrames' setLightPosition; default\n[0, 0, 1, 0], a headlight). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: position (4) [x, y, z, w], eye coordinates (not all 0) procedure, public :: set_light_specular private  subroutine set_light_specular (self, rgb) The specular color of the window's light (see set_light_ambient ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rgb (3) procedure, public :: set_scene private  subroutine set_scene (self, fm) Show the scene of fm (which must stay alive while shown). For now, set\nit before the window's first frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self type( FrameManager ), intent(in), target :: fm procedure, public :: set_sky private  subroutine set_sky (self, sky) Draw sky behind the scene (it must stay alive while shown; it can be\nshown in several windows), in place of the window's sky so far; at any\ntime (its texture and stars can change too). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self type( SkySphere ), intent(inout), target :: sky procedure, public :: set_time private  subroutine set_time (self, t) Set the simulation time (limited to the time range). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t simulation time procedure, public :: set_time_range private  subroutine set_time_range (self, t_min, t_max) Limit the simulation time to [t_min, t_max] (ignored if t_max < t_min). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t_min simulation times real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t_max simulation times procedure, public :: set_time_scale private  subroutine set_time_scale (self, scale) Simulation seconds per wall-clock second (may be 0 or negative). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: scale procedure, public :: set_view_transition private  subroutine set_view_transition (self, seconds) The time (s) a change of view or a reset flies from one camera to the\nother (default 0: a cut, as OpenFrames). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: seconds wall-clock s (0: a cut) procedure, public :: set_zoom_speed private  subroutine set_zoom_speed (self, speed) How fast the mouse zooms (default 1, VSG's: 10% per wheel step, and a\nright drag's rate): e.g. 0.3 for a gentler zoom. Scales scroll steps\nhowever they come (a mouse wheel, a trackpad, a host's scroll ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: speed (> 0; 1: the default) procedure, public :: sky private  function sky (self) result(s) The sky drawn behind the scene (null if none). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value type( SkySphere ), pointer procedure, public :: start_recording private  function start_recording (self, file, fps, quality, codec, scale, options, watermark, watermark_width, watermark_opacity, ffmpeg) result(ok) Start recording the frames drawn to the video file (see the module\ndocumentation), fps frames per second (default 30). Encoded by codec (an ffmpeg encoder; default libx264, H.264) at quality (for\nlibx264, libx265 and libvpx-vp9 the CRF: 0 lossless to 51, default 18,\nvisually lossless), scaled by scale (default 1; e.g. 0.5 for half the\nsize of a Retina window's pixels), the size made even. options replaces the encoder options (codec, quality; and the scale, unless\nthere is a watermark), e.g. '-c:v prores_ks -profile:v 3'. watermark : an image (e.g. a logo; PNG, SVG, ... with transparency)\ndrawn over the video's bottom right corner by ffmpeg, watermark_width of the video's width (default 0.2), watermark_opacity opaque (default\n0.6). ffmpeg : the program (default: VKFRAMES_FFMPEG, else ffmpeg on\nthe path). Returns false if the window isn't open, is already\nrecording or the watermark doesn't exist; ffmpeg's errors (e.g. an\nunknown encoder) show when it starts, at the next frame, and end the\nrecording. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: file the video file (e.g. .mp4, .mov, .webm) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: fps frames per second of the video (default 30) integer, intent(in), optional :: quality the CRF (default 18; lower is better) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: codec an ffmpeg encoder (default libx264) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: scale of the window's pixels (default 1) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: options ffmpeg's encoder options, instead of those above character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: watermark an image file drawn at the bottom right real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: watermark_width its width, of the video's (default 0.2) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: watermark_opacity 0 to 1 (default 0.6) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: ffmpeg the ffmpeg program Return Value logical procedure, public :: stop_recording private  function stop_recording (self, frames) result(ok) Stop recording: ffmpeg finishes the file. The window's time goes on\nfrom where the video was, on the wall clock again. frames : the\nframes written. Returns false if not recording or if the recording\nfailed (ffmpeg's messages are on the standard error). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self integer(kind=int64), intent(out), optional :: frames frames written to the video Return Value logical procedure, public :: stop_transition private  subroutine stop_transition (self) End a flight where the camera is now. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self procedure, public :: time private  function time (self) The simulation time (at the last frame). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) procedure, public :: time_range private  subroutine time_range (self, t_min, t_max) The simulation time range ( set_time_range ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: t_min real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: t_max procedure, public :: time_scale private  function time_scale (self) Simulation seconds per wall-clock second. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) procedure, public :: view => window_view private  function window_view (self, i) result(v) View i (1 to num_views). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i Return Value type( View ), pointer procedure, public :: view_transition private pure function view_transition (self) The time (s) a change of view or a reset flies ( set_view_transition ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) procedure, public :: viewer => window_viewer private  function window_viewer (self) result(v) The window's viewer handle in the rendering layer (null until open), for\nadding low-level nodes (src/vsg/vkf_layer.f90). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value type(c_ptr) procedure, public :: zoom_speed private pure function zoom_speed (self) The zoom speed (set_zoom_speed). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) Source Code type , public :: WindowProxy private type ( c_ptr ) :: viewer_ = c_null_ptr !! the rendering layer's viewer (null while closed) type ( FrameManager ), pointer :: scene => null () !! the scene shown (not owned) integer :: scene_seen = - 1 !! the scene's updates at this window's last frame type ( SimulationClock ) :: clock_ !! the window's simulation clock logical :: scene_added = . false . !! scene, sky, HUD texts given to the viewer real ( wp ) :: background ( 3 ) = [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp ] !! background color [r, g, b] (0 to 1) logical :: running = . false . !! open, and not closed by the user integer :: width_ = 1 , height_ = 1 !! logical size (for the views' aspect ratio) real ( wp ) :: pixel_ratio_ = 1.0_wp !! framebuffer pixels per window unit (a host's window) ! views type ( ViewPointer ), allocatable :: views (:) !! not owned (first n_views used) integer :: n_views = 0 , current = 0 !! number of views; the current one (0: none) type ( View ) :: default_view !! used when there are no views type ( View ), pointer :: shown => null () !! the view whose camera is in the renderer ! HUD text type ( HUDEntry ), allocatable :: huds (:) !! the HUD texts shown (first n_huds used) integer :: n_huds = 0 !! number of HUD texts type ( SkySphere ), pointer :: sky_ => null () !! the background sky ! the window's light (OpenFrames' default: a headlight) real ( wp ) :: light_ambient_ ( 3 ) = 0.2_wp , light_diffuse_ ( 3 ) = 1.0_wp , light_specular_ ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! [r, g, b] real ( wp ) :: light_position_ ( 4 ) = [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp ] !! eye coordinates (w 0: directional) logical :: light_on = . true . !! the window's light enabled (no frame's light source) ! keyboard and mouse class ( WindowEventHandler ), pointer :: handler => null () !! the program's event handler (not owned) class ( DragHandle ), pointer :: hovered_handle => null () !! the handle under the cursor (not owned) class ( DragHandle ), pointer :: dragged_handle => null () !! the handle grabbed (not owned) logical :: default_keys_ = . true . !! the built-in keys on logical :: hosted = . false . !! in a host's window (its size from `resize`) ! camera transitions real ( wp ) :: transition_ = 0.0_wp !! s, for view changes and resets real ( wp ) :: switch_duration = - 1.0_wp !! s, for the next view change (< 0: transition_) type ( CameraFlight ) :: flight !! the camera flight (when active) real ( wp ) :: zoom_speed_ = 1.0_wp !! the trackball's zoom per scroll step and drag (1: VSG's) logical :: camera_throw_ = . true . !! the camera keeps moving after a drag released while moving ! video recording logical :: recording_ = . false . !! recording (start_recording) real ( wp ) :: record_fps = 3 0.0_wp !! the video's frames per second real ( wp ) :: record_wall = 0.0_wp !! the wall time at the start (s) integer ( int64 ) :: record_frames = 0_int64 !! frames drawn while recording ! diagnostics (render_stats) real ( wp ) :: rate_start = - 1.0_wp !! the wall time the frames are counted from (s; -1: none) integer :: rate_frames = 0 !! frames since then real ( wp ) :: fps_ = 0.0_wp !! frames per second (the last count's) real ( wp ) :: frame_ms_ = 0.0_wp !! milliseconds between frames (the last count's) real ( wp ) :: last_frame_ms = 0.0_wp !! the last frame()'s duration (ms) contains procedure :: open , close , is_open , pixel_ratio procedure :: set_scene procedure :: frame , run procedure :: capture ! video recording (see the module documentation) procedure :: start_recording , stop_recording , is_recording , recorded_frames ! diagnostics (vkf_diagnostics) procedure :: render_stats , device_info , scene_counts procedure :: set_background_color , background_color ! views (OpenFrames' RenderRectangle) procedure :: add_view , remove_view , remove_all_views procedure :: select_view , next_view , previous_view procedure :: current_view , num_views ! the camera (OpenFrames' trackball transformation), smooth transitions procedure :: get_camera , set_camera procedure :: set_view_transition , view_transition , in_transition , stop_transition procedure :: set_zoom_speed , zoom_speed , set_camera_throw , camera_throw ! picking (see the module documentation), and where points are on the screen procedure :: pick => window_pick procedure :: screen_position , cursor_ray ! GUI panels (vkf_gui) procedure :: gui => window_gui ! HUD text (OpenFrames' RenderRectangle HUD) procedure :: add_hud_text , remove_hud_text procedure :: set_sky , sky procedure :: set_light_ambient , set_light_diffuse , set_light_specular , set_light_position procedure :: light_ambient , light_diffuse , light_specular , light_position procedure :: view => window_view ! simulation time (OpenFrames' WindowProxy time control) procedure :: set_time , time , pause_time , is_time_paused , set_time_scale , time_scale procedure :: set_time_range , time_range , clock procedure :: viewer => window_viewer ! events from a host window procedure :: mouse , scroll , key , resize ! the program's event handler (OpenFrames' callbacks), built-in keys procedure :: set_event_handler , clear_event_handler , event_handler procedure :: set_default_keys , default_keys end type WindowProxy","tags":"","url":"type/windowproxy.html"},{"title":"HUDText – vkframes ","text":"type, public :: HUDText HUD text (see the module documentation). Inherited by type~~hudtext~~InheritedByGraph type~hudtext HUDText type~hudentry HUDEntry type~hudentry->type~hudtext p type~windowproxy WindowProxy type~windowproxy->type~hudentry huds Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, private :: alignment_ = ALIGN_LEFT_BOTTOM the point of the text at position_ (ALIGN_*) real(kind=wp), private :: color_ (4) = [1.0_wp, 1.0_wp, 1.0_wp, 1.0_wp] [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) character(len=:), private, allocatable :: font_ font file (unallocated: the default font) real(kind=wp), private :: position_ (2) = [0.01_wp, 0.01_wp] [x, y] (0 to 1 across the window, y up) integer, private :: revision_ = 0 incremented by each change logical, private :: shown = .true. false while hidden real(kind=wp), private :: size_ = 20.0_wp character height (window units) character(len=:), private, allocatable :: text_ the text Constructor public        interface HUDText The HUDText constructor: HUDText(...) makes one (see new_hud_text for its\narguments). private  function new_hud_text (text, position, alignment, size, color, font) result(h) HUD text text , optionally at position ([x, y], 0 to 1; default near\nthe bottom left), with alignment (default ALIGN_LEFT_BOTTOM), size (window units; default 20), color ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]; default\nwhite) and font (default: the default font). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: text real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: position (2) [x, y] (0 to 1 across the window, y up) integer, intent(in), optional :: alignment an ALIGN_* constant real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: size character height (window units) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: color (:) [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: font font file Return Value type( HUDText ) Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: alignment private pure function alignment (self) Which point of the text is at its position (an ALIGN_* constant). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: color private pure function color (self) result(c) The color: [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (4) procedure, public :: font private  function font (self) result(f) The font file ('' for the default font). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(in) :: self Return Value character(len=:), allocatable procedure, public :: is_shown private pure function is_shown (self) True if the text is shown. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: position private pure function position (self) result(p) Where the text is: [x, y] (0 to 1 across the window, y up). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (2) procedure, public :: revision private pure function revision (self) Number of changes so far (for the windows drawing the text to update it). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: set_alignment private  subroutine set_alignment (self, alignment) Set which point of the text is at its position. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: alignment an ALIGN_* constant procedure, public :: set_color private  subroutine set_color (self, color) [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: color (:) procedure, public :: set_font private  subroutine set_font (self, font) Set the font (the text is made again when next drawn). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: font font file procedure, public :: set_position private  subroutine set_position (self, position) Set where the text is. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: position (2) [x, y] (0 to 1 across the window, y up) procedure, public :: set_size private  subroutine set_size (self, size) Set the size of the text. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: size character height (window units) procedure, public :: set_text private  subroutine set_text (self, text) Set the text (up to 256 characters, or twice the first text's length; see the module documentation). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: text procedure, public :: show private  subroutine show (self, shown) Show (true) or hide the text (OpenFrames' enable HUD text). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: shown procedure, public :: size private pure function size (self) The size of the text: character height (window units). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) procedure, public :: text private  function text (self) result(t) The text (as shown: '' while hidden). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( HUDText ), intent(in) :: self Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Source Code type , public :: HUDText private character ( len = :), allocatable :: text_ !! the text real ( wp ) :: position_ ( 2 ) = [ 0.01_wp , 0.01_wp ] !! [x, y] (0 to 1 across the window, y up) integer :: alignment_ = ALIGN_LEFT_BOTTOM !! the point of the text at `position_` (ALIGN_*) real ( wp ) :: size_ = 2 0.0_wp !! character height (window units) real ( wp ) :: color_ ( 4 ) = [ 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) character ( len = :), allocatable :: font_ !! font file (unallocated: the default font) logical :: shown = . true . !! false while hidden integer :: revision_ = 0 !! incremented by each change contains procedure :: set_text , text procedure :: set_position , position procedure :: set_alignment , alignment procedure :: set_size , size procedure :: set_color , color procedure :: set_font , font procedure :: show , is_shown procedure :: revision end type HUDText","tags":"","url":"type/hudtext.html"},{"title":"DragHandle – vkframes ","text":"type, public, abstract, extends( ReferenceFrame ) :: DragHandle A handle the mouse drags (see the module documentation): extensions\ngive its point and draw it. Inherits type~~draghandle~~InheritsGraph type~draghandle DragHandle type~referenceframe ReferenceFrame type~draghandle->type~referenceframe c_ptr c_ptr type~referenceframe->c_ptr light_node, light_switch, node_, contents_node, axis_node, axis_label_node, axis_arrow, axis_text, name_label_node, name_text type~framepointer FramePointer type~referenceframe->type~framepointer children, parents type~trajectoryfollower TrajectoryFollower type~referenceframe->type~trajectoryfollower follower_ type~framepointer->type~referenceframe p type~datasource DataSource type~trajectoryfollower->type~datasource sources_ type~trajectorypointer TrajectoryPointer type~trajectoryfollower->type~trajectorypointer trajs type~trajectory Trajectory type~trajectorypointer->type~trajectory p Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Inherited by type~~draghandle~~InheritedByGraph type~draghandle DragHandle type~timehandle TimeHandle type~timehandle->type~draghandle type~vectorhandle VectorHandle type~vectorhandle->type~draghandle type~windowproxy WindowProxy type~windowproxy->type~draghandle hovered_handle, dragged_handle Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=wp), private :: axis_ (3) = [0.0_wp, 0.0_wp, 1.0_wp] the plane's normal or the line's direction (frame coordinates) integer, private :: constraint_ = HANDLE_FREE HANDLE_* logical, private :: draggable_ = .true. the mouse may grab it logical, private :: dragged_ = .false. grabbed, until released logical, private :: far_side = .false. (HANDLE_SPHERE) grabbed on the far side logical, private :: hovered_ = .false. under the cursor real(kind=wp), private :: offset (3) = 0.0_wp the point's offset from the cursor's integer, private :: priority_ = 0 over other handles on the same spot (higher first) real(kind=wp), private :: radius = 0.0_wp (HANDLE_SPHERE) the sphere's radius real(kind=wp), private :: ref_axis (3) = 0.0_wp the plane's normal or the line's direction then real(kind=wp), private :: ref_point (3) = 0.0_wp the point when grabbed Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: add_child private  function add_child (self, child) result(ok) Add child to this frame's children. Returns false (and does nothing)\nfor this frame itself or an ancestor of it; true if it is already a child. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout), target :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout), target :: child Return Value logical procedure, public :: attitude private pure function attitude (self) result(q) Attitude relative to the parent frame, a quaternion [x, y, z, w]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (4) procedure, public :: axes_labels_shown private pure function axes_labels_shown (self) Which axes labels are shown (as axes_shown ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: axes_shown private pure function axes_shown (self) Which axes vectors are shown (NO_AXES, or X_AXIS, Y_AXIS, Z_AXIS combined). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: axis_label private  function axis_label (self, axis) result(text) The label text of axis X_AXIS, Y_AXIS or Z_AXIS. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: axis Return Value character(len=:), allocatable procedure, public :: bound private  subroutine bound (self, center, radius) The bounding sphere of what the frame draws, in its own coordinates\n(radius 0 if it draws nothing; extensions override it). Views use it for\ntheir default distance. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: center (3) frame's coordinates real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: radius frame's coordinates procedure, public :: build_contents private  subroutine build_contents (self, viewer, group) Add what this frame draws to group (a node handle). ReferenceFrame\ndraws nothing itself (its axes and labels come later); extensions such as\nSphere and Model override this. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer (viewer: as realize 's) type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: group (viewer: as realize 's) procedure, public :: child private  function child (self, i) result(c) Child i (1 to num_children). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i Return Value class( ReferenceFrame ), pointer procedure, public :: child_index private  function child_index (self, frame) Index of frame among the children, or 0. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), target :: frame Return Value integer procedure, public :: color private pure function color (self) result(c) The color of the frame's decorations, [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (4) procedure, public :: constraint private pure function constraint (self) The handle's constraint (HANDLE_*). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: constraint_axis private pure function constraint_axis (self) result(axis) The constraint's normal or direction (unit vector, frame coordinates). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: contents_shown private pure function contents_shown (self) Whether what the frame draws is shown ( show_contents ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: detach private  subroutine detach (self) Remove this frame from all its parents and children (before it goes out\nof scope or is deallocated while in a tree). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout), target :: self procedure, public :: drag private  function drag (self, origin, dir) result(moved) Drag the grabbed handle to the cursor's ray (origin, unit dir; root\nframe), held to its constraint. False (and not moved) if it isn't\ngrabbed or the ray doesn't meet the constraint. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: origin (3) the cursor's ray (root frame) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dir (3) the cursor's ray (root frame) Return Value logical procedure, public :: draggable private pure function draggable (self) Whether the mouse may grab the handle. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: dragged private pure function dragged (self) The handle is grabbed (until released). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: follow private  subroutine follow (self, traj, data, mode, add) Follow traj (in addition to trajectories already followed, if add is true), with what to follow ( data : FOLLOW_POSITION and/or\nFOLLOW_ATTITUDE; default both) and how ( mode : FOLLOW_LOOP, the\ndefault, or FOLLOW_LIMIT). traj must stay alive while followed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self type( Trajectory ), intent(in), target :: traj the trajectory to follow (not owned) integer, intent(in), optional :: data FOLLOW_POSITION/FOLLOW_ATTITUDE; FOLLOW_LOOP/FOLLOW_LIMIT integer, intent(in), optional :: mode FOLLOW_POSITION/FOLLOW_ATTITUDE; FOLLOW_LOOP/FOLLOW_LIMIT logical, intent(in), optional :: add (true: in addition to those followed (default false)) procedure, public :: follower private  function follower (self) result(f) The frame's trajectory follower, for finer control (data sources, time\noffset, ...). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), target :: self Return Value type( TrajectoryFollower ), pointer procedure, public :: frame_info private  function frame_info (self) result(info) What kind of frame this is (shown by frame_string ; extensions override it). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value character(len=:), allocatable procedure, public :: frame_string private recursive function frame_string (self, prefix) result(str) The tree below this frame, one line per frame (\"name (info)\"), in\nOpenFrames' createFrameString format: children are prefixed \"|-->\". Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: prefix before this frame's line (default ' ') Return Value character(len=:), allocatable procedure, public :: grab private  function grab (self, origin, dir) result(ok) Grab the handle with the cursor's ray (origin, unit dir; root frame):\nits constraint is taken as it is now, and the point's offset from where\nthe ray meets it. False if it isn't draggable. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: origin (3) the cursor's ray (root frame) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dir (3) the cursor's ray (root frame) Return Value logical procedure( handle_point_interface ), public, deferred :: handle_point pure function handle_point_interface(self) result(p) Prototype The point the mouse grabs (frame coordinates). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: has_light_source private recursive function has_light_source (self) result(has) Whether this frame or one of its descendants has a light source enabled. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: hovered private pure function hovered (self) The handle is under the cursor. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: is_following private pure function is_following (self) Whether the frame follows trajectories (at least one, since follow ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: label_alignment private pure function label_alignment (self) The labels' alignment (ALIGN_*). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: label_font private  function label_font (self) result(font) The labels' font as set ('' for the renderer's default). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value character(len=:), allocatable procedure, public :: label_size private pure function label_size (self) The labels' size in pixels. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: late_update private recursive subroutine late_update (self, t) After the whole tree's update for time t (all frames at their positions\nfor t): for contents that depend on other frames' positions, e.g.\nCustomLineSegments between spacecraft. Here, only the descendants'. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t simulation time procedure, public :: light_ambient private pure function light_ambient (self) result(rgb) The light source's ambient color [r, g, b]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: light_diffuse private pure function light_diffuse (self) result(rgb) The light source's diffuse color [r, g, b]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: light_source_enabled private pure function light_source_enabled (self) Whether this frame carries a light source. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: light_specular private pure function light_specular (self) result(rgb) The light source's specular color [r, g, b]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: local_matrix private pure function local_matrix (self) result(m) The transform from this frame to its parent (4x4). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (4,4) procedure( move_handle_point_interface ), public, deferred :: move_handle_point subroutine move_handle_point_interface(self, p) Prototype Move the point to p (frame coordinates), and the drawing with it. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: p (3) the new point (frame coordinates) procedure, public :: move_x_axis private  subroutine move_x_axis (self, base, length, head_ratio, body_radius, head_radius) Place the x axis vector: from base , length long, with a head of head_ratio of the length (default 0.3) and body and head radii (default\n0.05 and 0.1 of the length); its label is at the tip, 0.4 of the length\ntall (at most label_size pixels). As OpenFrames' moveXAxis. Set before\nthe frame is first shown. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: base (3) (base: frame's coordinates) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: length (base: frame's coordinates) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: head_ratio real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: body_radius real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: head_radius procedure, public :: move_y_axis private  subroutine move_y_axis (self, base, length, head_ratio, body_radius, head_radius) Place the y axis vector (as move_x_axis ; OpenFrames' moveYAxis). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: base (3) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: length real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: head_ratio real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: body_radius real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: head_radius procedure, public :: move_z_axis private  subroutine move_z_axis (self, base, length, head_ratio, body_radius, head_radius) Place the z axis vector (as move_x_axis ; OpenFrames' moveZAxis). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: base (3) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: length real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: head_ratio real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: body_radius real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: head_radius procedure, public :: name private  function name (self) result(n) The frame's name ('' if none). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value character(len=:), allocatable procedure, public :: name_label_on_top private pure function name_label_on_top (self) Whether the name label is drawn on top of the scene ( set_name_label_on_top ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: name_label_shown private pure function name_label_shown (self) Whether the name label is shown. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: node private  function node (self) result(n) The frame's transform node (null until realized). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value type(c_ptr) procedure, public :: num_children private pure function num_children (self) Number of children. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: num_parents private pure function num_parents (self) Number of parents. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: parent private  function parent (self, i) result(p) Parent i (1 to num_parents). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i Return Value class( ReferenceFrame ), pointer procedure, public :: parent_index private  function parent_index (self, frame) Index of frame among the parents, or 0. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), target :: frame Return Value integer procedure, public :: pick private  subroutine pick (self, cam, to_root, hits, n) Pick what the frame draws (see the module documentation): to_root is its transform to the root frame; hits are added to hits(1:n). A\nplain frame: its origin, if it shows axes or its name label. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), target :: self type( PickCamera ), intent(in) :: cam the cursor's ray and the pick's settings real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: to_root (4,4) the frame's transform to the root frame type( PickHit ), intent(inout), allocatable :: hits (:) hits so far (grown as needed) integer, intent(inout) :: n number of hits in hits procedure, public :: pickable private pure function pickable (self) Whether pick tests what this frame draws ( set_pickable ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: position private pure function position (self) result(p) Position relative to the parent frame. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: position_of private  function position_of (self, other) result(p) The origin of other (a frame of the same tree) in this frame's\ncoordinates, from both frames' transforms to the root (through their\nfirst parents). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: other Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) procedure, public :: priority private pure function priority (self) The handle's priority over others on the same spot. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: realize private recursive subroutine realize (self, viewer) Create the render nodes of this frame and its descendants (once; for viewer , a window's viewer handle, which some contents need while they\nare built (not kept); null: headless). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer a window's viewer handle (null: headless) procedure, public :: release private  subroutine release (self) Let the handle go. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(inout) :: self procedure, public :: remove_child private  function remove_child (self, child) result(ok) Remove child from this frame's children. Returns false if it is not one. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout), target :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout), target :: child Return Value logical procedure, public :: reposition_axes private  subroutine reposition_axes (self) Place the axes for what the frame draws, when it is first shown (unless\nmove_*_axis was called): at its bound's surface, half the bound's radius\nlong (as OpenFrames' Sphere and Model do); at the origin, 1 long, for a\nframe that draws nothing. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self procedure, public :: set_attitude private  subroutine set_attitude (self, q) Attitude relative to the parent frame, a quaternion [x, y, z, w]\n(normalized here; overridden by a followed trajectory). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: q (4) procedure, public :: set_color private  subroutine set_color (self, color) The color of the frame's decorations: [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: color (:) procedure, public :: set_constraint private  subroutine set_constraint (self, constraint, axis) Where the handle can be dragged (HANDLE_*; see the module documentation),\nwith axis : the plane's normal (HANDLE_PLANE) or the line's direction\n(HANDLE_LINE), in the frame's coordinates. Taken when the handle is\nnext grabbed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: constraint HANDLE_* real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: axis (3) (frame coordinates; any length but 0) procedure, public :: set_draggable private  subroutine set_draggable (self, draggable) Whether the mouse may grab the handle (default true). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: draggable true: the mouse may grab it procedure, public :: set_hovered private  subroutine set_hovered (self, hovered) The handle is under the cursor (set by the window), or not. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: hovered true: under the cursor procedure, public :: set_label_alignment private  subroutine set_label_alignment (self, alignment) The alignment of the labels relative to their positions (ALIGN_*;\ndefault ALIGN_LEFT_BASE_LINE). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: alignment procedure, public :: set_label_font private  subroutine set_label_font (self, font) The font of the labels: a font file name (found on the data search\npath) or a full path; default: the renderer's default font. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: font procedure, public :: set_label_size private  subroutine set_label_size (self, size) The size of the labels in pixels (default 20): the name label's size,\nand the maximum size of the axes labels (which shrink with distance). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: size procedure, public :: set_light_ambient private  subroutine set_light_ambient (self, rgb) The light source's ambient, diffuse and specular colors ([r, g, b], 0\nto 1; defaults 0.05, 0.8 and 0.05 gray). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rgb (3) procedure, public :: set_light_diffuse private  subroutine set_light_diffuse (self, rgb) The light source's diffuse color (see set_light_ambient ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rgb (3) procedure, public :: set_light_source_enabled private  subroutine set_light_source_enabled (self, enable) Whether this frame carries a light source: a point light at its origin\n(e.g. the Sun), not dimmed with distance (default false; OpenFrames'\nsetLightSourceEnabled). While any frame of a window's scene has one, the\nwindow's own light (WindowProxy%set_light_*) is off. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: enable procedure, public :: set_light_specular privat