r pixels) end type RenderStats","tags":"","url":"type/renderstats.html"},{"title":"SceneCounts – vkframes ","text":"type, public :: SceneCounts The size of a window's scene graph: what is switched off isn't counted. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=int64), public :: draws = 0_int64 draw commands integer(kind=int64), public :: nodes = 0_int64 nodes integer(kind=int64), public :: vertices = 0_int64 vertices drawn (indices for indexed draws, times instances) Source Code type , public :: SceneCounts integer ( int64 ) :: nodes = 0_int64 !! nodes integer ( int64 ) :: draws = 0_int64 !! draw commands integer ( int64 ) :: vertices = 0_int64 !! vertices drawn (indices for indexed draws, times instances) end type SceneCounts","tags":"","url":"type/scenecounts.html"},{"title":"ShadowCones – vkframes ","text":"type, public, extends( ReferenceFrame ) :: ShadowCones A body's shadow cones (see the module documentation). Inherits type~~shadowcones~~InheritsGraph type~shadowcones ShadowCones type~referenceframe ReferenceFrame type~shadowcones->type~referenceframe body_, light_ type~shadowcones->type~referenceframe type~shadowregion ShadowRegion type~shadowcones->type~shadowregion region c_ptr c_ptr type~referenceframe->c_ptr light_node, light_switch, node_, contents_node, axis_node, axis_label_node, axis_arrow, axis_text, name_label_node, name_text type~framepointer FramePointer type~referenceframe->type~framepointer children, parents type~trajectoryfollower TrajectoryFollower type~referenceframe->type~trajectoryfollower follower_ type~shadowregion->c_ptr switch, mesh type~framepointer->type~referenceframe p type~datasource DataSource type~trajectoryfollower->type~datasource sources_ type~trajectorypointer TrajectoryPointer type~trajectoryfollower->type~trajectorypointer trajs type~trajectory Trajectory type~trajectorypointer->type~trajectory p Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial class( ReferenceFrame ), private, pointer :: body_ => null() the body casting the shadow (not owned) real(kind=wp), private :: body_radius_ = 0.0_wp (0: the frames' own) real(kind=wp), private :: distance_ = 0.0_wp body to light at the last update (scene units) real(kind=wp), private :: drawn_length_ = 0.0_wp the length drawn at the last update (scene units) real(kind=wp), private :: length_ = 0.0_wp (0: automatic) class( ReferenceFrame ), private, pointer :: light_ => null() the light (not owned) real(kind=wp), private :: light_radius_ = 0.0_wp (0: the frames' own) type( ShadowRegion ), private :: region (n_regions) umbra, penumbra and antumbra integer, private :: regions_ = SHADOW_ALL an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA, SHADOW_ANTUMBRA real(kind=wp), private :: shaped (4) = -1.0_wp R, Rs, d and length the cones have now Constructor public        interface ShadowCones The ShadowCones constructor: ShadowCones(...) makes one (see new_shadow_cones for its\narguments). private  function new_shadow_cones (name, body, light, body_radius, light_radius) result(s) The shadow named name of body in the light of light (frames of the\nsame tree; optional here, set later with set_body and set_light), with\ntheir radii if given (else the frames': see the module documentation).\nIts axes and name label are hidden. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), optional, target :: body class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), optional, target :: light real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: body_radius scene units (default: the frames' own) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: light_radius scene units (default: the frames' own) Return Value type( ShadowCones ) Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: add_child private  function add_child (self, child) result(ok) Add child to this frame's children. Returns false (and does nothing)\nfor this frame itself or an ancestor of it; true if it is already a child. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout), target :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout), target :: child Return Value logical procedure, public :: attitude private pure function attitude (self) result(q) Attitude relative to the parent frame, a quaternion [x, y, z, w]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (4) procedure, public :: axes_labels_shown private pure function axes_labels_shown (self) Which axes labels are shown (as axes_shown ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: axes_shown private pure function axes_shown (self) Which axes vectors are shown (NO_AXES, or X_AXIS, Y_AXIS, Z_AXIS combined). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer procedure, public :: axis_label private  function axis_label (self, axis) result(text) The label text of axis X_AXIS, Y_AXIS or Z_AXIS. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: axis Return Value character(len=:), allocatable procedure, public :: body private  function body (self) result(p) The body casting the shadow (null if not set). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(in) :: self Return Value class( ReferenceFrame ), pointer procedure, public :: body_radius private  function body_radius (self) The body's radius used (0: none known). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) procedure, public :: bound => shadow_bound private  subroutine shadow_bound (self, center, radius) The drawn regions' bounding sphere (frame coordinates). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: center (3) the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: radius the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) procedure, public :: build_contents => shadow_build_contents private  subroutine shadow_build_contents (self, viewer, group) A switch with a mesh for each region (vertices written at each change\nof shape), under group . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer a window's viewer (null: headless) type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: group the frame's contents group procedure, public :: child private  function child (self, i) result(c) Child i (1 to num_children). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i Return Value class( ReferenceFrame ), pointer procedure, public :: child_index private  function child_index (self, frame) Index of frame among the children, or 0. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), target :: frame Return Value integer procedure, public :: color private pure function color (self) result(c) The color of the frame's decorations, [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (4) procedure, public :: contents_shown private pure function contents_shown (self) Whether what the frame draws is shown ( show_contents ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical procedure, public :: detach private  subroutine detach (self) Remove this