c~set_x_data->proc~data_valid proc~verify_data Trajectory%verify_data proc~data_valid->proc~verify_data Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code logical function set_x_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src self % sources_ ( 1 ) = src self % default_data = . false . valid = self % data_valid () end function set_x_data","tags":"","url":"proc/set_x_data.html"},{"title":"set_y_data – vkframes","text":"private  function set_y_data(self, src) result(valid) Where the y of the followed position comes from (see set_x_data ). Type Bound TrajectoryFollower Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryFollower ), intent(inout) :: self type( DataSource ), intent(in) :: src Return Value logical Calls proc~~set_y_data~~CallsGraph proc~set_y_data TrajectoryFollower%set_y_data proc~data_valid TrajectoryFollower%data_valid proc~set_y_data->proc~data_valid proc~verify_data Trajectory%verify_data proc~data_valid->proc~verify_data Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code logical function set_y_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src self % sources_ ( 2 ) = src self % default_data = . false . valid = self % data_valid () end function set_y_data","tags":"","url":"proc/set_y_data.html"},{"title":"set_z_data – vkframes","text":"private  function set_z_data(self, src) result(valid) Where the z of the followed position comes from (see set_x_data ). Type Bound TrajectoryFollower Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryFollower ), intent(inout) :: self type( DataSource ), intent(in) :: src Return Value logical Calls proc~~set_z_data~~CallsGraph proc~set_z_data TrajectoryFollower%set_z_data proc~data_valid TrajectoryFollower%data_valid proc~set_z_data->proc~data_valid proc~verify_data Trajectory%verify_data proc~data_valid->proc~verify_data Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code logical function set_z_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src self % sources_ ( 3 ) = src self % default_data = . false . valid = self % data_valid () end function set_z_data","tags":"","url":"proc/set_z_data.html"},{"title":"using_default_data – vkframes","text":"private pure function using_default_data(self) True if the followed position is the trajectories' positions ( set_default_data ). Type Bound TrajectoryFollower Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryFollower ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical Source Code pure logical function using_default_data ( self ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self using_default_data = self % default_data end function using_default_data","tags":"","url":"proc/using_default_data.html"},{"title":"wrapped_time – vkframes","text":"private  function wrapped_time(self, t) result(tw) For FOLLOW_LOOP, t wrapped into the combined time range of the trajectories. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( TrajectoryFollower ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t Return Value real(kind=wp) Calls proc~~wrapped_time~~CallsGraph proc~wrapped_time wrapped_time proc~time_range Trajectory%time_range proc~wrapped_time->proc~time_range Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~wrapped_time~~CalledByGraph proc~wrapped_time wrapped_time proc~update TrajectoryFollower%update proc~update->proc~wrapped_time proc~update~3 ReferenceFrame%update proc~update~3->proc~update proc~drawable_update DrawableTrajectory%drawable_update proc~drawable_update->proc~update~3 proc~fm_update FrameManager%fm_update proc~fm_update->proc~update~3 proc~sphere_update Sphere%sphere_update proc~sphere_update->proc~update~3 proc~terrain_update TerrainBody%terrain_update proc~terrain_update->proc~update~3 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code real ( wp ) function wrapped_time ( self , t ) result ( tw ) type ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t real ( wp ) :: t0 , tf , a , b integer :: k tw = t if ( self % mode_ == FOLLOW_LIMIT ) return t0 = huge ( 1.0_wp ) tf = - huge ( 1.0_wp ) do k = 1 , self % n if (. not . self % trajs ( k )% p % time_range ( a , b )) cycle t0 = min ( t0 , a ) tf = max ( tf , b ) end do if ( t0 == huge ( 1.0_wp )) return if ( tf - t0 <= 8.0_wp * tiny ( 1.0_wp )) then tw = t0 else tw = t0 + modulo ( t - t0 , tf - t0 ) ! t - floor((t - t0)/(tf - t0)) * (tf - t0), in real arithmetic end if end function wrapped_time","tags":"","url":"proc/wrapped_time.html"},{"title":"add_trajectory – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine add_trajectory(self, traj) Also follow traj (no effect if it is already followed). Type Bound TrajectoryFollower Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TrajectoryFollower ), intent(inout) :: self type( Trajectory ), intent(in), pointer :: traj Calls proc~~add_trajectory~~CallsGraph proc~add_trajectory TrajectoryFollower%add_trajectory proc~set_default_data TrajectoryFollower%set_default_data proc~add_trajectory->proc~set_default_data proc~dof Trajectory%dof proc~set_default_data->proc~dof proc~position_sources position_sources proc~set_default_data->proc~position_sources Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours 