 self % trajs ( self % n )% p => traj if ( self % default_data ) call self % set_default_data () end subroutine add_trajectory","tags":"","url":"proc/add_trajectory.html"},{"title":"interpolate_attitude – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine interpolate_attitude(traj, t, status, index, attitude, ok) Slerp of the attitude at time t; the first/last attitude outside the time\nrange. status and index : the trajectory's time_index for t. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( Trajectory ), intent(in) :: traj real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t integer, intent(in) :: status integer, intent(in) :: index real(kind=wp), intent(inout) :: attitude (4) quaternion [x, y, z, w] logical, intent(out) :: ok false if there is no attitude (attitude unchanged) Calls proc~~interpolate_attitude~~CallsGraph proc~interpolate_attitude interpolate_attitude proc~attitude~2 Trajectory%attitude proc~interpolate_attitude->proc~attitude~2 proc~num_attitudes Trajectory%num_attitudes proc~interpolate_attitude->proc~num_attitudes proc~quat_slerp quat_slerp proc~interpolate_attitude->proc~quat_slerp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~interpolate_attitude~~CalledByGraph proc~interpolate_attitude interpolate_attitude proc~update TrajectoryFollower%update proc~update->proc~interpolate_attitude proc~update~3 ReferenceFrame%update proc~update~3->proc~update proc~drawable_update DrawableTrajectory%drawable_update proc~drawable_update->proc~update~3 proc~fm_update