e Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function pick_camera ( eye , center , up , perspective , fovy , aspect , ortho , width , height , x , y , tolerance ) & result ( cam ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eye ( 3 ), center ( 3 ), up ( 3 ) !! the camera (root frame) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: fovy !! vertical field of view (degrees; perspective) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: aspect !! width / height (perspective) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: ortho ( 4 ) !! left, right, bottom, top (orthographic) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x , y !! the cursor (-1 to 1, y up) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tolerance !! (framebuffer pixels) logical , intent ( in ) :: perspective !! (true: perspective; false: orthographic) integer , intent ( in ) :: width , height !! the viewport (framebuffer pixels) type ( PickCamera ) :: cam real ( wp ) :: f ( 3 ), r ( 3 ), d f = center - eye d = norm2 ( f ) if ( d > 0.0_wp ) f = f / d r = cross ( f , up ) if ( norm2 ( r ) > 0.0_wp ) r = r / norm2 ( r ) cam % eye = eye cam % forward = f cam % right = r cam % up = cross ( r , f ) cam % perspective = perspective cam % tan_y = tan ( 0.5_wp * fovy * pi / 18 0.0_wp ) cam % aspect = aspect cam % ortho = ortho cam % half_w = 0.5_wp * max ( 1 , width ) cam % half_h = 0.5_wp * max ( 1 , height ) cam % x = x cam % y = y cam % tolerance = tolerance cam % near = 1.0e-6_wp * max ( d , tiny ( 1.0_wp )) ! (as the renderer's near plane) end function pick_camera","tags":"","url":"proc/pick_camera.html"},{"title":"point_pick – vkframes","text":"public  function point_pick(cam, p, pixels, depth, extra) result(hit) Point p (root frame) is within the tolerance (plus extra pixels, e.g.\nhalf a marker's