ii, distance, point, local) result(hit) Where the ray (origin, unit dir) first meets the ellipsoid centered at center with semi-axes radii along the columns of axes (unit\nvectors): the distance along the ray, the point, and the point in the\nellipsoid's axes (from its center). False if it misses (or the\nellipsoid is behind). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: origin (3) the ray (dir: a unit vector) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dir (3) the ray (dir: a unit vector) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: center (3) the ellipsoid's center real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: axes (3,3) its axes (columns: unit vectors) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: radii (3) its semi-axes along them real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: distance along the ray (huge() if missed) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: point (3) the point met real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: local (3) the point in the ellipsoid's axes, from its center Return Value logical Called by proc~~ray_ellipsoid~~CalledByGraph proc~ray_ellipsoid ray_ellipsoid proc~pick_ellipsoid pick_ellipsoid proc~pick_ellipsoid->proc~ray_ellipsoid proc~model_pick Model%model_pick proc~model_pick->proc~pick_ellipsoid proc~sphere_pick Sphere%sphere_pick proc~sphere_pick->proc~pick_ellipsoid proc~terrain_pick TerrainBody%terrain_pick proc~terrain_pick->proc~pick_ellipsoid Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code logical function ray_ellipsoid ( origin , dir , center , axes , radii , distance , point , local ) result ( hit ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the ray (dir: a unit vector) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: center ( 3 ) !! the ellipsoid's center real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: axes ( 3 , 3 ) !! its axes (columns: unit vectors) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radii ( 3 ) !! its semi-axes along them real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: distance !! along the ray (huge() if missed) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: point ( 3 ) !! the point met real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: local ( 3 ) !! the point in the ellipsoid's axes, from its center real ( wp ) :: o ( 3 ), d ( 3 ), qa , qb , qc , disc , t hit = . false . distance = huge ( 1.0_wp ) point = 0.0_wp local = 0.0_wp if ( any ( radii <= 0.0_wp )) return o = matmul ( transpose ( axes ), origin - center ) / radii ! (the unit sphere) d = matmul ( transpose ( axes ), dir ) / radii qa = dot_product ( d , d ) qb = 2.0_wp * dot_product ( o , d ) qc = dot_product ( o , o ) - 1.0_wp disc = qb * qb - 4.0_wp * qa * qc if ( disc < 0.0_wp . or . qa <= 0.0_wp ) return t = ( - qb - sqrt ( disc )) / ( 2.0_wp * qa ) if ( t < 0.0_wp ) t = ( - qb + sqrt ( disc )) / ( 2.0_wp * qa ) ! (the eye inside it: where the ray leaves) if ( t < 0.0_wp ) return distance = t point = origin + t * dir local = ( o + t * d ) * radii hit = . true . end function ray_ellipsoid","tags":"","url":"proc/ray_ellipsoid.html"},{"title":"ray_line – vkframes","text":"public  function ray_line(origin, dir, point, axis, s, line_point) result(hit) The point of the line through point along axis closest to the ray\n(origin, unit dir): its parameter s (the point is point + s * axis,\naxis normalized) and the point. False if the ray and the line are\nparallel (within 1e-6 of it, as a sine squared), or the closest point\nof the ray is behind its origin. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: origin (3) the ray (dir: a unit vector) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dir (3) the ray (dir: a unit vector) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: p