), b , d , e , denom hit = . false . s = 0.0_wp line_point = point if ( norm2 ( axis ) <= 0.0_wp ) return u = axis / norm2 ( axis ) w = point - origin b = dot_product ( u , dir ) d = dot_product ( u , w ) e = dot_product ( dir , w ) denom = 1.0_wp - b * b if ( denom < 1.0e-6_wp ) return s = ( b * e - d ) / denom if (( e + b * s ) < 0.0_wp ) return ! (the ray's closest point: origin + (e + b s) dir) line_point = point + s * u hit = . true . end function ray_line","tags":"","url":"proc/ray_line.html"},{"title":"ray_plane – vkframes","text":"public  function ray_plane(origin, dir, point, normal, distance, hit_point) result(hit) Where the ray (origin, unit dir) meets the plane through point with\nnormal normal : the distance along the ray and the point. False if the\nray is parallel to the plane (within 1e-6 of it, as a cosine) or the\nplane is behind. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: origin (3) the ray (dir: a unit vector) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dir (3) the ray (dir: a unit vector) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: point (3) the plane (normal: any length but 0) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: normal (3) the plane (normal: any length but 0) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: distance along the ray (huge() if missed) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: hit_point (3) the point met Return Value logical Called by proc~~ray_plane~~CalledByGraph proc~ray_plane ray_plane proc~constrained constrained proc~constrained->proc~ray_plane proc~drag DragHandle%drag proc~drag->proc~constrained proc~grab DragHandle%grab proc~grab->proc~constrained proc~drag_handle drag_handle proc~drag_handle->proc~drag proc~grab_handle grab_handle proc~grab_handle->proc~grab proc~dispatch_event dispatch_event proc~dispatch_event->proc~drag_handle proc~dispatch_event->proc~grab_handle proc~dispatch_events dispatch_events proc~dispatch_events->proc~dispatch_event proc~frame WindowProxy%frame proc~frame->proc~dispatch_events proc~resize WindowProxy%resize proc~resize->proc~fr