 Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure subroutine ray ( cam , origin , dir ) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) if ( cam % perspective ) then origin = cam % eye dir = cam % forward + cam % x * cam % tan_y * cam % aspect * cam % right + cam % y * cam % tan_y * cam % up dir = dir / norm2 ( dir ) else origin = cam % eye + cam % right * ( cam % ortho ( 1 ) + 0.5_wp * ( cam % x + 1.0_wp ) * ( cam % ortho ( 2 ) - cam % ortho ( 1 ))) & + cam % up * ( cam % ortho ( 3 ) + 0.5_wp * ( cam % y + 1.0_wp ) * ( cam % ortho ( 4 ) - cam % ortho ( 3 ))) dir = cam % forward end if end subroutine ray","tags":"","url":"proc/ray.html"},{"title":"button – vkframes","text":"private  function button(self, label) A button: true once after it was clicked. Type Bound Gui Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Gui ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: label Return Value logical Calls proc~~button~~CallsGraph proc~button Gui%button interface~vkf_gui_button vkf_gui_button proc~button->interface~vkf_gui_button Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code logical funct