c = sources n = min ( self % n_times , self % num_points ( src )) if ( n == 0 ) return status = self % time_index ( t , i ) if ( status == TIME_NOT_FOUND ) return if ( i < 1 ) then v = self % point ( 1 , src ) else if ( i >= n ) then v = self % point ( n , src ) else v = self % point_between ( i , i + 1 , t , src ) end if if ( present ( ok )) ok = . true . end function point_at","tags":"","url":"proc/point_at.html"},{"title":"point_between – vkframes","text":"private pure function point_between(self, k, k2, t, sources) result(v) The point at time t between points k and k2 (components from sources ): linear in time, within the two (time_fraction). Point k if\nk2 isn't a point (beyond the ends, or more times than data). Type Bound Trajectory Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: k a point (1 to num_points(sources)) integer, intent(in) :: k2 the other point (e.g. k + 1) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t the time type( DataSource ), intent(in) :: sources (3) where the components come from Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) Calls proc~~point_between~~CallsGraph proc~point_between Trajectory%point_between proc~num_points Trajectory%num_points proc~point_between->proc~num_points proc~point Trajectory%point proc~point_between->proc~point proc~time_fraction Trajectory%time_fraction proc~point_between->proc~time_fraction Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~point_between~~CalledB