ation interface~vkf_rocky_add_image vkf_rocky_add_image proc~apply_layer->interface~vkf_rocky_add_image proc~find_data_file find_data_file proc~apply_layer->proc~find_data_file proc~apply_settings->proc~name interface~vkf_rocky_map_settings vkf_rocky_map_settings proc~apply_settings->interface~vkf_rocky_map_settings proc~color~3 ReferenceFrame%color proc~apply_settings->proc~color~3 proc~find_in_dirs find_in_dirs proc~find_data_file->proc~find_in_dirs Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine terrain_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer handle (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the group node to build under if (. not . c_associated ( viewer )) return if (. not . rocky_available ()) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: TerrainBody ' // self % name () // ': vkframes was built without Rocky ' // & '(pixi run -e rocky rocky-build, then run in the rocky environment)' return end if self % map_group = group call make_map ( self , viewer ) end subroutine terrain_build_contents","tags":"","url":"proc/terrain_build_contents.html"},{"title":"terrain_pick – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine terrain_pick(self, cam, to_root, hits, n) Picked on a sphere of the body's radius (not the terrain's heights), with\nthe latitude and longitude of the point hit; else the frame's origin. Type Bound TerrainBody Arguments 