roc~sphere_near proc~project project proc~point_pick->proc~project proc~segment_pick->proc~project proc~sphere_near->proc~project Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~curve_pick~~CalledByGraph proc~curve_pick curve_pick proc~drawable_pick DrawableTrajectory%drawable_pick proc~drawable_pick->proc~curve_pick Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine curve_pick ( a , frame , cam , m , hits , n ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ), target :: a class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: frame !! the frame drawing it (for the hit) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits are added to hits(1:n) integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: pos real ( wp ) :: extra , lo ( 3 ), hi ( 3 ), c ( 3 ), p0 ( 3 ), p1 ( 3 ), px , s , depth , best_px , best_depth , best_s , t0 , t1 , frac integer :: j , first , count , i1 , i2 , i , best_i , best_j , nd , d1 , d2 logical :: xyz type ( PickHit ) :: h if (. not . associated ( a % traj ) . or . . not . a % chain % is_built ()) return nd = a % n_drawn if ( nd < 1 ) return d1 = a % first_drawn_ ! (the points drawn: d1 .. d2) d2 = d1 + nd - 1 extra = 0.5_wp * a % width_ * cam % pixel_ratio xyz = is_position_xyz ( a % sources_ ) if ( xyz ) call a % traj % positions ( pos ) best_px = huge ( 1.0_wp ) best_depth = huge ( 1.0_wp ) best_i = 0 best_j = 0 ! (the hit is between points best_i and best_j) best_s = 0.0_wp if ( nd == 1 ) then ! (a single point) if ( point_pick ( cam , root_point ( d1 ), px , depth , extra )) then best_px = px best_depth = depth best_i = d1 end if end if do j = 1 , a % chain % num_chunks () ! the segments drawn, chunk by chunk call a % chain % chunk_bounds ( j , first , count , lo , hi ) i1 = max ( first , d1 ) i2 = min ( first + count - 1 , d2 ) if ( count < 2 . or . i2 <= i1 ) cycle c = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), 0.5_wp * ( lo + hi )) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) if (. not . sphere_near ( cam , c , 0.5_wp * norm2 ( hi - lo ), extra )) cycle ! (a chunk far off: skipped) p0 = root_point ( i1 ) do i = i1 , i2 - 1 p1 = root_point ( i + 1 ) if ( segment_pick ( cam , p0 , p1 , px , s , depth , extra )) then if ( better ( px , depth , best_px , best_depth )) then best_px = px best_depth = depth best_i = i best_j = i + 1 best_s = s end if end if p0 = p1 end do end do ! trace mode: the tail from the latest point passed to the point at the time drawn if ( a % trace . and . a % tail_shown ) then t0 = a % traj % time ( a % tail_from ) t1 = a % traj % time ( a % tail_to ) frac = 0.0_wp if ( t1 /= t0 ) frac = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , ( a % tail_time - t0 ) / ( t1 - t0 ))) p0 = root_point ( a % tail_from ) p1 = p0 + frac * ( root_point ( a % tail_to ) - p0 ) if ( segment_pick ( cam , p0 , p1 , px , s , depth , extra )) then if ( better ( px , depth , best_px , best_depth )) then best_px = px best_depth = depth best_i = a % tail_from best_j = a % tail_to best_s = s * frac end if end if end if if ( best_i == 0 ) return h % kind = PICK_CURVE h % frame => frame h % artist => a h % trajectory => a % traj h % index = best_i if ( best_j > 0 ) h % index = min ( best_i , best_j ) ! (the point the hit is after, in point order) h % local = local_point ( best_i ) h % time = a % traj % time ( best_i ) if ( best_j > 0 ) then h % local = h % local + best_s * ( local_point ( best_j ) - h % local ) h % time = h % time + best_s * ( a % traj % time ( best_j ) - h % time ) end if h % position = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), h % local ) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) h % distance = best_depth h % pixels = best_px call add_pick_hit ( hits , n , h ) contains !> Point i in the frame's coordinates (straight from the positions if they are the sources). function local_point ( i ) result ( v ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) if ( xyz ) then v = pos (:, i ) else v = a % traj % point ( i , a % sources_ ) end if end function local_point !> Point i in the root frame. function root_point ( i ) result ( v ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) v = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), local_point ( i )) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) end function root_point end subroutine curve_pick","tags":"","url":"proc/curve_pick.html"},{"title":"curve_set_color – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine curve_set_color(self, color) The line's color: [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1\n(with the trajectory's point colors drawn: for points without one). Type Bound CurveArtist Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: color (:) Calls proc~~curve_set_color~~CallsGraph proc~curve_set_color CurveArtist%curve_set_color is_colored is_colored proc~curve_set_color->is_colored proc~curve_style CurveArtist%curve_style proc~curve_set_color->proc~curve_style proc~set_rgba set_rgba proc~curve_set_color->proc~set_rgba proc~curve_style->is_colored proc~apply_highlight apply_highlight proc~curve_style->proc~apply_highlight set_pattern set_pattern proc~curve_style->set_pattern set_style set_style proc~curve_style->set_style style_node style_node proc~curve_style->style_node proc~set_highlight LineChain%set_highlight proc~apply_highlight->proc~set_highlight proc~apply_style~2 apply_style proc~set_highlight->proc~apply_style~2 interface~vkf_line_set_dash_mode vkf_line_set_dash_mode proc~apply_style~2->interface~vkf_line_set_dash_mode interface~vkf_line_set_highlight vkf_line_set_highlight proc~apply_style~2->interface~vkf_line_set_highlight interface~vkf_line_set_trail vkf_line_set_trail proc~apply_style~2->interface~vkf_line_set_trail proc~check_status check_status proc~apply_style~2->proc~check_status proc~line_set_pattern line_set_pattern proc~apply_style~2->proc~line_set_pattern proc~line_set_style line_set_style proc~apply_style~2->proc~line_set_style proc~marker_set_style marker_set_style proc~apply_style~2->proc~marker_set_style interface~vkf_line_style vkf_line_style proc~line_set_pattern->interface~vkf_line_style interface~vkf_line_style_changed vkf_line_style_changed proc~line_set_pattern->interface~vkf_line_style_changed proc~line_set_style->interface~vkf_line_style proc~line_set_style->interface~vkf_line_style_changed proc~marker_set_style->interface~vkf_line_style proc~marker_set_style->interface~vkf_line_style_changed Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~curve_set_color~~CalledByGraph proc~curve_set_color CurveArtist%curve_set_color proc~new_curve_artist new_curve_artist proc~new_curve_artist->proc~curve_set_color interface~curveartist CurveArtist interface~curveartist->proc~new_curve_artist Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine curve_set_color ( self , color ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) call set_rgba ( self % color_ , color ) call curve_style ( self ) if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) self % seen_generation = - 1 ! (points without colors redrawn) end subroutine curve_set_color","tags":"","url":"proc/curve_set_color.html"},{"title":"curve_set_dash_mode – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine curve_set_dash_mode(self, mode, length) How the dash pattern (and a trail's) is laid out: DASH_SCENE (the\ndefault) anchored to the line: a dash stays put on it as the view\nchanges, its size in scene units (one per line and view, from 0.7 to\n1.4 times the pattern's on screen, changing by doubling as it zooms);\nDASH_SCREEN screen-locked, as OpenGL's line stipple (OpenFrames'):\nevery dash the pattern's length in pixels, at any zoom and depth,\nsliding along the line as the view changes; DASH_FIXED a fixed\nlength of the line, as paint on it: never changing, so zooming in the\ndashes grow on screen, and out they shrink (under a pixel, blending\ninto a fainter solid line); length (scene units, for the whole\npattern: the other patterns, a trail's future's and the arrows', in\nproportion), else the pattern's length on screen where the line is\nfirst drawn. DASH_SCREEN and DASH_FIXED cost projecting the points\ndrawn on the CPU, per view and frame. Type Bound CurveArtist Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: mode DASH_SCENE, DASH_SCREEN or DASH_FIXED real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: length (DASH_FIXED) the pattern's length, scene units Calls proc~~curve_set_dash_mode~~CallsGraph proc~curve_set_dash_mode CurveArtist%curve_set_dash_mode set_dash_mode set_dash_mode proc~curve_set_dash_mode->set_dash_mode style_node style_node proc~curve_set_dash_mode->style_node Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine curve_set_dash_mode ( self , mode , length ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: mode !! DASH_SCENE, DASH_SCREEN or DASH_FIXED real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: length !! (DASH_FIXED) the pattern's length, scene units real ( wp ) :: l l = 0.0_wp if ( present ( length )) l = max ( 0.0_wp , length ) call self % chain % set_dash_mode ( mode , l ) if ( c_associated ( self % tail )) call self % chain % style_node ( self % tail ) end subroutine curve_set_dash_mode","tags":"","url":"proc/curve_set_dash_mode.html"},{"title":"curve_set_highlight – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine curve_set_highlight(self, mode, color, arrow_spacing, arrow_speed, band_width, pulse_period) Highlight the curve (see the module documentation): mode a sum of\nHIGHLIGHT_PULSE and HIGHLIGHT_ARROWS (HIGHLIGHT_NONE: not highlighted),\nin color ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]; default white). The other\nsettings are kept when not given. Type Bound CurveArtist Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: mode HIGHLIGHT_* (added) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: color (:) [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: arrow_spacing between arrows (window units; default 40) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: arrow_speed (window units per second; default 50) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: band_width of the arrows' band (window units; default 12) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: pulse_period (s; default 1.5) Calls proc~~curve_set_highlight~~CallsGraph proc~curve_set_highlight CurveArtist%curve_set_highlight proc~curve_style CurveArtist%curve_style proc~curve_set_highlight->proc~curve_style proc~update_highlight update_highlight proc~curve_set_highlight->proc~update_highlight is_colored is_colored proc~curve_style->is_colored proc~apply_highlight apply_highlight proc~curve_style->proc~apply_highlight set_pattern set_pattern proc~curve_style->set_pattern set_style set_style proc~curve_style->set_style style_node style_node proc~curve_style->style_node proc~set_rgba set_rgba proc~update_highlight->proc~set_rgba proc~set_highlight LineChain%set_highlight proc~apply_highlight->proc~set_highlight proc~apply_style~2 apply_style proc~set_highlight->proc~apply_style~2 interface~vkf_line_set_dash_mode vkf_line_set_dash_mode proc~apply_style~2->interface~vkf_line_set_dash_mode interface~vkf_line_set_highlight vkf_line_set_highlight proc~apply_style~2->interface~vkf_line_set_highlight interface~vkf_line_set_trail vkf_line_set_trail proc~apply_style~2->interfa