it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine curve_update ( self , t ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the current time logical :: changed if (. not . write_changed ( self , changed )) return if ( self % trail_ % on ) then ! a trail: the window about time t if (. not . changed . and . t == self % tail_time ) return call draw_trail ( self , t ) self % tail_time = t return end if call draw_written ( self , t , changed ) end subroutine curve_update","tags":"","url":"proc/curve_update.html"},{"title":"draw_trail – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine draw_trail(self, t) A trail at time t: the points within its window (and the one beyond\neach end: the GPU cuts the segments at the cutoffs) drawn, and the\ndistances along the curve at t and at the window's edges given to the\nshader (see vkf_line_set_trail), as distances from t's in the\ndirection of time; times beyond the trajectory's are extrapolated from\nits end segments. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( CurveArtist ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t Calls proc~~draw_trail~~CallsGraph proc~draw_trail draw_trail distance distance proc~draw_trail->distance draw_range draw_range proc~draw_trail->draw_range interface~vkf_line_set_range vkf_line_set_range proc~draw_trail->interface~vkf_line_set_range proc~check_status check_status proc~draw_trail->proc~check_status proc~decreasing_times decreasing_times proc~draw_trail->proc~decreasing_times set_trail set_trail proc~draw_trail->set_trail Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~draw_trail~~CalledByGraph proc~draw_trail draw_trail proc~curve_update CurveArtist%curve_update proc~curve_update->proc~draw_trail Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine draw_trail ( self , t ) type ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t real ( wp ), parameter :: unlimited = 0.5_wp * huge ( 1.0_wp ) real ( c_float ), parameter :: far = 1.0e30_c_float real ( c_float ) :: values ( 20 ), hi real ( wp ) :: sgn , lo_key , hi_key , s_now , fade integer :: n , i1 , i2 , k call check_status ( vkf_line_set_range ( self % tail , 1_c_int , 0_c_int ), 'trajectory artists' ) self % tail_shown = . false . n = self % n_written self % n_drawn = 0 self % first_drawn_ = 1 values = 0.0_c_float if (. not . associated ( self % traj ) . or . n < 2 ) then call self % chain % draw_range ( 1 , 0 ) call self % chain % set_trail ( values ) return end if sgn = merge ( - 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , decreasing_times ( self % traj , n )) ! (keys sgn * time increase with the index) lo_key = sgn * t - merge ( huge ( 1.0_wp ), self % trail_ % past , self % trail_ % past >= unlimited ) hi_key = sgn * t + merge ( huge ( 1.0_wp ), self % trail_ % future , self % trail_ % future >= unlimited ) if ( sgn < 0.0_wp ) then ! (the past is at the larger keys) lo_key = sgn * t - merge ( huge ( 1.0_wp ), self % trail_ % future , self % trail_ % future >= unlimited ) hi_key = sgn * t + merge ( huge ( 1.0_wp ), self % trail_ % past , self % trail_ % past >= unlimited ) end if if ( hi_key < key ( 1 ) . or . lo_key > key ( n )) then ! (the window misses the trajectory) call self % chain % draw_range ( 1 , 0 ) call self % chain % set_trail ( values ) return end if i1 = max ( 1 , keys_up_to ( lo_key , . true .)) ! the last point before the window, or the first i2 = min ( n , keys_up_to ( hi_key , . false .) + 1 ) ! the first after it, or the last self % first_drawn_ = i1 self % n_drawn = i2 - i1 + 1 call self % chain % draw_range ( i1 , i2 ) s_now = s_at ( t ) hi = real ( s_now , c_float ) fade = 1.0_wp - self % trail_ % fade values ( 1 : 4 ) = [ hi , real ( s_now - real ( hi , wp ), c_float ), real ( sgn , c_float ), & real ( merge ( 1 , 0 , self % trail_ % replace ( 1 )) + merge ( 2 , 0 , self % trail_ % replace ( 2 )), c_float )] if ( self % trail_ % past >= unlimited ) then values ( 5 : 6 ) = - far else values ( 5 ) = real ( sgn * ( s_at ( t - self % trail_ % past ) - s_now ), c_float ) values ( 6 ) = real ( sgn * ( s_at ( t - fade * self % trail_ % past ) - s_now ), c_float ) end if if ( self % trail_ % future >= unlimited ) then values ( 7 : 8 ) = far else values ( 7 ) = real ( sgn * ( s_at ( t + fade * self % trail_ % future ) - s_now ), c_float ) values ( 8 ) = real ( sgn * ( s_at ( t + self % trail_ % future ) - s_now ), c_float ) end if do k = 1 , 2 ! each part's color (or the line's: then its alpha only) values ( 9 + 4 * ( k - 1 ): 12 + 4 * ( k - 1 )) = real ( self % trail_ % color (:, k ), c_float ) values ( 12 + 4 * ( k - 1 )) = real ( self % trail_ % opacity ( k ) * merge ( self % trail_ % color ( 4 , k ), 1.0_wp , & self % trail_ % replace ( k )), c_float ) end do values ( 17 : 20 ) = real ([ self % trail_ % pattern ( 1 ), self % trail_ % factor ( 1 ), self % trail_ % pattern ( 2 ), & self % trail_ % factor ( 2 )], c_float ) call self % chain % set_trail ( values ) contains !> Point i's key: its time, increasing with the index. real ( wp ) function key ( i ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i key = sgn * self % traj % time ( i ) end function key !> The number of points with keys below x, or at most x if `inclusive` !> (bisection: the keys increase). integer function keys_up_to ( x , inclusive ) result ( m ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x !! the key logical , intent ( in ) :: inclusive !! keys equal to x counted integer :: low , high , mid low = 0 high = n + 1 do while ( high - low > 1 ) mid = ( low + high ) / 2 if ( key ( mid ) < x . or . ( inclusive . and . key ( mid ) == x )) then low = mid else high = mid end if end do m = low end function keys_up_to !> The distance along the curve at time tt: interpolated between the !> points about it (extrapolated beyond the ends). real ( wp ) function s_at ( tt ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tt integer :: j real ( wp ) :: t0 , t1 j = max ( 1 , min ( n - 1 , keys_up_to ( sgn * tt , . true .))) t0 = self % traj % time ( j ) t1 = self % traj % time ( j + 1 ) s_at = self % chain % distance ( j ) if ( t1 /= t0 ) s_at = s_at + ( tt - t0 ) / ( t1 - t0 ) * ( self % chain % distance ( j + 1 ) - s_at ) end function s_at end subroutine draw_trail","tags":"","url":"proc/draw_trail.html"},{"title":"draw_written – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine draw_written(self, t, changed) Draw the points written: all of them (the tail hidden) or, in trace\nmode, those passed by time t (times up to it) and the tail from the\nlatest of them to the point at t (unchanged if nothing changed and t\nis the time it was drawn for). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ChainArtist ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t the current time logical, intent(in) :: changed points were written (write_changed) Calls proc~~draw_written~~CallsGraph proc~draw_written draw_written draw_tail draw_tail proc~draw_written->draw_tail interface~vkf_line_set_range vkf_line_set_range proc~draw_written->interface~vkf_line_set_range proc~chain_points_per_point chain_points_per_point proc~draw_written->proc~chain_points_per_point proc~check_status check_status proc~draw_written->proc~check_status proc~draw LineChain%draw proc~draw_written->proc~draw proc~draw_range LineChain%draw_range proc~draw_written->proc~draw_range proc~tail_ends tail_ends proc~draw_written->proc~tail_ends proc~trace_range trace_range proc~draw_written->proc~trace_range chain_kind chain_kind proc~chain_points_per_point->chain_kind proc~draw->proc~draw_range proc~draw_range->interface~vkf_line_set_range proc~draw_range->proc~check_status proc~decreasing_times decreasing_times proc~tail_ends->proc~decreasing_times proc~trace_range->proc~decreasing_times Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~draw_written~~CalledByGraph proc~draw_written draw_written proc~chain_update ChainArtist%chain_update proc~chain_update->proc~draw_written proc~curve_update CurveArtist%curve_update proc~curve_update->proc~draw_written Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine draw_written ( self , t , changed ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the current time logical , intent ( in ) :: changed !! points were written (write_changed) integer :: m , i1 , i2 , k , k2 m = chain_points_per_point ( self ) if (. not . self % trace ) then self % n_drawn = self % n_written self % first_drawn_ = 1 call self % chain % draw ( m * self % n_drawn ) if ( c_associated ( self % tail )) call check_status ( vkf_line_set_range ( self % tail , 1_c_int , 0_c_int ), 'trajectory artists' ) self % tail_shown = . false . self % tail_time = huge ( 1.0_wp ) return end if if (. not . changed . and . t == self % tail_time ) return i1 = 1 i2 = 0 if ( associated ( self % traj )) call trace_range ( self % traj , t , self % n_written , i1 , i2 ) self % first_drawn_ = i1 self % n_drawn = max ( 0 , i2 - i1 + 1 ) call self % chain % draw_range ( m * ( i1 - 1 ) + 1 , m * i2 ) call tail_ends ( self % traj , self % n_written , i1 , i2 , k , k2 ) call self % draw_tail ( t , k , k2 ) self % tail_time = t end subroutine draw_written","tags":"","url":"proc/draw_written.html"},{"title":"drawable_build_contents – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine drawable_build_contents(self, viewer, group) Build the artists' nodes under group ( viewer , may be null: those made\nlater are compiled if not null). Type Bound DrawableTrajectory Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DrawableTrajectory ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: group Calls proc~~drawable_build_contents~~CallsGraph proc~drawable_build_contents DrawableTrajectory%drawable_build_contents proc~build_artist bui