d include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine marker_build ( self , viewer , group ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer , group self % group = group self % shown = c_associated ( viewer ) call build_marker_nodes ( self , compile = . false .) end subroutine marker_build","tags":"","url":"proc/marker_build.html"},{"title":"marker_pick – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine marker_pick(a, frame, cam, m, hits, n) A marker artist's best hit: its start, end and intermediate markers drawn. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( MarkerArtist ), intent(in), target :: a class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), target :: frame the frame drawing it (for the hit) type( PickCamera ), intent(in) :: cam real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: m (4,4) the frame's transform to the root frame type( PickHit ), intent(inout), allocatable :: hits (:) hits are added to hits(1:n) integer, intent(inout) :: n number of hits Calls proc~~marker_pick~~CallsGraph proc~marker_pick marker_pick proc~add_pick_hit add_pick_hit proc~marker_pick->proc~add_pick_hit proc~better better proc~marker_pick->proc~better proc~drawn_marker MarkerArtist%drawn_marker proc~marker_pick->proc~drawn_marker proc~point_pick point_pick proc~marker_pick->proc~point_pick proc~source_points source_points proc~marker_pick->proc~source_points proc~point~2 LineChain%point proc~drawn_marker->proc~point~2 proc~project project proc~point_pick->proc~project proc~num_points Trajectory%num_points proc~source_points->proc~num_points proc~verify_data Trajectory%verify_data proc~source_points->proc~verify_data proc~line_buffer line_buffer proc~point~2->proc~line_buffer interface~vkf_line_points vkf_line_points proc~line_buffer->interface~vkf_line_points Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~marker_pick~~CalledByGraph proc~marker_pick marker_pick proc~drawable_pick DrawableTrajectory%drawable_pick proc~drawable_pick->proc~marker_pick Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine marker_pick ( a , frame , cam , m , hits , n ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ), target :: a class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: frame !! the frame drawing it (for the hit) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits are added to hits(1:n) integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits real ( wp ) :: extra , v ( 3 ), px , depth , best_px , best_depth , best_v ( 3 ) integer :: k , which , best_which , best_k , npts type ( PickHit ) :: h extra = 0.5_wp * a % size_ * cam % pixel_ratio best_px = huge ( 1.0_wp ) best_depth = huge ( 1.0_wp ) best_which = 0 best_k = 0 best_v = 0.0_wp do which = 1 , 3 ! start, end, the intermediate ones select case ( which ) case ( 1 ) if ( a % drawn_marker ( MARKER_START , v )) call consider ( MARKER_START , 0 ) case ( 2 ) if ( a % drawn_marker ( MARKER_END , v )) call consider ( MARKER_END , 0 ) case ( 3 ) do k = a % inter_first , a % inter_first + a % n_inter_drawn - 1 if ( a % drawn_marker ( MARKER_INTERMEDIATE , v , k )) call consider ( MARKER_INTERMEDIATE , k ) end do end select end do if ( best_which == 0 ) return h % kind = PICK_MARKER h % frame => frame h % artist => a h % marker = best_which npts = 0 if ( associated ( a % traj )) then h % trajectory => a % traj npts = source_points ( a % traj , a % sources_ ) end if select case ( best_which ) case ( MARKER_START ) h % index = min ( 1 , npts ) if ( npts > 0 ) h % time = a % traj % time ( 1 ) case ( MARKER_END ) h % index = npts if ( npts > 0 ) h % time = a % traj % time ( npts ) case default h % index = best_k h % time = a % inter_t ( best_k ) end select h % local = best_v h % position = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), best_v ) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) h % distance = best_depth h % pixels = best_px call add_pick_hit ( hits , n , h ) contains !> Take the marker at `v` (`kind`, intermediate number k) as the best hit if picked and better. subroutine consider ( kind , k ) integer , intent ( in ) :: kind , k if (. not . point_pick ( cam , matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), v ) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ), px , depth , extra )) return if (. not . better ( px , depth , best_px , best_depth )) return best_px = px best_depth = depth best_which = kind best_k = k best_v = v end subroutine consider end subroutine marker_pick","tags":"","url":"proc/marker_pick.html"},{"title":"marker_release – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine marker_release(self) Forget the render nodes (see artist_release). Type Bound MarkerArtist Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( MarkerArtist ), intent(inout) :: self Calls proc~~marker_release~~CallsGraph proc~marker_release MarkerArtist%marker_release proc~artist_release TrajectoryArtist%artist_release