 Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine marker_update ( self , t ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t logical :: changed , redraw , zero , passed_start , passed_end integer :: n if (. not . c_associated ( self % group )) return zero = all ( self % sources_ % src == SOURCE_ZERO ) . or . . not . associated ( self % traj ) ! (a marker at the origin) if ( zero ) then n = 1 ! a marker at the origin else n = source_points ( self % traj , self % sources_ ) end if ! the trajectory's colors drawn or not (its first colors, or the setting, ! changed): the marker nodes made again, with or without colors if ( marker_uses_colors ( self ) . neqv . self % inter % is_colored ()) call rebuild_markers ( self ) changed = data_changed ( self , redraw ) if (. not . self % drawn ) then changed = . true . redraw = . true . self % drawn = . true . end if if ( changed ) then if ( self % inter % is_colored ()) then ! (colors added or changed: all written again) if ( self % traj % num_colors () /= self % n_colors_seen ) redraw = . true . self % n_colors_seen = self % traj % num_colors () end if if ( redraw . or . n < self % n_seen ) call reset_markers ( self ) call update_bounds ( self , n , zero ) if ( n >= 1 ) call write_marker ( self % start_node , marker_point ( self , 1 , zero ), & ! (none: nothing drawn) end_rgba ( self , 1 , self % start_color )) if ( n > 1 ) call write_marker ( self % end_node , marker_point ( self , n , zero ), end_rgba ( self , n , self % end_color )) if ( iand ( self % markers_ , MARKER_INTERMEDIATE ) /= 0 . and . . not . zero . and . n > 2 ) call add_intermediates ( self , n ) end if ! what is drawn: everything, or in trace mode the markers whose times ! have passed (the start and end markers at their points' times) passed_start = . true . passed_end = . true . if ( self % trace . and . . not . zero . and . n >= 1 ) then passed_start = self % traj % time ( 1 ) <= t passed_end = self % traj % time ( n ) <= t end if self % start_shown = iand ( self % markers_ , MARKER_START ) /= 0 . and . n >= 1 . and . passed_start call self % start_node % draw ( merge ( 1 , 0 , self % start_shown )) self % end_shown = iand ( self % markers_ , MARKER_END ) /= 0 . and . n > 1 . and . passed_end call self % end_node % draw ( merge ( 1 , 0 , self % end_shown )) self % inter_first = 1 self % n_inter_drawn = self % n_inter_written if ( self % trace . and . self % n_inter_written > 0 ) call markers_passed ( self , t , self % inter_first , self % n_inter_drawn ) call self % inter % draw_range ( self % inter_first , self % inter_first + self % n_inter_drawn - 1 ) end subroutine marker_update","tags":"","url":"proc/marker_update.html"},{"title":"markers_passed – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine markers_passed(self, t, first, count) The intermediate markers (in trajectory order) whose times are at most\nt: count from first (the first ones for increasing times, the last\nfor decreasing), by bisection. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( MarkerArtist ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t integer, intent(out) :: first integer, intent(out) :: count Calls proc~~markers_passed~~CallsGraph proc~markers_passed markers_passed num_times num_times proc~markers_passed->num_times proc~decreasing_times decreasing_times proc~markers_passed->proc~decreasing_times Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~markers_passed~~CalledByGraph proc~markers_passed markers_passed proc~marker_update MarkerArtist%marker_update proc~marker_update->proc~markers_passed Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine markers_passed ( self , t , first , count ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t integer , intent ( out ) :: first , count integer :: low , high , mid , m m = self % n_inter_written low = 0 high = m + 1 if (. not . decreasing_times ( self % traj , self % traj % num_times ())) then ! markers 1 .. low passed do while ( high - low > 1 ) mid = ( low + high ) / 2 if ( self % inter_t ( mid ) <= t ) then low = mid else high = mid end if end do first = 1 count = low else ! markers high .. m passed do while ( high - low > 1 ) mid = ( low + high ) / 2 if ( self % inter_t ( mid ) <= t ) then high = mid else low = mid end if end do first = high count = m - high + 1 end if end subroutine markers_passed","tags":"","url":"proc/markers_passed.html"},{"title":"push_intermediate – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine push_intermediate(self, v, t) Append an intermediate marker at v , time t (the arrays grown as needed). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( MarkerArtist ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: v (3) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: 