eric interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code real ( wp ) function update ( self , wall ) result ( t ) class ( SimulationClock ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: wall !! wall time (s; default: wall_time()) if ( associated ( self % sync )) then self % time_ = self % sync % time () else if (. not . self % started ) call self % set_time ( self % time_ , wall ) if (. not . self % paused_ ) & self % time_ = max ( self % t_min , min ( self % t_max , self % offset + ( now ( wall ) - self % wall_ref ) * self % scale_ )) end if t = self % time_ end function update","tags":"","url":"proc/update~2.html"},{"title":"wall_time – vkframes","text":"public  function wall_time() Wall-clock time in seconds (system_clock), for the clock's default. Arguments None Return Value real(kind=wp) Called by proc~~wall_time~~CalledByGraph proc~wall_time wall_time proc~count_frame count_frame proc~count_frame->proc~wall_time proc~frame WindowProxy%frame proc~frame->proc~wall_time proc~frame->proc~count_frame proc~stop_recording WindowProxy%stop_recording proc~frame->proc~stop_recording proc~window_wall window_wall proc~frame->proc~window_wall proc~update~2 SimulationClock%update proc~frame->proc~update~2 proc~place_camera place_camera proc~frame->proc~place_camera proc~now now proc~now->proc~wall_time proc~start_recording WindowProxy%start_recording proc~start_recording->proc~wall_time proc~stop_recording->proc~wall_time proc~stop_recording->proc~window_wall proc~set_time~2 SimulationClock%set_time proc~stop_recording->proc~set_time~2 proc~window_wall->proc~wall_time proc~close WindowProxy%close proc~close->proc~stop_recording proc~fly fly proc~fly->proc~window_wall proc~pause_time WindowProxy%pause_time proc~pause_time->proc~window_wall proc~resize WindowProxy%resize proc~resize->proc~frame proc~run WindowProxy%run proc~run->proc~frame proc~set_time_scale~2 WindowProxy%set_time_scale proc~set_time_scale~2->pr