 Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. public  function vkf_viewer_create(width, height, title, title_len, native_window, pixel_ratio, vsync) bind(C, name=\"vkf_viewer_create\") Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=c_int), value :: width window size (window units: logical pixels) integer(kind=c_int), value :: height window size (window units: logical pixels) character(kind=c_char, len=1), intent(in), dimension(*) :: title window title integer(kind=c_int), value :: title_len the length of title integer(kind=c_long_long), value :: native_window 0 for a window of its own, or the native handle of\nan existing window to render into (e.g. a Qt\nQWindow's winId(): an NSView* on macOS, an HWND on\nWindows, an xcb window on Linux) real(kind=c_double), value :: pixel_ratio framebuffer pixels per window unit of an existing window\n(Qt's devicePixelRatio); ignored for a window of its own integer(kind=c_int), value :: vsync 1 to present at the display's refresh (FIFO), 0 as soon as a frame is\nready (IMMEDIATE where the driver has it, else FIFO), e.g. for benchmarks Return Value type(c_ptr) Description A viewer with one window, an empty scene and a trackball camera; null on failure.\nWith an existing window ( native_window not 0) the host owns that window's events and\nforwards them (vkf_viewer_mouse, ..., vkf_viewer_resize).","tags":"","url":"interface/vkf_viewer_create.html"},{"title":"vkf_viewer_delete – vkframes","text":"interface Called by interface~~vkf_viewer_delete~~CalledByGraph interface~vkf_viewer_delete vkf_viewer_delete proc~close WindowProxy%close proc~close->interface~vkf_viewer_delete Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. public  subroutine vkf_viewer_delete(viewer) bind(C, name=\"vkf_viewer_delete\") Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: viewer viewer handle (vkf_viewer_create) Description Delete a viewer (its window, GUI and default light; waits for the device to be idle first).","tags":"","url":"interface/vkf_viewer_delete.html"},{"title":"vkf_viewer_device_info – vkframes","text":"interface Called by interface~~vkf_viewer_device_info~~CalledByGraph interface~vkf_viewer_device_info vkf_viewer_device_info proc~device_info WindowProxy%device_info proc~device_info->interface~vkf_viewer_device_info Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. public  function vkf_viewer_device_info(viewer, which, buf, buflen) bind(C, name=\"vkf_viewer_device_info\") Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: viewer viewer handle (vkf_viewer_create) integer(kind=c_int), value :: which 1 to 5 (see above) character(kind=c_char, len=1), intent(out) :: buf (*) integer(kind=c_int), value :: buflen the length of buf Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Description The viewer's Vulkan device into buf (blank-padded): which = 1 its name, 2 its type, 3 the Vulkan\nversion it supports, 4 its driver's name, 5 its driver's information. Returns the length, or -1.","tags":"","url":"interface/vkf_viewer_device_info.html"},{"title":"vkf_viewer_events – vkframes","text":"interface Called by interface~~vkf_viewer_events~~CalledByGraph interface~vkf_viewer_events vkf_viewer_events proc~dispatch_events dispatch_events proc~dispatch_events->interface~vkf_viewer_events proc~frame WindowProxy%frame proc~frame->proc~dispatch_events proc~resize WindowProxy%resize proc~resize->proc~frame proc~run WindowProxy%run proc~run->proc~frame Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. public  function vkf_viewer_events(viewer, events, capacity) bind(C, name=\"vkf_viewer_events\") Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: viewer viewer handle (vkf_viewer_create) integer(kind=c_int), intent(out) :: events (12,*) the events, 12 integers each integer(kind=c_int), value :: capacity the most events events holds Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Description The keyboard and mouse events since the last call, oldest first, up to capacity of them.\nReturns how many were copied (the rest are kept for the next call), or -1 on failure.\nEach event (a column of events ): kind (1 key press, 2 key release, 3 pointer move, 4 button press,\n5 button release), key (modified: 'V' with shift), key base, modifiers, button, buttons held (mask),\nx, y (framebuffer pixels from the top left), and the render area (offset x, y, width, height).\nPointer events have key 1 while the mouse is grabbed (vkf_viewer_set_grab). Events taken by a\nGUI panel are not included.","tags":"","url":"interface/vkf_viewer_events.html"},{"title":"vkf_viewer_frame – vkframes","text":"interface public  function vkf_viewer_frame(viewer) bind(C, name=\"vkf_viewer_frame\") Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: viewer viewer handle (vkf_viewer_create) Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Description Render one frame (vkf_viewer_frame_begin, then vkf_viewer_frame_draw). Returns 1 while the viewer is\nrunning, 0 once its window has been closed, -1 on failure.","tags":"","url":"interface/vkf_viewer_frame.html"},{"title":"vkf_viewer_frame_begin – vkframes","text":"interface Called by interface~~vkf_viewer_frame_begin~~CalledByGraph interface~vkf_viewer_frame_begin vkf_viewer_frame_begin proc~frame WindowProxy%frame proc~frame->interface~vkf_viewer_frame_begin proc~resize WindowProxy%resize proc~resize->proc~frame proc~run WindowProxy%run proc~run->proc~frame Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. public  function vkf_viewer_frame_begin(viewer) bind(C, name=\"vkf_viewer_frame_begin\") Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: viewer viewer handle (vkf_viewer_create) Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Description The first part of a frame (compiling the scene on the first call): up to the window's events handled\n(the trackball has moved the camera), before the scene is drawn (vkf_viewer_frame_draw): a program can\nstill change the scene for this frame in between. Returns 1 while the viewer is running, 0 once its\nwindow has been closed, -1 on failure.","tags":"","url":"interface/vkf_viewer_frame_begin.html"},{"title":"vkf_viewer_frame_draw – vkframes","text":"interface Called by interface~~vkf_viewer_frame_draw~~CalledByGraph interface~vkf_viewer_frame_draw vkf_viewer_frame_draw proc~frame WindowProxy%frame proc~frame->interface~vkf_viewer_frame_draw proc~resize WindowProxy%resize proc~resize->proc~frame proc~run WindowProxy%run proc~run->proc~frame Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. public  function vkf_viewer_frame_draw(viewer) bind(C, name=\"vkf_viewer_frame_draw\") Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(c_ptr), value :: viewer viewer handle (vkf_viewer_create) Return Value integer(kind=c_int) Description The rest of a frame begun by vkf_viewer_frame_begin: the scene's updates, drawn and presented.\nReturns 1, or -1 on failure.","tags":"","url":"interface/vkf_viewer_frame_draw.html"},{"title":"vkf_viewer_get_look_at – vkframes","text":"interface