x proc~camera_between->proc~quat_to_matrix proc~cross cross proc~camera_orientation->proc~cross proc~quat_from_matrix quat_from_matrix proc~camera_orientation->proc~quat_from_matrix Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~camera_between~~CalledByGraph proc~camera_between camera_between proc~fly fly proc~fly->proc~camera_between proc~place_camera place_camera proc~place_camera->proc~fly proc~frame WindowProxy%frame proc~frame->proc~place_camera proc~resize WindowProxy%resize proc~resize->proc~frame proc~run WindowProxy%run proc~run->proc~frame Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function camera_between ( s , from , to ) result ( cam ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: s !! fraction of the way (0: `from`, 1: `to`) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: from ( 3 , 3 ) !! (columns: eye, center, up) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: to ( 3 , 3 ) !! (columns: eye, center, up) real ( wp ) :: cam ( 3 , 3 ) real ( wp ) :: q0 ( 4 ), q1 ( 4 ), m ( 3 , 3 ), d0 , d1 , d , c ( 3 ) call camera_orientation ( from , q0 , d0 ) call camera_orientation ( to , q1 , d1 ) c = from (:, 2 ) + s * ( to (:, 2 ) - from (:, 2 )) d = d0 * ( d1 / d0 ) ** s m = quat_to_matrix ( quat_normalize ( quat_slerp ( s , q0 , q1 ))) ! columns: right, up, back cam (:, 1 ) = c + d * m (:, 3 ) cam (:, 2 ) = c cam (:, 3 ) = m (:, 2 ) end function camera_between","tags":"","url":"proc/camera_between.html"},{"title":"default_view_distance – vkframes","text":"private pure function default_view_distance(self) The radius framed when the view is reset (<= 0: the viewed frame's bound). Type Bound View Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( View ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) Source Code pure real ( wp ) function default_view_distance ( self ) class ( View ), intent ( in ) :: self default_view_distance = self % default_distance end function default_view_distance","tags":"","url":"proc/default_view_distance.html"},{"title":"field_of_view – vkframes","text":"private pure function field_of_view(self) result(fovy) The vertical field of view (degrees) of the perspective projection. Type Bound View Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( View ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) Called by proc~~field_of_view~~CalledByGraph proc~field_of_view View%field_of_view proc~place_camera place_camera proc~place_camera->proc~field_of_view proc~view_camera view_camera proc~view_camera->proc~field_of_view proc~cursor_ray WindowProxy%cursor_ray proc~cursor_ray->proc~view_camera proc~frame WindowProxy%frame proc~frame->proc~place_camera proc~dispatch_events dispatch_events proc~frame->proc~dispatch_events proc~screen_position WindowProxy%screen_position proc~screen_position->proc~view_camera proc~window_pick WindowProxy%window_pick proc~window_pick->proc~view_camera proc~drag_handle drag_handle proc~drag_handle->proc~cursor_ray proc~grab_handle grab_handle proc~grab_handle->proc~cursor_ray proc~ho