tine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~place_camera~~CalledByGraph proc~place_camera place_camera proc~frame WindowProxy%frame proc~frame->proc~place_camera proc~resize WindowProxy%resize proc~resize->proc~frame proc~run WindowProxy%run proc~run->proc~frame Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine place_camera ( self ) type ( WindowProxy ), intent ( inout ), target :: self type ( View ), pointer :: v , from class ( ReferenceFrame ), pointer :: root real ( wp ) :: eye ( 3 ), center ( 3 ), up ( 3 ), dist , near , far , bounds ( 4 ), cam ( 3 , 3 ), from_cam ( 3 , 3 ), duration logical :: have_target v => self % current_view () if ( associated ( v , self % default_view ) . and . associated ( self % scene )) then root => self % scene % frame () if ( associated ( root ) . and . . not . self % default_view % is_valid ()) call self % default_view % set_view_frame ( root , root ) end if ! the camera shown (to fly from), and the new one: a view changed to (its ! camera set, kept, or reset), a camera set, or a reset from => null () if ( associated ( self % shown )) then if ( vkf_viewer_get_look_at ( self % viewer_ , from_cam (:, 1 ), from_cam (:, 2 ), from_cam (:, 3 )) == 0 ) & from => self % shown end if duration = self % transition_ have_target = . false . if (. not . associated ( v , self % shown )) then if ( associated ( from )) call from % save_state ( from_cam (:, 1 ), from_cam (:, 2 ), from_cam (:, 3 )) if ( self % switch_duration >= 0.0_wp ) duration = self % switch_duration self % switch_duration = - 1.0_wp if ( v % take_camera ( cam )) then have_target = . true . else if ( v % saved_state ( eye , center , up )) then cam = reshape ([ eye , center , up ], [ 3 , 3 ]) have_target = . true . else call v % reset_view () end if self % shown => v else if ( v % take_camera ( cam )) then have_target = . true . duration = 0.0_wp ! (View%set_camera: at once) end if if ( v % take_reset ()) then call v % home ( aspect_ratio ( self ), eye , center , up ) cam = reshape ([ eye , center , up ], [ 3 , 3 ]) have_target = . true . end if if ( have_target ) then if ( associated ( from ) . and . duration > 0.0_wp ) then call start_flight ( self , from , from_cam , v , cam , duration ) else self % flight % active = . false . call put_camera ( self , cam ) end if end if call fly ( self , v ) if ( vkf_viewer_set_view_transform ( self % viewer_ , v % world_to_view ()) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: could not set the view' ! near and far planes from the camera's distance to its center (reverse-Z ! float depth covers the wide ratio) if ( vkf_viewer_get_look_at ( self % viewer_ , eye , center , up ) /= 0 ) return dist = max ( norm2 ( eye - center ), tiny ( 1.0_wp )) near = 1.0e-6_wp * dist far = 1.0e9_wp * dist if ( v % projection_type () == PERSPECTIVE ) then if ( vkf_viewer_perspective ( self % viewer_ , v % field_of_view (), near , far ) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: could not set the projection' else bounds = v % orthographic_bounds () if ( vkf_viewer_