0: away from the user; fractions\nfor a trackpad's small steps: Qt's angleDelta / 120) Calls proc~~scroll~~CallsGraph proc~scroll WindowProxy%scroll interface~vkf_viewer_scroll vkf_viewer_scroll proc~scroll->interface~vkf_viewer_scroll Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine scroll ( self , dy ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dy !! wheel steps (> 0: away from the user; fractions !! for a trackpad's small steps: Qt's angleDelta / 120) if (. not . c_associated ( self % viewer_ )) return if ( vkf_viewer_scroll ( self % viewer_ , real ( dy , c_float )) /= 0 ) write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: scroll event failed' end subroutine scroll","tags":"","url":"proc/scroll.html"},{"title":"select_view – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine select_view(self, i, duration) Show view i (1 to num_views), flying there over duration s (default:\nthe view transition, set_view_transition ; 0: a cut). Type Bound WindowProxy Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: duration Called by proc~~select_view~~CalledByGraph proc~select_view WindowProxy%select_view proc~next_view WindowProxy%next_view proc~next_view->proc~select_view proc~previous_view WindowProxy%previous_view proc~previous_view->proc~select_view proc~default_key default_key proc~default_key->proc~next_view proc~default_key->proc~previous_view proc~dispatch_event dispatch_event proc~dispatch_event->proc~default_key proc~dispatch_events dispatch_events proc~dispatch_events->proc~dispatch_event proc~frame WindowProxy%frame proc~frame->proc~dispatch_events proc~resize WindowProxy%resize proc~resize->proc~frame proc~run WindowProxy%run proc~run->proc~frame Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine select_view ( self , i , duration ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: duration if ( i < 1 . or . i > self % n_views . or . i == self % current ) return self % current = i if ( present ( duration )) self % switch_duration = max ( 0.0_wp , duration ) end subroutine select_view","tags":"","url":"proc/select_view.html"},{"title":"set_background_color – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_background_color(self, rgb) The background color [r, g, b] (0 to 1; default black). Type Bound WindowProxy Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rgb (3) Calls proc~~set_background_color~~CallsGraph proc~set_background_color WindowProxy%set_background_color interface~vkf_viewer_set_background vkf_viewer_set_background proc~set_background_color->interface~vkf_viewer_set_background Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~set_background_color~~CalledByGraph proc~set_background_color WindowProxy%set_background_color proc~open WindowProxy%open proc~open->proc~set_background_color Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_background_color ( self , rgb ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rgb ( 3 ) self % background = rgb if ( c_associated ( self % viewer_ )) then if ( vkf_viewer_set_background ( self % viewer_ , real ([ rgb , 1.0_wp ], c_float )) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: could not set the background color' end if end subroutine set_background_color","tags":"","url":"proc/set_background_color.html"},{"title":"set_camera – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_camera(self, eye, center, up, duration, in_root) Set the camera of the current view: eye, center and up in the view\nframe's coordinates (OpenFrames' trackball setTransformation), or in its\nroot frame's if in_root (as the frames are now). With duration (s),\nfly there from the camera shown. Before the view is shown, it is its\ncamera when it is (View%set_camera). Type Bound WindowProxy Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout), target :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: eye (3) view frame's coordinates (or root's) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: center (3) view frame's coordinates (or root's) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: up (3) view frame's coordinates (or root's) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: duration s (default: at once) logical, intent(in), optional :: in_root Calls proc~~set_camera~~CallsGraph proc~set_camera WindowProxy%set_camera interface~vkf_viewer_get_look_at vkf_viewer_get_look_at proc~set_camera->interface~vkf_viewer_get_look_at proc~current_view WindowProxy%current_view proc~set_camera->proc~current_view proc~is_open WindowProxy%is_open proc~set_camera->proc~is_open proc~put_camera put_camera proc~set_camera->proc~put_camera proc~start_flight start_flight proc~set_camera->proc~start_flight proc~transform_camera transform_camera proc~set_camera->proc~transform_camera proc~view_set_camera View%view_set_camera proc~set_camera->proc~view_set_camera proc~world_to_view View%world_to_view proc~set_camera->proc~world_to_view interface~vkf_viewer_look_at vkf_viewer_look_at proc~put_camera->interface~vkf_viewer_look_at proc~window_wall window_wall proc~start_flight->proc~window_wall proc~frame_to_root frame_to_root proc~world_to_view->proc~frame_to_root proc~identity_matrix identity_matrix proc~world_to_view->proc~identity_matrix proc~quat_from_vectors quat_from_vectors proc~world_to_view->proc~quat_from_vectors proc~quat_to_matrix quat_to_matrix proc~world_to_view->proc~quat_to_matrix proc~rigid_inverse rigid_inverse proc~world_to_view->proc~rigid_inverse proc~rotated rotated proc~world_to_view->proc~rotated proc~translation_matrix translation_matrix proc~world_to_view->proc~translation_matrix proc~frame_to_root->proc~rigid_inverse proc~world_matrix ReferenceFrame%world_matrix proc~frame_to_root->proc~world_matrix proc~cross cross proc~quat_from_vectors->proc~cross proc~quat_normalize quat_normalize proc~quat_from_vectors->proc~quat_normalize proc~translation_matrix->proc~identity_matrix proc~wall_time wall_time proc~window_wall->proc~wall_time proc~world_matrix->proc~world_matrix proc~local_matrix ReferenceFrame%local_matrix proc~world_matrix->proc~local_matrix proc~frame_matrix frame_matrix proc~local_matrix->proc~frame_matrix proc~frame_matrix->proc~quat_to_matrix Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_camera ( self , eye , center , up , duration , in_root ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( inout ), target :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eye ( 3 ), center ( 3 ), up ( 3 ) !! view frame's coordinates (or root's) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: duration !! s (default: at once) logical , intent ( in ), optional :: in_root type ( View ), pointer :: v real ( wp ) :: cam ( 3 , 3 ), now ( 3 , 3 ) logical :: root v => self % current_view () cam = reshape ([ eye , center , up ], [ 3 , 3 ]) root = . false . if ( present ( in_root )) root = in_root if ( root ) cam = transform_camera ( v % world_to_view (), cam ) if (. not . self % is_open () . or . . not . associated ( self % shown , v )) then call v % set_camera ( cam (:, 1 ), cam (:, 2 ), cam (:, 3 )) return end if if ( present ( duration )) then if ( duration > 0.0_wp . and . vkf_viewer_get_look_at ( self % viewer_ , now (:, 1 ), now (:, 2 ), now (:, 3 )) == 0 ) then call start_flight ( self , v , now , v , cam , duration ) return end if end if self % flight % active = . false . call put_camera ( self , cam ) end subroutine set_camera","tags":"","url":"proc/set_camera.html"},{"title":"set_camera_throw – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_camera_throw(self, enabled) Whether the camera keeps moving (turning, zooming, panning) after a drag\nis released while the mouse moves (default true, VSG's and OSG's throw);\nfalse: it stops where it is released. Type Bound WindowProxy Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: enabled Calls proc~~set_camera_throw~~CallsGraph proc~set_camera_throw WindowProxy%set_camera_throw proc~apply_camera_controls apply_camera_controls proc~set_camera_throw->proc~apply_camera_controls interface~vkf_viewer_set_camera_controls vkf_viewer_set_camera_controls proc~apply_camera_controls->interface~vkf_viewer_set_camera_controls Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_camera_throw ( self , enabled ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: enabled self % camera_throw_ = enabled call apply_camera_controls ( self ) end subroutine set_camera_throw","tags":"","url":"proc/set_camera_throw.html"},{"title":"set_default_keys – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_default_keys(self, on) The built-in keys (default on): v the next view, V the previous\none, the space bar resets the view. Type Bound WindowProxy Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: on Source Code subroutine set_default_keys ( self , on ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: on self % default_keys_ = on end subroutine set_default_keys","tags":"","url":"proc/set_default_keys.html"},{"title":"set_event_handler – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_event_handler(self, handler) Give the window's keyboard and mouse events to handler (not owned: it\nmust stay alive while set), in place of any handler set before. Type Bound WindowProxy Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self class( WindowEventHandler ), intent(in), target :: handler not owned Source Code subroutine set_event_handler ( self , handler ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( WindowEventHandler ), intent ( in ), target :: handler !! not owned self % handler => handler end subroutine set_event_handler","tags":"","url":"proc/set_event_handler.html"},{"title":"set_light_ambient – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_light_ambient(self, rgb) The ambient, diffuse and specular colors ([r, g, b], 0 to 1) of the\nwindow's light (OpenFrames' defaults: 0.2 gray, white, none). The\nwindow's light is used while no frame of the scene has a light source\n(ReferenceFrame%set_light_source_enabled). Type Bound WindowProxy Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rgb (3) Calls proc~~set_light_ambient~~CallsGraph proc~set_light_ambient WindowProxy%set_light_ambient proc~apply_window_light apply_window_light proc~set_light_ambient->proc~apply_window_light interface~vkf_light_set vkf_light_set proc~apply_window_light->interface~vkf_light_set interface~vkf_viewer_light vkf_viewer_light proc~apply_window_light->interface~vkf_viewer_light Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represen