o_root proc~world_to_view->proc~frame_to_root proc~quat_from_vectors quat_from_vectors proc~world_to_view->proc~quat_from_vectors proc~rotated rotated proc~world_to_view->proc~rotated proc~translation_matrix translation_matrix proc~world_to_view->proc~translation_matrix proc~frame_to_root->proc~rigid_inverse proc~world_matrix ReferenceFrame%world_matrix proc~frame_to_root->proc~world_matrix proc~quat_from_vectors->proc~cross proc~quat_normalize quat_normalize proc~quat_from_vectors->proc~quat_normalize proc~translation_matrix->proc~identity_matrix proc~world_matrix->proc~local_matrix proc~world_matrix->proc~world_matrix Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~window_pick~~CalledByGraph proc~window_pick WindowProxy%window_pick proc~hover_handle hover_handle proc~hover_handle->proc~window_pick proc~dispatch_event dispatch_event proc~dispatch_event->proc~hover_handle proc~release_handle release_handle proc~dispatch_event->proc~release_handle proc~release_handle->proc~hover_handle proc~dispatch_events dispatch_events proc~dispatch_events->proc~dispatch_event proc~frame WindowProxy%frame proc~frame->proc~dispatch_events proc~resize WindowProxy%resize proc~resize->proc~frame proc~run WindowProxy%run proc~run->proc~frame Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine window_pick ( self , x , y , hits , tolerance , kinds , nearest ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( in ), target :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x , y !! -1 to 1 across the window, y up type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: hits (:) !! what is there, nearest first real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: tolerance !! window units (default 4) integer , intent ( in ), optional :: kinds (:) !! PICK_* (default: all) logical , intent ( in ), optional :: nearest !! default false class ( ReferenceFrame ), pointer :: root type ( PickCamera ) :: cam type ( PickHit ) :: h integer :: n , i , j logical :: only_nearest n = 0 only_nearest = . false . if ( present ( nearest )) only_nearest = nearest allocate ( hits ( 8 )) root => null () if ( associated ( self % scene )) root => self % scene % frame () if (. not . associated ( root ) . or . . not . view_camera ( self , x , y , cam )) then hits = hits ( 1 : 0 ) return end if cam % tolerance = 4.0_wp * cam % pixel_ratio if ( present ( tolerance )) cam % tolerance = tolerance * cam % pixel_ratio if ( present ( kinds )) then cam % kinds = 0 do i = 1 , size ( kinds ) if ( kinds ( i ) >= 0 . and . kinds ( i ) < bit_size ( cam % kinds )) cam % kinds = ibset ( cam % kinds , kinds ( i )) end do end if call pick_frame ( root , identity_matrix ()) ! (the root frame's coordinates: the camera's) do i = 2 , n ! nearest first h = hits ( i ) j = i - 1 do while ( j >= 1 ) if ( hits ( j )% distance <= h % distance ) exit hits ( j + 1 ) = hits ( j ) j = j - 1 end do hits ( j + 1 ) = h end do hits = hits ( 1 : n ) contains !> Frame f (at transform m to the root) and its children, under each of !> their parents. recursive subroutine pick_frame ( f , m ) class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: f real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) class ( ReferenceFrame ), pointer :: c integer :: k , best if ( f % pickable ()) call f % pick ( cam , m , hits , n ) if ( only_nearest . and . n > 1 ) then ! (keep the nearest; skip what is deeper) best = minloc ( hits ( 1 : n )% distance , dim = 1 ) hits ( 1 ) = hits ( best ) n = 1 end if if ( only_nearest . and . n == 1 ) cam % max_depth = hits ( 1 )% distance do k = 1 , f % num_children () c => f % child ( k ) call pick_frame ( c , matmul ( m , c % local_matrix ())) end do end subroutine pick_frame end subroutine window_pick","tags":"","url":"proc/window_pick.html"},{"title":"FrameManager – vkframes","text":"public interface FrameManager The FrameManager constructor: FrameManager(...) makes one (see new_frame_manager for its\narguments). Calls interface~~framemanager~~CallsGraph interface~framemanager FrameManager proc~new_frame_manager new_frame_manager interface~framemanager->proc~new_frame_manager proc~fm_set_frame FrameManager%fm_set_frame proc~new_frame_manager->proc~fm_set_frame interface~vkf_driver_preload vkf_driver_preload proc~fm_set_frame->interface~vkf_driver_preload Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Module Procedures private  function new_frame_manager (frame) result(fm) A frame manager for the scene with root frame (optional). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attribute