nt from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~new_vector_handle~~CalledByGraph proc~new_vector_handle new_vector_handle interface~vectorhandle VectorHandle interface~vectorhandle->proc~new_vector_handle Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function new_vector_handle ( name , vector , color , scale ) result ( h ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! the frame's name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: vector ( 3 ) !! frame coordinates real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: scale !! display scale (scene units per vector unit; > 0) type ( VectorHandle ) :: h h % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) call h % show_decorations (. false .) if ( present ( vector )) h % vector_ = vector if ( present ( scale )) then if ( scale > 0.0_wp ) h % scale_ = scale end if end function new_vector_handle","tags":"","url":"proc/new_vector_handle.html"},{"title":"priority – vkframes","text":"private pure function priority(self) The handle's priority over others on the same spot. Type Bound DragHandle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer Source Code pure integer function priority ( self ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self priority = self % priority_ end function priority","tags":"","url":"proc/priority.html"},{"title":"time – vkframes","text":"private pure function time(self) The handle's time. Type Bound TimeHandle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TimeHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) Source Code function new_time_handle ( name , path , time , t_min , t_max , color ) result ( h ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! the frame's name class ( TimePath ), intent ( in ), target :: path !! the path it moves along real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: time !! its time real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: t_min , t_max !! the times a drag may reach real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) type ( TimeHandle ) :: h h % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) call h % show_decorations (. false .) h % priority_ = 1 ! (a marker over an arrow on the same spot) h % path_ => path if ( present ( time )) h % time_ = time h % t_min = h % time_ h % t_max = h % time_ if ( present ( t_min )) h % t_min = t_min if ( present ( t_max )) h % t_max = t_max call h % set_time ( h % time_ ) end function new_time_handle !> The path the handle moves along (which must stay alive while used); its !> time kept (the frame placed on the new path). subroutine set_path ( self , path ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( TimePath ), intent ( in ), target :: path !! the path self % path_ => path call self % set_time ( self % time_ ) end subroutine set_path !> The handle's time (kept within its time range): the frame placed at the !> path's point for it. subroutine set_time ( self , time ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: time !! the time self % time_ = max ( self % t_min , min ( self % t_max , time )) if ( associated ( self % path_ )) call self % set_position ( self % path_ % position ( self % time_ )) end subroutine set_time !> The handle's time. pure real ( wp ) function time ( self ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self time = self % time_ end function time","tags":"","url":"proc/time~4.html"},{"title":"time_drag – vkframes","text":"private  function time_drag(self, origin, dir) result(moved) Drag the grabbed handle to the cursor's ray (origin, unit dir; root\nframe): its time where the path is nearest the ray (see the module\ndocumentation). False (not moved) if it isn't grabbed or the path is\nall behind the eye. Type Bound TimeHandle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TimeHandle ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: origin (3) the cursor's ray (root frame) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dir (3) the cursor's ray (root frame) Return Value logical Calls proc~~time_drag~~CallsGraph proc~time_drag TimeHandle%time_drag position position proc~time_drag->position proc~local_matrix ReferenceFrame%local_matrix proc~time_drag->proc~local_matrix proc~rigid_inverse rigid_inverse proc~time_drag->proc~rigid_inverse proc~set_time~4 TimeHandle%set_time proc~time_drag->proc~set_time~4 proc~world_matrix ReferenceFrame%world_matrix proc~time_drag->proc~world_matrix proc~frame_matrix frame_matrix proc~local_matrix->proc~frame_matrix proc~set_time~4->position proc~set_position~2 ReferenceFrame%set_position proc~set_time~4->proc~set_position~2 proc~world_matrix->proc~local_matrix proc~world_matrix->proc~world_matrix proc~quat_to_matrix quat_to_matrix proc~frame_matrix->proc~quat_to_matrix Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code logical function time_drag ( self , origin , dir ) result ( moved ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the cursor's ray (root frame) real ( wp ) :: parent ( 4 , 4 ), miss ( path_samples ), best , t_best real ( wp ) :: t_min ( path_samples ), m_min ( path_samples ) !! the local minima refined: their times and misses integer :: k , n_min logical :: found moved = . false . if (. not . ( self % dragged_ . and . allocated ( self % sample_t ) . and . associated ( self % path_ ))) return parent = matmul ( self % world_matrix (), rigid_inverse ( self % local_matrix ())) ! (the path's coordinates to the root) do k = 1 , path_samples miss ( k ) = ray_miss ( self % sample_p (:, k )) end do if ( minval ( miss ) >= huge ( 1.0_wp )) return ! each local minimum of the samples refined; of those nearly as near as ! the nearest (a path passing the same place again: orbits), the one ! nearest in time to the handle's n_min = 0 do k = 1 , path_samples if (. not . is_minimum ( k )) cycle n_min = n_min + 1 call refine ( k , t_min ( n_min ), m_min ( n_min )) end do if ( n_min == 0 ) return best = minval ( m_min ( 1 : n_min )) found = . false . t_best = self % time_ do k = 1 , n_min if ( m_min ( k ) > 1.5_wp * best + 1.0e-4_wp ) cycle if ( found . and . abs ( t_min ( k ) - self % time_ ) >= abs ( t_best - self % time_ )) cycle t_best = t_min ( k ) found = . true . end do if (. not . found ) return call self % set_time ( t_best ) moved = . true . contains !> How far point p (the path's coordinates) is from the ray, as seen !> from its origin (the tangent of the angle; huge() behind it). real ( wp ) function ray_miss ( p ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p ( 3 ) !! the point (the path's coordinates) real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ), along v = matmul ( parent ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), p ) + parent ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) - origin along = dot_product ( v , dir ) ray_miss = huge ( 1.0_wp ) if ( along > 0.0_wp ) ray_miss = norm2 ( v - along * dir ) / along end function ray_miss !> Sample k is a local minimum of the samples' misses (in front of the eye). logical function is_minimum ( j ) integer , intent ( in ) :: j !! the sample is_minimum = miss ( j ) < huge ( 1.0_wp ) if ( j > 1 ) is_minimum = is_minimum . and . miss ( j - 1 ) >= miss ( j ) if ( j < path_samples ) is_minimum = is_minimum . and . miss ( j + 1 ) > miss ( j ) end function is_minimum !> The time of the least miss between sample j's neighbours (golden-section !> search), and that miss. subroutine refine ( j , t , m ) integer , intent ( in ) :: j !! the sample real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: t !! the time found real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: m !! its miss real ( wp ), parameter :: golden = 0.5_wp * ( sqrt ( 5.0_wp ) - 1.0_wp ) real ( wp ) :: a , b , c , d , fc , fd integer :: it a = self % sample_t ( max ( 1 , j - 1 )) b = self % sample_t ( min ( path_samples , j + 1 )) c = b - golden * ( b - a ) d = a + golden * ( b - a ) fc = ray_miss ( self % path_ % position ( c )) fd = ray_miss ( self % path_ % position ( d )) do it = 1 , 40 if ( fc < fd ) then b = d d = c fd = fc c = b - golden * ( b - a ) fc = ray_miss ( self % path_ % position ( c )) else a = c c = d fc = fd d = a + golden * ( b - a ) fd = ray_miss ( self % path_ % position ( d )) end if end do t = 0.5_wp * ( a + b ) m = min ( fc , fd ) end subroutine refine end function time_drag","tags":"","url":"proc/time_drag.html"},{"title":"time_frame_info – vkframes","text":"private  function time_frame_info(self) result(info) What kind of frame this is: 'TimeHandle'. Type Bound TimeHandle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TimeHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Source Code function time_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :