 module. Source Code logical function time_grab ( self , origin , dir ) result ( ok ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the cursor's ray (root frame) integer :: k ok = . false . if (. not . ( self % draggable () . and . associated ( self % path_ ))) return if ( allocated ( self % sample_t )) deallocate ( self % sample_t , self % sample_p ) allocate ( self % sample_t ( path_samples ), self % sample_p ( 3 , path_samples )) do k = 1 , path_samples self % sample_t ( k ) = self % t_min + ( self % t_max - self % t_min ) * ( k - 1 ) / ( path_samples - 1 ) self % sample_p (:, k ) = self % path_ % position ( self % sample_t ( k )) end do self % dragged_ = . true . call self % show_state () ok = . true . end function time_grab","tags":"","url":"proc/time_grab.html"},{"title":"time_handle_point – vkframes","text":"private pure function time_handle_point(self) result(p) The point the mouse grabs: the marker, at the frame's origin. Type Bound TimeHandle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TimeHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) Source Code pure function time_handle_point ( self ) result ( p ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) p = 0.0_wp end function time_handle_point","tags":"","url":"proc/time_handle_point.html"},{"title":"tip – vkframes","text":"private pure function tip(self) result(p) The arrow's tip: the display scale times the vector (frame coordinates). Type Bound VectorHandle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( VectorHandle ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) Called by proc~~tip~~CalledByGraph proc~tip VectorHandle%tip proc~arrow_sizes arrow_sizes proc~arrow_sizes->proc~tip proc~update_arrow update_arrow proc~update_arrow->proc~tip proc~update_arrow->proc~arrow_sizes proc~vector_bound VectorHandle%vector_bound proc~vector_bound->proc~tip proc~vector_handle_point VectorHandle%vector_handle_poi