on in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_path ( self , path ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( TimePath ), intent ( in ), target :: path !! the path self % path_ => path call self % set_time ( self % time_ ) end subroutine set_path","tags":"","url":"proc/set_path.html"},{"title":"set_priority – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_priority(self, priority) The handle's priority over others on the same spot of the screen (higher\nfirst; default 0, a TimeHandle's 1; see the module documentation). Type Bound DragHandle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( DragHandle ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: priority higher: hovered first Source Code subroutine set_priority ( self , priority ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: priority !! higher: hovered first self % priority_ = priority end subroutine set_priority","tags":"","url":"proc/set_priority.html"},{"title":"set_time – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_time(self, time) The handle's time (kept within its time range): the frame placed at the\npath's point for it. Type Bound TimeHandle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TimeHandle ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: time the time Calls proc~~set_time~4~~CallsGraph proc~set_time~4 TimeHandle%set_time position position proc~set_time~4->position proc~set_position~2 ReferenceFrame%set_position proc~set_time~4->proc~set_position~2 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a gener