ssociated ( self % marker )) return rgba = self % color () size = self % size_ light = 0.0_wp if ( self % dragged ()) then light = 0.6_wp size = 1.4_wp * size else if ( self % hovered ()) then light = 0.35_wp size = 1.2_wp * size end if rgba ( 1 : 3 ) = rgba ( 1 : 3 ) + light * ( 1.0_wp - rgba ( 1 : 3 )) call check_status ( marker_set_style ( self % marker , real ( rgba , c_float ), real ( size , c_float ), self % shape_ , & 0.0_c_float )) end subroutine time_show_state","tags":"","url":"proc/time_show_state.html"},{"title":"update_arrow – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine update_arrow(self) The shaft and head placed for the vector (hidden if it is 0). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( VectorHandle ), intent(inout) :: self Calls proc~~update_arrow~~CallsGraph proc~update_arrow update_arrow interface~vkf_switch_set vkf_switch_set proc~update_arrow->interface~vkf_switch_set interface~vkf_transform_set_matrix vkf_transform_set_matrix proc~update_arrow->interface~vkf_transform_set_matrix proc~arrow_sizes arrow_sizes proc~update_arrow->proc~arrow_sizes proc~check_status check_status proc~update_arrow->proc~check_status proc~cross cross proc~update_arrow->proc~cross proc~tip VectorHandle%tip proc~update_arrow->proc~tip proc~arrow_sizes->proc~tip Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~update_arrow~~CalledByGraph proc~update_arrow update_arrow proc~set_display_scale VectorHandle%set_display_scale proc~set_display_scale->proc~update_arrow proc~set_head_size VectorHandle%set_head_size proc~set_head_size->proc~update_arrow proc~set_vector VectorHandle%set_vector proc~set_vector->proc~update_arrow proc~vector_build_contents VectorHandle%vector_build_contents proc~vector_build_contents->proc~update_arrow proc~vector_move_handle_point VectorHandle%vector_move_handle_point proc~vector_move_handle_point->proc~set_vector Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine update_arrow ( self ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ) :: len , head_len , head_radius , u ( 3 ), a ( 3 ), b ( 3 ), m ( 4 , 4 ) if (. not . c_associated ( self % switch )) return call arrow_sizes ( self , len , head_len , head_radius ) call check_status ( vkf_switch_set ( self % switch , merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , len > 0.0_wp ))) if ( len <= 0.0_wp ) return u = self % tip () / len a = cross ( u , [ 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp ]) if ( norm2 ( a ) < 1.0e-6_wp ) a = cross ( u , [ 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp ]) a = a / norm2 ( a ) b = cross ( u , a ) ! (a, b, u right-handed) m = 0.0_wp m ( 4 , 4 ) = 1.0_wp m ( 1 : 3 , 1 ) = 0.4_wp * head_radius * a ! the shaft: 0.4 of the head's radius m ( 1 : 3 , 2 ) = 0.4_wp * head_radius * b m ( 1 : 3 , 3 ) = ( len - head_len ) * u call check_status ( vkf_transform_set_matrix ( self % shaft , m )) m ( 1 : 3 , 1 ) = head_radius * a m ( 1 : 3 , 2 ) = head_radius * b m ( 1 : 3 , 3 ) = head_len * u m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) = ( len - head_len ) * u call check_status ( vkf_transform_set_matrix ( self % head , m )) end subroutine update_arrow","tags":"","url":"proc/update_arrow.html"},{"title":"vector_bound – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine vector_bound(self, center, radius) The arrow's bounding sphere (frame coordinates). Type Bound VectorHandle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( VectorHandle ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: center (3) the bound's center (frame coordinates) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: radius its radius (scene units) Calls proc~~vector_bound~~CallsGraph proc~vector_bound VectorHandle%vector_bound proc~tip VectorHandle%tip proc~vector_bound->proc~tip Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine vector_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ) !! the bound's center (frame coordinates) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: radius !! its radius (scene units) center = 0.5_wp * self % tip () radius = 0.5_wp * norm2 ( self % tip ()) end subroutine vector_bound","tags":"","url":"proc/vector_bound.html"},{"title":"vector_build_contents – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine vector_build_contents(self, viewer, group) The arrow: a unit shaft and head under their transforms, in a switch. Type Bound VectorHandle Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( VectorHandle ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer a window's viewer (null: headle