 Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine vector_show_state ( self ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( c_float ) :: color ( 4 ), glow ( 4 ) if (. not . c_associated ( self % shaft_mesh )) return color = real ( self % color (), c_float ) glow = 0.0_c_float if ( self % dragged ()) then glow ( 1 : 3 ) = 0.45_c_float else if ( self % hovered ()) then glow ( 1 : 3 ) = 0.25_c_float end if call check_status ( mesh_set_material ( self % shaft_mesh , [ 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], color , & [ 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], glow , 0.0_c_float )) call check_status ( mesh_set_material ( self % head_mesh , [ 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], color , & [ 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], glow , 0.0_c_float )) end subroutine vector_show_state","tags":"","url":"proc/vector_show_state.html"},{"title":"TimeHandle – vkframes","text":"public interface TimeHandle The TimeHandle constructor: TimeHandle(...) makes one (see new_time_handle for its\narguments). Calls interface~~timehandle~~CallsGraph interface~timehandle TimeHandle proc~new_time_handle new_time_handle interface~timehandle->proc~new_time_handle proc~set_time~4 TimeHandle%set_time proc~new_time_handle->proc~set_time~4 proc~show_decorations ReferenceFrame%show_decorations proc~new_time_handle->proc~show_decorations position position proc~set_time~4->position proc~set_position~2 ReferenceFrame%set_position proc~set_time~4->proc~set_position~2 proc~show_axes ReferenceFrame%show_axes proc~show_decorations->proc~show_axes proc~show_axes_labels ReferenceFrame%show_axes_labels proc~show_decorations-