from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~new_model~~CalledByGraph proc~new_model new_model interface~model Model interface~model->proc~new_model Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function new_model ( name , file , color ) result ( m ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: file real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) type ( Model ) :: m logical :: ok m % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) if ( present ( file )) ok = m % set_model ( file ) end function new_model","tags":"","url":"proc/new_model.html"},{"title":"set_model – vkframes","text":"private  function set_model(self, file) result(ok) Read the model file (now, so its bound is known). Returns false if it\ncould not be read. Set it before a window first shows the model. Type Bound Model Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Model ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: file Return Value logical Calls proc~~set_model~~CallsGraph proc~set_model Model%set_model interface~vkf_model_read vkf_model_read proc~set_model->interface~vkf_model_read interface~vkf_node_bound vkf_node_bound proc~set_model->interface~vkf_node_bound Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~set_model~~CalledByGraph proc~set_model Model%set_model proc~new_model new_model proc~new_model->proc~set_model interface~model Model interface~model->proc~new_model Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code logical function set_model ( self , file ) result ( ok ) class ( Model ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: file type ( c_ptr ) :: node node = vkf_model_read ( file , len ( file , kind = c_int )) ok = c_associated ( node ) if (. not . ok ) return self % file = file self % model_ = node if ( vkf_node_bound ( node , self % bound_center , self % bound_radius ) /= 0 ) then self % bound_center = 0.0_wp self % bound_radius = 0.0_wp end if end function set_model","tags":"","url":"proc/set_model.html"},{"title":"share_model – vkframes","text":"private  function share_model(self, other) result(ok) Use the model already read by other (