 ) / s + 1 ! segments at stride s if ( m == 0 ) exit if (. not . allocated ( c % lod ( k )% bound )) allocate ( c % lod ( k )% bound ( 0 :( c % capacity - 2 ) / s )) do seg = max ( 0 , q0 - 1 ) / s , m - 1 ! the segments the points written change a = seg * s e = min ( a + s , n - 1 ) mid = a + s / 2 b0 = 0.0_wp ! the halves' bounds (none at stride 1) b1 = 0.0_wp if ( k > 1 ) b0 = c % lod ( k - 1 )% bound ( 2 * seg ) if ( mid < e ) then ! two halves: also the middle point's distance if ( k > 1 ) b1 = c % lod ( k - 1 )% bound ( 2 * seg + 1 ) c % lod ( k )% bound ( seg ) = real ( max ( b0 , b1 ) + segment_distance ( pt ( mid ), pt ( a ), pt ( e )), c_float ) else c % lod ( k )% bound ( seg ) = real ( b0 , c_float ) end if end do end do end associate call send_lod ( self , j ) contains !> Local point i of the chunk, in double precision. function pt ( i ) result ( v ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) if ( present ( x )) then v = x (:, self % chunks ( j )% first + i ) else v = real ( p ( 1 : 3 , 1 , i + 1 ), wp ) + real ( p ( 1 : 3 , 2 , i + 1 ), wp ) end if end function pt end subroutine update_lod","tags":"","url":"proc/update_lod.html"},{"title":"written – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine written(self, i1, i2, x) Points i1 .. i2 were written: measure a strip's distances along it (from\nthe distance at point i1-1), update its level of detail, and upload the\nchunks holding them. x : the points in double precision, x(:, i) for\nchain point i (at least i1-1 .. i2), to measure from; without it, from\nthe floats written. (i2 is the last point written in the chain.) Type Bound LineChain Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( LineChain ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i1 integer, intent(in) :: i2 real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: x (:,:) (3, at least i1-1 .. i2): the points Calls proc~~written~~CallsGraph proc~written LineChain%written interface~vkf_line_points_changed vkf_line_points_changed proc~written->interface~v