calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine arrow ( base , direction , body_length , head_length , body_radius , head_radius , n_segments , & xyz , normals , uv , indices ) real ( c_double ), intent ( in ) :: base ( 3 ) real ( c_double ), intent ( in ) :: direction ( 3 ) !! the arrow's axis (need not be unit length) real ( c_double ), intent ( in ) :: body_length , head_length , body_radius , head_radius integer , intent ( in ) :: n_segments real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: xyz !! (3, n_vertices) real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: normals !! (3, n_vertices) real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), intent ( out ) :: uv !! (2, n_vertices): zero integer ( c_int32_t ), dimension (:), intent ( out ) :: indices !! (n_indices) real ( c_double ), parameter :: pi = acos ( - 1.0_c_double ) real ( c_double ) :: w ( 3 ), u ( 3 ), v ( 3 ), r ( 3 ), a , cone_normal ( 3 ) integer :: i , n , nv , ni , body0 , cap0 , head0 , apex0 , disk0 n = n_segments w = direction / norm2 ( direction ) u = cross ( w , [ 1.0_c_double , 0.0_c_double , 0.0_c_double ]) if ( norm2 ( u ) < 1.0e-6_c_double ) u = cross ( w , [ 0.0_c_double , 1.0_c_double , 0.0_c_double ]) u = u / norm2 ( u ) v = cross ( w , u ) uv = 0.0_c_float nv = 0 ni = 0 ! body side: rings at the base and the top of the body body0 = nv do i = 0 , n r = radial ( i ) call put ( base + body_radius * r , r ) call put ( base + body_radius * r + body_length * w , r ) end do ! body bottom cap (facing -w): center, then a ring cap0 = nv call put ( base , - w ) do i = 0 , n call put ( base + body_radius * radial ( i ), - w ) end do ! head side: ring at the head's base, and the apex for each segment head0 = nv do i = 0 , n r = radial ( i ) cone_normal = r * head_length + w * head_radius call put ( base + body_length * w + head_radius * r , cone_normal / norm2 ( cone_normal )) end do apex0 = nv do i = 0 , n a = 2.0_c_double * pi * ( real ( i , c_double ) + 0.5_c_double ) / real ( n , c_double ) r = cos ( a ) * u + sin ( a ) * v cone_normal = r * head_length + w * head_radius call put ( base + ( body_length + head_length ) * w , cone_normal / norm2 ( cone_normal )) end do ! head base disk (facing -w): center, then a ring disk0 = nv call put ( base + body_length * w , - w ) do i = 0 , n call put ( base + body_length * w + head_radius * radial ( i ), - w ) end do do i = 0 , n - 1 ! body side: (a_i, a_i+1, b_i+1) and (a_i, b_i+1, b_i) call tri ( body0 + 2 * i , body0 + 2 * ( i + 1 ), body0 + 2 * ( i + 1 ) + 1 ) call tri ( body0 + 2 * i , body0 + 2 * ( i + 1 ) + 1 , body0 + 2 * i + 1 ) ! caps facing -w: (center, ring_i+1, ring_i) call tri ( cap0 , cap0 + 1 + i + 1 , cap0 + 1 + i ) call tri ( disk0 , disk0 + 1 + i + 1 , disk0 + 1 + i ) ! head side: (ring_i, ring_i+1, apex_i) call tri ( head0 + i , head0 + i + 1 , apex0 + i ) end do contains !> The unit vector at angle 2 pi k / n around the arrow's axis. pure function radial ( k ) result ( rad ) integer , intent ( in ) :: k real ( c_double ) :: rad ( 3 ), ang ang = 2.0_c_double * pi * real ( k , c_double ) / real ( n , c_double ) rad = cos ( ang ) * u + sin ( ang ) * v end function radial !> Append a vertex at `p` with normal `nrm`. subroutine put ( p , nrm ) real ( c_double ), intent ( in ) :: p ( 3 ), nrm ( 3 ) nv = nv + 1 xyz (:, nv ) = real ( p , c_float ) normals (:, nv ) = real ( nrm , c_float ) end subroutine put !> Append a triangle of (0-based) vertex indices i1, i2, i3. subroutine tri ( i1 , i2 , i3 ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i1 , i2 , i3 indices ( ni + 1 : ni + 3 ) = int ([ i1 , i2 , i3 ], c_int32_t ) ni = ni + 3 end subroutine tri end subroutine arrow","tags":"","url":"proc/arrow.html"},{"title":"arrow_size – vkframes","text":"public pure subroutine arrow_size(n_segments, n_vertices, n_indices) Number of vertic