s Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function surface_node ( xyz , idx , rgba , normals , colors , two_sided , sphere ) result ( node ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: xyz (:,:) integer , intent ( in ) :: idx (:,:) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rgba ( 4 ) !! color [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: normals (:,:) !! (3, n): lit real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: colors (:,:) !! (4, n) logical , intent ( in ), optional :: two_sided !! (lit) both faces (default: front only) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: sphere ( 4 ) !! (lit, translucent) center and radius type ( c_ptr ) :: node real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: v , n , uv , c integer ( c_int32_t ), dimension (:), pointer :: indices integer :: nv , ni , flags , i logical :: lit , translucent node = c_null_ptr nv = size ( xyz , 2 ) ni = size ( idx ) if ( nv < 3 . or . ni < 3 ) return lit = present ( normals ) flags = 1 if ( lit ) then translucent = rgba ( 4 ) < 1.0_wp if ( present ( colors )) translucent = translucent . or . any ( colors ( 4 , :) < 1.0_wp ) flags = 0 if ( translucent ) flags = flags + 8 if ( present ( two_sided )) then if ( two_sided ) flags = flags + 16 end if end if if ( present ( colors )) flags = flags + 32 node = vkf_mesh_create ( int ( nv , c_int ), int ( ni , c_int ), real ( rgba , c_float ), c_null_ptr , c_null_ptr , & int ( flags , c_int )) if (. not . c_associated ( node )) return call mesh_arrays ( node , nv , ni , v , n , uv , indices ) v = real ( xyz , c_float ) if ( lit ) then n = real ( normals , c_float ) else n = 0.0_c_float n ( 3 , :) = 1.0_c_float end if uv = 0.0_c_float indices = int ( reshape ( idx , [ ni ]) - 1 , c_int32_t ) if ( present ( colors )) then call c_f_pointer ( vkf_mesh_array ( node , 5_c_int ), c , [ 4 , nv ]) do i = 1 , nv c (:, i ) = real ( colors (:, i ) * rgba , c_float ) end do end if if ( lit . and . iand ( flags , 8 ) /= 0 . and . present ( sphere )) & call check_status ( vkf_mesh_set_bound ( node , real ( sphere ( 1 ), c_double ), real ( sphere ( 2 ), c_double ), & real ( sphere ( 3 ), c_double ), real ( sphere ( 4 ), c_double )), 'shapes' ) end function surface_node","tags":"","url":"proc/surface_node.html"},{"title":"surface_point – vkframes","text":"private pure function surface_point(r, lat, lon) result(p) The point at geodetic latitude lat and longitude lon on the ellipsoid\n(OpenFrames' LatLonGrid formula: the surface point whose normal has\nthose angles). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r (3) semi-axes (scene units) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: lat radians real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: lon radians Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) Called by proc~~surface_point~~CalledByGraph proc~surface_point surface_point proc~make_grid make_grid proc~make_grid->proc~surface_point proc~grid_build_contents LatLonGrid%grid_build_contents proc~grid_build_contents->proc~make_grid proc~grid_set_color LatLonGrid%grid_set_color proc~grid_set_color->proc~make_grid proc~grid_set_parameters LatLonGrid%grid_set_parameters proc~grid_set_parameters->proc~make_grid proc~set_line_widths LatLonGrid%set_line_widths proc~set_line_widths->proc~make_grid Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function surface_point ( r , lat , lon ) result ( p ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: r ( 3 ) !! semi-axes (scene units) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: lat , lon !! radians real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ), n ( 3 ), r2 ( 3 ) n = [ cos ( lat ) * cos ( lon ), cos ( lat ) * sin ( lon ), sin ( lat )] r2 = r ** 2 p = r2 * n / sqrt ( dot_product ( r2 , n ** 2 )) end function surface_point","tags":"","url":"proc/surface_point.html"},{"title":"tick_image – vkframes","text":"private  function tick_image(self) result(file) The tick image file ('' for none). Type Bound CoordinateAxes Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CoordinateAxes ), intent(in) :: self Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Source Code function tick_image ( self ) result ( file ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: file file = self % image_file end function tick_image","tags":"","url":"proc/tick_image.html"},{"title":"tick_shape – vkframes","text":"private pure function tick_shape(self) Tick shape: a MARKER_* shape. Type Bound CoordinateAxes Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( CoordinateAxes ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer Source Code pure integer function tick_shape ( self ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self tick_shape = self % shape_ end function tick_shape","tags":"","url":"proc/tick_shape.html"},{"title":"two_sided – vkframes","text":"private pure function two_sided(self) Whether both sides are drawn. Type Bound Polyhedron Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Polyhedron ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical Source Code function surface_node ( xyz , idx , rgba , normals , colors , two_sided , sphere ) result ( node ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: xyz (:,:) integer , intent ( in ) :: idx (:,:) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: rgba ( 4 ) !! color [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: normals (:,:) !! (3, n): lit real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: colors (:,:) !! (4, n) logical , intent ( in ), optional :: two_sided !! (lit) both faces (default: front only) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: sphere ( 4 ) !! (lit, translucent) center and radius type ( c_ptr ) :: node real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: v , n , uv , c integer ( c_int32_t ), dimension (:), pointer :: indices integer :: nv , ni , flags , i logical :: lit , translucent node = c_null_ptr nv = size ( xyz , 2 ) ni = size ( idx ) if ( nv < 3 . or . ni < 3 ) return lit = present ( normals ) flags = 1 if ( lit ) then translucent = rgba ( 4 ) < 1.0_wp if ( present ( colors )) translucent = translucent . or . any ( colors ( 4 , :) < 1.0_wp ) flags = 0 if ( translucent ) flags = flags + 8 if ( present ( two_sided )) then if ( two_sided ) flags = flags + 16 end if end if if ( present ( colors )) flags = flags + 32 node = vkf_mesh_create ( int ( nv , c_int ), int ( ni , c_int ), real ( rgba , c_float ), c_null_ptr , c_null_ptr , & int ( flags , c_int )) if (. not . c_associated ( node )) return call mesh_arrays ( node , nv , ni , v , n , uv , indices ) v = real ( xyz , c_float ) if ( lit ) then n = real ( normals , c_float ) else n = 0.0_c_float n ( 3 , :) = 1.0_c_float end if uv = 0.0_c_float indices = int ( reshape ( idx , [ ni ]) - 1 , c_int32_t ) if ( present ( colors )) then call c_f_pointer ( vkf_mesh_array ( node , 5_c_int ), c , [ 4 , nv ]) do i = 1 , nv c (:, i ) = real ( colors (:, i ) * rgba , c_float ) end do end if if ( lit . and . iand ( flags , 8 ) /= 0 . and . present ( sphere )) & call check_status ( vkf_mesh_set_bound ( node , real ( sphere ( 1 ), c_double ), real ( sphere ( 2 ), c_double ), & real ( sphere ( 3 ), c_double ), real ( sphere ( 4 ), c_double )), 'shapes' ) end function surface_node !> Points along a closed curve, as separate segments: pairs (p(i), p(i+1)). pure function closed_segments ( p ) result ( s ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p (:,:) real ( wp ) :: s ( 3 , 2 * size ( p , 2 )) integer :: i , n n = size ( p , 2 ) do i = 1 , n s (:, 2 * i - 1 ) = p (:, i ) s (:, 2 * i ) = p (:, modulo ( i , n ) + 1 ) end do end function closed_segments !> Points along an open curve, as separate segments. pure function open_segments ( p ) result ( s ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p (:,:) real ( wp ) :: s ( 3 , 2 * ( size ( p , 2 ) - 1 )) integer :: i do i = 1 , size ( p , 2 ) - 1 s (:, 2 * i - 1 ) = p (:, i ) s (:, 2 * i ) = p (:, i + 1 ) end do end function open_segments !> Append points b to a (allocatable, (3, n)). pure subroutine append ( a , b ) real ( wp ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: a (:,:) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: b (:,:) real ( wp ), allocatable :: tmp (:,:) if (. not . allocated ( a )) allocate ( a ( 3 , 0 )) allocate ( tmp ( 3 , size ( a , 2 ) + size ( b , 2 ))) tmp (:, 1 : size ( a , 2 )) = a tmp (:, size ( a , 2 ) + 1 :) = b call move_alloc ( tmp , a ) end subroutine append ! ================================================================== ! CoordinateAxes !> Coordinate axes named `name`, of color `color` ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, !> a]), 1 long, with major ticks every 0.5 and minor every 0.25 (OpenFrames' !> defaults). function new_coordinate_axes ( name , color ) result ( a ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) type ( CoordinateAxes ) :: a a % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) a % image_file = '' call place_axes ( a , a % length_ ) end function new_coordinate_axes !> The frame's own axes (arrows) at `length` along x, y and z, half as long. subroutine place_axes ( self , length ) class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: length !! scene units call self % move_x_axis ([ length , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp ], 0.5_wp * length ) call self % move_y_axis ([ 0.0_wp , length , 0.0_wp ], 0.5_wp * length ) call self % move_z_axis ([ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , length ], 0.5_wp * length ) end subroutine place_axes !> The axes' length (scene units, >= 0; default 1); the frame's own axes are !> moved to the lines' ends. subroutine set_axis_length ( self , length ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: length !! scene units (< 0: ignored) if ( length < 0.0_wp ) return self % length_ = length call place_axes ( self , length ) call make_axes ( self ) end subroutine set_axis_length !> The axes' length (scene units). pure real ( wp ) function axis_length ( self ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self axis_length = self % length_ end function axis_length !> Which axes to draw: an ior of X_AXIS, Y_AXIS, Z_AXIS. subroutine set_draw_axes ( self , axes ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: axes self % drawn = axes call make_axes ( self ) end subroutine set_draw_axes !> Which axes are drawn: an ior of X_AXIS, Y_AXIS, Z_AXIS. pure integer function draw_axes ( self ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self draw_axes = self % drawn end function draw_axes !> The axis lines' width (window units; default 1). subroutine set_axis_width ( self , width ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: width !! window units (<= 0: ignored) if ( width <= 0.0_wp ) return self % width_ = width call make_axes ( self ) end subroutine set_axis_width !> The axis lines' width (window units). pure real ( wp ) function axis_width ( self ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self axis_width = self % width_ end function axis_width !> Major and minor tick spacings (>= 0; 0 for none). subroutine set_tick_spacing ( self , major , minor ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: major , minor !! scene units (< 0: unchanged) if ( major >= 0.0_wp ) self % major = major if ( minor >= 0.0_wp ) self % minor = minor call make_axes ( self ) end subroutine set_tick_spacing !> Major and minor tick spacings. pure subroutine tick_spacing ( self , major , minor ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: major , minor !! scene units major = self % major minor = self % minor end subroutine tick_spacing !> Major and minor tick sizes (window units; default 8 and 4). subroutine set_tick_size ( self , major , minor ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: major , minor !! window units (<= 0: unchanged) if ( major > 0.0_wp ) self % major_size = major if ( minor > 0.0_wp ) self % minor_size = minor call make_axes ( self ) end subroutine set_tick_size !> Major and minor tick sizes (window units). pure subroutine tick_size ( self , major , minor ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: major , minor !! window units major = self % major_size minor = self % minor_size end subroutine tick_size !> Tick shape: a MARKER_* shape (default MARKER_DISK; OpenFrames' !> setTickShader with its marker shaders). subroutine set_tick_shape ( self , shape ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: shape !! a MARKER_* shape self % shape_ = shape call make_axes ( self ) end subroutine set_tick_shape !> Tick shape: a MARKER_* shape. pure integer function tick_shape ( self ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self tick_shape = self % shape_ end function tick_shape !> Draw the ticks as an image (OpenFrames' setTickImage; found with !> find_data_file; '' for disks again). False if it cannot be read. logical function set_tick_image ( self , file ) result ( ok ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: file !! image file ('' for disks) character ( len = :), allocatable :: path type ( c_ptr ) :: image ok = . true . image = c_null_ptr if ( len_trim ( file ) > 0 ) then path = find_data_file ( file ) if ( len ( path ) > 0 ) image = vkf_image_read ( path , len ( path , kind = c_int )) ok = c_associated ( image ) if (. not . ok ) return end if if ( c_associated ( self % image )) call vkf_image_delete ( self % image ) self % image = image self % image_file = trim ( file ) self % shape_ = merge ( MARKER_IMAGE , MARKER_DISK , c_associated ( image )) call make_axes ( self ) end function set_tick_image !> The tick image file ('' for none). function tick_image ( self ) result ( file ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: file file = self % image_file end function tick_image !> The axes' color (lines and ticks). subroutine axes_set_color ( self , color ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call self % ReferenceFrame % set_color ( color ) call make_axes ( self ) end subroutine axes_set_color !> What kind of frame this is: 'CoordinateAxes'. function axes_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'CoordinateAxes' end function axes_frame_info !> The bounding sphere: the origin, radius the axis length. subroutine axes_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius !! the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) center = 0.0_wp radius = self % length_ end subroutine axes_bound !> Draw the axes under `group` (the contents); with a window's `viewer`, later !> drawings are compiled. subroutine axes_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the frame's contents group self % nodes % contents = group call make_axes ( self ) self % nodes % shown = c_associated ( viewer ) end subroutine axes_build_contents !> Make the axes' lines and tick marks, in place of the old (nothing before !> build_contents). subroutine make_axes ( self ) class ( CoordinateAxes ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), allocatable :: lines (:,:), major (:,:), minor (:,:) real ( wp ) :: e ( 3 ), mark , f type ( c_ptr ) :: group integer :: k , i if (. not . c_associated ( self % nodes % contents )) return allocate ( lines ( 3 , 0 ), major ( 3 , 0 ), minor ( 3 , 0 )) do k = 1 , 3 if ( iand ( self % drawn , 2 ** ( k - 1 )) == 0 ) cycle e = 0.0_wp e ( k ) = 1.0_wp call append ( lines , reshape ([ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , self % length_ * e ], [ 3 , 2 ])) if ( self % major > 0.0_wp ) then do i = 1 , int ( self % length_ / self % major + 1.0e-9_wp ) call append ( major , reshape ( i * self % major * e , [ 3 , 1 ])) end do end if if ( self % minor > 0.0_wp ) then do i = 1 , int ( self % length_ / self % minor + 1.0e-9_wp ) mark = i * self % minor if ( self % major > 0.0_wp ) then ! not where a major tick is f = mark / self % major if ( abs ( f - nint ( f )) < 1.0e-6_wp ) cycle end if call append ( minor , reshape ( mark * e , [ 3 , 1 ])) end do end if end do group = vkf_switch_create () call add ( group , line_node ( lines , self % color (), self % width_ , . true .)) call add ( group , marker_node ( major , self % color (), self % major_size , self % shape_ , self % length_ , self % image )) call add ( group , marker_node ( minor , self % color (), self % minor_size , self % shape_ , self % length_ , self % image )) call self % nodes % replace ( group ) end subroutine make_axes ! ================================================================== ! LatLonGrid !> A latitude/longitude grid named `name`, of color `color`, on a unit !> sphere, every 30 degrees (OpenFrames' defaults). function new_lat_lon_grid ( name , color ) result ( g ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) type ( LatLonGrid ) :: g g % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) call place_grid_axes ( g ) end function new_lat_lon_grid !> The frame's own axes (arrows) at the ellipsoid's semi-axes, half as long. subroutine place_grid_axes ( self ) type ( LatLonGrid ), intent ( inout ) :: self call self % move_x_axis ([ self % radii_ ( 1 ), 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp ], 0.5_wp * self % radii_ ( 1 )) call self % move_y_axis ([ 0.0_wp , self % radii_ ( 2 ), 0.0_wp ], 0.5_wp * self % radii_ ( 2 )) call self % move_z_axis ([ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , self % radii_ ( 3 )], 0.5_wp * self % radii_ ( 3 )) end subroutine place_grid_axes !> The ellipsoid's semi-axes (> 0; e.g. a Sphere's radii, a little larger !> to draw above its surface) and the line spacings (radians; 0 for no !> latitude or longitude lines), as OpenFrames' setParameters. subroutine grid_set_parameters ( self , radius_x , radius_y , radius_z , lat_spacing , lon_spacing ) class ( LatLonGrid ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radius_x , radius_y , radius_z !! scene units (<= 0: unchanged) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: lat_spacing , lon_spacing !! radians (< 0: unchanged) if ( radius_x > 0.0_wp ) self % radii_ ( 1 ) = radius_x if ( radius_y > 0.0_wp ) self % radii_ ( 2 ) = radius_y if ( radius_z > 0.0_wp ) self % radii_ ( 3 ) = radius_z if ( lat_spacing >= 0.0_wp ) self % lat_spacing = lat_spacing if ( lon_spacing >= 0.0_wp ) self % lon_spacing = lon_spacing call place_grid_axes ( self ) call make_grid ( self ) end subroutine grid_set_parameters !> The ellipsoid's semi-axes and the line spacings, as OpenFrames' getParameters. pure subroutine grid_parameters ( self , radius_x , radius_y , radius_z , lat_spacing , lon_spacing ) class ( LatLonGrid ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: radius_x , radius_y , radius_z !! scene units real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: lat_spacing , lon_spacing !! radians radius_x = self % radii_ ( 1 ) radius_y = self % radii_ ( 2 ) radius_z = self % radii_ ( 3 ) lat_spacing = self % lat_spacing lon_spacing = self % lon_spacing end subroutine grid_parameters !> Widths of the grid lines and of the equator and prime meridian (window !> units; defaults 1 and 3). subroutine set_line_widths ( self , width , main_width ) class ( LatLonGrid ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: width , main_width !! window units (<= 0: unchanged) if ( width > 0.0_wp ) self % width_ = width if ( main_width > 0.0_wp ) self % main_width = main_width call make_grid ( self ) end subroutine set_line_widths !> Widths of the grid lines and of the equator and prime meridian (window !> units). pure subroutine line_widths ( self , width , main_width ) class ( LatLonGrid ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: width , main_width !! window units width = self % width_ main_width = self % main_width end subroutine line_widths !> The lines' color. subroutine grid_set_color ( self , color ) class ( LatLonGrid ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call self % ReferenceFrame % set_color ( color ) call make_grid ( self ) end subroutine grid_set_color !> What kind of frame this is: 'LatLonGrid'. function grid_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( LatLonGrid ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'LatLonGrid' end function grid_frame_info !> The bounding sphere: the origin, radius the largest semi-axis. subroutine grid_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( LatLonGrid ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius !! the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) center = 0.0_wp radius = maxval ( self % radii_ ) end subroutine grid_bound !> Draw the grid under `group` (the contents); with a window's `viewer`, later !> drawings are compiled. subroutine grid_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( LatLonGrid ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the frame's contents group self % nodes % contents = group call make_grid ( self ) self % nodes % shown = c_associated ( viewer ) end subroutine grid_build_contents !> The point at geodetic latitude lat and longitude lon on the ellipsoid !> (OpenFrames' LatLonGrid formula: the surface point whose normal has !> those angles). pure function surface_point ( r , lat , lon ) result ( p ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: r ( 3 ) !! semi-axes (scene units) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: lat , lon !! radians real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ), n ( 3 ), r2 ( 3 ) n = [ cos ( lat ) * cos ( lon ), cos ( lat ) * sin ( lon ), sin ( lat )] r2 = r ** 2 p = r2 * n / sqrt ( dot_product ( r2 , n ** 2 )) end function surface_point !> Make the grid's lines (circles in 1 degree steps, meridians in 0.5 degree !> steps), in place of the old. subroutine make_grid ( self ) type ( LatLonGrid ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , parameter :: n_around = 360 , n_meridian = 360 ! 1 and 0.5 degree steps real ( wp ), allocatable :: grid (:,:), main (:,:) real ( wp ) :: circle ( 3 , n_around ), meridian ( 3 , n_meridian + 1 ), lat , lon type ( c_ptr ) :: group integer :: i , k , sgn if (. not . c_associated ( self % nodes % contents )) return allocate ( grid ( 3 , 0 ), main ( 3 , 0 )) if ( self % lat_spacing > 0.0_wp ) then ! the equator, then pairs north and south k = 0 do while ( k * self % lat_spacing < 0.5_wp * pi - 1.0e-6_wp ) do sgn = 1 , merge ( 1 , 2 , k == 0 ) lat = merge ( 1.0_wp , - 1.0_wp , sgn == 1 ) * k * self % lat_spacing do i = 1 , n_around circle (:, i ) = surface_point ( self % radii_ , lat , 2.0_wp * pi * ( i - 1 ) / n_around ) end do if ( k == 0 ) then call append ( main , closed_segments ( circle )) else call append ( grid , closed_segments ( circle )) end if end do k = k + 1 end do end if if ( self % lon_spacing > 0.0_wp ) then ! the prime meridian, then the others k = 0 do while ( k * self % lon_spacing < 2.0_wp * pi - 1.0e-6_wp ) lon = k * self % lon_spacing do i = 1 , n_meridian + 1 meridian (:, i ) = surface_point ( self % radii_ , - 0.5_wp * pi + pi * ( i - 1 ) / n_meridian , lon ) end do if ( k == 0 ) then call append ( main , open_segments ( meridian )) else call append ( grid , open_segments ( meridian )) end if k = k + 1 end do end if group = vkf_switch_create () call add ( group , line_node ( grid , self % color (), self % width_ , . true .)) call add ( group , line_node ( main , self % color (), self % main_width , . true .)) call self % nodes % replace ( group ) end subroutine make_grid ! ================================================================== ! RadialPlane !> A radial plane named `name` (decorations of color `color`): radius 1, !> circles every 0.5, radial lines every 30 degrees, light gray and !> transparent (OpenFrames' defaults). function new_radial_plane ( name , color ) result ( p ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) type ( RadialPlane ) :: p p % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) call place_axes ( p , p % radius_ ) end function new_radial_plane !> The plane's radius (> 0), circle spacing and radial line spacing !> (radians; 0 for none), as OpenFrames' setParameters. subroutine plane_set_parameters ( self , radius , radial_spacing , lon_spacing ) class ( RadialPlane ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radius !! scene units (<= 0: unchanged) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radial_spacing !! scene units (< 0: unchanged) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: lon_spacing !! radians (< 0: unchanged) if ( radius > 0.0_wp ) self % radius_ = radius if ( radial_spacing >= 0.0_wp ) self % radial_spacing = radial_spacing if ( lon_spacing >= 0.0_wp ) self % lon_spacing = lon_spacing call place_axes ( self , self % radius_ ) call make_plane ( self ) end subroutine plane_set_parameters !> The plane's radius, circle spacing and radial line spacing, as OpenFrames' !> getParameters. pure subroutine plane_parameters ( self , radius , radial_spacing , lon_spacing ) class ( RadialPlane ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: radius , radial_spacing !! scene units real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: lon_spacing !! radians radius = self % radius_ radial_spacing = self % radial_spacing lon_spacing = self % lon_spacing end subroutine plane_parameters !> The plane's color ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]; default 0.8 gray, 0.2 opaque). subroutine set_plane_color ( self , color ) class ( RadialPlane ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call set_rgba ( self % plane_color_ , color ) call make_plane ( self ) end subroutine set_plane_color !> The plane's color [r, g, b, a]. pure function plane_color ( self ) result ( c ) class ( RadialPlane ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = self % plane_color_ end function plane_color !> The lines' color (default white, 0.2 opaque). subroutine plane_set_line_color ( self , color ) class ( RadialPlane ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call set_rgba ( self % line_color_ , color ) call make_plane ( self ) end subroutine plane_set_line_color !> The lines' color [r, g, b, a]. pure function plane_line_color ( self ) result ( c ) class ( RadialPlane ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = self % line_color_ end function plane_line_color !> What kind of frame this is: 'RadialPlane'. function plane_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( RadialPlane ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'RadialPlane' end function plane_frame_info !> The bounding sphere: the origin, radius the plane's radius. subroutine plane_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( RadialPlane ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius !! the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) center = 0.0_wp radius = self % radius_ end subroutine plane_bound !> Draw the plane under `group` (the contents); with a window's `viewer`, later !> drawings are compiled. subroutine plane_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( RadialPlane ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the frame's contents group self % nodes % contents = group call make_plane ( self ) self % nodes % shown = c_associated ( viewer ) end subroutine plane_build_contents !> Make the disk, its circles and its radial lines (1 degree steps), in place of !> the old. subroutine make_plane ( self ) type ( RadialPlane ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , parameter :: n = 360 ! points around a circle (1 degree) real ( wp ) :: disk ( 3 , n + 1 ), circle ( 3 , n ), a , r integer :: idx ( 3 , n ), i , k real ( wp ), allocatable :: lines (:,:), main (:,:) type ( c_ptr ) :: group if (. not . c_associated ( self % nodes % contents )) return ! the disk: a fan around the center disk (:, n + 1 ) = 0.0_wp do i = 1 , n a = 2.0_wp * pi * ( i - 1 ) / n disk (:, i ) = self % radius_ * [ cos ( a ), sin ( a ), 0.0_wp ] idx (:, i ) = [ n + 1 , i , modulo ( i , n ) + 1 ] end do allocate ( lines ( 3 , 0 ), main ( 3 , 0 )) ! circles: the edge, and every radial_spacing from the center if ( self % radial_spacing > 0.0_wp ) then call append ( lines , closed_segments ( disk (:, 1 : n ))) k = 1 do while ( k * self % radial_spacing < self % radius_ * ( 1.0_wp - 1.0e-6_wp )) r = k * self % radial_spacing circle = r / self % radius_ * disk (:, 1 : n ) call append ( lines , closed_segments ( circle )) k = k + 1 end do end if ! radial lines: along +x (thicker), then every lon_spacing if ( self % lon_spacing > 0.0_wp ) then k = 0 do while ( k * self % lon_spacing < 2.0_wp * pi - 1.0e-6_wp ) a = k * self % lon_spacing if ( k == 0 ) then call append ( main , reshape ([ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , self % radius_ * [ cos ( a ), sin ( a ), 0.0_wp ]], [ 3 , 2 ])) else call append ( lines , reshape ([ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , self % radius_ * [ cos ( a ), sin ( a ), 0.0_wp ]], [ 3 , 2 ])) end if k = k + 1 end do end if group = vkf_switch_create () call add ( group , surface_node ( disk , idx , self % plane_color_ )) call add ( group , line_node ( lines , self % line_color_ , 1.0_wp , . true .)) call add ( group , line_node ( main , self % line_color_ , 3.0_wp , . true .)) call self % nodes % replace ( group ) end subroutine make_plane ! ================================================================== ! PolyhedralCone !> A polyhedral cone named `name`, of color `color` (its sides and lines): !> 3 vertices at clock angles 0, 120 and 240 degrees, cone angles 45 !> degrees, 1 long (OpenFrames' defaults). function new_polyhedral_cone ( name , color ) result ( c ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) type ( PolyhedralCone ) :: c c % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) c % cone_color_ = c % color () c % line_color_ = c % color () c % clock = [ 0.0_wp , 12 0.0_wp , 24 0.0_wp ] * pi / 18 0.0_wp c % cone = [ 4 5.0_wp , 4 5.0_wp , 4 5.0_wp ] * pi / 18 0.0_wp end function new_polyhedral_cone !> The vertices: clock angles (from +x toward +y) and cone angles (from the !> boresight, -z; below 90 degrees), radians, the same number of each (>= 3). subroutine set_vertex_angles ( self , clock , cone ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: clock (:), cone (:) !! radians if ( size ( clock ) /= size ( cone ) . or . size ( clock ) < 3 ) return self % clock = clock self % cone = cone call make_cone ( self ) end subroutine set_vertex_angles !> The vertices' clock angles (radians). pure function clock_angles ( self ) result ( a ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), allocatable :: a (:) a = self % clock end function clock_angles !> The vertices' cone angles (radians). pure function cone_angles ( self ) result ( a ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), allocatable :: a (:) a = self % cone end function cone_angles !> The cone's length along the boresight (> 0; default 1). subroutine set_cone_length ( self , length ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: length !! scene units (<= 0: ignored) if ( length <= 0.0_wp ) return self % length_ = length call make_cone ( self ) end subroutine set_cone_length !> The cone's length along the boresight (scene units). pure real ( wp ) function cone_length ( self ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( in ) :: self cone_length = self % length_ end function cone_length !> The sides' color ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]; their alpha makes them !> transparent). subroutine set_cone_color ( self , color ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call set_rgba ( self % cone_color_ , color ) call make_cone ( self ) end subroutine set_cone_color !> The sides' color [r, g, b, a]. pure function cone_color ( self ) result ( c ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = self % cone_color_ end function cone_color !> The edges' and base outline's color. subroutine cone_set_line_color ( self , color ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call set_rgba ( self % line_color_ , color ) call make_cone ( self ) end subroutine cone_set_line_color !> The edges' and base outline's color [r, g, b, a]. pure function cone_line_color ( self ) result ( c ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = self % line_color_ end function cone_line_color !> What to draw: an ior of CONE_SIDES, CONE_EDGES, CONE_BASE_OUTLINE. subroutine set_draw_mode ( self , mode ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: mode self % mode = mode call make_cone ( self ) end subroutine set_draw_mode !> What is drawn: an ior of CONE_SIDES, CONE_EDGES, CONE_BASE_OUTLINE. pure integer function draw_mode ( self ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( in ) :: self draw_mode = self % mode end function draw_mode !> Place the cone's apex at `apex` (in the parent frame) with its boresight !> along `dir` and its +y axis toward `up` (OpenFrames' makeConeLookAt). subroutine make_cone_look_at ( self , apex , dir , up ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: apex ( 3 ) !! parent frame coordinates (scene units) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dir ( 3 ) !! boresight direction (any length > 0) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: up ( 3 ) !! toward the cone's +y axis (any length) real ( wp ) :: f ( 3 ), s ( 3 ), u ( 3 ), m ( 3 , 3 ) if ( norm2 ( dir ) <= 0.0_wp ) return f = dir / norm2 ( dir ) s = cross ( f , up ) if ( norm2 ( s ) <= 1.0e-12_wp ) s = cross ( f , [ 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp ]) if ( norm2 ( s ) <= 1.0e-12_wp ) s = cross ( f , [ 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp ]) s = s / norm2 ( s ) u = cross ( s , f ) m (:, 1 ) = s ! the cone's axes in the parent frame m (:, 2 ) = u m (:, 3 ) = - f call self % set_position ( apex ) call self % set_attitude ( quat_from_matrix ( m )) end subroutine make_cone_look_at !> Whether `point` (in the cone's frame) is inside the cone, between !> distances `min_distance` and `max_distance` along the boresight !> (defaults 0 and unlimited): inside the polygon of the vertices' directions !> (OpenFrames' isVisible; its PolyhedralCone always answers false). logical function cone_is_visible ( self , point , min_distance , max_distance ) result ( visible ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: point ( 3 ) !! in the cone's frame (scene units) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: min_distance , max_distance !! along the boresight (scene units) real ( wp ) :: q ( 2 ), a ( 2 ), b ( 2 ) integer :: i , n , winding visible = in_range ( point , min_distance , max_distance ) if (. not . visible . or . norm2 ( point ) == 0.0_wp ) return q = point ( 1 : 2 ) / ( - point ( 3 )) ! on the plane z = -1 n = size ( self % clock ) winding = 0 ! winding number of the polygon around q do i = 1 , n a = tan ( self % cone ( i )) * [ cos ( self % clock ( i )), sin ( self % clock ( i ))] b = tan ( self % cone ( modulo ( i , n ) + 1 )) * [ cos ( self % clock ( modulo ( i , n ) + 1 )), sin ( self % clock ( modulo ( i , n ) + 1 ))] if ( a ( 2 ) <= q ( 2 )) then if ( b ( 2 ) > q ( 2 ) . and . side ( a , b , q ) > 0.0_wp ) winding = winding + 1 else if ( b ( 2 ) <= q ( 2 ) . and . side ( a , b , q ) < 0.0_wp ) winding = winding - 1 end if end do visible = winding /= 0 end function cone_is_visible !> Along the boresight (-z) between the distances (a point ahead of the apex). pure logical function in_range ( point , min_distance , max_distance ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: point ( 3 ) !! in the cone's frame (scene units) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: min_distance , max_distance !! along the boresight (scene units) real ( wp ) :: d d = - point ( 3 ) in_range = d >= 0.0_wp if ( present ( min_distance )) in_range = in_range . and . d >= min_distance if ( present ( max_distance )) in_range = in_range . and . d <= max_distance end function in_range !> Which side of the line from a to b q is on: > 0 left, < 0 right, 0 on it !> (twice the signed area of the triangle a, b, q). pure real ( wp ) function side ( a , b , q ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: a ( 2 ), b ( 2 ), q ( 2 ) side = ( b ( 1 ) - a ( 1 )) * ( q ( 2 ) - a ( 2 )) - ( q ( 1 ) - a ( 1 )) * ( b ( 2 ) - a ( 2 )) end function side !> What kind of frame this is: 'PolyhedralCone'. function cone_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'PolyhedralCone' end function cone_frame_info !> The bound of the apex and the base. subroutine cone_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius !! the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) real ( wp ) :: r r = self % length_ * maxval ( tan ( self % cone )) center = [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , - 0.5_wp * self % length_ ] radius = sqrt (( 0.5_wp * self % length_ ) ** 2 + r ** 2 ) end subroutine cone_bound !> Draw the cone under `group` (the contents); with a window's `viewer`, later !> drawings are compiled. subroutine cone_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the frame's contents group self % nodes % contents = group call make_cone ( self ) self % nodes % shown = c_associated ( viewer ) end subroutine cone_build_contents !> Make the sides, edges and base outline (those the draw mode says), in place !> of the old. subroutine make_cone ( self ) class ( PolyhedralCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), allocatable :: v (:,:), edges (:,:) integer , allocatable :: idx (:,:) type ( c_ptr ) :: group integer :: i , n if (. not . c_associated ( self % nodes % contents )) return n = size ( self % clock ) allocate ( v ( 3 , n + 1 ), idx ( 3 , n ), edges ( 3 , 2 * n )) v (:, n + 1 ) = 0.0_wp ! the apex do i = 1 , n v (:, i ) = self % length_ * [ tan ( self % cone ( i )) * cos ( self % clock ( i )), tan ( self % cone ( i )) * sin ( self % clock ( i )), - 1.0_wp ] idx (:, i ) = [ n + 1 , i , modulo ( i , n ) + 1 ] edges (:, 2 * i - 1 ) = 0.0_wp edges (:, 2 * i ) = v (:, i ) end do group = vkf_switch_create () if ( iand ( self % mode , CONE_SIDES ) /= 0 ) call add ( group , surface_node ( v , idx , self % cone_color_ )) if ( iand ( self % mode , CONE_EDGES ) /= 0 ) call add ( group , line_node ( edges , self % line_color_ , self % width_ , . true .)) if ( iand ( self % mode , CONE_BASE_OUTLINE ) /= 0 ) & call add ( group , line_node ( closed_segments ( v (:, 1 : n )), self % line_color_ , self % width_ , . true .)) call self % nodes % replace ( group ) end subroutine make_cone ! ================================================================== ! EllipticCone and RectangularCone !> An elliptic cone named `name`, of color `color` (sides and base outline drawn). function new_elliptic_cone ( name , color ) result ( c ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) type ( EllipticCone ) :: c c % PolyhedralCone = PolyhedralCone ( name , color ) c % mode = ior ( CONE_SIDES , CONE_BASE_OUTLINE ) call elliptic_vertices ( c ) end function new_elliptic_cone !> The half-angles along x (a) and y (b), radians (0 to 90 degrees). subroutine elliptic_set_primary_angles ( self , a , b ) class ( EllipticCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: a , b !! radians self % a = a self % b = b call elliptic_vertices ( self ) call make_cone ( self ) end subroutine elliptic_set_primary_angles !> The half-angles along x (a) and y (b), radians. pure subroutine elliptic_primary_angles ( self , a , b ) class ( EllipticCone ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: a , b !! radians a = self % a b = self % b end subroutine elliptic_primary_angles !> 120 vertices (every 3 degrees), cone angle a b / sqrt(b&#94;2 cos&#94;2 + a&#94;2 sin&#94;2) !> (OpenFrames' createEllipticCone). subroutine elliptic_vertices ( self ) type ( EllipticCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , parameter :: n = 120 integer :: i real ( wp ) :: t if ( allocated ( self % clock )) deallocate ( self % clock , self % cone ) allocate ( self % clock ( n ), self % cone ( n )) do i = 1 , n t = 2.0_wp * pi * ( i - 1 ) / n self % clock ( i ) = t self % cone ( i ) = self % a * self % b / sqrt ( self % b ** 2 * cos ( t ) ** 2 + self % a ** 2 * sin ( t ) ** 2 ) end do end subroutine elliptic_vertices !> Inside the elliptic cone (exactly; OpenFrames' EllipticCone::isVisible). logical function elliptic_is_visible ( self , point , min_distance , max_distance ) result ( visible ) class ( EllipticCone ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: point ( 3 ) !! in the cone's frame (scene units) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: min_distance , max_distance !! along the boresight (scene units) real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ), cone , clock visible = in_range ( point , min_distance , max_distance ) if (. not . visible . or . norm2 ( point ) == 0.0_wp ) return p = point / ( - point ( 3 )) cone = atan ( norm2 ( p ( 1 : 2 ))) clock = atan2 ( p ( 2 ), p ( 1 )) visible = cone <= self % a * self % b / sqrt ( self % b ** 2 * cos ( clock ) ** 2 + self % a ** 2 * sin ( clock ) ** 2 ) end function elliptic_is_visible !> What kind of frame this is: 'EllipticCone'. function elliptic_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( EllipticCone ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'EllipticCone' end function elliptic_frame_info !> A rectangular cone named `name`, of color `color`. function new_rectangular_cone ( name , color ) result ( c ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) type ( RectangularCone ) :: c c % PolyhedralCone = PolyhedralCone ( name , color ) call rect_vertices ( c ) end function new_rectangular_cone !> The half-angles along x and y, radians (0 to 90 degrees). subroutine rect_set_primary_angles ( self , x , y ) class ( RectangularCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x , y !! radians self % x = x self % y = y call rect_vertices ( self ) call make_cone ( self ) end subroutine rect_set_primary_angles !> The half-angles along x and y, radians. pure subroutine rect_primary_angles ( self , x , y ) class ( RectangularCone ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: x , y !! radians x = self % x y = self % y end subroutine rect_primary_angles !> The 4 corners (OpenFrames' createRectangularCone). subroutine rect_vertices ( self ) type ( RectangularCone ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ) :: xl , yl , cone , clock xl = tan ( self % x ) yl = tan ( self % y ) cone = atan ( sqrt ( xl ** 2 + yl ** 2 )) clock = atan2 ( yl , xl ) self % clock = [ clock , pi - clock , pi + clock , - clock ] self % cone = [ cone , cone , cone , cone ] end subroutine rect_vertices !> What kind of frame this is: 'RectangularCone'. function rect_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( RectangularCone ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'RectangularCone' end function rect_frame_info ! ================================================================== ! Polyhedron !> A polyhedron named `name`, of color `color` (its faces, edges and !> vertices), with no faces yet (set_faces, set_triangles or set_grid). function new_polyhedron ( name , color ) result ( p ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) type ( Polyhedron ) :: p p % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) p % face_color_ = p % color () p % line_color_ = p % color () p % point_color_ = p % color () allocate ( p % v ( 3 , 0 ), p % tri ( 3 , 0 ), p % edge ( 2 , 0 )) end function new_polyhedron !> Faces given as polygons: `faces` the vertex numbers (1-based) of each !> polygon in turn, `sizes` how many each has (>= 3; convex, or at least !> star-shaped from its first vertex: drawn as a fan of triangles from !> it); the edges are the polygons' sides. E.g. a cube: 8 vertices, 6 !> faces of 4. A face's front: its vertices counterclockwise. subroutine set_faces ( self , vertices , faces , sizes ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: vertices (:,:) !! (3, n), frame coordinates integer , intent ( in ) :: faces (:) !! (sum(sizes)) vertex numbers integer , intent ( in ) :: sizes (:) !! each face's number of vertices integer :: f , k , j , nt , ne , first integer , allocatable :: sides (:,:) self % v = vertices nt = sum ( max ( sizes - 2 , 0 )) if ( allocated ( self % tri )) deallocate ( self % tri ) allocate ( self % tri ( 3 , nt ), sides ( 2 , sum ( sizes ))) nt = 0 ne = 0 first = 0 do f = 1 , size ( sizes ) do k = 2 , sizes ( f ) - 1 ! a fan from the first vertex nt = nt + 1 self % tri (:, nt ) = [ faces ( first + 1 ), faces ( first + k ), faces ( first + k + 1 )] end do do k = 1 , sizes ( f ) j = modulo ( k , sizes ( f )) + 1 ne = ne + 1 sides (:, ne ) = [ faces ( first + k ), faces ( first + j )] end do first = first + sizes ( f ) end do self % edge = unique_edges ( sides (:, 1 : ne ), size ( vertices , 2 )) call drop_colors ( self ) call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_faces !> Faces given as triangles (3, m) of vertex numbers (1-based); the edges !> are their sides (each once). subroutine set_triangles ( self , vertices , triangles ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: vertices (:,:) !! (3, n), frame coordinates integer , intent ( in ) :: triangles (:,:) !! (3, m) self % v = vertices self % tri = triangles self % edge = unique_edges ( reshape ([ triangles ( 1 : 2 , :), triangles ( 2 : 3 , :), triangles ( 3 : 1 : - 2 , :)], & [ 2 , 3 * size ( triangles , 2 )]), size ( vertices , 2 )) call drop_colors ( self ) call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_triangles !> Faces given as a grid of points (3, nu, nv): quadrilaterals between !> neighbours (two triangles each), joined around if `closed_u` (the last !> point i to the first, for each j; e.g. a tube's circumference) or !> `closed_v`. The edges: the grid's lines, those of constant i (along j) !> every lines(1) and of constant j (along i) every lines(2) (default: !> every one; 0 for none). subroutine set_grid ( self , points , closed_u , closed_v , lines ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: points (:,:,:) !! (3, nu, nv), frame coordinates logical , intent ( in ), optional :: closed_u , closed_v integer , intent ( in ), optional :: lines ( 2 ) integer :: nu , nv , mu , mv , i , j , i2 , j2 , nt , ne , every ( 2 ) logical :: cu , cv nu = size ( points , 2 ) nv = size ( points , 3 ) cu = . false . cv = . false . if ( present ( closed_u )) cu = closed_u . and . nu > 2 if ( present ( closed_v )) cv = closed_v . and . nv > 2 every = 1 if ( present ( lines )) every = max ( lines , 0 ) self % v = reshape ( points , [ 3 , nu * nv ]) mu = merge ( nu , nu - 1 , cu ) ! quadrilaterals along i, j mv = merge ( nv , nv - 1 , cv ) if ( allocated ( self % tri )) deallocate ( self % tri ) allocate ( self % tri ( 3 , 2 * max ( mu , 0 ) * max ( mv , 0 ))) nt = 0 do j = 1 , mv j2 = modulo ( j , nv ) + 1 do i = 1 , mu i2 = modulo ( i , nu ) + 1 self % tri (:, nt + 1 ) = [ at ( i , j ), at ( i2 , j ), at ( i2 , j2 )] self % tri (:, nt + 2 ) = [ at ( i , j ), at ( i2 , j2 ), at ( i , j2 )] nt = nt + 2 end do end do if ( allocated ( self % edge )) deallocate ( self % edge ) allocate ( self % edge ( 2 , nu * nv * 2 )) ne = 0 if ( every ( 1 ) > 0 ) then ! lines of constant i, along j do i = 1 , nu if (. not . shown_line ( i , nu , every ( 1 ), cu )) cycle do j = 1 , mv ne = ne + 1 self % edge (:, ne ) = [ at ( i , j ), at ( i , modulo ( j , nv ) + 1 )] end do end do end if if ( every ( 2 ) > 0 ) then ! lines of constant j, along i do j = 1 , nv if (. not . shown_line ( j , nv , every ( 2 ), cv )) cycle do i = 1 , mu ne = ne + 1 self % edge (:, ne ) = [ at ( i , j ), at ( modulo ( i , nu ) + 1 , j )] end do end do end if self % edge = self % edge (:, 1 : ne ) call drop_colors ( self ) call make_polyhedron ( self ) contains pure integer function at ( i_ , j_ ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i_ , j_ at = i_ + ( j_ - 1 ) * nu end function at !> Line k of n drawn, every `step` (and the last, if the grid is open). pure logical function shown_line ( k , n , step , closed ) integer , intent ( in ) :: k , n , step logical , intent ( in ) :: closed shown_line = modulo ( k - 1 , step ) == 0 . or . ( k == n . and . . not . closed ) end function shown_line end subroutine set_grid !> The edges drawn (2, k) (vertex numbers), in place of the faces' (after !> set_faces, set_triangles or set_grid). subroutine set_edges ( self , edges ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: edges (:,:) self % edge = edges call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_edges !> Move the vertices (3, n), keeping the faces and edges (as many as !> before; e.g. a surface changing in time). subroutine set_vertices ( self , vertices ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: vertices (:,:) if ( size ( vertices , 2 ) /= size ( self % v , 2 )) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Polyhedron ' // self % name () // ': set_vertices needs as many vertices as before' return end if self % v = vertices call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_vertices !> The number of vertices. pure integer function num_vertices ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self num_vertices = size ( self % v , 2 ) end function num_vertices !> The number of triangles drawn (polygons: as fans). pure integer function num_triangles ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self num_triangles = size ( self % tri , 2 ) end function num_triangles !> The number of edges. pure integer function num_edges ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self num_edges = size ( self % edge , 2 ) end function num_edges !> A color per vertex (4, n) or (3, n) ([r, g, b(, a)], 0 to 1), for the !> faces, blended across them (in place of the face color; the opacity !> still applies). Dropped when the faces are set again. subroutine set_vertex_colors ( self , colors ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: colors (:,:) integer :: i if ( size ( colors , 2 ) /= size ( self % v , 2 ) . or . size ( colors , 1 ) < 3 ) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Polyhedron ' // self % name () // ': set_vertex_colors needs a color per vertex' return end if if ( allocated ( self % vertex_colors_ )) deallocate ( self % vertex_colors_ ) allocate ( self % vertex_colors_ ( 4 , size ( colors , 2 ))) do i = 1 , size ( colors , 2 ) call set_rgba ( self % vertex_colors_ (:, i ), colors (:, i )) end do call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_vertex_colors !> The face color again, for every vertex. subroutine remove_vertex_colors ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self call drop_colors ( self ) call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine remove_vertex_colors !> Whether the faces have a color per vertex. pure logical function has_vertex_colors ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self has_vertex_colors = allocated ( self % vertex_colors_ ) end function has_vertex_colors !> The faces' color (the alpha times the opacity). subroutine set_face_color ( self , color ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call set_rgba ( self % face_color_ , color ) call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_face_color !> The faces' color [r, g, b, a]. pure function face_color ( self ) result ( c ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = self % face_color_ end function face_color !> The edges' color. subroutine poly_set_line_color ( self , color ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call set_rgba ( self % line_color_ , color ) call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine poly_set_line_color !> The edges' color [r, g, b, a]. pure function poly_line_color ( self ) result ( c ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = self % line_color_ end function poly_line_color !> The vertices' color (POLY_VERTICES). subroutine set_point_color ( self , color ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call set_rgba ( self % point_color_ , color ) call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_point_color !> The vertices' color [r, g, b, a]. pure function point_color ( self ) result ( c ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = self % point_color_ end function point_color !> The faces' opacity (0 to 1; default 1, opaque): below 1 translucent. subroutine poly_set_opacity ( self , opacity ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: opacity self % opacity_ = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , opacity )) call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine poly_set_opacity !> The faces' opacity. pure real ( wp ) function poly_opacity ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self poly_opacity = self % opacity_ end function poly_opacity !> The edges' width (window units; default 1). subroutine poly_set_line_width ( self , width ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: width self % width_ = max ( 0.0_wp , width ) call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine poly_set_line_width !> The edges' width (window units). pure real ( wp ) function poly_line_width ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self poly_line_width = self % width_ end function poly_line_width !> The vertices' size (window units; default 6). subroutine set_point_size ( self , size_ ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: size_ self % point_size_ = max ( 0.0_wp , size_ ) call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_point_size !> The vertices' size (window units). pure real ( wp ) function point_size ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self point_size = self % point_size_ end function point_size !> What to draw: an ior of POLY_FACES, POLY_EDGES, POLY_VERTICES (default !> faces and edges). subroutine poly_set_draw_mode ( self , mode ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: mode self % mode = mode call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine poly_set_draw_mode !> What is drawn: an ior of POLY_FACES, POLY_EDGES, POLY_VERTICES. pure integer function poly_draw_mode ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self poly_draw_mode = self % mode end function poly_draw_mode !> Faces lit by the scene's lights (the default), or unlit (their color !> as is, transparent as a cone's sides: writing no depth). subroutine set_lit ( self , lit ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: lit self % lit_ = lit call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_lit !> Whether the faces are lit. pure logical function lit ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self lit = self % lit_ end function lit !> Shading smooth across the vertices (normals averaged over the faces !> around each: a curved surface, e.g. a grid's), or flat faces (the !> default: a polyhedron's). subroutine set_smooth ( self , smooth ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: smooth self % smooth_ = smooth call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_smooth !> Whether the shading is smooth. pure logical function smooth ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self smooth = self % smooth_ end function smooth !> Both sides of the faces drawn and lit (the default: open surfaces), or !> only their fronts (a closed surface, its faces counterclockwise seen !> from outside: translucent, its far side isn't drawn through it). subroutine set_two_sided ( self , two_sided ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: two_sided self % two_sided_ = two_sided call make_polyhedron ( self ) end subroutine set_two_sided !> Whether both sides are drawn. pure logical function two_sided ( self ) class ( Polyhedron ), intent ( in ) :: self two_sided = self % two_sided_ end function two_sided","tags":"","url":"proc/two_sided.html"},{"title":"unique_edges – vkframes","text":"private  function unique_edges(pairs, n) result(edges) Edges (2, k) of vertex numbers (1 to n), each once whichever its\ndirection (sorted by their smaller vertex, then the larger). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: pairs (:,:) integer, intent(in) :: n the number of vertices Return Value integer, allocatable, (:,:) Calls proc~~unique_edges~~CallsGraph proc~unique_edges unique_edges proc~sort_keys sort_keys proc~unique_edges->proc~sort_keys Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~unique_edges~~CalledByGraph proc~unique_edges unique_edges proc~set_faces Polyhedron%set_faces proc~set_faces->proc~unique_edges proc~set_triangles Polyhedron%set_triangles proc~set_triangles->proc~unique_edges Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function unique_edges ( pairs , n ) result ( edges ) integer , intent ( in ) :: pairs (:,:) integer , intent ( in ) :: n !! the number of vertices integer , allocatable :: edges (:,:) integer ( int64 ), allocatable :: keys (:) integer :: k , m allocate ( keys ( size ( pairs , 2 ))) keys = int ( min ( pairs ( 1 , :), pairs ( 2 , :)), int64 ) * ( int ( n , int64 ) + 1 ) + int ( max ( pairs ( 1 , :), pairs ( 2 , :)), int64 ) call sort_keys ( keys ) allocate ( edges ( 2 , size ( keys ))) m = 0 do k = 1 , size ( keys ) if ( k > 1 ) then if ( keys ( k ) == keys ( k - 1 )) cycle end if m = m + 1 edges (:, m ) = [ int ( keys ( k ) / ( int ( n , int64 ) + 1 )), int ( modulo ( keys ( k ), int ( n , int64 ) + 1 ))] end do edges = edges (:, 1 : m ) end function unique_edges","tags":"","url":"proc/unique_edges.html"},{"title":"unit_normal – vkframes","text":"private pure function unit_normal(a, b, c) result(n) A triangle's unit normal (counterclockwise: its front), or +z if it has\nno area. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: a (3) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: b (3) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: c (3) Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) Calls proc~~unit_normal~~CallsGraph proc~unit_normal unit_normal proc~cross cross proc~unit_normal->proc~cross Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~unit_normal~~CalledByGraph proc~unit_normal unit_normal proc~make_polyhedron make_polyhedron proc~make_polyhedron->proc~unit_normal proc~poly_build_contents Polyhedron%poly_build_contents proc~poly_build_contents->proc~make_polyhedron proc~poly_set_draw_mode Polyhedron%poly_set_draw_mode proc~poly_set_draw_mode->proc~make_polyhedron proc~poly_set_line_color Polyhedron%poly_set_line_color proc~poly_set_line_color->proc~make_polyhedron proc~poly_set_line_width Polyhedron%poly_set_line_width proc~poly_set_line_width->proc~make_polyhedron proc~poly_set_opacity Polyhedron%poly_set_opacity proc~poly_set_opacity->proc