":"proc/region_index.html"},{"title":"regions – vkframes","text":"private pure function regions(self) The regions drawn: an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA and\nSHADOW_ANTUMBRA. Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer Source Code pure integer function regions ( self ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self regions = self % regions_ end function regions","tags":"","url":"proc/regions.html"},{"title":"shadow_frame_info – vkframes","text":"private  function shadow_frame_info(self) result(info) What kind of frame this is: 'ShadowCones'. Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(in) :: self Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Source Code function shadow_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'ShadowCones' end function shadow_frame_info","tags":"","url":"proc/shadow_frame_info.html"},{"title":"umbra_length – vkframes","text":"private pure function umbra_length(self) The distance from the body's center to the umbra's apex at the last\nupdate (huge() for a body no smaller than its light; 0 before). Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) Source Code pure real ( wp ) function umbra_length ( self ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: r , rs , d r = self % shaped ( 1 ) rs = self % shaped ( 2 ) d = self % shaped ( 3 ) umbra_length = 0.0_wp if ( d <= 0.0_wp ) return if ( rs > r ) then umbra_length = d * r / ( rs - r ) else umbra_length = huge ( 1.0_wp ) end if end function umbra_length","tags":"","url":"proc/umbra_length.html"},{"title":"apply_color – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine apply_color(g) A region's color, through its mesh's material (the unlit shader\nmultiplies the vertex color, white, by the diffuse color). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ShadowRegion ), intent(in) :: g Calls proc~~apply_color~~CallsGraph proc~apply_color apply_color proc~check_status check_status proc~apply_color->proc~check_status proc~mesh_set_material mesh_set_material proc~apply_color->proc~mesh_set_material interface~vkf_mesh_material vkf_mesh_material proc~mesh_set_material->interface~vkf_mesh_material interface~vkf_mesh_material_changed vkf_mesh_material_changed proc~mesh_set_material->interface~vkf_mesh_material_changed Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~apply_color~~CalledByGraph proc~apply_color apply_color proc~set_region_color ShadowCones%set_region_color proc~set_region_color->proc~apply_color proc~shadow_build_contents ShadowCones%shadow_build_contents proc~shadow_build_contents->proc~apply_color Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine apply_color ( g ) type ( ShadowRegion ), intent ( in ) :: g real ( c_float ) :: c ( 4 ) if (. not . c_associated ( g % mesh )) return c = real ( g % color , c_float ) call check_status ( mesh_set_material ( g % mesh , c , c , [ 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], & [ 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], 0.0_c_float ), 'shadow' ) end subroutine apply_color","tags":"","url":"proc/apply_color.html"},{"title":"place – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine place(self) Move the shadow to the body's center (in the parent's coordinates) with its\n+z axis away from the light, and reshape the cones if the radii, the\ndistance or the length set changed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self Calls proc~~place~~CallsGraph proc~place place proc~body_radius~2 ShadowCones%body_radius proc~place->proc~body_radius~2 proc~light_radius ShadowCones%light_radius proc~place->proc~light_radius proc~local_matrix ReferenceFrame%local_matrix proc~place->proc~local_matrix proc~quat_from_vectors quat_from_vectors proc~place->proc~quat_from_vectors proc~rigid_inverse rigid_inverse proc~place->proc~rigid_inverse proc~set_attitude~2 ReferenceFrame%set_attitude proc~place->proc~set_attitude~2 proc~set_position~2 ReferenceFrame%set_position proc~place->proc~set_position~2 proc~shape_regions shape_regions proc~place->proc~shape_regions proc~world_matrix ReferenceFrame%world_matrix proc~place->proc~world_matrix proc~frame_radius frame_radius proc~body_radius~2->proc~frame_radius proc~light_radius->proc~frame_radius proc~frame_matrix frame_matrix proc~local_matrix->proc~frame_matrix proc~cross cross proc~quat_from_vectors->proc~cross proc~quat_normalize quat_normalize proc~quat_from_vectors->proc~quat_normalize proc~set_attitude~2->proc~quat_normalize proc~write_region write_region proc~shape_regions->proc~write_region proc~world_matrix->proc~local_matrix proc~world_matrix->proc~world_matrix proc~quat_to_matrix quat_to_matrix proc~frame_matrix->proc~quat_to_matrix body_radius body_radius proc~frame_radius->body_radius radii radii proc~frame_radius->radii interface~vkf_mesh_vertices_changed vkf_mesh_vertices_changed proc~write_region->interface~vkf_mesh_vertices_changed interface~vkf_switch_set vkf_switch_set proc~write_region->interface~vkf_switch_set proc~check_status check_status proc~write_region->proc~check_status proc~mesh_arrays mesh_arrays proc~write_region->proc~mesh_arrays interface~vkf_mesh_array vkf_mesh_array proc~mesh_arrays->interface~vkf_mesh_array Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~place~~CalledByGraph proc~place place proc~shadow_late_update ShadowCones%shadow_late_update proc~shadow_late_update->proc~place Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine place ( self ) type ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ) :: to_parent ( 4 , 4 ), m ( 4 , 4 ), b ( 3 ), s ( 3 ), u ( 3 ), d , now ( 4 ) ! the body's and the light's centers in the parent's coordinates to_parent = rigid_inverse ( matmul ( self % world_matrix (), rigid_inverse ( self % local_matrix ()))) m = matmul ( to_parent , self % body_ % world_matrix ()) b = m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) m = matmul ( to_parent , self % light_ % world_matrix ()) s = m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) u = b - s d = norm2 ( u ) self % distance_ = d call self % set_position ( b ) if ( d > 0.0_wp ) call self % set_attitude ( quat_from_vectors ([ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp ], u / d )) now = [ self % body_radius (), self % light_radius (), d , self % length_ ] if ( all ( now == self % shaped )) return self % shaped = now call shape_regions ( self , now ( 1 ), now ( 2 ), d ) end subroutine place","tags":"","url":"proc/place.html"},{"title":"region_extent – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine region_extent(self, region, drawn, z0, r0, z1, r1) A region's surface at the last update, along the frame's +z axis (away\nfrom the light; the body's center at the origin): drawn, from z0\n(radius r0) to z1 (radius r1). Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: region SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA or SHADOW_ANTUMBRA logical, intent(out) :: drawn it has a surface and is drawn real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: z0 scene units real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: r0 scene units real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: z1 scene units real(kind=wp), intent(out), optional :: r1 scene units Calls proc~~region_extent~~CallsGraph proc~region_extent ShadowCones%region_extent proc~region_index region_index proc~region_extent->proc~region_index Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine region_extent ( self , region , drawn , z0 , r0 , z1 , r1 ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: region !! SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA or SHADOW_ANTUMBRA logical , intent ( out ) :: drawn !! it has a surface and is drawn real ( wp ), intent ( out ), optional :: z0 , r0 , z1 , r1 !! scene units type ( ShadowRegion ) :: g integer :: k k = region_index ( region ) if ( k > 0 ) g = self % region ( k ) drawn = k > 0 . and . g % drawn if ( present ( z0 )) z0 = g % z0 if ( present ( r0 )) r0 = g % r0 if ( present ( z1 )) z1 = g % z1 if ( present ( r1 )) r1 = g % r1 end subroutine region_extent","tags":"","url":"proc/region_extent.html"},{"title":"set_body – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_body(self, body, radius) The body casting the shadow (it must stay alive while set), and its\nradius (optional: see set_body_radius). Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), target :: body real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: radius scene units (see set_body_radius) Calls proc~~set_body~~CallsGraph proc~set_body ShadowCones%set_body proc~set_body_radius ShadowCones%set_body_radius proc~set_body->proc~set_body_radius Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_body ( self , body , radius ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: body real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: radius !! scene units (see set_body_radius) self % body_ => body if ( present ( radius )) call self % set_body_radius ( radius ) end subroutine set_body","tags":"","url":"proc/set_body.html"},{"title":"set_body_radius – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_body_radius(self, radius) The body's radius (scene units; 0: the body's own, a Sphere's\nequatorial radius or a TerrainBody's). Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: radius scene units (0: the body's own) Called by proc~~set_body_radius~~CalledByGraph proc~set_body_radius ShadowCones%set_body_radius proc~new_shadow_cones new_shadow_cones proc~new_shadow_cones->proc~set_body_radius proc~set_body ShadowCones%set_body proc~set_body->proc~set_body_radius interface~shadowcones ShadowCones interface~shadowcones->proc~new_shadow_cones Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_body_radius ( self , radius ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radius !! scene units (0: the body's own) self % body_radius_ = max ( 0.0_wp , radius ) end subroutine set_body_radius","tags":"","url":"proc/set_body_radius.html"},{"title":"set_length – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_length(self, length) How far behind the body's center the shadow is drawn (scene units; 0:\nautomatic, twice the umbra's length). Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: length scene units (0: automatic) Source Code subroutine set_length ( self , length ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: length !! scene units (0: automatic) self % length_ = max ( 0.0_wp , length ) end subroutine set_length","tags":"","url":"proc/set_length.html"},{"title":"set_light – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_light(self, light, radius) The light (e.g. the Sun; it must stay alive while set), and its radius\n(optional: see set_light_radius). Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), target :: light real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: radius scene units (see set_light_radius) Calls proc~~set_light~~CallsGraph proc~set_light ShadowCones%set_light proc~set_light_radius ShadowCones%set_light_radius proc~set_light->proc~set_light_radius Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_light ( self , light , radius ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: light real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: radius !! scene units (see set_light_radius) self % light_ => light if ( present ( radius )) call self % set_light_radius ( radius ) end subroutine set_light","tags":"","url":"proc/set_light.html"},{"title":"set_light_radius – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_light_radius(self, radius) The light's radius (scene units; 0: the light's own, if a Sphere). Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: radius scene units (0: the light's own) Called by proc~~set_light_radius~~CalledByGraph proc~set_light_radius ShadowCones%set_light_radius proc~new_shadow_cones new_shadow_cones proc~new_shadow_cones->proc~set_light_radius proc~set_light ShadowCones%set_light proc~set_light->proc~set_light_radius interface~shadowcones ShadowCones interface~shadowcones->proc~new_shadow_cones Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_light_radius ( self , radius ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radius !! scene units (0: the light's own) self % light_radius_ = max ( 0.0_wp , radius ) end subroutine set_light_radius","tags":"","url":"proc/set_light_radius.html"},{"title":"set_region_color – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_region_color(self, region, color) A region's color (region: one of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA,\nSHADOW_ANTUMBRA; [r, g, b], alpha unchanged, or [r, g, b, a]). Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: region SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA or SHADOW_ANTUMBRA real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: color (:) [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1 Calls proc~~set_region_color~~CallsGraph proc~set_region_color ShadowCones%set_region_color proc~apply_color apply_color proc~set_region_color->proc~apply_color proc~region_index region_index proc~set_region_color->proc~region_index proc~check_status check_status proc~apply_color->proc~check_status proc~mesh_set_material mesh_set_material proc~apply_color->proc~mesh_set_material interface~vkf_mesh_material vkf_mesh_material proc~mesh_set_material->interface~vkf_mesh_material interface~vkf_mesh_material_changed vkf_mesh_material_changed proc~mesh_set_material->interface~vkf_mesh_material_changed Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_region_color ( self , region , color ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: region !! SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA or SHADOW_ANTUMBRA real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1 integer :: k , n k = region_index ( region ) if ( k == 0 ) return n = min ( 4 , size ( color )) self % region ( k )% color ( 1 : n ) = color ( 1 : n ) call apply_color ( self % region ( k )) end subroutine set_region_color","tags":"","url":"proc/set_region_color.html"},{"title":"set_regions – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_regions(self, regions) The regions to draw: an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA and\nSHADOW_ANTUMBRA (default SHADOW_ALL). Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: regions an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA, SHADOW_ANTUMBRA Source Code subroutine set_regions ( self , regions ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: regions !! an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA, SHADOW_ANTUMBRA self % regions_ = iand ( regions , SHADOW_ALL ) self % shaped = - 1.0_wp ! (redrawn at the next update) end subroutine set_regions","tags":"","url":"proc/set_regions.html"},{"title":"shadow_bound – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine shadow_bound(self, center, radius) The drawn regions' bounding sphere (frame coordinates). Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: center (3) the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: radius the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) Source Code subroutine shadow_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius !! the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) real ( wp ) :: lo , hi , r integer :: k center = 0.0_wp radius = 0.0_wp lo = huge ( 1.0_wp ) hi = - huge ( 1.0_wp ) r = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , n_regions if (. not . self % region ( k )% drawn ) cycle lo = min ( lo , self % region ( k )% z0 ) hi = max ( hi , self % region ( k )% z1 ) r = max ( r , self % region ( k )% r0 , self % region ( k )% r1 ) end do if ( hi < lo ) return center ( 3 ) = 0.5_wp * ( lo + hi ) radius = hypot ( 0.5_wp * ( hi - lo ), r ) end subroutine shadow_bound","tags":"","url":"proc/shadow_bound.html"},{"title":"shadow_build_contents – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine shadow_build_contents(self, viewer, group) A switch with a mesh for each region (vertices written at each change\nof shape), under group . Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer a window's viewer (null: headless) type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: group the frame's contents group Calls proc~~shadow_build_contents~~CallsGraph proc~shadow_build_contents ShadowCones%shadow_build_contents interface~vkf_mesh_create vkf_mesh_create proc~shadow_build_contents->interface~vkf_mesh_create interface~vkf_node_add_child vkf_node_add_child proc~shadow_build_contents->interface~vkf_node_add_child interface~vkf_switch_create vkf_switch_create proc~shadow_build_contents->interface~vkf_switch_create interface~vkf_switch_set vkf_switch_set proc~shadow_build_contents->interface~vkf_switch_set proc~apply_color apply_color proc~shadow_build_contents->proc~apply_color proc~check_status check_status proc~shadow_build_contents->proc~check_status proc~mesh_arrays mesh_arrays proc~shadow_build_contents->proc~mesh_arrays proc~apply_color->proc~check_status proc~mesh_set_material mesh_set_material proc~apply_color->proc~mesh_set_material interface~vkf_mesh_array vkf_mesh_array proc~mesh_arrays->interface~vkf_mesh_array interface~vkf_mesh_material vkf_mesh_material proc~mesh_set_material->interface~vkf_mesh_material interface~vkf_mesh_material_changed vkf_mesh_material_changed proc~mesh_set_material->interface~vkf_mesh_material_changed Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine shadow_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the frame's contents group real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: v , normals , uv integer ( c_int32_t ), dimension (:), pointer :: indices integer :: k , i , j , n n = n_around do k = 1 , n_regions associate ( g => self % region ( k )) g % mesh = vkf_mesh_create ( int ( 2 * n , c_int ), int ( 6 * n , c_int ), [ 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , & 1.0_c_float ], c_null_ptr , c_null_ptr , 5_c_int ) ! unlit, transparent; vertices change if (. not . c_associated ( g % mesh )) cycle call mesh_arrays ( g % mesh , 2 * n , 6 * n , v , normals , uv , indices ) v = 0.0_c_float normals = 0.0_c_float normals ( 3 , :) = 1.0_c_float uv = 0.0_c_float do i = 1 , n ! ring 0: vertices 0..n-1; ring 1: n..2n-1 j = modulo ( i , n ) indices ( 6 * i - 5 : 6 * i ) = int ([ i - 1 , j , n + i - 1 , j , n + j , n + i - 1 ], c_int32_t ) end do call apply_color ( g ) g % switch = vkf_switch_create () call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( g % switch , g % mesh ), 'shadow' ) call check_status ( vkf_switch_set ( g % switch , 0_c_int ), 'shadow' ) ! (until shaped) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( group , g % switch ), 'shadow' ) end associate end do self % shaped = - 1.0_wp ! (shaped at the next update) end subroutine shadow_build_contents","tags":"","url":"proc/shadow_build_contents.html"},{"title":"shadow_late_update – vkframes","text":"private recursive subroutine shadow_late_update(self, t) After the tree's update for time t: the shadow moved to the body, turned\naway from the light, and reshaped if the distance or a setting changed. Type Bound ShadowCones Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t the scene time Calls proc~~shadow_late_update~~CallsGraph proc~shadow_late_update ShadowCones%shadow_late_update proc~contents_shown ReferenceFrame%contents_shown proc~shadow_late_update->proc~contents_shown proc~late_update ReferenceFrame%late_update proc~shadow_late_update->proc~late_update proc~place place proc~shadow_late_update->proc~place proc~late_update->proc~late_update proc~body_radius~2 ShadowCones%body_radius proc~place->proc~body_radius~2 proc~light_radius ShadowCones%light_radius proc~place->proc~light_radius proc~local_matrix ReferenceFrame%local_matrix proc~place->proc~local_matrix proc~quat_from_vectors quat_from_vectors proc~place->proc~quat_from_vectors proc~rigid_inverse rigid_inverse proc~place->proc~rigid_inverse proc~set_attitude~2 ReferenceFrame%set_attitude proc~place->proc~set_attitude~2 proc~set_position~2 ReferenceFrame%set_position proc~place->proc~set_position~2 proc~shape_regions shape_regions proc~place->proc~shape_regions proc~world_matrix ReferenceFrame%world_matrix proc~place->proc~world_matrix proc~frame_radius frame_radius proc~body_radius~2->proc~frame_radius proc~light_radius->proc~frame_radius proc~frame_matrix frame_matrix proc~local_matrix->proc~frame_matrix proc~cross cross proc~quat_from_vectors->proc~cross proc~quat_normalize quat_normalize proc~quat_from_vectors->proc~quat_normalize proc~set_attitude~2->proc~quat_normalize proc~write_region write_region proc~shape_regions->proc~write_region proc~world_matrix->proc~local_matrix proc~world_matrix->proc~world_matrix proc~quat_to_matrix quat_to_matrix proc~frame_matrix->proc~quat_to_matrix body_radius body_radius proc~frame_radius->body_radius radii radii proc~frame_radius->radii interface~vkf_mesh_vertices_changed vkf_mesh_vertices_changed proc~write_region->interface~vkf_mesh_vertices_changed interface~vkf_switch_set vkf_switch_set proc~write_region->interface~vkf_switch_set proc~check_status check_status proc~write_region->proc~check_status proc~mesh_arrays mesh_arrays proc~write_region->proc~mesh_arrays interface~vkf_mesh_array vkf_mesh_array proc~mesh_arrays->interface~vkf_mesh_array Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code recursive subroutine shadow_late_update ( self , t ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the scene time if ( associated ( self % body_ ) . and . associated ( self % light_ ) . and . self % contents_shown ()) call place ( self ) call self % ReferenceFrame % late_update ( t ) end subroutine shadow_late_update","tags":"","url":"proc/shadow_late_update.html"},{"title":"shape_regions – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine shape_regions(self, r, rs, d) The regions' frustums for body radius r, light radius rs and distance d\n(see the module documentation), written to their meshes. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r scene units real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rs scene units real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: d scene units Calls proc~~shape_regions~~CallsGraph proc~shape_regions shape_regions proc~write_region write_region proc~shape_regions->proc~write_region interface~vkf_mesh_vertices_changed vkf_mesh_vertices_changed proc~write_region->interface~vkf_mesh_vertices_changed interface~vkf_switch_set vkf_switch_set proc~write_region->interface~vkf_switch_set proc~check_status check_status proc~write_region->proc~check_status proc~mesh_arrays mesh_arrays proc~write_region->proc~mesh_arrays interface~vkf_mesh_array vkf_mesh_array proc~mesh_arrays->interface~vkf_mesh_array Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~shape_regions~~CalledByGraph proc~shape_regions shape_regions proc~place place proc~place->proc~shape_regions proc~shadow_late_update ShadowCones%shadow_late_update proc~shadow_late_update->proc~place Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine shape_regions ( self , r , rs , d ) type ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: r , rs , d !! scene units real ( wp ) :: sa , ca , ta , sb , cb , tb , apex , len integer :: k self % region % drawn = . false . self % drawn_length_ = 0.0_wp if ( r > 0.0_wp . and . rs > 0.0_wp . and . d > r + rs ) then sa = ( rs - r ) / d ! the umbra's half-angle (sine; < 0: widening) ca = sqrt ( 1.0_wp - sa ** 2 ) ta = sa / ca sb = ( rs + r ) / d ! the penumbra's cb = sqrt ( 1.0_wp - sb ** 2 ) tb = sb / cb apex = huge ( 1.0_wp ) if ( sa > 0.0_wp ) apex = r / sa len = self % length_ if ( len <= 0.0_wp ) then len = 10 0.0_wp * r if ( sa > 0.0_wp ) len = 2.0_wp * apex end if self % drawn_length_ = len ! the umbra: from the outer tangents' circle on the body to the apex (or len) associate ( g => self % region ( umbra )) g % z0 = r * sa g % r0 = r * ca g % z1 = min ( apex , len ) g % r1 = max ( 0.0_wp , g % r0 - ( g % z1 - g % z0 ) * ta ) if ( g % z1 >= apex ) g % r1 = 0.0_wp g % drawn = g % z1 > g % z0 end associate ! the antumbra: from the apex to len associate ( g => self % region ( antumbra )) g % z0 = apex g % r0 = 0.0_wp g % z1 = len g % r1 = ( len - apex ) * ta g % drawn = sa > 0.0_wp . and . len > apex end associate ! the penumbra: from the inner tangents' circle (on the light's side) to len associate ( g => self % region ( penumbra )) g % z0 = - r * sb g % r0 = r * cb g % z1 = len g % r1 = g % r0 + ( len - g % z0 ) * tb g % drawn = len > g % z0 end associate end if self % region ( umbra )% drawn = self % region ( umbra )% drawn . and . iand ( self % regions_ , SHADOW_UMBRA ) /= 0 self % region ( penumbra )% drawn = self % region ( penumbra )% drawn . and . iand ( self % regions_ , SHADOW_PENUMBRA ) /= 0 self % region ( antumbra )% drawn = self % region ( antumbra )% drawn . and . iand ( self % regions_ , SHADOW_ANTUMBRA ) /= 0 do k = 1 , n_regions call write_region ( self % region ( k )) end do end subroutine shape_regions","tags":"","url":"proc/shape_regions.html"},{"title":"write_region – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine write_region(g) A region's frustum into its mesh (uploaded), and shown or hidden. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ShadowRegion ), intent(in) :: g Calls proc~~write_region~~CallsGraph proc~write_region write_region interface~vkf_mesh_vertices_changed vkf_mesh_vertices_changed proc~write_region->interface~vkf_mesh_vertices_changed interface~vkf_switch_set vkf_switch_set proc~write_region->interface~vkf_switch_set proc~check_status check_status proc~write_region->proc~check_status proc~mesh_arrays mesh_arrays proc~write_region->proc~mesh_arrays interface~vkf_mesh_array vkf_mesh_array proc~mesh_arrays->interface~vkf_mesh_array Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Called by proc~~write_region~~CalledByGraph proc~write_region write_region proc~shape_regions shape_regions proc~shape_regions->proc~write_region proc~place place proc~place->proc~shape_regions proc~shadow_late_update ShadowCones%shadow_late_update proc~shadow_late_update->proc~place Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine write_region ( g ) type ( ShadowRegion ), intent ( in ) :: g real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: v , normals , uv integer ( c_int32_t ), dimension (:), pointer :: indices real ( wp ) :: a integer :: i , n if (. not . c_associated ( g % mesh )) return n = n_around if ( g % drawn ) then call mesh_arrays ( g % mesh , 2 * n , 6 * n , v , normals , uv , indices ) do i = 1 , n a = 2.0_wp * pi * ( i - 1 ) / n v (:, i ) = real ([ g % r0 * cos ( a ), g % r0 * sin ( a ), g % z0 ], c_float ) v (:, n + i ) = real ([ g % r1 * cos ( a ), g % r1 * sin ( a ), g % z1 ], c_float ) end do call check_status ( vkf_mesh_vertices_changed ( g % mesh ), 'shadow' ) end if call check_status ( vkf_switch_set ( g % switch , merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , g % drawn )), 'shadow' ) end subroutine write_region","tags":"","url":"proc/write_region.html"},{"title":"ShadowCones – vkframes","text":"public interface ShadowCones The ShadowCones constructor: ShadowCones(...) makes one (see new_shadow_cones for its\narguments). Calls interface~~shadowcones~~CallsGraph interface~shadowcones ShadowCones proc~new_shadow_cones new_shadow_cones interface~shadowcones->proc~new_shadow_cones proc~set_body_radius ShadowCones%set_body_radius proc~new_shadow_cones->proc~set_body_radius proc~set_light_radius ShadowCones%set_light_radius proc~new_shadow_cones->proc~set_light_radius proc~show_axes ReferenceFrame%show_axes proc~new_shadow_cones->proc~show_axes proc~show_axes_labels ReferenceFrame%show_axes_labels proc~new_shadow_cones->proc~show_axes_labels proc~show_name_label ReferenceFrame%show_name_label proc~new_shadow_cones->proc~show_name_label proc~update_switches update_switches proc~show_axes->proc~update_switches proc~show_axes_labels->proc~update_switches proc~show_name_label->proc~update_switches interface~vkf_switch_set vkf_switch_set proc~update_switches->interface~vkf_switch_set proc~check_status check_status proc~update_switches->proc~check_status Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Module Procedures private  function new_shadow_cones (name, body, light, body_radius, light_radius) result(s) The shadow named name of body in the light of light (frames of the\nsame tree; optional here, set later with set_body and set_light), with\ntheir radii if given (else the frames': see the module documentation).\nIts axes and name label are hidden. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), optional, target :: body class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), optional, target :: light real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: body_radius scene units (default: the frames' own) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: light_radius scene units (default: the frames' own) Return Value type( ShadowCones )","tags":"","url":"interface/shadowcones.html"},{"title":"auto_lod – vkframes","text":"private pure function auto_lod(self) Whether level of detail is on. Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical Source Code pure logical function auto_lod ( self ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self auto_lod = self % auto_lod_ end function auto_lod","tags":"","url":"proc/auto_lod.html"},{"title":"new_sphere – vkframes","text":"private  function new_sphere(name, radius, color) result(s) A sphere named name , of radius radius (default 1) and color color ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]; default white, 90% opaque). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: name real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: radius scene units (default 1) real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: color (:) [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) Return Value type( Sphere ) Called by proc~~new_sphere~~CalledByGraph proc~new_sphere new_sphere interface~sphere Sphere interface~sphere->proc~new_sphere Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code function new_sphere ( name , radius , color ) result ( s ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: radius !! scene units (default 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) type ( Sphere ) :: s s % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) if ( present ( radius )) s % radius_ = radius end function new_sphere","tags":"","url":"proc/new_sphere.html"},{"title":"night_texture_map – vkframes","text":"private  function night_texture_map(self) result(file) The night texture file ('' for none). Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(in) :: self Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Source Code function night_texture_map ( self ) result ( file ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: file file = '' if ( allocated ( self % night_texture )) file = self % night_texture end function night_texture_map","tags":"","url":"proc/night_texture_map.html"},{"title":"num_lod_meshes – vkframes","text":"private  function num_lod_meshes(self) result(n) Number of level-of-detail meshes built so far (0 without level of detail). Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer Source Code integer function num_lod_meshes ( self ) result ( n ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self integer :: k n = 0 do k = 1 , size ( self % lod_mesh ) if ( c_associated ( self % lod_mesh ( k ))) n = n + 1 end do end function num_lod_meshes","tags":"","url":"proc/num_lod_meshes.html"},{"title":"opacity – vkframes","text":"private pure function opacity(self) The body's opacity (set_opacity). Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) Source Code pure real ( wp ) function opacity ( self ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self opacity = self % opacity_ end function opacity","tags":"","url":"proc/opacity.html"},{"title":"radii – vkframes","text":"private pure function radii(self) result(r) The semi-axes: radius * sphere_scale. Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp), (3) Called by proc~~radii~~CalledByGraph proc~radii Sphere%radii proc~sphere_bound Sphere%sphere_bound proc~sphere_bound->proc~radii proc~sphere_build_contents Sphere%sphere_build_contents proc~sphere_build_contents->proc~radii proc~update_sphere_transform update_sphere_transform proc~sphere_build_contents->proc~update_sphere_transform proc~sphere_pick Sphere%sphere_pick proc~sphere_pick->proc~radii proc~update_sphere_transform->proc~radii proc~set_radius Sphere%set_radius proc~set_radius->proc~update_sphere_transform proc~set_sphere_attitude Sphere%set_sphere_attitude proc~set_sphere_attitude->proc~update_sphere_transform proc~set_sphere_position Sphere%set_sphere_position proc~set_sphere_position->proc~update_sphere_transform proc~set_sphere_scale Sphere%set_sphere_scale proc~set_sphere_scale->proc~update_sphere_transform Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code pure function radii ( self ) result ( r ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: r ( 3 ) r = self % radius_ * self % scale_ end function radii","tags":"","url":"proc/radii.html"},{"title":"radius – vkframes","text":"private pure function radius(self) The sphere's radius (scene units). Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=wp) Source Code function new_sphere ( name , radius , color ) result ( s ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: radius !! scene units (default 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) type ( Sphere ) :: s s % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) if ( present ( radius )) s % radius_ = radius end function new_sphere !> The sphere's radius (scene units, > 0; default 1); can change at any time. subroutine set_radius ( self , radius ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radius !! scene units (<= 0: ignored) if ( radius <= 0.0_wp ) return self % radius_ = radius call update_sphere_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_radius !> The body's color (used without a texture); [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]. subroutine sphere_set_color ( self , color ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call self % ReferenceFrame % set_color ( color ) call apply_material ( self ) end subroutine sphere_set_color !> The body's opacity, 0 (invisible) to 1 (opaque, the default): below 1 !> it is drawn translucent (see the module documentation). Set below 1 !> before a window first shows it to make it translucent; then the !> opacity can change at any time (a translucent body stays translucent, !> an opaque one opaque). subroutine set_opacity ( self , opacity ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: opacity !! 0 to 1 self % opacity_ = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , opacity )) call apply_material ( self ) end subroutine set_opacity !> The body's opacity (set_opacity). pure real ( wp ) function opacity ( self ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self opacity = self % opacity_ end function opacity !> The sphere's radius (scene units). pure real ( wp ) function radius ( self ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self radius = self % radius_ end function radius","tags":"","url":"proc/radius.html"},{"title":"read_texture – vkframes","text":"private  function read_texture(self, file) result(image) An image handle for texture file file (null if none or unreadable). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( Sphere ), intent(in) :: self character(len=:), intent(in), allocatable :: file found with find_data_file (unallocated or '': none) Return Value type(c_ptr) Calls proc~~read_texture~~CallsGraph proc~read_texture read_texture interface~vkf_image_read vkf_image_read proc~read_texture->interface~vkf_image_read proc~find_data_file find_data_file proc~read_texture->proc~find_data_file proc~name ReferenceFrame%name proc~read_texture->proc~name proc~find_in_dirs find_in_dirs proc~find_data_file->proc~find_in_dirs Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis co