enFrames' setMaterial; each optional): ambient, diffuse,\nspecular and emission colors ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1) and\nshininess (0 to 128: the specular highlight's sharpness; 0 for none).\nThe ambient and diffuse colors scale the body's color or texture (VSG's\nPhong); the specular color is reflected from the lights' specular parts.\nDefaults: ambient and diffuse white, no specular reflection or emission. Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: ambient (:) [r, g, b(, a)], 0 to 1 real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: diffuse (:) [r, g, b(, a)], 0 to 1 real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: specular (:) [r, g, b(, a)], 0 to 1 real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: emission (:) [r, g, b(, a)], 0 to 1 real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: shininess 0 to 128 (< 0: 0) Calls proc~~set_material~~CallsGraph proc~set_material Sphere%set_material proc~apply_material apply_material proc~set_material->proc~apply_material proc~apply_material_to apply_material_to proc~apply_material->proc~apply_material_to interface~vkf_mesh_set_twilight vkf_mesh_set_twilight proc~apply_material_to->interface~vkf_mesh_set_twilight proc~color~3 ReferenceFrame%color proc~apply_material_to->proc~color~3 proc~mesh_set_material mesh_set_material proc~apply_material_to->proc~mesh_set_material proc~name ReferenceFrame%name proc~apply_material_to->proc~name interface~vkf_mesh_material vkf_mesh_material proc~mesh_set_material->interface~vkf_mesh_material interface~vkf_mesh_material_changed vkf_mesh_material_changed proc~mesh_set_material->interface~vkf_mesh_material_changed Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_material ( self , ambient , diffuse , specular , emission , shininess ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: ambient (:), diffuse (:), specular (:), emission (:) !! [r, g, b(, a)], 0 to 1 real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: shininess !! 0 to 128 (< 0: 0) if ( present ( ambient )) self % ambient_ ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( ambient ))) = ambient ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( ambient ))) if ( present ( diffuse )) self % diffuse_ ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( diffuse ))) = diffuse ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( diffuse ))) if ( present ( specular )) self % specular_ ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( specular ))) = specular ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( specular ))) if ( present ( emission )) self % emission_ ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( emission ))) = emission ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( emission ))) if ( present ( shininess )) self % shininess_ = max ( 0.0_wp , shininess ) call apply_material ( self ) end subroutine set_material","tags":"","url":"proc/set_material.html"},{"title":"set_night_texture_map – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_night_texture_map(self, file) The texture for the side away from the light (e.g. city lights; an\nequirectangular image file as the texture, '' for none), shown where the\ndiffuse light is weak. Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: file found with find_data_file; '' for none Source Code subroutine set_night_texture_map ( self , file ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: file !! found with find_data_file; '' for none self % night_texture = file end subroutine set_night_texture_map","tags":"","url":"proc/set_night_texture_map.html"}