ution – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_resolution(self, n_lon, n_lat) The mesh resolution without level of detail: segments in longitude and\nlatitude (default 128 x 64). Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: n_lon segments in longitude (at least 3) integer, intent(in) :: n_lat segments in latitude (at least 2) Source Code subroutine set_resolution ( self , n_lon , n_lat ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n_lon !! segments in longitude (at least 3) integer , intent ( in ) :: n_lat !! segments in latitude (at least 2) self % n_lon = max ( 3 , n_lon ) self % n_lat = max ( 2 , n_lat ) end subroutine set_resolution","tags":"","url":"proc/set_resolution.html"},{"title":"set_sphere_attitude – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_sphere_attitude(self, q) Attitude of the body in its frame (quaternion [x, y, z, w]), e.g. to\norient its texture. Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: q (4) quaternion [x, y, z, w] (normalized here) Calls proc~~set_sphere_attitude~~CallsGraph proc~set_sphere_attitude Sphere%set_sphere_attitude proc~quat_normalize quat_normalize proc~set_sphere_attitude->proc~quat_normalize proc~update_sphere_transform update_sphere_transform proc~set_sphere_attitude->proc~update_sphere_transform interface~vkf_transform_set_matrix vkf_transform_set_matrix proc~update_sphere_transform->interface~vkf_transform_set_matrix proc~frame_matrix frame_matrix proc~update_sphere_transform->proc~frame_matrix proc~name ReferenceFrame%name proc~update_sphere_transform->proc~name proc~radii Sphere%radii proc~update_sphere_transform->proc~radii proc~quat_to_matrix quat_to_matrix proc~frame_matrix->proc~quat_to_matrix Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_sphere_attitude ( self , q ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q ( 4 ) !! quaternion [x, y, z, w] (normalized here) self % sphere_attitude_ = quat_normalize ( q ) call update_sphere_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_sphere_attitude","tags":"","url":"proc/set_sphere_attitude.html"},{"title":"set_sphere_position – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_sphere_position(self, position) Position of the body's center in its frame. Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: position (3) scene units Calls proc~~set_sphere_position~~CallsGraph proc~set_sphere_position Sphere%set_sphere_position proc~update_sphere_transform update_sphere_transform proc~set_sphere_position->proc~update_sphere_transform interface~vkf_transform_set_matrix vkf_transform_set_matrix proc~update_sphere_transform->interface~vkf_transform_set_matrix proc~frame_matrix frame_matrix proc~update_sphere_transform->proc~frame_matrix proc~name ReferenceFrame%name proc~update_sphere_transform->proc~name proc~radii Sphere%radii proc~update_sphere_transform->proc~radii proc~quat_to_matrix quat_to_matrix proc~frame_matrix->proc~quat_to_matrix Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_sphere_position ( self , position ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: position ( 3 ) !! scene units self % sphere_position_ = position call update_sphere_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_sphere_position","tags":"","url":"proc/set_sphere_position.html"},{"title":"set_sphere_scale – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_sphere_scale(self, scale) Scale the sphere along its x, y and z axes (all > 0), making an\nellipsoid with semi-axes radius * scale. Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: scale (3) along x, y and z (all > 0, else ignored) Calls proc~~set_sphere_scale~~CallsGraph proc~set_sphere_scale Sphere%set_sphere_scale proc~update_sphere_transform update_sphere_transform proc~set_sphere_scale->proc~update_sphere_transform interface~vkf_transform_set_matrix vkf_transform_set_matrix proc~update_sphere_transform->interface~vkf_transform_set_matrix proc~frame_matrix frame_matrix proc~update_sphere_transform->proc~frame_matrix proc~name ReferenceFrame%name proc~update_sphere_transform->proc~name proc~radii Sphere%radii proc~update_sphere_transform->proc~radii proc~quat_to_matrix quat_to_matrix proc~frame_matrix->proc~quat_to_matrix Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_sphere_scale ( self , scale ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: scale ( 3 ) !! along x, y and z (all > 0, else ignored) if ( any ( scale <= 0.0_wp )) return self % scale_ = scale call update_sphere_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_sphere_scale","tags":"","url":"proc/set_sphere_scale.html"},{"title":"set_texture_map – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_texture_map(self, file) The texture: an equirectangular image file ('' for none). Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(inout) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: file found with find_data_file; '' for none Source Code subroutine set_texture_map ( self , file ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: file !! found with find_data_file; '' for none self % texture = file end subroutine set_texture_map","tags":"","url":"proc/set_texture_map~2.html"},{"title":"set_twilight – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine set_twilight(self, angle) The twilight: the diffuse light extended past the terminator to where\nthe light is angle (radians, 0 to 1.5) below the horizon, fading out\nsmoothly (where it meets the light on the day side: the same brightness\nand slope, so no line shows), and the night texture fading in across it.\n0 (the default): none, the light ends at the terminator (an airless\nbody). Not in OpenFrames. Can change at any time. Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: angle radians below the horizon (clamped to 0 to 1.5) Calls proc~~set_twilight~~CallsGraph proc~set_twilight Sphere%set_twilight proc~apply_material apply_material proc~set_twilight->proc~apply_material proc~apply_material_to apply_material_to proc~apply_material->proc~apply_material_to interface~vkf_mesh_set_twilight vkf_mesh_set_twilight proc~apply_material_to->interface~vkf_mesh_set_twilight proc~color~3 ReferenceFrame%color proc~apply_material_to->proc~color~3 proc~mesh_set_material mesh_set_material proc~apply_material_to->proc~mesh_set_material proc~name ReferenceFrame%name proc~apply_material_to->proc~name interface~vkf_mesh_material vkf_mesh_material proc~mesh_set_material->interface~vkf_mesh_material interface~vkf_mesh_material_changed vkf_mesh_material_changed proc~mesh_set_material->interface~vkf_mesh_material_changed Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine set_twilight ( self , angle ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! radians below the horizon (clamped to 0 to 1.5) self % twilight_ = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.5_wp , angle )) call apply_material ( self ) end subroutine set_twilight","tags":"","url":"proc/set_twilight.html"},{"title":"sphere_bound – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine sphere_bound(self, center, radius) The body's bounding sphere: its center, and its largest semi-axis. Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: center (3) the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: radius the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) Calls proc~~sphere_bound~~CallsGraph proc~sphere_bound Sphere%sphere_bound proc~radii Sphere%radii proc~sphere_bound->proc~radii Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Source Code subroutine sphere_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius !! the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) center = self % sphere_position_ radius = maxval ( self % radii ()) end subroutine sphere_bound","tags":"","url":"proc/sphere_bound.html"},{"title":"sphere_build_contents – vkframes","text":"private  subroutine sphere_build_contents(self, viewer, group) The body: an ellipsoid mesh under the sphere's transform. Type Bound Sphere Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Sphere ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer a window's viewer (null: headless) type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: group the frame's contents group Calls proc~~sphere_build_contents~~CallsGraph proc~sphere_build_contents Sphere%sphere_build_contents interface~vkf_image_delete vkf_image_delete proc~sphere_build_contents->interface~vkf_image_delete interface~vkf_node_add_child vkf_node_add_child proc~sphere_build_contents->interface~vkf_node_add_child interface~vkf_sphere_lod_create vkf_sphere_lod_create proc~sphere_build_contents->interface~vkf_sphere_lod_create interface~vkf_transform_create vkf_transform_create proc~sphere_build_contents->interface~vkf_transform_create proc~apply_material apply_material proc~sphere_build_contents->proc