interface in a parent module. Source Code pure subroutine vsg_alignment ( alignment , h , v ) integer , intent ( in ) :: alignment !! an ALIGN_* constant of vkf_frames integer , intent ( out ) :: h , v !! VSG_* horizontal and vertical alignments integer , parameter :: horizontal ( 0 : 11 ) = [ VSG_LEFT , VSG_LEFT , VSG_LEFT , VSG_CENTER , VSG_CENTER , VSG_CENTER , & VSG_RIGHT , VSG_RIGHT , VSG_RIGHT , VSG_LEFT , VSG_CENTER , VSG_RIGHT ] integer , parameter :: vertical ( 0 : 11 ) = [ VSG_TOP , VSG_CENTER , VSG_BOTTOM , VSG_TOP , VSG_CENTER , VSG_BOTTOM , & VSG_TOP , VSG_CENTER , VSG_BOTTOM , VSG_BASELINE , VSG_BASELINE , VSG_BASELINE ] integer :: a a = max ( 0 , min ( 11 , alignment )) h = horizontal ( a ) v = vertical ( a ) end subroutine vsg_alignment","tags":"","url":"proc/vsg_alignment.html"},{"title":"vkf_sky – vkframes","text":"The sky behind a scene (OpenFrames' SkySphere): a texture map and/or stars\nfrom a star catalog, at infinity (they turn with the view, never move with\nit), in the root frame's axes turned by the sky's attitude. A window shows\na sky with WindowProxy%set_sky; one sky can be shown in several windows. Texture: an equirectangular image of the sky (right ascension across,\n  declination down; as a Sphere's texture map), e.g. OpenFrames'\n  Images/StarMap.tif. Stars: a star catalog in OpenFrames' text format (e.g. the HYG v3\n  catalog of OpenFrames, data/Stars_HYGv3.txt): a header line\n  \"ra[_limit] dec mag ci proper\", then a star per line: right ascension (in\n  hours, or 0 to limit if the header says \"ra_limit\", e.g. \"ra_360.0\"),\n  declination (degrees), apparent magnitude, optional B-V color index and\n  name. Stars in a magnitude range are drawn (at most a number of them, in\n  catalog order), sized from their brightness between a minimum and a\n  maximum size (window units), colored from their color index, and the\n  smaller dimmed (OpenFrames' SkySphere::processStars and StarToPoint). Star names: the names of the catalog's named stars drawn (those of\n  them up to a magnitude), as labels beside them, at infinity as the stars\n  (behind the scene); off by default (set_star_names). Shown with the\n  stars (draw mode SKY_STARS). Constellations: faint lines between their stars, from a constellation\n  file (e.g. data/inp_Constellation.txt, Chris Dolan's outlines): \"N name\"\n  starts a constellation, then a line per segment, \"dec1 ra1 dec2 ra2\"\n  (degrees, hours), then an optional \"# comment\"; lines starting with \"#\"\n  are comments. Off by default (set_constellations); at infinity, behind\n  the stars, shown unless the draw mode is SKY_NONE. Both are drawn when given (draw mode SKY_TEXTURE + SKY_STARS); the stars\nover the texture, by the brighter color. Uses iso_c_binding vkf_text vkf_files vkf_layer vkf_math module~~vkf_sky~~UsesGraph module~vkf_sky vkf_sky iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~vkf_sky->iso_c_binding module~vkf_files vkf_files module~vkf_sky->module~vkf_files module~vkf_layer vkf_layer module~vkf_sky->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_math vkf_math module~vkf_sky->module~vkf_math module~vkf_text vkf_text module~vkf_sky->module~vkf_text module~vkf_layer->iso_c_binding iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~vkf_math->iso_fortran_env module~vkf_text->iso_c_binding module~vkf_text->module~vkf_files module~vkf_text->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_text->module~vkf_math Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~vkf_sky~~UsedByGraph module~vkf_sky vkf_sky module~vkf_window vkf_window module~vkf_window->module~vkf_sky module~vkframes vkframes module~vkframes->module~vkf_sky module~vkframes->module~vkf_window Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours r