tent(in) :: ci apparent magnitude and B-V color index real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: dir (3) unit vector real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: rgb (3) color (0 to 1) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: size raw size (as raw_size)","tags":"","url":"module/vkf_sky.html"},{"title":"vkf_follower – vkframes","text":"Following trajectories: the position and attitude of a frame from one or more\ntrajectories at the current time, as OpenFrames' TrajectoryFollower. With several trajectories, the one followed at time t is the one whose time\nrange contains t, or the closest one. If t is outside all of them, FOLLOW_LOOP\nwraps it into their combined time range and FOLLOW_LIMIT holds the ends.\nPositions are interpolated linearly, attitudes by slerp. The time is either the global simulation time plus an offset\n( set_offset_time , the default with offset 0) or a fixed time ( set_time ).\nThe trajectories are not owned: they must stay alive while followed. Uses vkf_trajectory vkf_math module~~vkf_follower~~UsesGraph module~vkf_follower vkf_follower module~vkf_math vkf_math module~vkf_follower->module~vkf_math module~vkf_trajectory vkf_trajectory module~vkf_follower->module~vkf_trajectory iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~vkf_math->iso_fortran_env module~vkf_trajectory->module~vkf_math iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~vkf_trajectory->iso_c_binding module~vkf_trajectory->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~vkf_follower~~UsedByGraph module~vkf_follower vkf_follower module~vkf_frames vkf_frames module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_follower module~vkframes vkframes module~vkframes->module~vkf_follower module~vkframes->module~vkf_frames module