 and the cursor's position (-1 to 1, y up, as the window's\nevents). Frames test their contents against it (ReferenceFrame%pick and\nits extensions):\n* points and line segments on the screen, within a tolerance in pixels\n  ( point_pick , segment_pick : the closest point of a segment, its\n  fraction along the segment in the scene, perspective-correct, and its\n  depth), for trajectories, markers and frames' origins;\n* a ray from the eye through the cursor against an ellipsoid ( ray , ray_ellipsoid ), for bodies;\n* the ray against a plane, a sphere and a line ( ray_plane , ray_sphere , ray_line ), for dragging (WindowProxy%cursor_ray, and\n  vkf_handles' constraints);\n* bounding spheres on the screen ( sphere_near ), to skip whole chunks of\n  a long trajectory.\nDepths are distances along the view direction (perspective) or from the\neye's plane (orthographic); points closer than near are behind the eye. Uses vkf_math module~~vkf_pick~~UsesGraph module~vkf_pick vkf_pick module~vkf_math vkf_math module~vkf_pick->module~vkf_math iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~vkf_math->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~vkf_pick~~UsedByGraph module~vkf_pick vkf_pick module~vkf_artists vkf_artists module~vkf_artists->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_frames vkf_frames module~vkf_artists->module~vkf_frames module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_handles vkf_handles module~vkf_handles->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_handles->module~vkf_artists module~vkf_handles->module~vkf_frames module~vkf_model vkf_model module~vkf_model->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_model->module~vkf_frames module~vkf_sphere vkf_sphere module~vkf_sphere-