memory). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(inout) :: self private  subroutine colors (self, c) Pointer to the colors (4, num_colors; single precision, as drawn),\nwithout copying. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(in), target :: self real(kind=c_float), intent(out), dimension(:,:), pointer :: c private  subroutine compact (self) Free the storage not used: each array is reallocated to the points it\nholds (one copy, an array at a time), and arrays holding none are\ndeallocated. For a trajectory that is complete: growing doubles the\nstorage, so up to about half of it can be unused. The data and what is\ndrawn of them don't change; pointers from times , positions , ...\nmust be fetched again. Points can still be added (storage grows again). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(inout) :: self private  subroutine grow_attitudes (self, n, exact) Grow the attitudes' storage to hold at least n . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( Trajectory ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: n logical, intent(in), optional :: exact private  subroutine grow_colors (self, n, exact) Grow the colors' storage to hold at least n . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( Trajectory ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: n logical, intent(in), optional :: exact private  subroutine grow_positions (self, n, exact) Grow the positions' (and optionals') storage to hold at least n . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( Trajectory ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: n logical, intent(in), optional :: exact private  subroutine grow_times (self, n, exact) Grow the times' storage to hold at least n (see new_capacity ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( Trajectory ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: n logical, intent(in), optional :: exact private pure subroutine points (self, i1, i2, sources, v, stride) Points i1, i1 + stride, ... (up to i2) with components from sources , into\nv(3, :) (as many columns as points; point for a range, a whole array\nslice per component). No checks: use verify_data and num_points first. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i1 integer, intent(in) :: i2 type( DataSource ), intent(in) :: sources (3) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: v (:,:) (3, number of points) integer, intent(in), optional :: stride step between points (default 1) private  subroutine positions (self, p) Pointer to the positions (3, num_positions), without copying. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(in), target :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:,:), pointer :: p private  subroutine reserve (self, n, positions, attitudes, colors) Reserve memory for n points: times, positions (with their optionals)\nunless positions is false, and attitudes and colors only if attitudes / colors is true. Optional: storage grows as needed, but\nreserving avoids reallocations for a known size. It never shrinks the\nstorage (see compact ). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: n number of points logical, intent(in), optional :: positions reserve positions (default true) logical, intent(in), optional :: attitudes reserve attitudes (default false) logical, intent(in), optional :: colors reserve colors (default false) private  subroutine set_dof (self, dof) Set the degrees of freedom (2 or 3) of positions and optionals; clears the trajectory. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: dof private  subroutine set_num_optionals (self, nopt) Set the number of optional vectors per position; clears the trajectory. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: nopt private  subroutine set_optional (self, index, v, ok) Set optional vector index (1 to num_optionals) of the most recently\nadded position. ok is false if there is no position or no such optional. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: index the optional (1 to num_optionals) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: v (:) the vector (its first dof elements are used) logical, intent(out), optional :: ok false if not set private  subroutine times (self, t) Pointer to the times (num_times), without copying. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( Trajectory ), intent(in), target :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out), dimension(:), pointer :: t private pure subroutine to_float_rgba (rgba, color) rgba from [r, g, b] (alpha 1) or [r, g, b, a]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=c_float), intent(out) :: rgba (4) [r, g, b, a] real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: color (:) [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1)","tags":"","url":"module/vkf_trajectory.html"},{"title":"vkf_terrain – vkframes","text":"Maps and terrain: a celestial body drawn from map layers by Rocky\n(https://github.com/pelicanmapping/rocky; optional: rocky_available() ),\ne.g. the Earth from tile services, or the Moon with NASA's imagery and\nLOLA's elevation. An addition to OpenFrames, which has only textured\nspheres. The body is centered on its frame's origin, in body-fixed axes (z through\nthe north pole, x through longitude 0), so the frame's attitude turns it.\nIts shape and coordinates come from Rocky's tiling profile: '' (Rocky's\ndefault) or 'global-geodetic' for the Earth (WGS84), 'moon' for the Moon\n(a sphere of 1737.4 km), or another of Rocky's profiles. Rocky works in\nmeters; the body is drawn at units_per_meter scene units per meter\n(default 1e-3: kilometers, as vkframes' examples). Layers ( add_image_layer , add_elevation_layer ) are tiled sources Rocky\npages in as the view needs them: a TMS service (LAYER_TMS), a file or\nservice GDAL reads (LAYER_GDAL; a file is found with find_data_file, e.g.\ndata/'s moon_lola_ldem16.tif from pixi run -e rocky moon-data ), or a\n{z}/{x}/{y} URL template of geodetic tiles on the body (LAYER_GEODETIC: 2 x\n1 tiles at level 0, rows from the top, as WMTS and NASA's Moon Trek) or of\nweb Mercator tiles (LAYER_MERCATOR: OpenStreetMap-style). Elevation is in\nmeters (ELEVATION_HEIGHTS) or encoded in RGB (ELEVATION_MAPBOX,\nELEVATION_TERRARIUM). Layers can be added before or after the body is\nshown. Lighting: lit by the scene's lights as a Sphere (a frame's light source, e.g.\nthe Sun, or the window's light; set_lighting(.false.) shows the imagery\nas it is). The frame's color is the color where no imagery covers the body. The map is made for a window that shows the body (Rocky's tiles are loaded\nthrough that window's viewer, and the map is drawn in that window only);\nwhen that window closes, it is made again for one still open (other\nwindows then show it). Headless (no viewer), the body has no map. Uses iso_c_binding vkf_math vkf_files vkf_pick vkf_frames vkf_layer module~~vkf_terrain~~UsesGraph module~vkf_terrain vkf_terrain iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~vkf_terrain->iso_c_binding module~vkf_files vkf_files module~vkf_terrain->module~vkf_files module~vkf_frames vkf_frames module~vkf_terrain->module~vkf_frames module~vkf_layer vkf_layer module~vkf_terrain->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_math vkf_math module~vkf_terrain->module~vkf_math module~vkf_pick vkf_pick module~vkf_terrain->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_frames->iso_c_binding module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_math module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_follower vkf_follower module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_follower module~vkf_geometry vkf_geometry module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_geometry module~vkf_text vkf_text module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_text module~vkf_trajectory vkf_trajectory module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_trajectory module~vkf_la