e( TerrainBody ), intent(inout) :: self private  subroutine make_map (self, viewer) The map (in the contents group) for viewer , with the settings and layers. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( TerrainBody ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer private  subroutine set_lighting (self, lit) Light the body with the scene's lights (default), or show its imagery as it is. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TerrainBody ), intent(inout) :: self logical, intent(in) :: lit private  subroutine terrain_bound (self, center, radius) The body's bounding sphere (frame coordinates): its equatorial radius, at the origin. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TerrainBody ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: center (3) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: radius private  subroutine terrain_build_contents (self, viewer, group) The map, made for the viewer showing the body (none headless or without Rocky). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TerrainBody ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer a window's viewer handle (null: headless) type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: group the group node to build under private  subroutine terrain_pick (self, cam, to_root, hits, n) Picked on a sphere of the body's radius (not the terrain's heights), with\nthe latitude and longitude of the point hit; else the frame's origin. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TerrainBody ), intent(in), target :: self type( PickCamera ), intent(in) :: cam the cursor's ray and the pick's settings real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: to_root (4,4) the frame's transform to the root frame type( PickHit ), intent(inout), allocatable :: hits (:) hits so far (grown as needed) integer, intent(inout) :: n number of hits in hits private recursive subroutine terrain_update (self, t) Each frame: if the map's window has closed (the map was released with\nit), the map again for a window still open (compiled for the windows\nrunning), then the frame's update. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( TerrainBody ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t simulation time (s)","tags":"","url":"module/vkf_terrain.html"},{"title":"vkf_artists – vkframes","text":"Trajectory artists: what draws a Trajectory, in a DrawableTrajectory frame, as\nOpenFrames' TrajectoryArtist, CurveArtist, SegmentArtist, MarkerArtist and\nDrawableTrajectory, and RibbonArtist (not in OpenFrames: a translucent\nsurface swept between two points at each trajectory point, e.g. an orbit's\nplane from the origin to the positions). A DrawableTrajectory is a frame (its points are in its coordinates) holding\nartists. Each frame update, an artist draws what changed in its trajectory:\nappended points are written into the GPU buffers in place, and only the\nbuffers written to are uploaded (see vkf_line_chain); a cleared trajectory\nis redrawn into the same buffers. The last point drawn is always rewritten,\nsince set_optional changes it. Trace mode ( set_trace_mode ) draws only the part of the trajectory up to\nthe current time: the points whose times are at most the current time,\nwhatever order they were added in (a change of the draw ranges, no\nupload): for increasing times its first points, for decreasing ones (a\ntrajectory propagated backwards) its last. A curve adds a two-point tail\nfrom the latest of them to the point interpolated at the current time\n(the only data uploaded each frame). So a trajectory propagated forwards\nand one propagated backwards to the same state trace one history as time\nruns (example/trace_directions.f90); with time running backwards, the\nhistory shrinks back. (A highlight's arrows still run in the order the\npoints were added: the propagation's direction.) Point colors (not in OpenFrames): a CurveArtist draws a trajectory with\ncolors (Trajectory%add_color, or add's color ) in them, each segment\nblended from its first point's color to its second's (one color: that\ncolor); without colors, or with set_point_colors(.false.) , in its own\ncolor. Its line buffers hold colors only then. Trails (not in OpenFrames): CurveArtist%set_trail(past, future, fade) draws only the part of the curve within past before the current time\nand future after it, each fading out over the last fade of its window\ntoward its cutoff; set_trail_style(TRAIL_PAST or TRAIL_FUTURE, ...) gives\neach part its own color (or translucency) and dash pattern (e.g. a solid\npast and a dashed future). The GPU fades and cuts the line by its distance\nalong it (shaders/line.vert): each frame only the distances at the current\ntime and at the window's edges are uploaded (a few floats per chunk), and\nthe range of points drawn changed. It replaces trace mode while set. Highlight (not in OpenFrames; e.g. a trajectory selected by the program or\nby picking): set_highlight on a curve or segment artist, or on a\nDrawableTrajectory for all of them. HIGHLIGHT_PULSE: the line widens and\nbrightens towards the highlight color, and back, over and over;\nHIGHLIGHT_ARROWS: a translucent band of the highlight color around it, with\nchevrons moving along it from its first point to its last (a trajectory's\ninitial time to its final; a segment's start to its end). Both together:\nHIGHLIGHT_PULSE + HIGHLIGHT_ARROWS. The GPU animates them (shaders/\nline.vert), so nothing is uploaded or computed each frame. In trace mode,\nonly the part drawn is highlighted. Artists and their trajectories are not owned: they must stay alive while\ndrawn. Picking (WindowProxy%pick): a DrawableTrajectory picks what its artists\ndraw, as drawn (in trace mode, up to the current time): a curve's segments\n(its chunks skipped by their bounds when far from the cursor), with the\npoint and the time there (interpolated); a segment artist's segments; a\nmarker artist's start, end and intermediate markers, with their times.\nLines are reached within the tolerance plus half their width, markers\nplus half their size. Each artist gives its best hit: the closest to the\ncursor (and of those, the nearest). Uses vkf_line_chain iso_c_binding vkf_math vkf_trajectory vkf_pick vkf_frames vkf_layer module~~vkf_artists~~UsesGraph module~vkf_artists vkf_artists iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~vkf_artists->iso_c_binding module~vkf_frames vkf_frames module~vkf_artists->module~vkf_frames module~vkf_layer vkf_layer module~vkf_artists->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_line_chain vkf_line_chain module~vkf_artists->module~vkf_line_chain module~vkf_math vkf_math module~vkf_artists->module~vkf_math module~vkf_pick vkf_pick module~vkf_artists->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_trajectory vkf_trajectory module~vkf_artists->module~vkf_trajectory module~vkf_frames->iso_c_binding module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_math module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_trajectory module~vkf_follower vkf_follower module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_follower module~vkf_geometry vkf_geometry module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_geometry module~vkf_text vkf_text module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_text module~vkf_layer->iso_c_binding module~vkf_line_chain->iso_c_binding module~vkf_line_chain->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_line_chain->module~vkf_math iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~vkf_math->iso_fortran_env module~vkf_pick->module~vkf_math module~vkf_trajectory->iso_c_binding module~vkf_trajectory->module~vkf_math module~vkf_trajectory->iso_fortran_env module~vkf_follower->module~vkf_math module~vkf_follower->module~vkf_trajectory module~vkf_geometry->iso_c_binding module~vkf_geometry->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_geometry->module~vkf_math module~vkf_text->iso_c_binding module~vkf_text->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_text->module~vkf_math module~vkf_files vkf_files module~vkf_text->module~vkf_files Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's 