butes Name type( LineChain ), intent(inout) :: chain real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: v (3) real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rgba (4) private  subroutine write_ribbon (self, i1, i2) Write the pairs of trajectory points i1 .. i2 into the chain, with their\ncolors (and upload the chunks written to). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( RibbonArtist ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i1 integer, intent(in) :: i2 private  subroutine write_segments (self, s1, s2) Write segments s1 .. s2 into the chain (and upload the chunks written to). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( SegmentArtist ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: s1 integer, intent(in) :: s2","tags":"","url":"module/vkf_artists.html"},{"title":"vkf_line_segments – vkframes","text":"Custom line segments, as OpenFrames' CustomLineSegments: a frame drawing\nline segments whose endpoints and colors (one per endpoint, blended along\nthe segment) are set by the program ( set_segments ), or computed each\nframe by a callback ( set_callback ): e.g. lines of sight between\nspacecraft, or links between ground stations and satellites. The endpoints are in the frame's own coordinates (the frame can move like\nany other); position_of(other) gives another frame's origin in them. The\ncallback, an extension of the abstract LineSegmentsCallback (OpenFrames'\nCustomLineSegments::Callback), is called once per scene update with the\nsimulation time, after the whole tree has been updated\n(ReferenceFrame%late_update), so the positions of other frames are those\nfor that time whatever their place in the tree; it sets the segments with set_segments . Setting the same segments again uploads nothing. The segments are drawn by a LineChain of separate segments (vkf_line_chain:\nthick lines in window units, square caps, dash patterns, points kept to\ndouble precision), with a color per point (vkf_line_create_colored).\nWithout colors, the segments take the frame's color ( set_color ).\n(OpenFrames' custom line shader, setLineShader, isn't available: it would\nneed GLSL compiled at run time.) Uses vkf_frames vkf_math vkf_line_chain iso_c_binding module~~vkf_line_segments~~UsesGraph module~vkf_line_segments vkf_line_segments iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~vkf_line_segments->iso_c_binding module~vkf_frames vkf_frames module~vkf_line_segments->module~vkf_frames module~vkf_line_chain vkf_line_chain module~vkf_line_segments->module~vkf_line_chain module~vkf_math vkf_math module~vkf_line_segments->module~vkf_math module~vkf_frames->iso_c_binding module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_math module~vkf_follower vkf_follower module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_follower module~vkf_geometry vkf_geometry module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_geometry module~vkf_layer vkf_layer module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_pick vkf_pick module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_text vkf_text module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_text module~vkf_trajectory vkf_trajectory module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_trajectory module~vkf_line_chain->iso_c_binding module~vkf_line_chain->module~vkf_math module~vkf_line_chain->module~vkf_layer iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~vkf_math->iso_fortran_env module~vkf_follower->module~vkf_math module~vkf_follower->module~vkf_trajectory module~vkf_geometry->iso_c_binding module~vkf_geometry->module~vkf_math module~vkf_geometry->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_layer->iso_c_binding module~vkf_pick->module~vkf_math module~vkf_text->iso_c_binding module~vkf_text->module~vkf_math module~vkf_text->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_files vkf_files module~vkf_text->module~vkf_files module~vkf_trajectory->iso_c_binding module~vkf_trajectory->module~vkf_math module~vkf_trajectory->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended fr