follows a frame: the camera's trackball (eye, center, up, which the\nmouse moves) is kept in the view frame's coordinates, so the camera moves\nwith the frame. The view frame is\n* RELATIVE_FRAME (the default): the viewed frame itself (a body-fixed view);\n* ABSOLUTE_FRAME: the root frame's axes, at the viewed frame's origin (an\n  inertial view that follows the frame as it moves).\nA view between frames ( set_view_between_frames ) looks from one frame at\nanother: the view frame is turned so that its +y axis (the trackball's\ninitial viewing direction) points at the second frame, in one direct rotation\n(VIEW_DIRECT) or first in azimuth, then elevation (VIEW_AZEL, the default,\nwhich keeps z up). The default camera ( reset_view ) looks along +y at the frame's bound from the\ndistance at which it fills the field of view (or from default_view_distance ,\nor from set_default_view_parameters ). Views are not owned by windows: a\nview, and the frames it refers to, must stay alive while used. The camera (OpenFrames' trackball get/setTransformation): a window's get_camera / set_camera for the view it shows (and smooth transitions,\nsee vkf_window), or View%set_camera for a view's camera when it is next\nshown. camera_between interpolates between two cameras (each eye, center,\nup): the center along a straight line, the distance geometrically, the\norientation by the shortest rotation. Uses vkf_math vkf_frames module~~vkf_view~~UsesGraph module~vkf_view vkf_view module~vkf_frames vkf_frames module~vkf_view->module~vkf_frames module~vkf_math vkf_math module~vkf_view->module~vkf_math module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_math iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~vkf_frames->iso_c_binding module~vkf_follower vkf_follower module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_follower module~vkf_geometry vkf_geometry module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_geometry module~vkf_layer vkf_layer module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_pick vkf_pick module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_text vkf_text module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_text module~vkf_trajectory vkf_trajectory module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_trajectory iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~vkf_math->iso_fortran_env module~vkf_follower->module~vkf_math module~vkf_follower->module~vkf_trajectory module~vkf_geometry->module~vkf_math module~vkf_geometry->iso_c_binding module~vkf_geometry->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_layer->iso_c_binding module~vkf_pick->module~vkf_math module~vkf_text->module~vkf_math module~vkf_text->iso_c_binding module~vkf_text->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_files vkf_files module~vkf_text->module~vkf_files module~vkf_trajectory->module~vkf_math module~vkf_trajectory->iso_c_binding module~vkf_trajectory->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Used by module~~vkf_view~~UsedByGraph module~vkf_view vkf_view module~vkf_window vkf_window module~vkf_window->module~vkf_view module~vkframes vkframes module~vkframes->module~vkf_view module~vkframes->module~vkf_window Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer, public, parameter :: ABSOLUTE_FRAME = 0 the base frame of the trackball (OpenFrames' ViewFrameType)\nthe root frame's axes, at the viewed frame's origin integer, public, parameter :: ORTHOGRAPHIC = 0 projections (OpenFrames' ProjectionType)\northographic projection integer, public, parameter :: PERSPECTIVE = 1 perspective projection integer, public, parameter :: RELATIVE_FRAME = 1 the viewed frame itself integer, public, parameter :: VIEW_AZEL = 1 azimuth, then elevation (keeps z up) integer, public, parameter :: VIEW_DIRECT = 0 how a view between frames turns toward the look-at frame (OpenFrames' ViewRotationType)\none direct rotation Interfaces public        interface View The View constructor: View(...) makes one (see new_view for its\narguments). private  function new_view (root, frame, lookat, frame_type, rotation_type) result(v) A view of frame (in the tree of root ), with base frame_type (default RELATIVE_FRAME); with lookat , a view from frame at lookat ,\nturned by rotation_type (default VIEW_AZEL). Without frames, the view\nlooks at the root frame's origin. The frames must stay alive while the\nview is used. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), optional, target :: root class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), optional, target :: frame class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), optional, target :: lookat integer, intent(in), optional :: frame_type ABSOLUTE_FRAME or RELATIVE_FRAME integer, intent(in), optional :: rotation_type VIEW_DIRECT or VIEW_AZEL Return Value type( View ) Derived Types type, public :: View A view (see the module documentation). Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial logical, private :: camera_pending = .false. true if pending is to be applied when shown real(kind=wp), private :: center (3) = 0.0_wp kept center real(kind=wp), private :: default_center (3) = 0.0_wp camera center after a reset (view-frame coordinates) real(kind=wp), private :: default_distance = 0.0_wp radius framed on reset (<= 0: the frame's bound) real(kind=wp), private :: default_eye (3) = 0.0_wp camera eye after a reset (view-frame coordinates) real(kind=wp), private :: default_up (3) = 0.0_wp camera up after a reset (zero: no default camera) real(kind=wp), private :: eye (3) = 0.0_wp kept eye real(kind=