ove all instances of v from the window's views. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self type( View ), intent(in), target :: v private  subroutine resize (self, width, height, pixel_ratio) The host window was resized (framebuffer pixels), and pixel_ratio : its\nframebuffer pixels per window unit (Qt's devicePixelRatio), if it may\nhave changed (the window moved to a screen of another scale, or the\ndisplay's scaling changed: sizes in window units, such as line widths,\nmarkers and labels, are scaled by it). Once the scene is shown, a frame\nof the new size is rendered at once (call this from the host's resize\nevent), so that the window isn't shown stretched or blank while it is\nresized. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: width framebuffer pixels integer, intent(in) :: height framebuffer pixels real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: pixel_ratio framebuffer pixels per window unit private  subroutine run (self, max_frames) Render frames until the window is closed (or for max_frames frames). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in), optional :: max_frames private  subroutine scroll (self, dy) The scroll wheel: dy > 0 away from the user. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: dy wheel steps (> 0: away from the user; fractions\nfor a trackpad's small steps: Qt's angleDelta / 120) private  subroutine select_view (self, i, duration) Show view i (1 to num_views), flying there over duration s (default:\nthe view transition, set_view_transition ; 0: a cut). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( WindowProxy ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: i real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: duration private  subroutine set_background_color (self, rgb) The background color [r, g, b]