dle, which some contents need while they\nare built (not kept); null: headless). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer a window's viewer handle (null: headless) private  subroutine relayout_labels (self) The labels' size and alignment changed: the name label's in place, the\naxes' labels made again. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self private  subroutine remake_axes (self) The axes and their labels made again (another color, size or font). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self private  subroutine replace_child (self, switch, old, new) Put new in switch in place of old (a kept handle, deleted). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: switch type(c_ptr), intent(inout) :: old type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: new private  subroutine reposition_axes (self) Place the axes for what the frame draws, when it is first shown (unless\nmove_*_axis was called): at its bound's surface, half the bound's radius\nlong (as OpenFrames' Sphere and Model do); at the origin, 1 long, for a\nframe that draws nothing. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self private  subroutine set_attitude (self, q) Attitude relative to the parent frame, a quaternion [x, y, z, w]\n(normalized here; overridden by a followed trajectory). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: q (4) private  subroutine set_color (self, color) The color of the frame's decorations: [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a]. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: color (:) private  subroutine set_label_alignment (self, alignment) The alignm