e Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: radius scene units (0: the body's own) private  subroutine set_length (self, length) How far behind the body's center the shadow is drawn (scene units; 0:\nautomatic, twice the umbra's length). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: length scene units (0: automatic) private  subroutine set_light (self, light, radius) The light (e.g. the Sun; it must stay alive while set), and its radius\n(optional: see set_light_radius). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self class( ReferenceFrame ), intent(in), target :: light real(kind=wp), intent(in), optional :: radius scene units (see set_light_radius) private  subroutine set_light_radius (self, radius) The light's radius (scene units; 0: the light's own, if a Sphere). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: radius scene units (0: the light's own) private  subroutine set_region_color (self, region, color) A region's color (region: one of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA,\nSHADOW_ANTUMBRA; [r, g, b], alpha unchanged, or [r, g, b, a]). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: region SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA or SHADOW_ANTUMBRA real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: color (:) [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1 private  subroutine set_regions (self, regions) The regions to draw: an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA and\nSHADOW_ANTUMBRA (default SHADOW_ALL). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(in) :: regions an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA, SHADOW_ANTUMBRA private  subroutine shadow_bound (self, center, radius) The drawn regions' bounding sphere (frame coordinates). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: center (3) the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) real(kind=wp), intent(out) :: radius the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) private  subroutine shadow_build_contents (self, viewer, group) A switch with a mesh for each region (vertices written at each change\nof shape), under group . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: viewer a window's viewer (null: headless) type(c_ptr), intent(in) :: group the frame's contents group private recursive subroutine shadow_late_update (self, t) After the tree's update for time t: the shadow moved to the body, turned\naway from the light, and reshaped if the distance or a setting changed. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: t the scene time private  subroutine shape_regions (self, r, rs, d) The regions' frustums for body radius r, light radius rs and distance d\n(see the module documentation), written to their meshes. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ShadowCones ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: r scene units real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: rs scene units real(kind=wp), intent(in) :: d scene units private  subroutine write_region (g) A region's frustum into its mesh (uploaded), and shown or hidden. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ShadowRegion ), intent(in) :: g","tags":"","url":"module/vkf_shadow.html"},{"title":"vkf_sphere – vkframes","text":"Spheres and ellipsoids: a textured celestial body, as OpenFrames' Sphere. The body is centered on its frame's origin (or at set_sphere_position ,\nturned by set_sphere_attitude , e.g. to orient a texture). Its shape is a\nsphere of radius , or an ellipsoid with semi-axes radius * sphere_scale ;\nthe ellipsoid is built directly (exact normals, geodetic texture mapping; see\nvkf_geometry), where OpenFrames scales a sphere. The texture is an\nequirectangular image (longitude -180 to 180, north at the top). The color is\nused when there is no texture. Lighting: the body is lit by the scene's lights (a frame's light source,\ne.g. the Sun, or the window's light), with a material ( set_material ;\nOpenFrames' default: no specular reflection). The night texture shows where\nthe surface is lit weakly (the night side: city lights), as OpenFrames'\nsetNightTextureMap: weighted by 1 - the lit color (the material's ambient\nand diffuse colors in the lights' colors and intensities, and its\nemission), per channel and per pixel, so a brighter light narrows the\nband where the day fades into the night, and ambient light dims the night\ntexture. The twilight ( set_twilight ; not in OpenFrames; default none:\nthe light ends at the terminator) extends the diffuse light past the\nterminator, to where the light is a given angle below the horizon, fading\nout: e.g. sunlight scattered by an atmosphere. Translucency (not in OpenFrames): set_opacity (default 1, opaque) below\n1 draws the body translucent: lit as usual, blended over what is behind\nit, drawn after the opaque scene (farthest first: VSG's depth-sorted bin)\nwithout writing depth, front faces only. Whether it is translucent is\ndecided when a window first shows it (as the textures); its opacity can\nthen change at any time (through the material's alpha). Texture files are found with find_data_file (a path, or a name on\nVKFRAMES_DATA_PATH, e.g. data/'s 2k_earth_daymap.jpg and\n2k_earth_nightmap.jpg). The textures and the mesh resolution are read when\na window first shows the sphere: set them before that. The radius, scale,\ncolor and material can change at any time: the meshes are built once, then\nscaled by their transform (radii / the built radii), and the color is applied\nthrough the material (the shaders multiply the vertex color, white here, by\nthe diffuse color). Level of detail ( set_auto_lod , on by default; OpenFrames' setAutoLOD): the\nbody has meshes of 32, 64, ... 1024 segments around (half as many from pole\nto pole), and each view draws the coarsest whose facets stay within half a\npixel of the true outline (src/vsg/vkf_layer.cpp: SphereLod), so that the\nbody isn't faceted however close the view. Meshes are built when a view\nfirst wants them (the 128-segment one at once), in the sphere's update.\nOff: one mesh of set_resolution 's segments (default 128 x 64). Uses iso_c_binding vkf_math vkf_files vkf_geometry vkf_pick vkf_frames vkf_layer module~~vkf_sphere~~UsesGraph module~vkf_sphere vkf_sphere iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~vkf_sphere->iso_c_binding module~vkf_files vkf_files module~vkf_sphere->module~vkf_files module~vkf_frames vkf_frames module~vkf_sphere->module~vkf_frames module~vkf_geometry vkf_geometry module~vkf_sphere->module~vkf_geometry module~vkf_layer vkf_layer module~vkf_sphere->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_math vkf_math module~vkf_sphere->module~vkf_math module~vkf_pick vkf_pick module~vkf_sphere->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_frames->iso_c_binding module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_geometry module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_math module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_pick module~vkf_follower vkf_follower module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_follower module~vkf_text vkf_text module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_text module~vkf_trajectory vkf_trajectory module~vkf_frames->module~vkf_trajectory module~vkf_geometry->iso_c_binding module~vkf_geometry->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_geometry->module~vkf_math module~vkf_layer->iso_c_binding iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~vkf_math->iso_fortran_env module~vkf_pick->module~vkf_math module~vkf_follower->module~vkf_math module~vkf_follower->module~vkf_trajectory module~vkf_text->iso_c_binding module~vkf_text->module~vkf_files module~vkf_text->module~vkf_layer module~vkf_text->module~vkf_math module~vkf_trajectory->iso_c_bind