in) :: alignment an ALIGN_* constant of vkf_frames Return Value logical Subroutines private pure subroutine vsg_alignment (alignment, h, v) The horizontal and vertical alignments of vsg::StandardLayout for an ALIGN_*\nconstant (vkf_frames: 0 left-top ... 8 right-bottom, 9 to 11 base line). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer, intent(in) :: alignment an ALIGN_* constant of vkf_frames integer, intent(out) :: h VSG_* horizontal and vertical alignments integer, intent(out) :: v VSG_* horizontal and vertical alignments","tags":"","url":"module/vkf_text.html"},{"title":"vkf_sky.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_sky.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_sky.f90 vkf_sky.f90 sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sky.f90->sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sky.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sky.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sky.f90->sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~vkf_sky.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_sky.f90 vkf_sky.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sky.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sky.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> The sky behind a scene (OpenFrames' SkySphere): a texture map and/or stars !> from a star catalog, at infinity (they turn with the view, never move with !> it), in the root frame's axes turned by the sky's attitude. A window shows !> a sky with WindowProxy%set_sky; one sky can be shown in several windows. !> !> * Texture: an equirectangular image of the sky (right ascension across, !>   declination down; as a Sphere's texture map), e.g. OpenFrames' !>   Images/StarMap.tif. !> * Stars: a star catalog in OpenFrames' text format (e.g. the HYG v3 !>   catalog of OpenFrames, data/Stars_HYGv3.txt): a header line !>   \"ra[_limit] dec mag ci proper\", then a star per line: right ascension (in !>   hours, or 0 to `limit` if the header says \"ra_limit\", e.g. \"ra_360.0\"), !>   declination (degrees), apparent magnitude, optional B-V color index and !>   name. Stars in a magnitude range are drawn (at most a number of them, in !>   catalog order), sized from their brightness between a minimum and a !>   maximum size (window units), colored from their color index, and the !>   smaller dimmed (OpenFrames' SkySphere::processStars and StarToPoint). !> !> * Star names: the names of the catalog's named stars drawn (those of !>   them up to a magnitude), as labels beside them, at infinity as the stars !>   (behind the scene); off by default (set_star_names). Shown with the !>   stars (draw mode SKY_STARS). !> * Constellations: faint lines between their stars, from a constellation !>   file (e.g. data/inp_Constellation.txt, Chris Dolan's outlines): \"N name\" !>   starts a constellation, then a line per segment, \"dec1 ra1 dec2 ra2\" !>   (degrees, hours), then an optional \"# comment\"; lines starting with \"#\" !>   are comments. Off by default (set_constellations); at infinity, behind !>   the stars, shown unless the draw mode is SKY_NONE. !> !> Both are drawn when given (draw mode SKY_TEXTURE + SKY_STARS); the stars !> over the texture, by the brighter color. module vkf_sky use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_ptr , c_null_ptr , c_associated , c_int , c_float , c_double , c_f_pointer use vkf_math , only : wp , pi , quat_to_matrix use vkf_files , only : find_data_file use vkf_text , only : label_create use vkf_layer , only : check_status , vkf_stars_create , vkf_sky_texture_create , vkf_sky_stars , vkf_sky_stars_changed , & vkf_sky_style , vkf_sky_style_changed , vkf_image_read , vkf_image_delete , & vkf_transform_create , vkf_switch_create , vkf_switch_set , vkf_node_add_child , & vkf_node_remove_child , vkf_node_delete , vkf_compile_node , vkf_transform_set_matrix , & vkf_label_set_at_infinity , vkf_sky_lines_create implicit none private !> What a sky draws (OpenFrames' SkySphere::DrawMode; add them). integer , parameter , public :: SKY_NONE = 0 , SKY_TEXTURE = 1 , SKY_STARS = 2 integer , parameter :: NAME_ALIGNMENT = 1 !! star names' alignment: vkf_frames' ALIGN_LEFT_CENTER !> The constellation file read when none is given: vkframes' (data/). character ( len =* ), parameter , public :: default_constellations = 'inp_Constellation.txt' !> A constellation of those read: its name and its lines (columns of !> self%lines). type :: Constellation character ( len = :), allocatable :: name !! the file's name for it integer :: first = 1 , last = 0 !! its lines: first .. last end type Constellation !> A named star of those read: its name and magnitude, its direction in !> the stars read (self%stars). type :: StarName character ( len = :), allocatable :: text !! the catalog's name integer :: star = 0 !! the star's column in self%stars real ( wp ) :: mag = 0.0_wp !! apparent magnitude end type StarName !> The sky behind a scene (OpenFrames' SkySphere; see the module documentation). type , public :: SkySphere private character ( len = :), allocatable :: texture_file !! texture image file (unallocated or '': none) character ( len = :), allocatable :: catalog !! star catalog file (unallocated or '': none) real ( wp ) :: min_mag = - 2.0_wp , max_mag = 8.0_wp !! OpenFrames' SkySphere defaults integer :: max_stars = 10000 !! the most stars drawn real ( wp ) :: min_size = 1.0_wp , max_size = 1 0.0_wp !! window units real ( wp ) :: min_dim = 0.5_wp !! the smallest stars' color scale (0 to 1) integer :: mode = SKY_TEXTURE + SKY_STARS !! SKY_NONE, or a sum of SKY_TEXTURE and SKY_STARS real ( wp ) :: attitude_ ( 4 ) = [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! in the root frame (quaternion [x, y, z, w]) real ( c_float ), allocatable :: stars (:,:) !! (8, n): direction, size, rgb, - integer :: n_stars = 0 !! stars read: columns of stars used real ( wp ) :: mag_range ( 2 ) = 0.0_wp !! of the stars read type ( StarName ), allocatable :: names (:) !! the named stars read (n_names of them) integer :: n_names = 0 !! named stars read ! star names logical :: names_shown = . false . !! the names are drawn real ( wp ) :: names_max_mag = huge ( 1.0_wp ) !! names of stars up to this magnitude real ( wp ) :: names_size = 1 2.0_wp !! window units real ( wp ) :: names_rgba ( 4 ) = [ 0.6_wp , 0.7_wp , 0.9_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! color character ( len = :), allocatable :: names_font !! font ('' or unallocated: the default) integer :: n_labels = 0 !! names drawn ! constellations character ( len = :), allocatable :: constellation_file !! the file read (unallocated: none yet) real ( c_float ), allocatable :: lines (:,:) !! (8, n): the lines' ends, directions (x, y, z, -) integer :: n_lines = 0 !! lines read: columns of lines used type ( Constellation ), allocatable :: groups (:) !! the constellations read (n_groups of them) integer :: n_groups = 0 !! constellations read logical :: lines_shown = . false . !! the constellations are drawn real ( wp ) :: lines_rgba ( 4 ) = [ 0.35_wp , 0.5_wp , 0.8_wp , 0.45_wp ] !! their color (faint) real ( wp ) :: lines_width = 1.0_wp !! window units ! rendering type ( c_ptr ) :: image = c_null_ptr !! the texture image (null: none) type ( c_ptr ) :: root = c_null_ptr !! the sky's node, a transform (null until made) type ( c_ptr ) :: texture_switch = c_null_ptr !! shows or hides the texture (draw mode) type ( c_ptr ) :: star_switch = c_null_ptr !! shows or hides the stars (draw mode) type ( c_ptr ) :: texture_node = c_null_ptr !! the texture drawing (null: none) type ( c_ptr ) :: star_node = c_null_ptr !! the stars drawing (null: none) type ( c_ptr ) :: name_node = c_null_ptr !! the star names, a transform: the attitude (null: none) type ( c_ptr ) :: line_switch = c_null_ptr !! shows or hides the constellations (draw mode) type ( c_ptr ) :: line_node = c_null_ptr !! the constellations drawing (null: none) logical :: shown = . false . !! made for a window: nodes made later are compiled contains procedure :: set_texture_map , texture_map procedure :: set_star_data , star_catalog , star_magnitudes , star_sizes procedure :: num_stars , star_magnitude_range , star procedure :: set_star_names , star_names , num_star_names , num_star_names_drawn , star_name procedure :: set_constellations , constellations , constellation_file_read , num_constellations procedure :: num_constellation_lines , constellation_name , constellation_lines , constellation_line procedure :: set_draw_mode , draw_mode procedure :: set_attitude , attitude procedure :: node end type SkySphere contains !> Draw an image file as the sky (found with find_data_file); '' for none. !> Returns false if it cannot be read (the sky is then unchanged). logical function set_texture_map ( self , file ) result ( ok ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: file !! image file; '' for none type ( c_ptr ) :: image character ( len = :), allocatable :: path ok = . true . image = c_null_ptr if ( len_trim ( file ) > 0 ) then path = find_data_file ( file ) ok = len ( path ) > 0 if ( ok ) image = vkf_image_read ( path , len ( path , kind = c_int )) ok = c_associated ( image ) if (. not . ok ) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: could not read the sky texture ' // trim ( file ) return end if end if if ( c_associated ( self % image )) call vkf_image_delete ( self % image ) self % image = image self % texture_file = trim ( file ) if ( c_associated ( self % root )) call make_texture_node ( self ) end function set_texture_map !> The texture file ('' for none). function texture_map ( self ) result ( file ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: file file = '' if ( allocated ( self % texture_file )) file = self % texture_file end function texture_map !> Draw the stars of `catalog` (found with find_data_file; '' for none) !> with magnitudes from `min_mag` to `max_mag` (default -2 to 8), at most !> `max_stars` (default 10000), sized from `min_size` to `max_size` window !> units (default 1 to 10) by brightness, the smallest dimmed to !> `min_dim_ratio` (0 to 1, default 0.5) of their color (OpenFrames' !> setSkySphereStarData). Returns false if the catalog cannot be read or the !> limits are invalid (min_mag > max_mag, max_stars < 1, min_size > !> max_size, a ratio outside 0 to 1). logical function set_star_data ( self , catalog , min_mag , max_mag , max_stars , min_size , max_size , min_dim_ratio ) & result ( ok ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: catalog !! star catalog file; '' for none real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: min_mag , max_mag !! apparent magnitudes real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: min_size , max_size !! window units real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: min_dim_ratio !! 0 to 1 integer , intent ( in ), optional :: max_stars real ( wp ) :: mags ( 2 ), sizes ( 2 ), dim integer :: n mags = [ self % min_mag , self % max_mag ] if ( present ( min_mag )) mags ( 1 ) = min_mag if ( present ( max_mag )) mags ( 2 ) = max_mag sizes = [ self % min_size , self % max_size ] if ( present ( min_size )) sizes ( 1 ) = min_size if ( present ( max_size )) sizes ( 2 ) = max_size dim = self % min_dim if ( present ( min_dim_ratio )) dim = min_dim_ratio n = self % max_stars if ( present ( max_stars )) n = max_stars ok = mags ( 1 ) <= mags ( 2 ) . and . n >= 1 . and . sizes ( 1 ) <= sizes ( 2 ) . and . dim >= 0.0_wp . and . dim <= 1.0_wp if (. not . ok ) return self % min_mag = mags ( 1 ) self % max_mag = mags ( 2 ) self % min_size = sizes ( 1 ) self % max_size = sizes ( 2 ) self % min_dim = dim self % max_stars = n self % catalog = trim ( catalog ) self % n_stars = 0 if ( len_trim ( catalog ) > 0 ) ok = read_stars ( self ) if ( c_associated ( self % root )) call make_star_node ( self ) end function set_star_data !> The star catalog file ('' for none). function star_catalog ( self ) result ( file ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: file file = '' if ( allocated ( self % catalog )) file = self % catalog end function star_catalog !> The magnitude range drawn (as set). pure function star_magnitudes ( self ) result ( m ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: m ( 2 ) m = [ self % min_mag , self % max_mag ] end function star_magnitudes !> The size range of the stars (window units). pure function star_sizes ( self ) result ( s ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: s ( 2 ) s = [ self % min_size , self % max_size ] end function star_sizes !> Number of stars read. pure integer function num_stars ( self ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self num_stars = self % n_stars end function num_stars !> The range of magnitudes of the stars read. pure function star_magnitude_range ( self ) result ( m ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: m ( 2 ) m = self % mag_range end function star_magnitude_range !> Star i (1 to num_stars): its direction (unit vector, sky frame), color !> (rgb, dimmed) and size (window units). pure subroutine star ( self , i , direction , rgb , size ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i !! 1 to num_stars real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: direction ( 3 ) !! unit vector, sky frame real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rgb ( 3 ) !! color, dimmed (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: size !! window units direction = real ( self % stars ( 1 : 3 , i ), wp ) size = real ( self % stars ( 4 , i ), wp ) rgb = real ( self % stars ( 5 : 7 , i ), wp ) end subroutine star !> Draw the names of the named stars drawn (those of the catalog's last !> field), beside them: `shown` (default false), of the stars up to !> magnitude `max_mag` (default all of them), `size` window units tall !> (default 12), in color `rgba` (default a pale blue) and font `font` !> ('' or default: vkframes' default font). Also while shown; the !> settings not given are kept. Returns false (nothing changed) if `size` !> isn't > 0. logical function set_star_names ( self , shown , max_mag , size , rgba , font ) result ( ok ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: shown !! draw the names real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: max_mag !! the dimmest named (apparent magnitude) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: size !! height in window units (> 0) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: rgba ( 4 ) !! color [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: font !! font file ('' for the default) ok = . true . if ( present ( size )) ok = size > 0.0_wp if (. not . ok ) return self % names_shown = shown if ( present ( max_mag )) self % names_max_mag = max_mag if ( present ( size )) self % names_size = size if ( present ( rgba )) self % names_rgba = rgba if ( present ( font )) self % names_font = font if ( c_associated ( self % root )) call make_name_node ( self ) end function set_star_names !> Whether the star names are drawn (as set). pure logical function star_names ( self ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self star_names = self % names_shown end function star_names !> Number of named stars read (of the stars read). pure integer function num_star_names ( self ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self num_star_names = self % n_names end function num_star_names !> Number of star names drawn now (0 until the sky is shown, or if the !> names aren't). pure integer function num_star_names_drawn ( self ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self num_star_names_drawn = self % n_labels end function num_star_names_drawn !> Named star i (1 to num_star_names): its name, apparent magnitude and !> star (1 to num_stars: see `star`). subroutine star_name ( self , i , name , mag , which ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i !! 1 to num_star_names character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: name !! the catalog's name real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: mag !! apparent magnitude integer , intent ( out ) :: which !! the star (1 to num_stars) name = self % names ( i )% text mag = self % names ( i )% mag which = self % names ( i )% star end subroutine star_name !> Draw the constellations: faint lines between their stars, from !> constellation file `file` (found with find_data_file; read when given, !> or when first shown without one: default_constellations), `shown` !> (default false), in color `rgba` (default a faint blue, alpha 0.45) and !> `width` window units wide (default 1). Also while shown; the settings !> not given are kept. Returns false if the file can't be read (the !> constellations read before are kept) or `width` isn't > 0 (nothing !> changed). logical function set_constellations ( self , shown , file , rgba , width ) result ( ok ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: shown !! draw the constellations character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: file !! constellation file real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: rgba ( 4 ) !! color [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: width !! window units (> 0) ok = . true . if ( present ( width )) ok = width > 0.0_wp if (. not . ok ) return self % lines_shown = shown if ( present ( rgba )) self % lines_rgba = rgba if ( present ( width )) self % lines_width = width if ( present ( file )) then ok = read_constellations ( self , file ) else if ( shown . and . . not . allocated ( self % constellation_file )) then ok = read_constellations ( self , default_constellations ) end if if ( c_associated ( self % root )) call make_line_node ( self ) end function set_constellations !> Whether the constellations are drawn (as set). pure logical function constellations ( self ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self constellations = self % lines_shown end function constellations !> The constellation file read ('' for none). function constellation_file_read ( self ) result ( file ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: file file = '' if ( allocated ( self % constellation_file )) file = self % constellation_file end function constellation_file_read !> Number of constellations read. pure integer function num_constellations ( self ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self num_constellations = self % n_groups end function num_constellations !> Number of constellation lines read (of all of them). pure integer function num_constellation_lines ( self ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self num_constellation_lines = self % n_lines end function num_constellation_lines !> Constellation i's name (1 to num_constellations). function constellation_name ( self , i ) result ( name ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i !! 1 to num_constellations character ( len = :), allocatable :: name name = self % groups ( i )% name end function constellation_name !> Constellation i's lines (1 to num_constellations): first .. last (see !> constellation_line; none if last < first). pure subroutine constellation_lines ( self , i , first , last ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i !! 1 to num_constellations integer , intent ( out ) :: first , last !! its lines first = self % groups ( i )% first last = self % groups ( i )% last end subroutine constellation_lines !> Constellation line i (1 to num_constellation_lines): its ends' !> directions (unit vectors, sky frame). pure subroutine constellation_line ( self , i , a , b ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i !! 1 to num_constellation_lines real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: a ( 3 ), b ( 3 ) !! unit vectors, sky frame a = real ( self % lines ( 1 : 3 , i ), wp ) b = real ( self % lines ( 5 : 7 , i ), wp ) end subroutine constellation_line !> What to draw: SKY_NONE, or SKY_TEXTURE + SKY_STARS (default; each only !> if given). subroutine set_draw_mode ( self , mode ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: mode !! SKY_NONE, or a sum of SKY_TEXTURE and SKY_STARS self % mode = mode call apply_mode ( self ) end subroutine set_draw_mode !> What is drawn: SKY_NONE, or a sum of SKY_TEXTURE and SKY_STARS. pure integer function draw_mode ( self ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self draw_mode = self % mode end function draw_mode !> The sky's attitude in the root frame (quaternion [x, y, z, w]): e.g. to !> turn an equatorial catalog into an ecliptic root frame. subroutine set_attitude ( self , q ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q ( 4 ) !! quaternion [x, y, z, w] (any length > 0) if ( norm2 ( q ) <= 0.0_wp ) return self % attitude_ = q / norm2 ( q ) call apply_attitude ( self , self % texture_node ) call apply_attitude ( self , self % star_node ) call apply_attitude ( self , self % line_node ) call apply_name_attitude ( self ) end subroutine set_attitude !> The sky's attitude in the root frame (quaternion [x, y, z, w]). pure function attitude ( self ) result ( q ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: q ( 4 ) q = self % attitude_ end function attitude !> The sky's node, made on first use, for a window (WindowProxy%set_sky). !> For a window's `viewer` (null: headless), nodes made later (a new texture !> or catalog) are compiled for the windows running. function node ( self , viewer ) result ( n ) class ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ) :: n if (. not . c_associated ( self % root )) then self % root = vkf_transform_create () self % texture_switch = vkf_switch_create () self % star_switch = vkf_switch_create () self % line_switch = vkf_switch_create () call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % root , self % texture_switch ), 'SkySphere' ) ! the texture first, call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % root , self % line_switch ), 'SkySphere' ) ! the constellations, call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % root , self % star_switch ), 'SkySphere' ) ! the stars over them call make_texture_node ( self ) call make_line_node ( self ) call make_star_node ( self ) self % shown = c_associated ( viewer ) ! (the first nodes are compiled with the scene) end if n = self % root end function node ! ================================================================== ! rendering !> The texture node for the current image, in place of the old one. subroutine make_texture_node ( self ) type ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self if ( c_associated ( self % texture_node )) then call check_status ( vkf_node_remove_child ( self % texture_switch , self % texture_node ), 'SkySphere' ) call vkf_node_delete ( self % texture_node ) self % texture_node = c_null_ptr end if if ( c_associated ( self % image )) then self % texture_node = vkf_sky_texture_create ( self % image ) if ( c_associated ( self % texture_node )) then call apply_attitude ( self , self % texture_node ) if ( self % shown ) call check_status ( vkf_compile_node ( self % texture_node ), 'SkySphere' ) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % texture_switch , self % texture_node ), 'SkySphere' ) end if end if call apply_mode ( self ) end subroutine make_texture_node !> The star node for the current stars, in place of the old one. subroutine make_star_node ( self ) type ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: p integer ( c_int ) :: capacity type ( c_ptr ) :: data if ( c_associated ( self % star_node )) then call check_status ( vkf_node_remove_child ( self % star_switch , self % star_node ), 'SkySphere' ) call vkf_node_delete ( self % star_node ) self % star_node = c_null_ptr end if if ( self % n_stars > 0 ) then self % star_node = vkf_stars_create ( int ( self % n_stars , c_int )) if ( c_associated ( self % star_node )) then data = vkf_sky_stars ( self % star_node , capacity ) if ( c_associated ( data )) then call c_f_pointer ( data , p , [ 8 , int ( capacity )]) p (:, 1 : self % n_stars ) = self % stars (:, 1 : self % n_stars ) call check_status ( vkf_sky_stars_changed ( self % star_node , int ( self % n_stars , c_int )), 'SkySphere' ) end if call apply_attitude ( self , self % star_node ) if ( self % shown ) call check_status ( vkf_compile_node ( self % star_node ), 'SkySphere' ) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % star_switch , self % star_node ), 'SkySphere' ) end if end if call make_name_node ( self ) ! (the names after the stars: in front of them) call apply_mode ( self ) end subroutine make_star_node !> The constellations node for the lines read and the settings, in place of !> the old one (none unless shown). subroutine make_line_node ( self ) type ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: p real ( c_float ), dimension (:), pointer :: style integer ( c_int ) :: capacity type ( c_ptr ) :: data if ( c_associated ( self % line_node )) then call check_status ( vkf_node_remove_child ( self % line_switch , self % line_node ), 'SkySphere' ) call vkf_node_delete ( self % line_node ) self % line_node = c_null_ptr end if if ( self % lines_shown . and . self % n_lines > 0 ) then self % line_node = vkf_sky_lines_create ( int ( self % n_lines , c_int )) if ( c_associated ( self % line_node )) then data = vkf_sky_stars ( self % line_node , capacity ) if ( c_associated ( data )) then call c_f_pointer ( data , p , [ 8 , int ( capacity )]) p (:, 1 : self % n_lines ) = self % lines (:, 1 : self % n_lines ) call check_status ( vkf_sky_stars_changed ( self % line_node , int ( self % n_lines , c_int )), 'SkySphere' ) end if data = vkf_sky_style ( self % line_node ) if ( c_associated ( data )) then ! (the attitude: apply_attitude) call c_f_pointer ( data , style , [ 24 ]) style ( 17 : 24 ) = real ([ self % lines_width , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , self % lines_rgba ], c_float ) end if call apply_attitude ( self , self % line_node ) if ( self % shown ) call check_status ( vkf_compile_node ( self % line_node ), 'SkySphere' ) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % line_switch , self % line_node ), 'SkySphere' ) end if end if call apply_mode ( self ) end subroutine make_line_node !> The star names node for the current names and settings, in place of the !> old one: a label per named star drawn up to the names' magnitude, under !> the stars' switch (shown with them), turned by the sky's attitude. subroutine make_name_node ( self ) type ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ) :: label integer :: i if ( c_associated ( self % name_node )) then call check_status ( vkf_node_remove_child ( self % star_switch , self % name_node ), 'SkySphere' ) call vkf_node_delete ( self % name_node ) self % name_node = c_null_ptr end if self % n_labels = 0 if (. not . self % names_shown . or . self % n_names == 0 ) return if (. not . allocated ( self % names_font )) self % names_font = '' self % name_node = vkf_transform_create () if (. not . c_associated ( self % name_node )) return do i = 1 , self % n_names if ( self % names ( i )% mag > self % names_max_mag ) cycle ! (two spaces: beside the star, not over it) label = label_create ( '  ' // self % names ( i )% text , real ( self % stars ( 1 : 3 , self % names ( i )% star ), wp ), & self % names_rgba , self % names_size , 0.0_wp , NAME_ALIGNMENT , self % names_font ) if (. not . c_associated ( label )) exit ! (no font: said) call check_status ( vkf_label_set_at_infinity ( label , 1_c_int ), 'SkySphere' ) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % name_node , label ), 'SkySphere' ) call vkf_node_delete ( label ) ! (held by the node) self % n_labels = self % n_labels + 1 end do call apply_name_attitude ( self ) if ( self % shown ) call check_status ( vkf_compile_node ( self % name_node ), 'SkySphere' ) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % star_switch , self % name_node ), 'SkySphere' ) call apply_mode ( self ) end subroutine make_name_node !> The sky's attitude into the star names' transform. subroutine apply_name_attitude ( self ) type ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( c_double ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) if (. not . c_associated ( self % name_node )) return m = 0.0_c_double m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ) = quat_to_matrix ( self % attitude_ ) m ( 4 , 4 ) = 1.0_c_double call check_status ( vkf_transform_set_matrix ( self % name_node , m ), 'SkySphere' ) end subroutine apply_name_attitude !> Show or hide the texture, the constellations and the stars (and their !> names), as the draw mode says. subroutine apply_mode ( self ) type ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self if ( c_associated ( self % texture_switch )) & call check_status ( vkf_switch_set ( self % texture_switch , merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , iand ( self % mode , SKY_TEXTURE ) /= 0 )), & 'SkySphere' ) if ( c_associated ( self % star_switch )) & call check_status ( vkf_switch_set ( self % star_switch , merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , iand ( self % mode , SKY_STARS ) /= 0 )), & 'SkySphere' ) if ( c_associated ( self % line_switch )) & call check_status ( vkf_switch_set ( self % line_switch , merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , self % mode /= SKY_NONE )), 'SkySphere' ) end subroutine apply_mode !> The attitude matrix (column-major 4x4) into a sky node's style. subroutine apply_attitude ( self , n ) type ( SkySphere ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: n !! a sky node, texture or stars (null: nothing done) real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: m type ( c_ptr ) :: style if (. not . c_associated ( n )) return style = vkf_sky_style ( n ) if (. not . c_associated ( style )) return call c_f_pointer ( style , m , [ 4 , 4 ]) m = 0.0_c_float m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ) = real ( quat_to_matrix ( self % attitude_ ), c_float ) m ( 4 , 4 ) = 1.0_c_float call check_status ( vkf_sky_style_changed ( n ), 'SkySphere' ) end subroutine apply_attitude ! ================================================================== ! the star catalog (OpenFrames' SkySphere::processStars) !> Read the stars of the catalog into self%stars. logical function read_stars ( self ) result ( ok ) type ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: path character ( len = 1024 ) :: line character ( len = 64 ) :: label real ( wp ) :: ra_limit , ra , dec , mag , ci , raw_min , raw_max , ratio , size , dim , dir ( 3 ), rgb ( 3 ) real ( c_float ), allocatable :: tmp (:,:) integer :: unit , status , k ok = . false . path = find_data_file ( self % catalog ) if ( len ( path ) == 0 ) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: star catalog ' // self % catalog // ' not found (set VKFRAMES_DATA_PATH)' return end if open ( newunit = unit , file = path , status = 'old' , action = 'read' , iostat = status ) if ( status /= 0 ) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: could not open the star catalog ' // path return end if ! right ascension in hours, unless the header says \"ra_<limit>\" ra_limit = 2 4.0_wp read ( unit , '(a)' , iostat = status ) line if ( status == 0 ) then read ( line , * , iostat = status ) label k = index ( label , '_' ) if ( status == 0 . and . k > 0 ) then read ( label ( k + 1 :), * , iostat = status ) ra_limit if ( status /= 0 . or . ra_limit <= 0.0_wp ) ra_limit = 2 4.0_wp end if end if ! sizes from brightness, scaled from [raw_min, raw_max] to [min_size, max_size] raw_max = raw_size ( self % min_mag ) ! the brightest: the largest raw_min = raw_size ( self % max_mag ) if (. not . allocated ( self % stars )) allocate ( self % stars ( 8 , min ( self % max_stars , 1024 ))) self % n_stars = 0 self % n_names = 0 self % mag_range = [ huge ( 1.0_wp ), - huge ( 1.0_wp )] do while ( self % n_stars < self % max_stars ) read ( unit , '(a)' , iostat = status ) line if ( status /= 0 ) exit read ( line , * , iostat = status ) ra , dec , mag , ci if ( status /= 0 ) then read ( line , * , iostat = status ) ra , dec , mag if ( status /= 0 ) cycle ci = 0.0_wp end if if ( mag < self % min_mag . or . mag > self % max_mag ) cycle call star_to_point ( ra / ra_limit * 2.0_wp * pi , dec * pi / 18 0.0_wp , mag , ci , dir , rgb , size ) ratio = 0.0_wp if ( raw_max /= raw_min ) then ratio = ( size - raw_min ) / ( raw_max - raw_min ) size = self % min_size + ratio * ( self % max_size - self % min_size ) else size = self % min_size end if dim = max ( self % min_dim , ratio ) ! big stars at full color, small ones dimmed if ( self % n_stars == size_of ( self % stars )) then allocate ( tmp ( 8 , min ( self % max_stars , 2 * self % n_stars ))) tmp (:, 1 : self % n_stars ) = self % stars (:, 1 : self % n_stars ) call move_alloc ( tmp , self % stars ) end if self % n_stars = self % n_stars + 1 self % stars (:, self % n_stars ) = real ([ dir , size , dim * rgb , 1.0_wp ], c_float ) self % mag_range = [ min ( self % mag_range ( 1 ), mag ), max ( self % mag_range ( 2 ), mag )] call add_name ( self , after_fields ( line , 4 ), mag ) end do close ( unit ) if ( self % n_stars == 0 ) self % mag_range = 0.0_wp ok = . true . end function read_stars !> Read the constellations of `file` (found with find_data_file; '' for !> none) into self%lines and self%groups, in place of those read before. !> False (those kept) if it can't be found or read. logical function read_constellations ( self , file ) result ( ok ) type ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: file !! constellation file ('' for none) character ( len = :), allocatable :: path character ( len = 1024 ) :: line real ( c_float ), allocatable :: lines (:,:), tmp (:,:) type ( Constellation ), allocatable :: groups (:), gtmp (:) real ( wp ) :: v ( 4 ) integer :: unit , status , n , ng , k ok = . true . if ( len_trim ( file ) == 0 ) then self % constellation_file = '' self % n_lines = 0 self % n_groups = 0 return end if ok = . false . path = find_data_file ( file ) if ( len ( path ) == 0 ) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: constellation file ' // trim ( file ) // ' not found (set VKFRAMES_DATA_PATH)' return end if open ( newunit = unit , file = path , status = 'old' , action = 'read' , iostat = status ) if ( status /= 0 ) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: could not open the constellation file ' // path return end if allocate ( lines ( 8 , 1024 ), groups ( 128 )) n = 0 ng = 0 do read ( unit , '(a)' , iostat = status ) line if ( status /= 0 ) exit k = scan ( line , achar ( 13 )) ! (CRLF line ends) if ( k > 0 ) line ( k :) = '' line = adjustl ( line ) if ( line ( 1 : 2 ) == 'N ' ) then ! a constellation if ( ng == size ( groups )) then allocate ( gtmp ( 2 * ng )) gtmp ( 1 : ng ) = groups ( 1 : ng ) call move_alloc ( gtmp , groups ) end if ng = ng + 1 groups ( ng ) = Constellation ( trim ( adjustl ( line ( 3 :))), n + 1 , n ) cycle end if if ( len_trim ( line ) == 0 . or . line ( 1 : 1 ) == '#' ) cycle k = index ( line , '#' ) ! (a comment after the line) if ( k > 0 ) line ( k :) = '' read ( line , * , iostat = status ) v ! dec1, ra1, dec2, ra2 (degrees, hours) if ( status /= 0 ) cycle if ( n == size ( lines , 2 )) then allocate ( tmp ( 8 , 2 * n )) tmp (:, 1 : n ) = lines (:, 1 : n ) call move_alloc ( tmp , lines ) end if n = n + 1 lines (:, n ) = real ([ sky_direction ( v ( 2 ), v ( 1 )), 0.0_wp , sky_direction ( v ( 4 ), v ( 3 )), 0.0_wp ], c_float ) if ( ng > 0 ) groups ( ng )% last = n end do close ( unit ) call move_alloc ( lines , self % lines ) call move_alloc ( groups , self % groups ) self % n_lines = n self % n_groups = ng self % constellation_file = trim ( file ) ok = . true . end function read_constellations !> The unit vector of a direction on the sky from its right ascension !> (hours) and declination (degrees), as the stars' (star_to_point). pure function sky_direction ( ra , dec ) result ( dir ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: ra !! right ascension (hours) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dec !! declination (degrees) real ( wp ) :: dir ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: a , d a = ra / 2 4.0_wp * 2.0_wp * pi d = dec * pi / 18 0.0_wp dir = [ cos ( a ) * cos ( d ), sin ( a ) * cos ( d ), sin ( d )] end function sky_direction !> Remember the name of the star just read (self%n_stars), if it has one. subroutine add_name ( self , name , mag ) type ( SkySphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! its name ('' for none) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: mag !! its apparent magnitude type ( StarName ), allocatable :: tmp (:) if ( len ( name ) == 0 ) return if (. not . allocated ( self % names )) allocate ( self % names ( 64 )) if ( self % n_names == size ( self % names )) then allocate ( tmp ( 2 * self % n_names )) tmp ( 1 : self % n_names ) = self % names ( 1 : self % n_names ) call move_alloc ( tmp , self % names ) end if self % n_names = self % n_names + 1 self % names ( self % n_names ) = StarName ( name , self % n_stars , mag ) end subroutine add_name !> The text of `line` after its first n fields (separated by blanks or !> tabs), trimmed: a star's name ('' if none: e.g. without a color index). pure function after_fields ( line , n ) result ( rest ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: line integer , intent ( in ) :: n !! fields skipped character ( len = :), allocatable :: rest character ( len =* ), parameter :: blanks = ' ' // achar ( 9 ) // achar ( 13 ) integer :: i , j , k rest = '' i = 1 do k = 1 , n j = verify ( line ( i :), blanks ) ! the field's start if ( j == 0 ) return i = i + j - 1 j = scan ( line ( i :), blanks ) ! the blank after it if ( j == 0 ) return i = i + j - 1 end do j = verify ( line ( i :), blanks ) ! the rest, without blanks around it if ( j == 0 ) return i = i + j - 1 k = verify ( line , blanks , back = . true .) rest = line ( i : k ) end function after_fields !> The number of columns of a (the stars' capacity). pure integer function size_of ( a ) real ( c_float ), intent ( in ) :: a (:,:) size_of = size ( a , 2 ) end function size_of !> A star's pixel diameter from its apparent magnitude, from its brightness !> and luminance (OpenFrames' getStarPixelSizeFromMagnitude). pure real ( wp ) function raw_size ( mag ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: mag !! apparent magnitude real ( wp ) :: la , l la = 10 0.0_wp ** ( - 2.0_wp / 5.0_wp ) ! transition luminance l = 10 0.0_wp ** ( - mag / 5.0_wp ) ! relative luminance raw_size = 2.0_wp * sqrt ( l / ( l ** ( 2.0_wp / 3.0_wp ) + la )) end function raw_size !> A star's direction, color (from its B-V color index: Ballesteros' !> temperature, then Tanner Helland's temperature to RGB) and raw size !> (OpenFrames' SkySphere::StarToPoint). pure subroutine star_to_point ( ra , dec , mag , ci , dir , rgb , size ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: ra , dec !! right ascension and declination (radians) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: mag , ci !! apparent magnitude and B-V color index real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: dir ( 3 ) !! unit vector real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: rgb ( 3 ) !! color (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: size !! raw size (as raw_size) real ( wp ) :: t dir = [ cos ( ra ) * cos ( dec ), sin ( ra ) * cos ( dec ), sin ( dec )] size = raw_size ( mag ) t = 0.01_wp * 460 0.0_wp * ( 1.0_wp / ( 0.92_wp * ci + 1.7_wp ) + 1.0_wp / ( 0.92_wp * ci + 0.62_wp )) if ( t <= 6 6.0_wp ) then rgb ( 1 ) = 25 5.0_wp rgb ( 2 ) = 9 9.4708025861_wp * log ( t ) - 16 1.1195681661_wp else rgb ( 1 ) = 32 9.698727446_wp * ( t - 6 0.0_wp ) ** ( - 0.1332047592_wp ) rgb ( 2 ) = 28 8.1221695283_wp * ( t - 6 0.0_wp ) ** ( - 0.0755148492_wp ) end if if ( t >= 6 6.0_wp ) then rgb ( 3 ) = 25 5.0_wp else if ( t <= 1 9.0_wp ) then rgb ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp else rgb ( 3 ) = 13 8.5177312231_wp * log ( t - 1 0.0_wp ) - 30 5.0447927307_wp end if rgb = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 25 5.0_wp , rgb )) / 25 5.0_wp end subroutine star_to_point end module vkf_sky","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_sky.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_follower.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_follower.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~vkf_follower.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90 vkf_hud.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90 vkf_line_segments.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90 vkf_model.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_model.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 vkf_shadow.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90 vkf_shapes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_view.f90 vkf_view.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_view.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_view.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_view.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> Following trajectories: the position and attitude of a frame from one or more !> trajectories at the current time, as OpenFrames' TrajectoryFollower. !> !> With several trajectories, the one followed at time t is the one whose time !> range contains t, or the closest one. If t is outside all of them, FOLLOW_LOOP !> wraps it into their combined time range and FOLLOW_LIMIT holds the ends. !> Positions are interpolated linearly, attitudes by slerp. !> !> The time is either the global simulation time plus an offset !> (`set_offset_time`, the default with offset 0) or a fixed time (`set_time`). !> The trajectories are not owned: they must stay alive while followed. module vkf_follower use vkf_math , only : wp , quat_slerp use vkf_trajectory , only : Trajectory , DataSource , position_sources , SOURCE_ZERO , & TIME_OUT_OF_RANGE , TIME_NOT_FOUND implicit none private !> follow modes (OpenFrames' FollowMode) integer , parameter , public :: FOLLOW_LOOP = 0 !! wrap the time into the trajectories' time range integer , parameter , public :: FOLLOW_LIMIT = 1 !! hold the first/last point outside the time range !> what to follow (OpenFrames' FollowData), combined with ior integer , parameter , public :: FOLLOW_POSITION = 1 !! follow the position integer , parameter , public :: FOLLOW_ATTITUDE = 2 !! follow the attitude !> A pointer to a followed trajectory (for an array of them). type :: TrajectoryPointer type ( Trajectory ), pointer :: p => null () !! the trajectory (not owned) end type TrajectoryPointer !> Follows trajectories (see the module documentation). type , public :: TrajectoryFollower private type ( TrajectoryPointer ), allocatable :: trajs (:) !! (capacity): the followed trajectories integer :: n = 0 !! number of followed trajectories integer :: current = 0 !! index (in trajs) of the trajectory last followed integer :: mode_ = FOLLOW_LOOP !! FOLLOW_LOOP or FOLLOW_LIMIT integer :: data_ = FOLLOW_POSITION + FOLLOW_ATTITUDE !! what is followed (FOLLOW_* combined with ior) type ( DataSource ) :: sources_ ( 3 ) !! where the followed position's x, y, z come from logical :: default_data = . true . !! (true: sources_ are the trajectories' positions) logical :: follow_time = . true . !! (true: simulation time + time_value; false: time_value) real ( wp ) :: time_value = 0.0_wp !! time offset or fixed time (s) real ( wp ) :: last_time_ = 0.0_wp !! time (after looping) at the last update (s) contains procedure :: set_trajectory , add_trajectory , remove_trajectory , remove_all procedure :: num_trajectories procedure :: set_follow_type , follow_mode , follow_data procedure :: set_x_data , set_y_data , set_z_data , data_sources procedure :: set_default_data , using_default_data , data_valid procedure :: set_time , set_offset_time , is_following_time procedure :: last_time , last_trajectory procedure :: update end type TrajectoryFollower contains ! ================================================================== ! trajectories !> Follow only `traj` (none if it is not associated). subroutine set_trajectory ( self , traj ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( Trajectory ), pointer , intent ( in ) :: traj call self % remove_all () if ( associated ( traj )) call self % add_trajectory ( traj ) end subroutine set_trajectory !> Also follow `traj` (no effect if it is already followed). subroutine add_trajectory ( self , traj ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( Trajectory ), pointer , intent ( in ) :: traj type ( TrajectoryPointer ), allocatable :: tmp (:) integer :: k if (. not . associated ( traj )) return do k = 1 , self % n if ( associated ( self % trajs ( k )% p , traj )) return end do if (. not . allocated ( self % trajs )) allocate ( self % trajs ( 4 )) if ( self % n == size ( self % trajs )) then allocate ( tmp ( 2 * self % n )) tmp ( 1 : self % n ) = self % trajs ( 1 : self % n ) call move_alloc ( tmp , self % trajs ) end if self % n = self % n + 1 self % trajs ( self % n )% p => traj if ( self % default_data ) call self % set_default_data () end subroutine add_trajectory !> Stop following `traj`. subroutine remove_trajectory ( self , traj ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( Trajectory ), pointer , intent ( in ) :: traj integer :: k do k = 1 , self % n if ( associated ( self % trajs ( k )% p , traj )) then self % trajs ( k : self % n - 1 ) = self % trajs ( k + 1 : self % n ) self % trajs ( self % n )% p => null () self % n = self % n - 1 if ( self % current >= k ) self % current = max ( 0 , self % current - 1 ) exit end if end do end subroutine remove_trajectory !> Stop following all trajectories. subroutine remove_all ( self ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer :: k do k = 1 , self % n self % trajs ( k )% p => null () end do self % n = 0 self % current = 0 end subroutine remove_all !> Number of trajectories followed. pure integer function num_trajectories ( self ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self num_trajectories = self % n end function num_trajectories ! ================================================================== ! settings !> What to follow (FOLLOW_POSITION and/or FOLLOW_ATTITUDE, combined with !> ior) and how (FOLLOW_LOOP or FOLLOW_LIMIT). subroutine set_follow_type ( self , data , mode ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: data !! FOLLOW_POSITION and/or FOLLOW_ATTITUDE (ior) integer , intent ( in ) :: mode !! FOLLOW_LOOP or FOLLOW_LIMIT self % data_ = data self % mode_ = mode end subroutine set_follow_type !> How time outside the trajectories is handled: FOLLOW_LOOP or FOLLOW_LIMIT. pure integer function follow_mode ( self ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self follow_mode = self % mode_ end function follow_mode !> What is followed: FOLLOW_POSITION and/or FOLLOW_ATTITUDE (combined with ior). pure integer function follow_data ( self ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self follow_data = self % data_ end function follow_data !> Where the x, y and z of the followed position come from (default: the !> trajectories' positions). Returns whether all followed trajectories have !> those data. logical function set_x_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src self % sources_ ( 1 ) = src self % default_data = . false . valid = self % data_valid () end function set_x_data !> Where the y of the followed position comes from (see `set_x_data`). logical function set_y_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src self % sources_ ( 2 ) = src self % default_data = . false . valid = self % data_valid () end function set_y_data !> Where the z of the followed position comes from (see `set_x_data`). logical function set_z_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src self % sources_ ( 3 ) = src self % default_data = . false . valid = self % data_valid () end function set_z_data !> Where the followed position's x, y and z come from. pure function data_sources ( self ) result ( s ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( DataSource ) :: s ( 3 ) s = self % sources_ end function data_sources !> Use the trajectories' positions (per the first trajectory's DOF). subroutine set_default_data ( self ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self if ( self % n > 0 ) then self % sources_ = position_sources ( self % trajs ( 1 )% p % dof ()) else self % sources_ = position_sources ( 0 ) end if self % default_data = . true . end subroutine set_default_data !> True if the followed position is the trajectories' positions (`set_default_data`). pure logical function using_default_data ( self ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self using_default_data = self % default_data end function using_default_data !> True if every followed trajectory has the data the position sources use. pure logical function data_valid ( self ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self integer :: k data_valid = . true . do k = 1 , self % n if (. not . self % trajs ( k )% p % verify_data ( self % sources_ )) data_valid = . false . end do end function data_valid !> Follow at a fixed time (independent of the simulation time). subroutine set_time ( self , t ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the time (s) self % time_value = t self % follow_time = . false . end subroutine set_time !> Follow at the simulation time plus `offset` (the default, offset 0). subroutine set_offset_time ( self , offset ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: offset !! added to the simulation time (s) self % time_value = offset self % follow_time = . true . end subroutine set_offset_time !> True if following the simulation time plus an offset, false for a fixed time. pure logical function is_following_time ( self ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self is_following_time = self % follow_time end function is_following_time !> The time (after looping) at the last update. pure real ( wp ) function last_time ( self ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self last_time = self % last_time_ end function last_time !> The trajectory followed at the last update (null if none). function last_trajectory ( self ) result ( traj ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( Trajectory ), pointer :: traj traj => null () if ( self % current >= 1 . and . self % current <= self % n ) traj => self % trajs ( self % current )% p end function last_trajectory ! ================================================================== ! following !> The position and attitude at simulation time `sim_time`. `has_position` !> and `has_attitude` say whether each could be computed (and is being !> followed); otherwise `position` / `attitude` are left unchanged. subroutine update ( self , sim_time , position , attitude , has_position , has_attitude ) class ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: sim_time !! simulation time (s) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: position ( 3 ) !! the followed position (in the trajectories' frame) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: attitude ( 4 ) !! the followed attitude (quaternion [x, y, z, w]) logical , intent ( out ) :: has_position , has_attitude type ( Trajectory ), pointer :: traj real ( wp ) :: t integer :: status , i has_position = . false . has_attitude = . false . if ( self % n == 0 ) return if ( self % follow_time ) then t = sim_time + self % time_value else t = self % time_value end if t = wrapped_time ( self , t ) self % last_time_ = t self % current = chosen_trajectory ( self , t ) traj => self % trajs ( self % current )% p status = traj % time_index ( t , i ) ! (once, for the position and the attitude) if ( iand ( self % data_ , FOLLOW_POSITION ) /= 0 . and . self % data_valid ()) & call interpolate_position ( traj , self % sources_ , t , status , i , position , has_position ) if ( iand ( self % data_ , FOLLOW_ATTITUDE ) /= 0 ) & call interpolate_attitude ( traj , t , status , i , attitude , has_attitude ) end subroutine update !> For FOLLOW_LOOP, t wrapped into the combined time range of the trajectories. real ( wp ) function wrapped_time ( self , t ) result ( tw ) type ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t real ( wp ) :: t0 , tf , a , b integer :: k tw = t if ( self % mode_ == FOLLOW_LIMIT ) return t0 = huge ( 1.0_wp ) tf = - huge ( 1.0_wp ) do k = 1 , self % n if (. not . self % trajs ( k )% p % time_range ( a , b )) cycle t0 = min ( t0 , a ) tf = max ( tf , b ) end do if ( t0 == huge ( 1.0_wp )) return if ( tf - t0 <= 8.0_wp * tiny ( 1.0_wp )) then tw = t0 else tw = t0 + modulo ( t - t0 , tf - t0 ) ! t - floor((t - t0)/(tf - t0)) * (tf - t0), in real arithmetic end if end function wrapped_time !> The trajectory to follow at time t: the current one if it contains t, !> else the first that does, else the closest. integer function chosen_trajectory ( self , t ) result ( k ) type ( TrajectoryFollower ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t real ( wp ) :: dist , min_dist integer :: j k = 1 if ( self % n == 1 ) return if ( self % current >= 1 . and . self % current <= self % n ) then if ( self % trajs ( self % current )% p % time_distance ( t ) <= 0.0_wp ) then k = self % current return end if end if min_dist = huge ( 1.0_wp ) do j = 1 , self % n dist = self % trajs ( j )% p % time_distance ( t ) if ( dist <= 0.0_wp ) then k = j return else if ( dist < min_dist ) then min_dist = dist k = j end if end do end function chosen_trajectory !> Linear interpolation of the position (from `sources`) at time t; the !> first/last point outside the time range. `status` and `index`: the !> trajectory's time_index for t. subroutine interpolate_position ( traj , sources , t , status , index , position , ok ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: traj type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: sources ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t integer , intent ( in ) :: status , index real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: position ( 3 ) logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! false if there is no position (position unchanged) integer :: n , i ok = . false . n = traj % num_points ( sources ) if ( n == 0 ) return if ( all ( sources % src == SOURCE_ZERO )) then position = 0.0_wp ok = . true . return end if i = index if ( status == TIME_NOT_FOUND ) return if ( status == TIME_OUT_OF_RANGE ) then position = traj % point ( merge ( 1 , n , i < 1 ), sources ) else if ( i >= n ) then position = traj % point ( n , sources ) ! (the last; or fewer points than times: the last available) else position = traj % point_between ( i , i + 1 , t , sources ) end if ok = . true . end subroutine interpolate_position !> Slerp of the attitude at time t; the first/last attitude outside the time !> range. `status` and `index`: the trajectory's time_index for t. subroutine interpolate_attitude ( traj , t , status , index , attitude , ok ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: traj real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t integer , intent ( in ) :: status , index real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: attitude ( 4 ) !! quaternion [x, y, z, w] logical , intent ( out ) :: ok !! false if there is no attitude (attitude unchanged) integer :: n , i real ( wp ) :: frac ok = . false . n = traj % num_attitudes () if ( n == 0 ) return i = index if ( status == TIME_NOT_FOUND ) return if ( status == TIME_OUT_OF_RANGE ) then i = merge ( 1 , n , i < 1 ) attitude = traj % attitude ( i ) else if ( i > n ) then attitude = traj % attitude ( n ) else attitude = traj % attitude ( i ) if ( i + 1 <= n ) then if ( traj % time ( i + 1 ) /= traj % time ( i )) then frac = ( t - traj % time ( i )) / ( traj % time ( i + 1 ) - traj % time ( i )) attitude = quat_slerp ( frac , attitude , traj % attitude ( i + 1 )) end if end if end if ok = . true . end subroutine interpolate_attitude end module vkf_follower","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_follower.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_pick.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_pick.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~vkf_pick.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90 vkf_model.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90 vkf_hud.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90 sourcefile~vkf_view.f90 vkf_view.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_view.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_model.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90 vkf_line_segments.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 vkf_shadow.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90 vkf_shapes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_view.f90 sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_view.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> Picking geometry: what is under a point of a window (WindowProxy%pick). !> !> A PickCamera is the camera and the cursor of a pick, in the scene's root !> frame: the eye and its axes (right, up, forward), the projection, the !> viewport's size and the cursor's position (-1 to 1, y up, as the window's !> events). Frames test their contents against it (ReferenceFrame%pick and !> its extensions): !> * points and line segments on the screen, within a tolerance in pixels !>   (`point_pick`, `segment_pick`: the closest point of a segment, its !>   fraction along the segment in the scene, perspective-correct, and its !>   depth), for trajectories, markers and frames' origins; !> * a ray from the eye through the cursor against an ellipsoid (`ray`, !>   `ray_ellipsoid`), for bodies; !> * the ray against a plane, a sphere and a line (`ray_plane`, !>   `ray_sphere`, `ray_line`), for dragging (WindowProxy%cursor_ray, and !>   vkf_handles' constraints); !> * bounding spheres on the screen (`sphere_near`), to skip whole chunks of !>   a long trajectory. !> Depths are distances along the view direction (perspective) or from the !> eye's plane (orthographic); points closer than `near` are behind the eye. module vkf_pick use vkf_math , only : wp , pi , cross implicit none private !> The camera and cursor of a pick (see the module documentation). type , public :: PickCamera real ( wp ) :: eye ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! the eye (root frame) real ( wp ) :: right ( 3 ) = [ 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp ] !! the camera's right axis (unit vector, root frame) real ( wp ) :: up ( 3 ) = [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! the camera's up axis (unit vector, root frame) real ( wp ) :: forward ( 3 ) = [ 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp ] !! the view direction (unit vector, root frame) logical :: perspective = . true . !! (true: perspective; false: orthographic) real ( wp ) :: tan_y = 0.0_wp !! tan(vertical field of view / 2) real ( wp ) :: aspect = 1.0_wp !! width / height real ( wp ) :: ortho ( 4 ) = [ - 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , - 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! (orthographic: left, right, bottom, top) real ( wp ) :: half_w = 1.0_wp , half_h = 1.0_wp !! half the viewport (framebuffer pixels) real ( wp ) :: x = 0.0_wp , y = 0.0_wp !! the cursor (-1 to 1, y up) real ( wp ) :: tolerance = 6.0_wp !! framebuffer pixels real ( wp ) :: pixel_ratio = 1.0_wp !! framebuffer pixels per window unit (for line widths, marker sizes) real ( wp ) :: near = 0.0_wp !! the smallest depth in front of the eye integer :: kinds = - 1 !! the kinds of hits wanted: bit k for kind k (all) real ( wp ) :: max_depth = huge ( 1.0_wp ) !! hits deeper than this aren't wanted (nearest only) end type PickCamera public :: pick_camera , project , point_pick , segment_pick , sphere_near , ray , ray_ellipsoid , wants public :: ray_plane , ray_sphere , ray_line contains !> The camera of a pick: eye, center and up (root frame), a perspective !> projection (`fovy`, degrees, and `aspect`) or an orthographic one !> (`ortho`: left, right, bottom, top), a viewport of `width` x `height` !> framebuffer pixels, the cursor (x, y: -1 to 1, y up) and the tolerance !> (framebuffer pixels). pure function pick_camera ( eye , center , up , perspective , fovy , aspect , ortho , width , height , x , y , tolerance ) & result ( cam ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: eye ( 3 ), center ( 3 ), up ( 3 ) !! the camera (root frame) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: fovy !! vertical field of view (degrees; perspective) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: aspect !! width / height (perspective) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: ortho ( 4 ) !! left, right, bottom, top (orthographic) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x , y !! the cursor (-1 to 1, y up) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tolerance !! (framebuffer pixels) logical , intent ( in ) :: perspective !! (true: perspective; false: orthographic) integer , intent ( in ) :: width , height !! the viewport (framebuffer pixels) type ( PickCamera ) :: cam real ( wp ) :: f ( 3 ), r ( 3 ), d f = center - eye d = norm2 ( f ) if ( d > 0.0_wp ) f = f / d r = cross ( f , up ) if ( norm2 ( r ) > 0.0_wp ) r = r / norm2 ( r ) cam % eye = eye cam % forward = f cam % right = r cam % up = cross ( r , f ) cam % perspective = perspective cam % tan_y = tan ( 0.5_wp * fovy * pi / 18 0.0_wp ) cam % aspect = aspect cam % ortho = ortho cam % half_w = 0.5_wp * max ( 1 , width ) cam % half_h = 0.5_wp * max ( 1 , height ) cam % x = x cam % y = y cam % tolerance = tolerance cam % near = 1.0e-6_wp * max ( d , tiny ( 1.0_wp )) ! (as the renderer's near plane) end function pick_camera !> Hits of `kind` (vkf_frames' PICK_*) are wanted. pure logical function wants ( cam , kind ) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam integer , intent ( in ) :: kind !! a PICK_* constant of vkf_frames wants = btest ( cam % kinds , kind ) end function wants !> The screen offset (framebuffer pixels) of point p (root frame) from the !> cursor, and its depth; false if it is behind the eye. logical function project ( cam , p , sx , sy , depth ) result ( visible ) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: sx , sy !! offset from the cursor (framebuffer pixels, y up) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: depth !! (scene units) real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ), nx , ny v = p - cam % eye depth = dot_product ( v , cam % forward ) sx = huge ( 1.0_wp ) sy = huge ( 1.0_wp ) visible = . false . if ( cam % perspective ) then if ( depth <= cam % near ) return nx = dot_product ( v , cam % right ) / ( depth * cam % tan_y * cam % aspect ) ny = dot_product ( v , cam % up ) / ( depth * cam % tan_y ) else nx = ( 2.0_wp * dot_product ( v , cam % right ) - ( cam % ortho ( 1 ) + cam % ortho ( 2 ))) / ( cam % ortho ( 2 ) - cam % ortho ( 1 )) ny = ( 2.0_wp * dot_product ( v , cam % up ) - ( cam % ortho ( 3 ) + cam % ortho ( 4 ))) / ( cam % ortho ( 4 ) - cam % ortho ( 3 )) end if sx = ( nx - cam % x ) * cam % half_w sy = ( ny - cam % y ) * cam % half_h visible = . true . end function project !> Point p (root frame) is within the tolerance (plus `extra` pixels, e.g. !> half a marker's size) of the cursor: its distance from it (pixels) and !> its depth. logical function point_pick ( cam , p , pixels , depth , extra ) result ( hit ) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: pixels !! distance from the cursor (framebuffer pixels) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: depth !! (scene units) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: extra !! added to the tolerance (framebuffer pixels) real ( wp ) :: sx , sy , reach hit = . false . pixels = huge ( 1.0_wp ) if (. not . project ( cam , p , sx , sy , depth )) return pixels = hypot ( sx , sy ) reach = cam % tolerance if ( present ( extra )) reach = reach + extra hit = pixels <= reach . and . depth <= cam % max_depth end function point_pick !> Segment a-b (root frame) passes within the tolerance (plus `extra` !> pixels, e.g. half the line's width) of the cursor: the distance !> (pixels) of its closest point, the fraction `s` of the way from a to b !> of that point in the scene (perspective-correct), and its depth. The !> part behind the eye is cut off. logical function segment_pick ( cam , a , b , pixels , s , depth , extra ) result ( hit ) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: a ( 3 ), b ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: pixels !! distance from the cursor (framebuffer pixels) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: s !! fraction of the way from a to b (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: depth !! (scene units) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: extra !! added to the tolerance (framebuffer pixels) real ( wp ) :: da , db , s0 , s1 , p0 ( 3 ), p1 ( 3 ), x0 , y0 , x1 , y1 , z0 , z1 , dx , dy , t , len2 , u hit = . false . pixels = huge ( 1.0_wp ) s = 0.0_wp depth = huge ( 1.0_wp ) ! the part in front of the eye: s0 .. s1 of a-b s0 = 0.0_wp s1 = 1.0_wp if ( cam % perspective ) then da = dot_product ( a - cam % eye , cam % forward ) db = dot_product ( b - cam % eye , cam % forward ) if ( da <= cam % near . and . db <= cam % near ) return if ( da <= cam % near ) s0 = ( cam % near - da ) / ( db - da ) * 1.000001_wp if ( db <= cam % near ) s1 = ( da - cam % near ) / ( da - db ) * 0.999999_wp end if p0 = a + s0 * ( b - a ) p1 = a + s1 * ( b - a ) if (. not . project ( cam , p0 , x0 , y0 , z0 )) return if (. not . project ( cam , p1 , x1 , y1 , z1 )) return ! the closest point on the screen segment (the cursor is at 0, 0) dx = x1 - x0 dy = y1 - y0 len2 = dx * dx + dy * dy t = 0.0_wp if ( len2 > 0.0_wp ) t = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , - ( x0 * dx + y0 * dy ) / len2 )) pixels = hypot ( x0 + t * dx , y0 + t * dy ) ! back to the scene: linear on the screen is not linear in depth u = t if ( cam % perspective ) u = t * z0 / ( t * z0 + ( 1.0_wp - t ) * z1 ) s = s0 + u * ( s1 - s0 ) depth = z0 + u * ( z1 - z0 ) hit = pixels <= cam % tolerance if ( present ( extra )) hit = pixels <= cam % tolerance + extra hit = hit . and . depth <= cam % max_depth end function segment_pick !> A sphere (root frame: center c, radius r) might be within the tolerance !> (plus `extra` pixels) of the cursor on the screen (false only if it !> surely isn't: to skip what it bounds). logical function sphere_near ( cam , c , r , extra ) result ( near ) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: c ( 3 ), r real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: extra !! added to the tolerance (framebuffer pixels) real ( wp ) :: sx , sy , depth , scale , reach near = . true . if ( dot_product ( c - cam % eye , cam % forward ) - r > cam % max_depth ) then ! (all deeper than a hit already found) near = . false . return end if if ( cam % perspective ) then depth = dot_product ( c - cam % eye , cam % forward ) if ( depth <= r + cam % near ) then ! (the eye inside it, or close: can't tell) near = depth > - r return end if if (. not . project ( cam , c , sx , sy , depth )) return scale = cam % half_h / ( cam % tan_y * ( depth - r )) ! pixels per scene unit at its nearest else if (. not . project ( cam , c , sx , sy , depth )) return scale = 2.0_wp * cam % half_h / ( cam % ortho ( 4 ) - cam % ortho ( 3 )) end if reach = cam % tolerance if ( present ( extra )) reach = reach + extra near = hypot ( sx , sy ) <= r * scale + reach end function sphere_near !> The ray from the eye through the cursor (root frame; `dir` a unit vector). pure subroutine ray ( cam , origin , dir ) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) if ( cam % perspective ) then origin = cam % eye dir = cam % forward + cam % x * cam % tan_y * cam % aspect * cam % right + cam % y * cam % tan_y * cam % up dir = dir / norm2 ( dir ) else origin = cam % eye + cam % right * ( cam % ortho ( 1 ) + 0.5_wp * ( cam % x + 1.0_wp ) * ( cam % ortho ( 2 ) - cam % ortho ( 1 ))) & + cam % up * ( cam % ortho ( 3 ) + 0.5_wp * ( cam % y + 1.0_wp ) * ( cam % ortho ( 4 ) - cam % ortho ( 3 ))) dir = cam % forward end if end subroutine ray !> Where the ray (origin, unit dir) first meets the ellipsoid centered at !> `center` with semi-axes `radii` along the columns of `axes` (unit !> vectors): the distance along the ray, the point, and the point in the !> ellipsoid's axes (from its center). False if it misses (or the !> ellipsoid is behind). logical function ray_ellipsoid ( origin , dir , center , axes , radii , distance , point , local ) result ( hit ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the ray (dir: a unit vector) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: center ( 3 ) !! the ellipsoid's center real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: axes ( 3 , 3 ) !! its axes (columns: unit vectors) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radii ( 3 ) !! its semi-axes along them real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: distance !! along the ray (huge() if missed) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: point ( 3 ) !! the point met real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: local ( 3 ) !! the point in the ellipsoid's axes, from its center real ( wp ) :: o ( 3 ), d ( 3 ), qa , qb , qc , disc , t hit = . false . distance = huge ( 1.0_wp ) point = 0.0_wp local = 0.0_wp if ( any ( radii <= 0.0_wp )) return o = matmul ( transpose ( axes ), origin - center ) / radii ! (the unit sphere) d = matmul ( transpose ( axes ), dir ) / radii qa = dot_product ( d , d ) qb = 2.0_wp * dot_product ( o , d ) qc = dot_product ( o , o ) - 1.0_wp disc = qb * qb - 4.0_wp * qa * qc if ( disc < 0.0_wp . or . qa <= 0.0_wp ) return t = ( - qb - sqrt ( disc )) / ( 2.0_wp * qa ) if ( t < 0.0_wp ) t = ( - qb + sqrt ( disc )) / ( 2.0_wp * qa ) ! (the eye inside it: where the ray leaves) if ( t < 0.0_wp ) return distance = t point = origin + t * dir local = ( o + t * d ) * radii hit = . true . end function ray_ellipsoid !> Where the ray (origin, unit dir) meets the plane through `point` with !> normal `normal`: the distance along the ray and the point. False if the !> ray is parallel to the plane (within 1e-6 of it, as a cosine) or the !> plane is behind. logical function ray_plane ( origin , dir , point , normal , distance , hit_point ) result ( hit ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the ray (dir: a unit vector) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: point ( 3 ), normal ( 3 ) !! the plane (normal: any length but 0) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: distance !! along the ray (huge() if missed) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: hit_point ( 3 ) !! the point met real ( wp ) :: n ( 3 ), d hit = . false . distance = huge ( 1.0_wp ) hit_point = 0.0_wp if ( norm2 ( normal ) <= 0.0_wp ) return n = normal / norm2 ( normal ) d = dot_product ( dir , n ) if ( abs ( d ) < 1.0e-6_wp ) return distance = dot_product ( point - origin , n ) / d if ( distance < 0.0_wp ) then distance = huge ( 1.0_wp ) return end if hit_point = origin + distance * dir hit = . true . end function ray_plane !> Where the ray (origin, unit dir) meets the sphere of `center` and !> `radius`: the distances along the ray of where it enters and leaves !> (`near` <= `far`; `near` < 0 if the origin is inside). False if it !> misses, or the sphere is behind. logical function ray_sphere ( origin , dir , center , radius , near , far ) result ( hit ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the ray (dir: a unit vector) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: center ( 3 ) !! the sphere's center real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radius !! its radius (> 0) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: near , far !! distances along the ray (huge() if missed) real ( wp ) :: o ( 3 ), b , c , disc hit = . false . near = huge ( 1.0_wp ) far = huge ( 1.0_wp ) if ( radius <= 0.0_wp ) return o = origin - center b = dot_product ( o , dir ) c = dot_product ( o , o ) - radius * radius disc = b * b - c if ( disc < 0.0_wp ) return if ( - b + sqrt ( disc ) < 0.0_wp ) return near = - b - sqrt ( disc ) far = - b + sqrt ( disc ) hit = . true . end function ray_sphere !> The point of the line through `point` along `axis` closest to the ray !> (origin, unit dir): its parameter `s` (the point is point + s * axis, !> axis normalized) and the point. False if the ray and the line are !> parallel (within 1e-6 of it, as a sine squared), or the closest point !> of the ray is behind its origin. logical function ray_line ( origin , dir , point , axis , s , line_point ) result ( hit ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the ray (dir: a unit vector) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: point ( 3 ), axis ( 3 ) !! the line (axis: any length but 0) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: s !! along the line (scene units, from `point`) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: line_point ( 3 ) !! the point of the line real ( wp ) :: u ( 3 ), w ( 3 ), b , d , e , denom hit = . false . s = 0.0_wp line_point = point if ( norm2 ( axis ) <= 0.0_wp ) return u = axis / norm2 ( axis ) w = point - origin b = dot_product ( u , dir ) d = dot_product ( u , w ) e = dot_product ( dir , w ) denom = 1.0_wp - b * b if ( denom < 1.0e-6_wp ) return s = ( b * e - d ) / denom if (( e + b * s ) < 0.0_wp ) return ! (the ray's closest point: origin + (e + b s) dir) line_point = point + s * u hit = . true . end function ray_line end module vkf_pick","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_pick.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_gui.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_gui.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_gui.f90 vkf_gui.f90 sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_gui.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_gui.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~vkf_gui.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_gui.f90 vkf_gui.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_gui.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_gui.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> GUI panels in a window (not in OpenFrames): Dear ImGui panels, buttons, !> checkboxes and sliders, drawn flat on top of the scene, through vsgImGui. !> !> A window's Gui (`WindowProxy%gui()`, made on first use) is described !> immediate-mode, each frame (e.g. in the event handler's `before_draw`, or !> in the frame loop before `frame()`): panels (`begin_panel` ... `end_panel`) !> holding text, buttons, checkboxes, sliders, combo boxes (drop-down !> menus), separators. A widget's call gives what the user did with it at the !> frame before: `button` is true once after a click; `checkbox`, `slider` !> and `combo` change the value given (and are true then). What isn't described in a frame isn't shown in it. !> !> A panel is placed where ImGui puts it (and can be moved), or at a position !> (0 to 1 across the window, y up, as HUD text), at first or every frame !> (`follow`): e.g. next to a picked object, kept at its screen position !> (WindowProxy%screen_position). A title starting with '##' gives no title !> bar (a callout). Clicks, drags and keys over a panel go to it: the camera, !> the event handler and picking don't get them. The GUI is scaled by the !> window's pixel ratio. A Gui is a handle (copies are the same GUI), valid !> while its window is open. module vkf_gui use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_ptr , c_null_ptr , c_associated , c_int , c_double use vkf_math , only : wp use vkf_layer , only : vkf_gui_begin , vkf_gui_end , vkf_gui_text , vkf_gui_button , vkf_gui_checkbox , vkf_gui_slider , & vkf_gui_separator , vkf_gui_same_line , vkf_gui_combo implicit none private !> A window's GUI panels (see the module documentation). type , public :: Gui type ( c_ptr ) :: handle = c_null_ptr !! the window's GUI in the C++ layer (null: none) contains procedure :: begin_panel , end_panel procedure :: text , button , checkbox , slider , combo , separator , same_line procedure :: is_valid end type Gui contains !> False if the window has no GUI (not open). pure logical function is_valid ( self ) class ( Gui ), intent ( in ) :: self is_valid = c_associated ( self % handle ) end function is_valid !> A panel titled `title` ('##name': no title bar), with the widgets up to !> `end_panel`. `position` ([x, y], 0 to 1 across the window, y up; default: !> where ImGui puts it) is where its point `pivot` is ([0, 0], the default: !> its top left; [0.5, 1]: the middle of its bottom); with `follow`, every !> frame (and it can't be moved), else at first. subroutine begin_panel ( self , title , position , pivot , follow ) class ( Gui ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: title real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: position ( 2 ) !! [x, y] (0 to 1 across the window, y up) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: pivot ( 2 ) !! the panel's point at `position` (0 to 1, from its top left) logical , intent ( in ), optional :: follow !! place it every frame (default false: at first) real ( wp ) :: p ( 2 ), q ( 2 ) integer ( c_int ) :: f p = - 1.0_wp q = 0.0_wp f = 0 if ( present ( position )) p = position if ( present ( pivot )) q = pivot if ( present ( follow )) f = merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , follow ) call vkf_gui_begin ( self % handle , title , len ( title , kind = c_int ), real ( p ( 1 ), c_double ), real ( p ( 2 ), c_double ), & real ( q ( 1 ), c_double ), real ( q ( 2 ), c_double ), f ) end subroutine begin_panel !> End the panel started by `begin_panel`. subroutine end_panel ( self ) class ( Gui ), intent ( inout ) :: self call vkf_gui_end ( self % handle ) end subroutine end_panel !> A line of text. subroutine text ( self , line ) class ( Gui ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: line call vkf_gui_text ( self % handle , line , len ( line , kind = c_int )) end subroutine text !> A button: true once after it was clicked. logical function button ( self , label ) class ( Gui ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: label button = vkf_gui_button ( self % handle , label , len ( label , kind = c_int )) /= 0 end function button !> A checkbox showing `value`: true (and `value` changed) after the user !> changed it. logical function checkbox ( self , label , value ) result ( changed ) class ( Gui ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: label logical , intent ( inout ) :: value integer ( c_int ) :: v v = merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , value ) changed = vkf_gui_checkbox ( self % handle , label , len ( label , kind = c_int ), v ) /= 0 value = v /= 0 end function checkbox !> A slider showing `value`, from `low` to `high`: true (and `value` !> changed) after the user moved it. `format`: how the value is shown !> (printf's, e.g. '%.0f km'; default '%.4g'). logical function slider ( self , label , value , low , high , format ) result ( changed ) class ( Gui ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: label real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: value real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: low , high character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: format real ( c_double ) :: v v = value if ( present ( format )) then changed = vkf_gui_slider ( self % handle , label , len ( label , kind = c_int ), v , real ( low , c_double ), & real ( high , c_double ), format , len ( format , kind = c_int )) /= 0 else changed = vkf_gui_slider ( self % handle , label , len ( label , kind = c_int ), v , real ( low , c_double ), & real ( high , c_double ), '' , 0_c_int ) /= 0 end if value = v end function slider !> A combo box (a drop-down menu) of `items` (trailing blanks trimmed), !> showing item `index` (1-based): true (and `index` changed) after the !> user chose another. logical function combo ( self , label , index , items ) result ( changed ) class ( Gui ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: label integer , intent ( inout ) :: index character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: items (:) character ( len = :), allocatable :: all integer ( c_int ) :: i integer :: k all = '' do k = 1 , size ( items ) all = all // trim ( items ( k )) if ( k < size ( items )) all = all // new_line ( 'a' ) end do i = int ( index - 1 , c_int ) changed = vkf_gui_combo ( self % handle , label , len ( label , kind = c_int ), i , all , len ( all , kind = c_int )) /= 0 index = i + 1 end function combo !> A horizontal separator line. subroutine separator ( self ) class ( Gui ), intent ( inout ) :: self call vkf_gui_separator ( self % handle ) end subroutine separator !> The next widget on the same line as the last. subroutine same_line ( self ) class ( Gui ), intent ( inout ) :: self call vkf_gui_same_line ( self % handle ) end subroutine same_line end module vkf_gui","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_gui.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_trajectory.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_trajectory.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~vkf_trajectory.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90 vkf_hud.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90 vkf_line_segments.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90 vkf_model.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_model.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 vkf_shadow.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90 vkf_shapes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_view.f90 vkf_view.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_view.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_view.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_hud.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_view.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> Trajectory data: times with positions, attitudes and optional data vectors, as !> in OpenFrames' Trajectory. !> !> Data are appended: each time may get one position (with `num_optionals` !> optional vectors), one attitude and one color, so there may be fewer !> positions, attitudes or colors than times (data can arrive separately). !> Colors are optional (not in OpenFrames): a CurveArtist draws a trajectory !> with colors in them, blended along each segment between its points' !> colors (see CurveArtist%set_point_colors). No sorting is done; times !> are expected to be monotonic, increasing or decreasing. Indices are 1-based. !> !> Differences from OpenFrames: !> * Storage grows by doubling, positions, attitudes and colors separately, so !>   a trajectory without attitudes (colors) holds no attitude (color) memory. !>   `reserve` sets it for a known size; `compact` frees what's unused once a !>   trajectory is complete (one copy of each array; `storage_bytes` says !>   what is held). !> * Instead of subscriber callbacks, a trajectory counts its changes !>   (`revision`) and clears (`generation`): a reader such as an artist compares !>   them with what it last saw and updates only what changed (e.g. uploads only !>   the points appended since). !> * No locking: vkframes updates and renders on one thread. !> !> Between points, a trajectory is linear in time: `point_at(t)` is the point !> at any time (the first or last point outside its times), and !> `point_between(k, k2, t)` and `time_fraction(k, k2, t)` the same between !> two points already found (followers, trace mode's tail, intermediate !> markers and time handles use them). module vkf_trajectory use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_float use , intrinsic :: iso_fortran_env , only : int64 use vkf_math , only : wp implicit none private !> where a component of a DataSource comes from (OpenFrames' SourceType) integer , parameter , public :: SOURCE_ZERO = 0 !! 0 integer , parameter , public :: SOURCE_TIME = 1 !! the time integer , parameter , public :: SOURCE_POSOPT = 2 !! an element of the position or of an optional integer , parameter , public :: SOURCE_ATTITUDE = 3 !! an element of the attitude quaternion !> results of Trajectory%time_index (as OpenFrames' getTimeIndex) integer , parameter , public :: TIME_NOT_FOUND = - 2 !! the search did not converge integer , parameter , public :: TIME_OUT_OF_RANGE = - 1 !! index = 0 (before the first time) or num_times + 1 (after the last) integer , parameter , public :: TIME_AT_BOUND = 0 !! index = 1 or num_times (at the first or last time) ! a positive result: found, with times(index) <= t < times(index+1) (for increasing times) !> Where one component (x, y or z) of a point is taken from, as OpenFrames' !> Trajectory::DataSource: `src` is a SOURCE_* constant; for SOURCE_POSOPT, !> `element` (1 to dof) of the position (`opt` = 0) or of optional `opt`; !> for SOURCE_ATTITUDE, `element` (1 to 4) of the quaternion. The value is !> multiplied by `scale`. type , public :: DataSource integer :: src = SOURCE_ZERO !! where the component comes from: a SOURCE_* constant integer :: element = 1 !! element (1 to dof, or 1 to 4 for SOURCE_ATTITUDE) integer :: opt = 0 !! (0: the position, k: optional k (SOURCE_POSOPT)) real ( wp ) :: scale = 1.0_wp !! factor the value is multiplied by end type DataSource !> A trajectory (see the module documentation). type , public :: Trajectory private integer :: dof_ = 3 !! degrees of freedom of positions and optionals (2 or 3) integer :: nopt_ = 0 !! optionals per position integer :: n_times = 0 !! number of times integer :: n_pos = 0 !! number of positions (<= n_times) integer :: n_att = 0 !! number of attitudes (<= n_times) integer :: n_col = 0 !! number of colors (<= n_times) real ( wp ), allocatable :: t (:) !! (capacity): times real ( wp ), allocatable :: posopt (:,:,:) !! (3, 0:nopt, capacity): position, then optionals real ( wp ), allocatable :: att (:,:) !! (4, capacity): quaternions [x, y, z, w] real ( c_float ), allocatable :: col (:,:) !! (4, capacity): colors [r, g, b, a] (as drawn) integer :: revision_ = 0 !! incremented on every change integer :: generation_ = 0 !! incremented when the data are cleared contains procedure :: reserve , compact , storage_bytes procedure :: clear procedure :: set_dof , dof procedure :: set_num_optionals , num_optionals procedure :: num_times , num_positions , num_attitudes , num_colors , is_empty procedure :: add_time , add_position , add_attitude , add_color , set_optional generic :: add => add_point , add_points procedure , private :: add_point , add_points procedure :: time , position , attitude , optional , color procedure :: times , positions , attitudes , colors procedure :: time_range , time_distance , time_index procedure :: point , points , verify_data , num_points procedure :: time_fraction , point_between , point_at procedure :: revision , generation end type Trajectory !> The Trajectory constructor: `Trajectory(...)` makes one (see `new_trajectory` for its !> arguments). interface Trajectory module procedure new_trajectory end interface Trajectory !> The DataSource constructor: `DataSource(...)` makes one (see `new_data_source` for its !> arguments). interface DataSource module procedure new_data_source end interface DataSource public :: position_sources , optional_sources contains ! ================================================================== ! construction and sizes !> A trajectory with `dof` (2 or 3, default 3) degrees of freedom and !> `nopt` (default 0) optional vectors per position. function new_trajectory ( dof , nopt ) result ( traj ) integer , intent ( in ), optional :: dof !! degrees of freedom (2 or 3, default 3) integer , intent ( in ), optional :: nopt !! optional vectors per position (default 0) type ( Trajectory ) :: traj if ( present ( dof )) traj % dof_ = max ( 2 , min ( 3 , dof )) if ( present ( nopt )) traj % nopt_ = max ( 0 , nopt ) end function new_trajectory !> A data source (see `DataSource`); `element` defaults to 1, `opt` to 0, !> `scale` to 1. pure function new_data_source ( src , element , opt , scale ) result ( s ) integer , intent ( in ) :: src !! a SOURCE_* constant integer , intent ( in ), optional :: element !! element (1 to dof, or 1 to 4 for an attitude; default 1) integer , intent ( in ), optional :: opt !! (0: the position (default), k: optional k) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: scale type ( DataSource ) :: s s % src = src if ( present ( element )) s % element = element if ( present ( opt )) s % opt = opt if ( present ( scale )) s % scale = scale end function new_data_source !> The sources of a trajectory's positions: x, y, (z) of the position, and !> zero for components beyond `dof`. pure function position_sources ( dof ) result ( s ) integer , intent ( in ) :: dof !! degrees of freedom (2 or 3) type ( DataSource ) :: s ( 3 ) integer :: k do k = 1 , 3 if ( k <= dof ) s ( k ) = DataSource ( SOURCE_POSOPT , element = k ) end do end function position_sources !> The sources of optional `opt`'s x, y, (z) (zero beyond `dof`, default !> 3), each times `scale` (default 1): e.g. a thrust vector stored per !> point, for SegmentArtist%set_end_data with relative ends. pure function optional_sources ( opt , dof , scale ) result ( s ) integer , intent ( in ) :: opt !! the optional (1 to num_optionals) integer , intent ( in ), optional :: dof real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: scale type ( DataSource ) :: s ( 3 ) integer :: k , d d = 3 if ( present ( dof )) d = dof do k = 1 , min ( 3 , d ) s ( k ) = DataSource ( SOURCE_POSOPT , element = k , opt = opt , scale = scale ) end do end function optional_sources !> Reserve memory for `n` points: times, positions (with their optionals) !> unless `positions` is false, and attitudes and colors only if !> `attitudes` / `colors` is true. Optional: storage grows as needed, but !> reserving avoids reallocations for a known size. It never shrinks the !> storage (see `compact`). subroutine reserve ( self , n , positions , attitudes , colors ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n !! number of points logical , intent ( in ), optional :: positions !! reserve positions (default true) logical , intent ( in ), optional :: attitudes !! reserve attitudes (default false) logical , intent ( in ), optional :: colors !! reserve colors (default false) logical :: pos , att , col pos = . true . att = . false . col = . false . if ( present ( positions )) pos = positions if ( present ( attitudes )) att = attitudes if ( present ( colors )) col = colors call grow_times ( self , n , exact = . true .) if ( pos ) call grow_positions ( self , n , exact = . true .) if ( att ) call grow_attitudes ( self , n , exact = . true .) if ( col ) call grow_colors ( self , n , exact = . true .) end subroutine reserve !> Free the storage not used: each array is reallocated to the points it !> holds (one copy, an array at a time), and arrays holding none are !> deallocated. For a trajectory that is complete: growing doubles the !> storage, so up to about half of it can be unused. The data and what is !> drawn of them don't change; pointers from `times`, `positions`, ... !> must be fetched again. Points can still be added (storage grows again). subroutine compact ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), allocatable :: t (:), posopt (:,:,:), att (:,:) real ( c_float ), allocatable :: col (:,:) if ( allocated ( self % t )) then if ( size ( self % t ) /= self % n_times ) then allocate ( t ( self % n_times )) t = self % t ( 1 : self % n_times ) call move_alloc ( t , self % t ) end if if ( self % n_times == 0 ) deallocate ( self % t ) end if if ( allocated ( self % posopt )) then if ( size ( self % posopt , 3 ) /= self % n_pos ) then allocate ( posopt ( 3 , 0 : self % nopt_ , self % n_pos )) posopt = self % posopt (:, :, 1 : self % n_pos ) call move_alloc ( posopt , self % posopt ) end if if ( self % n_pos == 0 ) deallocate ( self % posopt ) end if if ( allocated ( self % att )) then if ( size ( self % att , 2 ) /= self % n_att ) then allocate ( att ( 4 , self % n_att )) att = self % att (:, 1 : self % n_att ) call move_alloc ( att , self % att ) end if if ( self % n_att == 0 ) deallocate ( self % att ) end if if ( allocated ( self % col )) then if ( size ( self % col , 2 ) /= self % n_col ) then allocate ( col ( 4 , self % n_col )) col = self % col (:, 1 : self % n_col ) call move_alloc ( col , self % col ) end if if ( self % n_col == 0 ) deallocate ( self % col ) end if end subroutine compact !> The memory the trajectory's data take (bytes), used or not: its !> storage's capacity (see `reserve`, `compact`). pure integer ( int64 ) function storage_bytes ( self ) result ( b ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self b = 0_int64 if ( allocated ( self % t )) b = b + storage_size ( self % t , int64 ) / 8 * size ( self % t , kind = int64 ) if ( allocated ( self % posopt )) b = b + storage_size ( self % posopt , int64 ) / 8 * size ( self % posopt , kind = int64 ) if ( allocated ( self % att )) b = b + storage_size ( self % att , int64 ) / 8 * size ( self % att , kind = int64 ) if ( allocated ( self % col )) b = b + storage_size ( self % col , int64 ) / 8 * size ( self % col , kind = int64 ) end function storage_bytes !> Remove all points (keeping the memory). subroutine clear ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self self % n_times = 0 self % n_pos = 0 self % n_att = 0 self % n_col = 0 self % generation_ = self % generation_ + 1 self % revision_ = self % revision_ + 1 end subroutine clear !> Set the degrees of freedom (2 or 3) of positions and optionals; clears the trajectory. subroutine set_dof ( self , dof ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: dof self % dof_ = max ( 2 , min ( 3 , dof )) call self % clear () end subroutine set_dof !> Degrees of freedom (2 or 3) of positions and optionals. pure integer function dof ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self dof = self % dof_ end function dof !> Set the number of optional vectors per position; clears the trajectory. subroutine set_num_optionals ( self , nopt ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: nopt if ( nopt /= self % nopt_ . and . allocated ( self % posopt )) deallocate ( self % posopt ) self % nopt_ = max ( 0 , nopt ) call self % clear () end subroutine set_num_optionals !> Number of optional vectors per position. pure integer function num_optionals ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self num_optionals = self % nopt_ end function num_optionals !> Number of times. pure integer function num_times ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self num_times = self % n_times end function num_times !> Number of positions (at most num_times). pure integer function num_positions ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self num_positions = self % n_pos end function num_positions !> Number of attitudes (at most num_times). pure integer function num_attitudes ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self num_attitudes = self % n_att end function num_attitudes !> Number of colors (at most num_times). pure integer function num_colors ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self num_colors = self % n_col end function num_colors !> True if the trajectory has no times. pure logical function is_empty ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self is_empty = self % n_times == 0 end function is_empty !> Number of changes so far (any added, set or cleared data). pure integer function revision ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self revision = self % revision_ end function revision !> Number of times the data were cleared (by `clear`, `set_dof` or !> `set_num_optionals`): while it is unchanged, data were only appended. pure integer function generation ( self ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self generation = self % generation_ end function generation ! ================================================================== ! adding data !> Add a time at the end of the time list. subroutine add_time ( self , t ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t call grow_times ( self , self % n_times + 1 ) self % n_times = self % n_times + 1 self % t ( self % n_times ) = t self % revision_ = self % revision_ + 1 end subroutine add_time !> Add a position (the first `dof` elements of `pos` are used) for the next !> time that has none. `ok` is false if every time already has a position. subroutine add_position ( self , pos , ok ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: pos (:) logical , intent ( out ), optional :: ok !! false if not added integer :: d if ( present ( ok )) ok = . false . if ( self % n_pos >= self % n_times ) return call grow_positions ( self , self % n_pos + 1 ) self % n_pos = self % n_pos + 1 d = min ( self % dof_ , size ( pos )) self % posopt (:, :, self % n_pos ) = 0.0_wp self % posopt ( 1 : d , 0 , self % n_pos ) = pos ( 1 : d ) self % revision_ = self % revision_ + 1 if ( present ( ok )) ok = . true . end subroutine add_position !> Add an attitude quaternion [x, y, z, w] for the next time that has none. !> `ok` is false if every time already has an attitude. subroutine add_attitude ( self , q , ok ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q ( 4 ) !! quaternion [x, y, z, w] logical , intent ( out ), optional :: ok !! false if not added if ( present ( ok )) ok = . false . if ( self % n_att >= self % n_times ) return call grow_attitudes ( self , self % n_att + 1 ) self % n_att = self % n_att + 1 self % att (:, self % n_att ) = q self % revision_ = self % revision_ + 1 if ( present ( ok )) ok = . true . end subroutine add_attitude !> Add a color ([r, g, b], alpha 1, or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1) for the next !> time that has none. `ok` is false if every time already has a color. subroutine add_color ( self , color , ok ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) logical , intent ( out ), optional :: ok !! false if not added if ( present ( ok )) ok = . false . if ( self % n_col >= self % n_times ) return call grow_colors ( self , self % n_col + 1 ) self % n_col = self % n_col + 1 call to_float_rgba ( self % col (:, self % n_col ), color ) self % revision_ = self % revision_ + 1 if ( present ( ok )) ok = . true . end subroutine add_color !> rgba from [r, g, b] (alpha 1) or [r, g, b, a]. pure subroutine to_float_rgba ( rgba , color ) real ( c_float ), intent ( out ) :: rgba ( 4 ) !! [r, g, b, a] real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) integer :: n n = min ( 4 , size ( color )) rgba = 1.0_c_float rgba ( 1 : n ) = real ( color ( 1 : n ), c_float ) end subroutine to_float_rgba !> Set optional vector `index` (1 to num_optionals) of the most recently !> added position. `ok` is false if there is no position or no such optional. subroutine set_optional ( self , index , v , ok ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: index !! the optional (1 to num_optionals) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: v (:) !! the vector (its first `dof` elements are used) logical , intent ( out ), optional :: ok !! false if not set integer :: d if ( present ( ok )) ok = . false . if ( index < 1 . or . index > self % nopt_ . or . self % n_pos == 0 ) return d = min ( self % dof_ , size ( v )) self % posopt ( 1 : d , index , self % n_pos ) = v ( 1 : d ) self % revision_ = self % revision_ + 1 if ( present ( ok )) ok = . true . end subroutine set_optional !> Add a point: a time with an optional position, attitude and color !> ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]). subroutine add_point ( self , t , pos , att , color ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! time real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: pos (:) !! position (first `dof` elements used) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: att ( 4 ) !! attitude quaternion [x, y, z, w] real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call self % add_time ( t ) if ( present ( pos )) call self % add_position ( pos ) if ( present ( att )) call self % add_attitude ( att ) if ( present ( color )) call self % add_color ( color ) end subroutine add_point !> Add points in bulk: times `t(n)`, with optional positions `pos(dof, n)`, !> attitudes `att(4, n)` and colors `color(3 or 4, n)`. Times, positions, !> attitudes and colors must all have been complete before (as many of each !> as times) for the given ones to line up with `t`. subroutine add_points ( self , t , pos , att , color ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t (:) !! (n): times real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: pos (:,:) !! (dof, n): positions real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: att (:,:) !! (4, n): attitude quaternions [x, y, z, w] real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:,:) !! (3 or 4, n): colors [r, g, b(, a)] (0 to 1) integer :: n , i0 , d n = size ( t ) i0 = self % n_times call grow_times ( self , i0 + n ) self % t ( i0 + 1 : i0 + n ) = t self % n_times = i0 + n if ( present ( pos )) then n = min ( size ( pos , 2 ), self % n_times - self % n_pos ) d = min ( self % dof_ , size ( pos , 1 )) call grow_positions ( self , self % n_pos + n ) self % posopt (:, :, self % n_pos + 1 : self % n_pos + n ) = 0.0_wp self % posopt ( 1 : d , 0 , self % n_pos + 1 : self % n_pos + n ) = pos ( 1 : d , 1 : n ) self % n_pos = self % n_pos + n end if if ( present ( att )) then n = min ( size ( att , 2 ), self % n_times - self % n_att ) call grow_attitudes ( self , self % n_att + n ) self % att (:, self % n_att + 1 : self % n_att + n ) = att (:, 1 : n ) self % n_att = self % n_att + n end if if ( present ( color )) then n = min ( size ( color , 2 ), self % n_times - self % n_col ) d = min ( 4 , size ( color , 1 )) call grow_colors ( self , self % n_col + n ) self % col (:, self % n_col + 1 : self % n_col + n ) = 1.0_c_float self % col ( 1 : d , self % n_col + 1 : self % n_col + n ) = real ( color ( 1 : d , 1 : n ), c_float ) self % n_col = self % n_col + n end if self % revision_ = self % revision_ + 1 end subroutine add_points ! ================================================================== ! reading data !> Time i. pure real ( wp ) function time ( self , i ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i time = self % t ( i ) end function time !> Position i (z = 0 for a 2-DOF trajectory). pure function position ( self , i ) result ( p ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) p = self % posopt (:, 0 , i ) end function position !> Attitude i (quaternion [x, y, z, w]). pure function attitude ( self , i ) result ( q ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: q ( 4 ) q = self % att (:, i ) end function attitude !> Color i ([r, g, b, a]). pure function color ( self , i ) result ( c ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = real ( self % col (:, i ), wp ) end function color !> Optional vector k (1 to num_optionals) of position i. pure function optional ( self , i , k ) result ( v ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i , k real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) v = self % posopt (:, k , i ) end function optional !> Pointer to the times (num_times), without copying. subroutine times ( self , t ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: self real ( wp ), dimension (:), pointer , intent ( out ) :: t if ( self % n_times == 0 ) then t => null () else t => self % t ( 1 : self % n_times ) end if end subroutine times !> Pointer to the positions (3, num_positions), without copying. subroutine positions ( self , p ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: self real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), pointer , intent ( out ) :: p if ( self % n_pos == 0 ) then p => null () else p => self % posopt (:, 0 , 1 : self % n_pos ) end if end subroutine positions !> Pointer to the attitudes (4, num_attitudes), without copying. subroutine attitudes ( self , q ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: self real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), pointer , intent ( out ) :: q if ( self % n_att == 0 ) then q => null () else q => self % att (:, 1 : self % n_att ) end if end subroutine attitudes !> Pointer to the colors (4, num_colors; single precision, as drawn), !> without copying. subroutine colors ( self , c ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: self real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer , intent ( out ) :: c if ( self % n_col == 0 ) then c => null () else c => self % col (:, 1 : self % n_col ) end if end subroutine colors !> The first and last times, ordered (t0 <= tf); false if there are no times. logical function time_range ( self , t0 , tf ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: t0 , tf time_range = self % n_times > 0 if (. not . time_range ) then t0 = 0.0_wp tf = 0.0_wp return end if t0 = min ( self % t ( 1 ), self % t ( self % n_times )) tf = max ( self % t ( 1 ), self % t ( self % n_times )) end function time_range !> The \"distance\" from time t to the time range [t0, tf]: > 0 outside it (to !> the nearer end), 0 at its ends, < 0 inside; huge() without times. !> (OpenFrames' getTimeDistance.) pure real ( wp ) function time_distance ( self , t ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t real ( wp ) :: t0 , tf if ( self % n_times == 0 ) then time_distance = huge ( 1.0_wp ) return end if t0 = min ( self % t ( 1 ), self % t ( self % n_times )) tf = max ( self % t ( 1 ), self % t ( self % n_times )) if ( t <= t0 ) then time_distance = t0 - t else if ( t >= tf ) then time_distance = t - tf else time_distance = ( t - t0 ) * ( t - tf ) end if end function time_distance !> Find the interval of the time list containing t, by bisection (times !> increasing or decreasing). Returns a TIME_* code, or the number of !> iterations (> 0) when found, with times(index) <= t < times(index+1) for !> increasing times (>= and > for decreasing). See the TIME_* constants for !> `index` in the other cases. integer function time_index ( self , t , index ) result ( status ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t integer , intent ( out ) :: index !! the interval's first index (see the TIME_* constants) integer :: low , high , mid , iter , n real ( wp ) :: dir , dist n = self % n_times if ( n == 0 ) then index = 0 status = TIME_OUT_OF_RANGE return end if dir = merge ( 1.0_wp , - 1.0_wp , self % t ( 1 ) <= self % t ( n )) dist = self % time_distance ( t ) if ( dist > 0.0_wp ) then index = merge ( 0 , n + 1 , dir * t < dir * self % t ( 1 )) status = TIME_OUT_OF_RANGE return else if ( dist == 0.0_wp ) then index = merge ( 1 , n , t == self % t ( 1 )) status = TIME_AT_BOUND return end if low = 1 high = n do iter = 1 , 64 mid = low + ( high - low ) / 2 if ( dir * t < dir * self % t ( mid )) then high = mid else low = mid end if if ( high - low <= 1 ) then index = low status = iter return end if end do index = low status = TIME_NOT_FOUND end function time_index !> The fraction of the way in time from point k to point k2 (any two !> points: e.g. k + 1, or k - 1 with times running backward) at time t, !> kept within 0 to 1 (0 if their times are the same). No checks: k and k2 !> must be times. pure real ( wp ) function time_fraction ( self , k , k2 , t ) result ( frac ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: k , k2 !! the points (1 to num_times) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the time frac = 0.0_wp if ( self % t ( k2 ) /= self % t ( k )) frac = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , ( t - self % t ( k )) / ( self % t ( k2 ) - self % t ( k )))) end function time_fraction !> The point at time t between points k and k2 (components from !> `sources`): linear in time, within the two (time_fraction). Point k if !> k2 isn't a point (beyond the ends, or more times than data). pure function point_between ( self , k , k2 , t , sources ) result ( v ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: k !! a point (1 to num_points(sources)) integer , intent ( in ) :: k2 !! the other point (e.g. k + 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the time type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: sources ( 3 ) !! where the components come from real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) v = self % point ( k , sources ) if ( k2 < 1 . or . k2 > self % num_points ( sources )) return v = v + self % time_fraction ( k , k2 , t ) * ( self % point ( k2 , sources ) - v ) end function point_between !> The point at time t (components from `sources`; default: the !> position's), linear in time between the points about it; outside the !> times, the first or last point. `ok` (optional) false, and v 0, if there !> is no point (or the search for the time failed). function point_at ( self , t , sources , ok ) result ( v ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the time type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ), optional :: sources ( 3 ) !! where the components come from (default: the position) logical , intent ( out ), optional :: ok !! a point was found real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) type ( DataSource ) :: src ( 3 ) integer :: n , i , status v = 0.0_wp if ( present ( ok )) ok = . false . src = position_sources ( self % dof_ ) if ( present ( sources )) src = sources n = min ( self % n_times , self % num_points ( src )) if ( n == 0 ) return status = self % time_index ( t , i ) if ( status == TIME_NOT_FOUND ) return if ( i < 1 ) then v = self % point ( 1 , src ) else if ( i >= n ) then v = self % point ( n , src ) else v = self % point_between ( i , i + 1 , t , src ) end if if ( present ( ok )) ok = . true . end function point_at !> Point i with components from `sources` (OpenFrames' getPoint). No checks: !> use `verify_data` and `num_points` first. pure function point ( self , i , sources ) result ( v ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: sources ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) integer :: k do k = 1 , 3 select case ( sources ( k )% src ) case ( SOURCE_TIME ) v ( k ) = sources ( k )% scale * self % t ( i ) case ( SOURCE_POSOPT ) v ( k ) = sources ( k )% scale * self % posopt ( sources ( k )% element , sources ( k )% opt , i ) case ( SOURCE_ATTITUDE ) v ( k ) = sources ( k )% scale * self % att ( sources ( k )% element , i ) case default v ( k ) = 0.0_wp end select end do end function point !> Points i1, i1 + stride, ... (up to i2) with components from `sources`, into !> v(3, :) (as many columns as points; `point` for a range, a whole array !> slice per component). No checks: use `verify_data` and `num_points` first. pure subroutine points ( self , i1 , i2 , sources , v , stride ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i1 , i2 type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: sources ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: v (:,:) !! (3, number of points) integer , intent ( in ), optional :: stride !! step between points (default 1) integer :: k , s s = 1 if ( present ( stride )) s = stride do k = 1 , 3 associate ( src => sources ( k )) select case ( src % src ) case ( SOURCE_TIME ) v ( k , :) = src % scale * self % t ( i1 : i2 : s ) case ( SOURCE_POSOPT ) v ( k , :) = src % scale * self % posopt ( src % element , src % opt , i1 : i2 : s ) case ( SOURCE_ATTITUDE ) v ( k , :) = src % scale * self % att ( src % element , i1 : i2 : s ) case default v ( k , :) = 0.0_wp end select end associate end do end subroutine points !> True if the trajectory has the data the sources refer to (elements and !> optionals in range). pure logical function verify_data ( self , sources ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: sources ( 3 ) integer :: k verify_data = . true . do k = 1 , 3 select case ( sources ( k )% src ) case ( SOURCE_ZERO , SOURCE_TIME ) case ( SOURCE_POSOPT ) if ( sources ( k )% element < 1 . or . sources ( k )% element > self % dof_ . or . & sources ( k )% opt < 0 . or . sources ( k )% opt > self % nopt_ ) verify_data = . false . case ( SOURCE_ATTITUDE ) if ( sources ( k )% element < 1 . or . sources ( k )% element > 4 ) verify_data = . false . case default verify_data = . false . end select end do end function verify_data !> Number of points available with these sources: the number of times, !> limited by the positions or attitudes they use; huge() if all are zero. pure integer function num_points ( self , sources ) class ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: sources ( 3 ) integer :: k if ( all ( sources % src == SOURCE_ZERO )) then num_points = huge ( 0 ) return end if num_points = self % n_times do k = 1 , 3 if ( sources ( k )% src == SOURCE_POSOPT ) num_points = min ( num_points , self % n_pos ) if ( sources ( k )% src == SOURCE_ATTITUDE ) num_points = min ( num_points , self % n_att ) end do end function num_points ! ================================================================== ! storage (amortized doubling) !> The capacity to grow to for `needed` points: twice the current, or what is !> needed and a quarter more (so that appending after a large bulk add !> doesn't copy everything at once); `exact` (reserve): what is needed. pure integer function new_capacity ( current , needed , exact ) integer , intent ( in ) :: current !! current capacity integer , intent ( in ) :: needed !! points needed logical , intent ( in ), optional :: exact new_capacity = max ( needed + needed / 4 , 2 * current , 16 ) if ( present ( exact )) then if ( exact ) new_capacity = needed end if end function new_capacity !> Grow the times' storage to hold at least `n` (see `new_capacity`). subroutine grow_times ( self , n , exact ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n logical , intent ( in ), optional :: exact real ( wp ), allocatable :: tmp (:) integer :: cap cap = 0 if ( allocated ( self % t )) cap = size ( self % t ) if ( n <= cap ) return allocate ( tmp ( new_capacity ( cap , n , exact ))) if ( self % n_times > 0 ) tmp ( 1 : self % n_times ) = self % t ( 1 : self % n_times ) call move_alloc ( tmp , self % t ) end subroutine grow_times !> Grow the positions' (and optionals') storage to hold at least `n`. subroutine grow_positions ( self , n , exact ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n logical , intent ( in ), optional :: exact real ( wp ), allocatable :: tmp (:,:,:) integer :: cap cap = 0 if ( allocated ( self % posopt )) cap = size ( self % posopt , 3 ) if ( n <= cap ) return allocate ( tmp ( 3 , 0 : self % nopt_ , new_capacity ( cap , n , exact ))) if ( self % n_pos > 0 ) tmp (:, :, 1 : self % n_pos ) = self % posopt (:, :, 1 : self % n_pos ) call move_alloc ( tmp , self % posopt ) end subroutine grow_positions !> Grow the attitudes' storage to hold at least `n`. subroutine grow_attitudes ( self , n , exact ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n logical , intent ( in ), optional :: exact real ( wp ), allocatable :: tmp (:,:) integer :: cap cap = 0 if ( allocated ( self % att )) cap = size ( self % att , 2 ) if ( n <= cap ) return allocate ( tmp ( 4 , new_capacity ( cap , n , exact ))) if ( self % n_att > 0 ) tmp (:, 1 : self % n_att ) = self % att (:, 1 : self % n_att ) call move_alloc ( tmp , self % att ) end subroutine grow_attitudes !> Grow the colors' storage to hold at least `n`. subroutine grow_colors ( self , n , exact ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n logical , intent ( in ), optional :: exact real ( c_float ), allocatable :: tmp (:,:) integer :: cap cap = 0 if ( allocated ( self % col )) cap = size ( self % col , 2 ) if ( n <= cap ) return allocate ( tmp ( 4 , new_capacity ( cap , n , exact ))) if ( self % n_col > 0 ) tmp (:, 1 : self % n_col ) = self % col (:, 1 : self % n_col ) call move_alloc ( tmp , self % col ) end subroutine grow_colors end module vkf_trajectory","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_trajectory.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_terrain.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_terrain.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~vkf_terrain.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 vkf_shadow.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> Maps and terrain: a celestial body drawn from map layers by Rocky !> (https://github.com/pelicanmapping/rocky; optional: `rocky_available()`), !> e.g. the Earth from tile services, or the Moon with NASA's imagery and !> LOLA's elevation. An addition to OpenFrames, which has only textured !> spheres. !> !> The body is centered on its frame's origin, in body-fixed axes (z through !> the north pole, x through longitude 0), so the frame's attitude turns it. !> Its shape and coordinates come from Rocky's tiling profile: '' (Rocky's !> default) or 'global-geodetic' for the Earth (WGS84), 'moon' for the Moon !> (a sphere of 1737.4 km), or another of Rocky's profiles. Rocky works in !> meters; the body is drawn at `units_per_meter` scene units per meter !> (default 1e-3: kilometers, as vkframes' examples). !> !> Layers (`add_image_layer`, `add_elevation_layer`) are tiled sources Rocky !> pages in as the view needs them: a TMS service (LAYER_TMS), a file or !> service GDAL reads (LAYER_GDAL; a file is found with find_data_file, e.g. !> data/'s moon_lola_ldem16.tif from `pixi run -e rocky moon-data`), or a !> {z}/{x}/{y} URL template of geodetic tiles on the body (LAYER_GEODETIC: 2 x !> 1 tiles at level 0, rows from the top, as WMTS and NASA's Moon Trek) or of !> web Mercator tiles (LAYER_MERCATOR: OpenStreetMap-style). Elevation is in !> meters (ELEVATION_HEIGHTS) or encoded in RGB (ELEVATION_MAPBOX, !> ELEVATION_TERRARIUM). Layers can be added before or after the body is !> shown. !> !> Lighting: lit by the scene's lights as a Sphere (a frame's light source, e.g. !> the Sun, or the window's light; `set_lighting(.false.)` shows the imagery !> as it is). The frame's color is the color where no imagery covers the body. !> !> The map is made for a window that shows the body (Rocky's tiles are loaded !> through that window's viewer, and the map is drawn in that window only); !> when that window closes, it is made again for one still open (other !> windows then show it). Headless (no viewer), the body has no map. module vkf_terrain use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_ptr , c_null_ptr , c_associated , c_int , c_float , c_double use vkf_math , only : wp , identity_matrix use vkf_frames , only : ReferenceFrame , PickHit , pick_ellipsoid use vkf_pick , only : PickCamera use vkf_layer , only : vkf_rocky_available , vkf_rocky_map_create , vkf_rocky_map_settings , vkf_rocky_map_alive , & vkf_rocky_add_image , vkf_rocky_add_elevation , vkf_rocky_elevation , vkf_node_add_child , & vkf_node_remove_child , vkf_node_delete , vkf_compile_node , vkf_viewer_any use vkf_files , only : find_data_file implicit none private public :: rocky_available !> layer sources (see the module documentation) integer , parameter , public :: LAYER_TMS = 0 !! a TMS service integer , parameter , public :: LAYER_GDAL = 1 !! a file or service GDAL reads integer , parameter , public :: LAYER_GEODETIC = 2 !! a {z}/{x}/{y} URL template of geodetic tiles integer , parameter , public :: LAYER_MERCATOR = 3 !! a {z}/{x}/{y} URL template of web Mercator tiles !> elevation encodings integer , parameter , public :: ELEVATION_HEIGHTS = 0 !! heights in meters integer , parameter , public :: ELEVATION_MAPBOX = 1 !! Mapbox Terrain-RGB integer , parameter , public :: ELEVATION_TERRARIUM = 2 !! Terrarium RGB real ( wp ), parameter :: earth_radius = 637813 7.0_wp !! m (WGS84) real ( wp ), parameter :: moon_radius = 173740 0.0_wp !! m !> A map layer as given (applied when the map is made). type :: MapLayer logical :: elevation = . false . !! (true: an elevation layer; false: an image layer) integer :: source = LAYER_TMS !! a LAYER_* constant integer :: encoding = ELEVATION_HEIGHTS !! (elevation: an ELEVATION_* constant) character ( len = :), allocatable :: uri !! URL, URL template or file end type MapLayer !> A body drawn from map layers by Rocky (see the module documentation). type , extends ( ReferenceFrame ), public :: TerrainBody private character ( len = :), allocatable :: profile_ !! Rocky's tiling profile ('': the Earth) real ( wp ) :: units_per_meter_ = 1.0e-3_wp !! scene units per meter logical :: lighting_ = . true . !! lit by the scene's lights type ( MapLayer ), allocatable :: layers (:) !! (capacity): the layers, in the order added integer :: n_layers = 0 !! number of layers type ( c_ptr ) :: map = c_null_ptr !! Rocky's map node (null: not made) type ( c_ptr ) :: map_group = c_null_ptr !! the group the map is in (once shown) contains procedure :: add_image_layer , add_elevation_layer , num_layers procedure :: set_lighting , lighting procedure :: profile , units_per_meter , body_radius , elevation procedure :: frame_info => terrain_frame_info procedure :: bound => terrain_bound procedure :: pick => terrain_pick procedure :: build_contents => terrain_build_contents procedure :: update => terrain_update end type TerrainBody !> The TerrainBody constructor: `TerrainBody(...)` makes one (see `new_terrain_body` for its !> arguments). interface TerrainBody module procedure new_terrain_body end interface TerrainBody contains !> Whether vkframes was built with Rocky (the `rocky` pixi environment). logical function rocky_available () rocky_available = vkf_rocky_available () /= 0 end function rocky_available !> A body named `name` in Rocky's tiling profile `profile` (default '': !> the Earth; 'moon': the Moon), drawn at `units_per_meter` scene units per !> meter (default 1e-3), in color `color` where it has no imagery ([r, g, b] !> or [r, g, b, a]; default the frame's). function new_terrain_body ( name , profile , units_per_meter , color ) result ( b ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: profile !! Rocky's tiling profile (default '') real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: units_per_meter !! scene units per meter (default 1e-3) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) type ( TerrainBody ) :: b b % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) b % profile_ = '' if ( present ( profile )) b % profile_ = profile if ( present ( units_per_meter )) b % units_per_meter_ = units_per_meter allocate ( b % layers ( 4 )) end function new_terrain_body !> Add an image layer: `uri` (a URL, URL template or file) of a `source` !> kind (LAYER_*; default LAYER_TMS). Layers added later are drawn on top. subroutine add_image_layer ( self , uri , source ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: uri integer , intent ( in ), optional :: source !! a LAYER_* constant (default LAYER_TMS) type ( MapLayer ) :: layer layer % uri = uri if ( present ( source )) layer % source = source call add_layer ( self , layer ) end subroutine add_image_layer !> Add an elevation layer: `uri` of a `source` kind (LAYER_*; default !> LAYER_TMS), heights in meters or `encoding` (ELEVATION_*; default !> ELEVATION_HEIGHTS). subroutine add_elevation_layer ( self , uri , source , encoding ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: uri integer , intent ( in ), optional :: source !! a LAYER_* constant (default LAYER_TMS) integer , intent ( in ), optional :: encoding !! an ELEVATION_* constant (default ELEVATION_HEIGHTS) type ( MapLayer ) :: layer layer % elevation = . true . layer % uri = uri if ( present ( source )) layer % source = source if ( present ( encoding )) layer % encoding = encoding call add_layer ( self , layer ) end subroutine add_elevation_layer !> Keep `layer`, and add it to the map if it is made. subroutine add_layer ( self , layer ) type ( TerrainBody ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( MapLayer ), intent ( in ) :: layer type ( MapLayer ), allocatable :: tmp (:) if (. not . allocated ( self % layers )) allocate ( self % layers ( 4 )) if ( self % n_layers == size ( self % layers )) then allocate ( tmp ( 2 * self % n_layers )) tmp ( 1 : self % n_layers ) = self % layers ( 1 : self % n_layers ) call move_alloc ( tmp , self % layers ) end if self % n_layers = self % n_layers + 1 self % layers ( self % n_layers ) = layer if ( c_associated ( self % map )) call apply_layer ( self , layer ) end subroutine add_layer !> Number of layers (image and elevation). pure integer function num_layers ( self ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( in ) :: self num_layers = self % n_layers end function num_layers !> Light the body with the scene's lights (default), or show its imagery as it is. subroutine set_lighting ( self , lit ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: lit self % lighting_ = lit call apply_settings ( self ) end subroutine set_lighting !> True if the body is lit by the scene's lights. pure logical function lighting ( self ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( in ) :: self lighting = self % lighting_ end function lighting !> Rocky's tiling profile ('': Rocky's default, the Earth). function profile ( self ) result ( p ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: p p = self % profile_ end function profile !> Scene units per meter the body is drawn at. pure real ( wp ) function units_per_meter ( self ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( in ) :: self units_per_meter = self % units_per_meter_ end function units_per_meter !> The body's equatorial radius in scene units (from its profile: the !> Moon's for 'moon', else the Earth's). pure real ( wp ) function body_radius ( self ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( in ) :: self if ( self % profile_ == 'moon' ) then body_radius = moon_radius * self % units_per_meter_ else body_radius = earth_radius * self % units_per_meter_ end if end function body_radius !> The height of the terrain (scene units, above the body's sphere or !> ellipsoid) at latitude and longitude `lat`, `lon` (degrees), from the !> last elevation layer added that is a file (LAYER_GDAL), read directly !> (also before the body is shown); `found` is false (and the height 0) !> without such a layer or data there, or without Rocky. function elevation ( self , lat , lon , found ) result ( h ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: lat , lon !! latitude and longitude (degrees) logical , intent ( out ), optional :: found !! false if there is no height there real ( wp ) :: h character ( len = :), allocatable :: file integer ( c_int ) :: ok integer :: k h = 0.0_wp if ( present ( found )) found = . false . if (. not . rocky_available ()) return do k = self % n_layers , 1 , - 1 if (. not . ( self % layers ( k )% elevation . and . self % layers ( k )% source == LAYER_GDAL )) cycle file = self % layers ( k )% uri if ( index ( file , '://' ) == 0 ) file = find_data_file ( file ) if ( len ( file ) == 0 ) return h = vkf_rocky_elevation ( file , len ( file , kind = c_int ), self % profile_ , len ( self % profile_ , kind = c_int ), & real ( lat , c_double ), real ( lon , c_double ), ok ) * self % units_per_meter_ if ( present ( found )) found = ok /= 0 return end do end function elevation !> The body's bounding sphere (frame coordinates): its equatorial radius, at the origin. subroutine terrain_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius center = 0.0_wp radius = self % body_radius () end subroutine terrain_bound !> The kind of frame: 'TerrainBody'. function terrain_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'TerrainBody' end function terrain_frame_info !> The map, made for the viewer showing the body (none headless or without Rocky). subroutine terrain_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer handle (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the group node to build under if (. not . c_associated ( viewer )) return if (. not . rocky_available ()) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: TerrainBody ' // self % name () // ': vkframes was built without Rocky ' // & '(pixi run -e rocky rocky-build, then run in the rocky environment)' return end if self % map_group = group call make_map ( self , viewer ) end subroutine terrain_build_contents !> The map (in the contents group) for `viewer`, with the settings and layers. subroutine make_map ( self , viewer ) type ( TerrainBody ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer integer :: k self % map = vkf_rocky_map_create ( viewer , self % profile_ , len ( self % profile_ , kind = c_int ), & real ( self % units_per_meter_ , c_double )) if (. not . c_associated ( self % map )) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: TerrainBody ' // self % name () // ': could not make the map' return end if call apply_settings ( self ) do k = 1 , self % n_layers call apply_layer ( self , self % layers ( k )) end do if ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % map_group , self % map ) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: TerrainBody ' // self % name () // ': could not build the scene' end subroutine make_map !> Each frame: if the map's window has closed (the map was released with !> it), the map again for a window still open (compiled for the windows !> running), then the frame's update. recursive subroutine terrain_update ( self , t ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! simulation time (s) type ( c_ptr ) :: viewer integer ( c_int ) :: status if ( c_associated ( self % map )) then if ( vkf_rocky_map_alive ( self % map ) == 0 ) then viewer = vkf_viewer_any () if ( c_associated ( viewer )) then status = vkf_node_remove_child ( self % map_group , self % map ) call vkf_node_delete ( self % map ) call make_map ( self , viewer ) if ( c_associated ( self % map )) then if ( vkf_compile_node ( self % map ) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: TerrainBody ' // self % name () // ': could not compile the map' end if end if end if end if call self % ReferenceFrame % update ( t ) end subroutine terrain_update !> Give the lighting and the frame's color to the map (if made). subroutine apply_settings ( self ) type ( TerrainBody ), intent ( inout ) :: self if (. not . c_associated ( self % map )) return if ( vkf_rocky_map_settings ( self % map , merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , self % lighting_ ), real ( self % color (), c_float )) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: TerrainBody ' // self % name () // ': could not apply the settings' end subroutine apply_settings !> Add `layer` to the map (a file found on VKFRAMES_DATA_PATH). subroutine apply_layer ( self , layer ) type ( TerrainBody ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( MapLayer ), intent ( in ) :: layer character ( len = :), allocatable :: uri integer ( c_int ) :: status uri = layer % uri if ( layer % source == LAYER_GDAL . and . index ( uri , '://' ) == 0 ) then ! a file: by name on VKFRAMES_DATA_PATH uri = find_data_file ( layer % uri ) if ( len ( uri ) == 0 ) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: TerrainBody ' // self % name () // ': could not find ' // layer % uri return end if end if if ( layer % elevation ) then status = vkf_rocky_add_elevation ( self % map , int ( layer % source , c_int ), uri , len ( uri , kind = c_int ), & int ( layer % encoding , c_int )) else status = vkf_rocky_add_image ( self % map , int ( layer % source , c_int ), uri , len ( uri , kind = c_int )) end if if ( status /= 0 ) write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: TerrainBody ' // self % name () // ': could not add layer ' // layer % uri end subroutine apply_layer !> Picked on a sphere of the body's radius (not the terrain's heights), with !> the latitude and longitude of the point hit; else the frame's origin. subroutine terrain_pick ( self , cam , to_root , hits , n ) class ( TerrainBody ), intent ( in ), target :: self type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam !! the cursor's ray and the pick's settings real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: to_root ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits so far (grown as needed) integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits in hits real ( wp ) :: r , m ( 4 , 4 ) r = self % body_radius () if ( self % contents_shown () . and . r > 0.0_wp ) then m = identity_matrix () if ( pick_ellipsoid ( self , cam , to_root , [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp ], m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), [ r , r , r ], . true ., hits , n )) return end if call self % ReferenceFrame % pick ( cam , to_root , hits , n ) end subroutine terrain_pick end module vkf_terrain","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_terrain.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_artists.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_artists.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_chain.f90 vkf_line_chain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_line_chain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_chain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_chain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~vkf_artists.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90 vkf_shapes.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_artists.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_shapes.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> Trajectory artists: what draws a Trajectory, in a DrawableTrajectory frame, as !> OpenFrames' TrajectoryArtist, CurveArtist, SegmentArtist, MarkerArtist and !> DrawableTrajectory, and RibbonArtist (not in OpenFrames: a translucent !> surface swept between two points at each trajectory point, e.g. an orbit's !> plane from the origin to the positions). !> !> A DrawableTrajectory is a frame (its points are in its coordinates) holding !> artists. Each frame update, an artist draws what changed in its trajectory: !> appended points are written into the GPU buffers in place, and only the !> buffers written to are uploaded (see vkf_line_chain); a cleared trajectory !> is redrawn into the same buffers. The last point drawn is always rewritten, !> since `set_optional` changes it. !> !> Trace mode (`set_trace_mode`) draws only the part of the trajectory up to !> the current time: the points whose times are at most the current time, !> whatever order they were added in (a change of the draw ranges, no !> upload): for increasing times its first points, for decreasing ones (a !> trajectory propagated backwards) its last. A curve adds a two-point tail !> from the latest of them to the point interpolated at the current time !> (the only data uploaded each frame). So a trajectory propagated forwards !> and one propagated backwards to the same state trace one history as time !> runs (example/trace_directions.f90); with time running backwards, the !> history shrinks back. (A highlight's arrows still run in the order the !> points were added: the propagation's direction.) !> !> Point colors (not in OpenFrames): a CurveArtist draws a trajectory with !> colors (Trajectory%add_color, or add's `color`) in them, each segment !> blended from its first point's color to its second's (one color: that !> color); without colors, or with `set_point_colors(.false.)`, in its own !> color. Its line buffers hold colors only then. !> !> Trails (not in OpenFrames): `CurveArtist%set_trail(past, future, fade)` !> draws only the part of the curve within `past` before the current time !> and `future` after it, each fading out over the last `fade` of its window !> toward its cutoff; `set_trail_style(TRAIL_PAST or TRAIL_FUTURE, ...)` gives !> each part its own color (or translucency) and dash pattern (e.g. a solid !> past and a dashed future). The GPU fades and cuts the line by its distance !> along it (shaders/line.vert): each frame only the distances at the current !> time and at the window's edges are uploaded (a few floats per chunk), and !> the range of points drawn changed. It replaces trace mode while set. !> !> Highlight (not in OpenFrames; e.g. a trajectory selected by the program or !> by picking): `set_highlight` on a curve or segment artist, or on a !> DrawableTrajectory for all of them. HIGHLIGHT_PULSE: the line widens and !> brightens towards the highlight color, and back, over and over; !> HIGHLIGHT_ARROWS: a translucent band of the highlight color around it, with !> chevrons moving along it from its first point to its last (a trajectory's !> initial time to its final; a segment's start to its end). Both together: !> HIGHLIGHT_PULSE + HIGHLIGHT_ARROWS. The GPU animates them (shaders/ !> line.vert), so nothing is uploaded or computed each frame. In trace mode, !> only the part drawn is highlighted. !> !> Artists and their trajectories are not owned: they must stay alive while !> drawn. !> !> Picking (WindowProxy%pick): a DrawableTrajectory picks what its artists !> draw, as drawn (in trace mode, up to the current time): a curve's segments !> (its chunks skipped by their bounds when far from the cursor), with the !> point and the time there (interpolated); a segment artist's segments; a !> marker artist's start, end and intermediate markers, with their times. !> Lines are reached within the tolerance plus half their width, markers !> plus half their size. Each artist gives its best hit: the closest to the !> cursor (and of those, the nearest). module vkf_artists use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_ptr , c_null_ptr , c_associated , c_int , c_float , c_f_pointer use vkf_math , only : wp , set_rgba use vkf_trajectory , only : Trajectory , DataSource , position_sources , SOURCE_ZERO , SOURCE_POSOPT , & TIME_OUT_OF_RANGE , TIME_NOT_FOUND use vkf_frames , only : ReferenceFrame , PickHit , add_pick_hit , PICK_CURVE , PICK_SEGMENT , PICK_MARKER use vkf_pick , only : PickCamera , point_pick , segment_pick , sphere_near , wants use vkf_layer , only : check_status , vkf_line_create , vkf_line_create_colored , vkf_line_colors , vkf_line_points_changed , & vkf_ribbon_create , & vkf_line_set_range , & vkf_node_add_child , vkf_node_remove_child , vkf_node_delete , vkf_switch_create , & vkf_compile_node , vkf_viewer_any , line_set_style , vkf_image_read , vkf_image_delete use vkf_line_chain , only : LineChain , CHAIN_STRIP , CHAIN_SEGMENTS , CHAIN_MARKERS , CHAIN_RIBBON , split_points , & split_distances , & line_buffer implicit none private !> The base of the trajectory artists (OpenFrames' TrajectoryArtist). type , abstract , public :: TrajectoryArtist private type ( Trajectory ), pointer :: traj => null () !! the trajectory drawn (not owned; null if none) logical :: trace = . false . !! trace mode: drawn up to the current time logical :: pickable_ = . true . !! picked (WindowProxy%pick) ! what was drawn integer :: seen_generation = - 1 , seen_revision = - 1 !! trajectory generation and revision drawn (-1: none) contains procedure :: set_trajectory , get_trajectory procedure :: set_trace_mode , trace_mode procedure :: set_pickable => artist_set_pickable , pickable => artist_pickable procedure :: release => artist_release procedure ( artist_build ), deferred :: build procedure ( artist_update ), deferred :: update end type TrajectoryArtist abstract interface !> Create the artist's render nodes under `group`. `viewer` (may be !> null) compiles the nodes it creates later. subroutine artist_build ( self , viewer , group ) import :: TrajectoryArtist , c_ptr implicit none class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer , group end subroutine artist_build !> Bring the drawing up to date with the trajectory at simulation time `t`. subroutine artist_update ( self , t ) import :: TrajectoryArtist , wp implicit none class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t end subroutine artist_update end interface !> how a curve's or segments' dash pattern is laid out (set_dash_mode) integer , parameter , public :: DASH_SCENE = 0 !! anchored to the line (sizes in scene units; the default) integer , parameter , public :: DASH_SCREEN = 1 !! screen-locked (a constant length in pixels; OpenGL's stipple) integer , parameter , public :: DASH_FIXED = 2 !! a fixed length of the line, as paint on it (curves) !> the parts of a curve's trail (set_trail_style) integer , parameter , public :: TRAIL_PAST = 1 , TRAIL_FUTURE = 2 !> A curve's trail (see the module documentation and set_trail). type :: TrailStyle logical :: on = . false . real ( wp ) :: past = 0.0_wp , future = 0.0_wp !! the window (s before and after the current time; huge: no limit) real ( wp ) :: fade = 0.25_wp !! of each part's window, faded toward its cutoff (0 to 1) real ( wp ) :: color ( 4 , 2 ) = 1.0_wp !! each part's color (if `replace`) [r, g, b, a] logical :: replace ( 2 ) = . false . !! each part in its own color (else the line's) real ( wp ) :: opacity ( 2 ) = 1.0_wp !! each part's alpha multiplied by it integer :: factor ( 2 ) = 1 , pattern ( 2 ) = int ( z 'FFFF' ) !! each part's dash pattern end type TrailStyle !> highlights of curve and segment artists (set_highlight; combine by adding) integer , parameter , public :: HIGHLIGHT_NONE = 0 !! not highlighted integer , parameter , public :: HIGHLIGHT_PULSE = 1 !! the line widens and brightens, and back, over and over integer , parameter , public :: HIGHLIGHT_ARROWS = 2 !! a band around the line, with arrows moving along it !> A line artist's highlight (see the module documentation and set_highlight). type :: HighlightStyle integer :: mode = HIGHLIGHT_NONE !! HIGHLIGHT_* (added) real ( wp ) :: color ( 4 ) = [ 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! [r, g, b, a] (default white) real ( wp ) :: arrow_spacing = 4 0.0_wp !! between arrows (window units) real ( wp ) :: arrow_speed = 5 0.0_wp !! window units per second real ( wp ) :: band_width = 1 2.0_wp !! (window units) real ( wp ) :: pulse_period = 1.5_wp !! (s) end type HighlightStyle !> The base of the artists drawing a trajectory's points through one chain !> of buffers (CurveArtist: a line, a chain point per trajectory point; !> RibbonArtist: a surface, a pair of chain points per trajectory point): !> the chain and how much of it is written and drawn, the trace tail, the !> trajectory's colors, and the update (chain_update: the points written !> as they change, then drawn all or, in trace mode, those passed and the !> tail to the point at the current time). Each extension says what its !> chain is (chain_kind), how many points it draws (points), its tail's !> node (new_tail), its style (apply_style), how its points are written !> (write_points) and its tail drawn (draw_tail). type , abstract , extends ( TrajectoryArtist ) :: ChainArtist private logical :: point_colors_ = . true . !! the trajectory's colors, if any (see set_point_colors) ! rendering type ( c_ptr ) :: group = c_null_ptr !! the chain's group (to make it again, colored or not) logical :: compile = . false . !! (chunks made later are compiled) type ( LineChain ) :: chain !! the buffers type ( c_ptr ) :: tail = c_null_ptr !! to the point at the current time (trace mode) integer :: n_written = 0 !! trajectory points written to the chain integer :: n_drawn = 0 !! trajectory points drawn from it integer :: first_drawn_ = 1 !! the first of them (trace mode, decreasing times: later) integer :: n_colored = 0 !! points written with the trajectory's own colors logical :: tail_shown = . false . !! the tail is drawn real ( wp ) :: tail_time = huge ( 1.0_wp ) !! the time the tail was drawn for contains procedure :: set_point_colors , point_colors procedure :: num_chunks , num_drawn , first_drawn procedure :: build => chain_build procedure :: update => chain_update procedure :: release => chain_release procedure :: init_chain => chain_init procedure ( chain_kind_interface ), deferred :: chain_kind procedure ( chain_points_interface ), deferred :: points procedure ( new_tail_interface ), deferred :: new_tail procedure ( apply_style_interface ), deferred :: apply_style procedure ( write_points_interface ), deferred :: write_points procedure ( draw_tail_interface ), deferred :: draw_tail end type ChainArtist abstract interface !> The kind of chain (LineChain's CHAIN_STRIP or CHAIN_RIBBON). pure integer function chain_kind_interface ( self ) import :: ChainArtist implicit none class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self end function chain_kind_interface !> The number of trajectory points to draw (0 if none). integer function chain_points_interface ( self ) result ( n ) import :: ChainArtist implicit none class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self end function chain_points_interface !> The trace tail's node (null on failure), made with the chain. function new_tail_interface ( self ) result ( node ) import :: ChainArtist , c_ptr implicit none class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( c_ptr ) :: node end function new_tail_interface !> The style (the artist's color, width, ...) given to the chain and the tail. subroutine apply_style_interface ( self ) import :: ChainArtist implicit none class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self end subroutine apply_style_interface !> Write trajectory points i1 .. i2 into the chain (and upload the chunks written to). subroutine write_points_interface ( self , i1 , i2 ) import :: ChainArtist implicit none class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i1 , i2 !! the trajectory points end subroutine write_points_interface !> The trace tail: from point k (the latest passed) to the point !> interpolated at time t toward point k2 (the next in time); none if !> either isn't a point written. subroutine draw_tail_interface ( self , t , k , k2 ) import :: ChainArtist , wp implicit none class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the current time integer , intent ( in ) :: k , k2 !! the tail's ends (0: none) end subroutine draw_tail_interface end interface !> Draws a trajectory's points connected by a line (OpenFrames' CurveArtist). !> The x, y and z of the points come from data sources (default: the !> trajectory's positions). The line is in the artist's color, or in the !> trajectory's point colors if it has any (see the module documentation). type , extends ( ChainArtist ), public :: CurveArtist private type ( DataSource ) :: sources_ ( 3 ) !! x, y, z data sources (default: the positions) logical :: default_data = . true . !! sources not set: the positions, per the DOF real ( wp ) :: color_ ( 4 ) = [ 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! line color [r, g, b, a] (default white) real ( wp ) :: width_ = 1.0_wp !! line width (window units) integer :: pattern_factor = 1 !! window units per pattern bit (>= 1) integer :: pattern_ = int ( z 'FFFF' ) !! 16-bit dash pattern (z'FFFF': solid) logical :: lod_ = . true . !! level of detail (see set_level_of_detail) type ( HighlightStyle ) :: highlight_ !! (see set_highlight) type ( TrailStyle ) :: trail_ !! (see set_trail) ! rendering (the chain: a line strip; the tail: a line of two points) integer :: tail_from = 0 , tail_to = 0 !! the tail: from point tail_from toward tail_to contains procedure :: set_trajectory => curve_set_trajectory procedure :: set_x_data , set_y_data , set_z_data , data_sources procedure :: set_color => curve_set_color , color => curve_color procedure :: set_width => curve_set_width , width => curve_width procedure :: set_pattern => curve_set_pattern , pattern => curve_pattern procedure :: set_highlight => curve_set_highlight , highlight => curve_highlight procedure :: set_trail , remove_trail , has_trail , set_trail_style procedure :: set_dash_mode => curve_set_dash_mode , dash_mode => curve_dash_mode procedure :: set_level_of_detail , level_of_detail , lod_error procedure :: drawn_color procedure :: update => curve_update procedure :: drawn_point , drawn_distance , trace_end procedure :: init_chain => curve_init_chain procedure :: chain_kind => curve_chain_kind procedure :: points => curve_points procedure :: new_tail => curve_new_tail procedure :: apply_style => curve_style procedure :: write_points => write_curve procedure :: draw_tail => update_tail end type CurveArtist !> The CurveArtist constructor: `CurveArtist(...)` makes one (see `new_curve_artist` for its !> arguments). interface CurveArtist module procedure new_curve_artist end interface CurveArtist !> Draws a line segment at every `stride`-th point of a trajectory !> (OpenFrames' SegmentArtist), from the point given by the start data !> sources to the one given by the end data sources: e.g. radius vectors !> (the origin to the positions), or from the positions to points stored as !> an optional (a target). Default (an addition to OpenFrames, which draws !> nothing until the sources are set): from the frame's origin to the !> trajectory's positions. !> !> Relative ends (`set_end_relative`, not in OpenFrames): the end sources !> give an offset from the start, so a vector stored per point (a thrust, !> a velocity) is drawn from each position, at a length set by the end !> sources' scale (`set_end_scale`), which can be changed without touching !> the trajectory (only this artist's segments are written again). Where !> the vector is zero (no thrust) nothing is drawn. type , extends ( TrajectoryArtist ), public :: SegmentArtist private type ( DataSource ) :: start_ ( 3 ), end_ ( 3 ) !! start and end points' x, y, z data sources logical :: default_data = . true . !! sources not set: the origin to the positions, per the DOF logical :: end_relative_ = . false . !! the end sources: an offset from the start integer :: stride_ = 1 !! a segment at every stride_-th point (>= 1) real ( wp ) :: color_ ( 4 ) = [ 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! segment color [r, g, b, a] (default white) real ( wp ) :: width_ = 1.0_wp !! segment width (window units) integer :: pattern_factor = 1 !! window units per pattern bit (>= 1) integer :: pattern_ = int ( z 'FFFF' ) !! 16-bit dash pattern (z'FFFF': solid) type ( HighlightStyle ) :: highlight_ !! (see set_highlight) ! rendering type ( LineChain ) :: chain !! the line buffers (a pair of points per segment) integer :: n_written = 0 !! segments written to the chain integer :: n_drawn = 0 !! segments drawn from it integer :: first_drawn_ = 1 !! the first of them (trace mode, decreasing times: later) contains procedure :: set_trajectory => segment_set_trajectory procedure :: set_start_x_data , set_start_y_data , set_start_z_data procedure :: set_end_x_data , set_end_y_data , set_end_z_data procedure :: set_start_data , set_end_data procedure :: start_data_sources , end_data_sources procedure :: set_end_relative , end_relative , set_end_scale procedure :: set_stride , stride procedure :: set_color => segment_set_color , color => segment_color procedure :: set_width => segment_set_width , width => segment_width procedure :: set_pattern => segment_set_pattern , pattern => segment_pattern procedure :: set_highlight => segment_set_highlight , highlight => segment_highlight procedure :: set_dash_mode => segment_set_dash_mode , dash_mode => segment_dash_mode procedure :: build => segment_build procedure :: update => segment_update procedure :: release => segment_release procedure :: num_chunks => segment_num_chunks , num_drawn => segment_num_drawn procedure :: first_drawn => segment_first_drawn procedure :: drawn_segment end type SegmentArtist !> The SegmentArtist constructor: `SegmentArtist(...)` makes one (see `new_segment_artist` for its !> arguments). interface SegmentArtist module procedure new_segment_artist end interface SegmentArtist !> Draws a translucent surface swept between two points at each point of !> a trajectory (not in OpenFrames): from the point given by the start data !> sources to the one given by the end data sources, with a quad between !> each point's pair and the next's. Default: from the frame's origin to the !> positions, sweeping out an orbit's plane (a fan, as the radius vectors of !> a SegmentArtist would fill it); other sources give e.g. a curtain from !> the positions down to a ground track stored as an optional. Unlit, seen !> from both sides, depth tested but writing no depth (as the equatorial !> plane of a RadialPlane), drawn to double precision as the curves (its !> edge on a CurveArtist's line through the same points). !> !> Trace mode draws the surface up to the current time: the quads passed !> (a draw range, no upload) and one from the last point passed to the !> point interpolated at the time. Point colors: a trajectory with colors !> colors the surface, each point's pair in its color, with the artist's !> opacity (its alpha times theirs); see set_point_colors. A trajectory !> going round several times covers the surface again each time, so it !> gets more opaque: trace one revolution, or lower the alpha. type , extends ( ChainArtist ), public :: RibbonArtist private type ( DataSource ) :: start_ ( 3 ), end_ ( 3 ) !! start and end points' x, y, z data sources logical :: default_data = . true . !! sources not set: the origin to the positions, per the DOF real ( wp ) :: color_ ( 4 ) = [ 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 0.25_wp ] !! surface color (default white, alpha 0.25) ! rendering: the chain a surface, trajectory point i its points 2i-1 (start) and 2i (end); the tail a quad contains procedure :: set_trajectory => ribbon_set_trajectory procedure :: set_start_x_data => ribbon_set_start_x_data , set_start_y_data => ribbon_set_start_y_data procedure :: set_start_z_data => ribbon_set_start_z_data procedure :: set_end_x_data => ribbon_set_end_x_data , set_end_y_data => ribbon_set_end_y_data procedure :: set_end_z_data => ribbon_set_end_z_data procedure :: start_data_sources => ribbon_start_data_sources , end_data_sources => ribbon_end_data_sources procedure :: set_color => ribbon_set_color , color => ribbon_color procedure :: drawn_pair , drawn_color => ribbon_drawn_color , trace_end => ribbon_trace_end procedure :: chain_kind => ribbon_chain_kind procedure :: points => ribbon_points procedure :: new_tail => ribbon_new_tail procedure :: apply_style => ribbon_style procedure :: write_points => write_ribbon procedure :: draw_tail => update_ribbon_tail end type RibbonArtist !> The RibbonArtist constructor: `RibbonArtist(...)` makes one (see `new_ribbon_artist` for its !> arguments). interface RibbonArtist module procedure new_ribbon_artist end interface RibbonArtist !> which markers a MarkerArtist draws (OpenFrames' DrawnMarkers; combine with ior) integer , parameter , public :: MARKER_START = 1 , MARKER_INTERMEDIATE = 2 , MARKER_END = 4 !> how intermediate markers are spaced (OpenFrames' IntermediateType) integer , parameter , public :: INTERMEDIATE_TIME = 1 !! every `spacing` time units integer , parameter , public :: INTERMEDIATE_DISTANCE = 2 !! every `spacing` of arc length integer , parameter , public :: INTERMEDIATE_DATA = 3 !! every `spacing`-th data point !> marker shapes (OpenFrames' disk, image, and its Demos/Shaders/Marker_*.frag) integer , parameter , public :: MARKER_DISK = 0 , MARKER_CIRCLE = 1 , MARKER_SQUARE = 2 , MARKER_PLUS = 3 , & MARKER_X = 4 , MARKER_TARGET = 5 , MARKER_ROSE = 6 , MARKER_CIRCLE_PULSE = 7 , & MARKER_DISK_PULSE = 8 , MARKER_SPIRAL = 9 , MARKER_IMAGE = 10 !> Draws markers at a trajectory's points (OpenFrames' MarkerArtist): at !> its start and end, and intermediate markers spaced by time, arc length !> or data points, counted from the start or from the end. Markers keep !> their size on screen (window units), or with auto-attenuation shrink !> when the camera is farther than the trajectory's size. In trace mode !> (an addition), the markers passed are drawn: the end marker (at the !> trajectory's end) only once the time reaches the end. Point colors (an !> addition, off by default: set_point_colors): each marker in the !> trajectory's color there (see set_point_colors). type , extends ( TrajectoryArtist ), public :: MarkerArtist private type ( DataSource ) :: sources_ ( 3 ) !! x, y, z data sources (default: the positions) logical :: default_data = . true . !! sources not set: the positions, per the DOF integer :: markers_ = ior ( MARKER_START , MARKER_END ) !! markers drawn (an ior of MARKER_* flags) integer :: intermediate_type_ = INTERMEDIATE_DATA !! INTERMEDIATE_TIME, _DISTANCE or _DATA real ( wp ) :: spacing_ = 1.0_wp !! intermediate spacing: time units, arc length or data points integer :: direction_ = MARKER_START !! intermediate markers counted from MARKER_START or MARKER_END real ( wp ) :: start_color ( 4 ) = [ 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! start marker color [r, g, b, a] (red) real ( wp ) :: end_color ( 4 ) = [ 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! end marker color (red) real ( wp ) :: intermediate_color ( 4 ) = [ 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! intermediate marker color (white) real ( wp ) :: size_ = 1 0.0_wp !! marker size (window units) integer :: shape_ = MARKER_DISK !! marker shape: a MARKER_* shape constant character ( len = :), allocatable :: image_file !! the marker image file ('': none) type ( c_ptr ) :: image = c_null_ptr !! the image read from it (owned; null: none) logical :: attenuate = . true . !! auto-attenuation (see set_auto_attenuate; on by default) logical :: point_colors_ = . false . !! the trajectory's colors, if any (see set_point_colors) ! rendering type ( c_ptr ) :: group = c_null_ptr !! the artist's group (null until built) logical :: shown = . false . !! built for a window (marker nodes made later are compiled) integer :: n_colors_seen = 0 !! the trajectory's colors when the markers were written type ( LineChain ) :: start_node , end_node , inter !! start, end and intermediate marker buffers logical :: drawn = . false . !! drawn at least once since built integer :: n_seen = 0 !! points seen (for the bounds) real ( wp ) :: lo ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp , hi ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! bounds of the points seen real ( wp ) :: radius = 0.0_wp !! attenuation radius applied ! intermediate markers: in trajectory order, and where to continue real ( wp ), allocatable :: inter_xyz (:,:), inter_t (:) !! intermediate markers' points and times (1:n_inter) real ( wp ), allocatable :: inter_rgba (:,:) !! (4, :) their colors (with point colors) integer :: n_inter = 0 , n_inter_written = 0 , n_inter_drawn = 0 !! intermediate markers computed, written, drawn integer :: inter_first = 1 !! the first intermediate marker drawn (trace, decreasing times: later) real ( wp ) :: next_time = 0.0_wp !! time of the next marker (INTERMEDIATE_TIME) integer :: next_index = 0 !! where to continue (0: not started) real ( wp ) :: arc = 0.0_wp , prev_arc = 0.0_wp , target = 0.0_wp , prev_point ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! arc length (INTERMEDIATE_DISTANCE): so far, at prev_point, and of the next marker; the last point logical :: start_shown = . false ., end_shown = . false . !! the start and end markers are drawn contains procedure :: set_trajectory => marker_set_trajectory procedure :: set_x_data => marker_set_x_data , set_y_data => marker_set_y_data procedure :: set_z_data => marker_set_z_data , data_sources => marker_data_sources procedure :: set_markers , markers procedure :: set_marker_color , marker_color procedure :: set_marker_size , marker_size procedure :: set_marker_shape , marker_shape procedure :: set_marker_image , marker_image_file procedure :: set_auto_attenuate , auto_attenuate procedure :: set_point_colors => marker_set_point_colors , point_colors => marker_point_colors procedure :: drawn_color => marker_drawn_color procedure :: set_intermediate_type , intermediate_type procedure :: set_intermediate_spacing , intermediate_spacing procedure :: set_intermediate_direction , intermediate_direction procedure :: build => marker_build procedure :: update => marker_update procedure :: release => marker_release procedure :: num_intermediate , drawn_marker end type MarkerArtist !> The MarkerArtist constructor: `MarkerArtist(...)` makes one (see `new_marker_artist` for its !> arguments). interface MarkerArtist module procedure new_marker_artist end interface MarkerArtist !> One of a DrawableTrajectory's artists: a pointer to it (Fortran has no !> arrays of pointers) and the node it is drawn under. type :: ArtistPointer class ( TrajectoryArtist ), pointer :: p => null () !! the artist (not owned) type ( c_ptr ) :: group = c_null_ptr !! the artist's node (null until built) end type ArtistPointer !> A frame for drawing trajectories (OpenFrames' DrawableTrajectory): it !> holds artists, which draw in its coordinates. type , extends ( ReferenceFrame ), public :: DrawableTrajectory private type ( ArtistPointer ), allocatable :: artists (:) !! the artists (1:n_artists; not owned) integer :: n_artists = 0 !! number of artists type ( c_ptr ) :: contents_group = c_null_ptr !! the artists' group (null until built) logical :: shown = . false . !! built for a window (artists added later are compiled) contains procedure :: add_artist , remove_artist , remove_all_artists , num_artists , artist procedure :: set_highlight => drawable_set_highlight procedure :: frame_info => drawable_frame_info procedure :: build_contents => drawable_build_contents procedure :: update => drawable_update procedure :: pick => drawable_pick end type DrawableTrajectory !> The DrawableTrajectory constructor: `DrawableTrajectory(...)` makes one (see `new_drawable_trajectory` for its !> arguments). interface DrawableTrajectory module procedure new_drawable_trajectory end interface DrawableTrajectory contains ! ================================================================== ! TrajectoryArtist !> Draw `traj` (it must stay alive while drawn). subroutine set_trajectory ( self , traj ) class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: traj self % traj => traj self % seen_generation = - 1 ! redraw end subroutine set_trajectory !> The trajectory drawn (null if none). function get_trajectory ( self ) result ( traj ) class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( Trajectory ), pointer :: traj traj => self % traj end function get_trajectory !> Whether `pick` tests what this artist draws (default true; e.g. false for !> a spacecraft's marker beside its orbit's curve). subroutine artist_set_pickable ( self , pickable ) class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: pickable self % pickable_ = pickable end subroutine artist_set_pickable !> Whether `pick` tests what this artist draws. pure logical function artist_pickable ( self ) class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self artist_pickable = self % pickable_ end function artist_pickable !> Draw only the part up to the current time (see the module documentation). subroutine set_trace_mode ( self , enabled ) class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: enabled self % trace = enabled end subroutine set_trace_mode !> Whether only the part up to the current time is drawn. pure logical function trace_mode ( self ) class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self trace_mode = self % trace end function trace_mode !> Forget the render nodes (after the artist's group was removed from the !> scene): build starts again. subroutine artist_release ( self ) class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self self % seen_generation = - 1 end subroutine artist_release !> Whether the trajectory changed since last drawn; `redraw` if everything !> must be drawn again (cleared, or a new trajectory or data sources). logical function data_changed ( self , redraw ) result ( changed ) class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( out ) :: redraw redraw = . false . changed = . false . if (. not . associated ( self % traj )) return if ( self % traj % generation () /= self % seen_generation ) then redraw = . true . self % seen_generation = self % traj % generation () self % seen_revision = - 1 end if changed = self % traj % revision () /= self % seen_revision self % seen_revision = self % traj % revision () end function data_changed !> The points of 1 .. n whose times are at most t (trace mode): i1 .. i2 !> (none: i2 < i1), the first points for increasing times, the last for !> decreasing ones (by bisection). subroutine trace_range ( traj , t , n , i1 , i2 ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: traj real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t integer , intent ( in ) :: n integer , intent ( out ) :: i1 , i2 integer :: low , high , mid i1 = 1 i2 = 0 if ( n < 1 ) return low = 0 high = n + 1 if (. not . decreasing_times ( traj , n )) then ! points 1 .. low have times <= t do while ( high - low > 1 ) mid = ( low + high ) / 2 if ( traj % time ( mid ) <= t ) then low = mid else high = mid end if end do i2 = low else ! points high .. n have times <= t do while ( high - low > 1 ) mid = ( low + high ) / 2 if ( traj % time ( mid ) <= t ) then high = mid else low = mid end if end do i1 = high i2 = n end if end subroutine trace_range !> Whether points 1 .. n have decreasing times (a trajectory propagated backwards). logical function decreasing_times ( traj , n ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: traj integer , intent ( in ) :: n decreasing_times = . false . if ( n > 1 ) decreasing_times = traj % time ( n ) < traj % time ( 1 ) end function decreasing_times !> Trace mode's tail, for the points passed i1 .. i2 of the n written: from !> the latest passed (k) toward the next in time (k2: i2 + 1, or i1 - 1 for !> decreasing times); none (0, 0) without a trajectory. subroutine tail_ends ( traj , n , i1 , i2 , k , k2 ) type ( Trajectory ), pointer , intent ( in ) :: traj !! the trajectory (null: none) integer , intent ( in ) :: n !! the points written integer , intent ( in ) :: i1 , i2 !! the points passed integer , intent ( out ) :: k , k2 !! the tail's ends k = 0 k2 = 0 if (. not . associated ( traj )) return if ( decreasing_times ( traj , n )) then k = i1 k2 = i1 - 1 else k = i2 k2 = i2 + 1 end if end subroutine tail_ends !> Number of points the data sources give: 0 for invalid sources or no !> trajectory, huge() if all are zero. integer function source_points ( traj , sources ) result ( n ) type ( Trajectory ), pointer , intent ( in ) :: traj type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: sources ( 3 ) n = 0 if (. not . associated ( traj )) return if (. not . traj % verify_data ( sources )) return n = traj % num_points ( sources ) end function source_points !> The sources are x, y, z of the position, unscaled. pure logical function is_position_xyz ( s ) type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: s ( 3 ) integer :: k is_position_xyz = . true . do k = 1 , 3 if ( s ( k )% src /= SOURCE_POSOPT . or . s ( k )% opt /= 0 . or . s ( k )% element /= k . or . s ( k )% scale /= 1.0_wp ) & is_position_xyz = . false . end do end function is_position_xyz ! ================================================================== ! ChainArtist !> Whether a trajectory with colors is drawn in them (default true); points !> without a color yet (colors arriving after positions) in the artist's !> color. A curve: each segment blended from its first point's color to its !> second's (with level of detail, a color lasting fewer points than are !> skipped may not show from far away); a surface: each point's pair in its !> color, times the artist's alpha. False: all in the artist's color. subroutine set_point_colors ( self , enabled ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: enabled !! true: the trajectory's colors self % point_colors_ = enabled end subroutine set_point_colors !> Whether a trajectory's colors are drawn. pure logical function point_colors ( self ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self point_colors = self % point_colors_ end function point_colors !> Number of buffers the artist is drawn with (0 until built). pure integer function num_chunks ( self ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self num_chunks = self % chain % num_chunks () end function num_chunks !> Number of trajectory points drawn now (all of them, or in trace mode !> those passed). pure integer function num_drawn ( self ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self num_drawn = self % n_drawn end function num_drawn !> The first point drawn (1, or in trace mode of decreasing times the !> earliest point passed): points first_drawn .. first_drawn + num_drawn - 1. pure integer function first_drawn ( self ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self first_drawn = self % first_drawn_ end function first_drawn !> Chain points per trajectory point: 1, or 2 for a surface (a pair each). pure integer function chain_points_per_point ( self ) result ( m ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self m = merge ( 2 , 1 , self % chain_kind () == CHAIN_RIBBON ) end function chain_points_per_point !> Create the chain of buffers (sized for the points now) and the trace !> tail under `group`. subroutine chain_build ( self , viewer , group ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! compiles what is made later (null: nothing to) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the artist's group self % group = group self % compile = . false . call self % init_chain () call self % chain % reserve ( chain_points_per_point ( self ) * self % points ()) ! compiled with the group self % compile = c_associated ( viewer ) call self % chain % set_compile ( self % compile ) self % tail = self % new_tail () ! (white unless the points' colors are drawn) if ( c_associated ( self % tail )) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( group , self % tail ), 'trajectory artists' ) call self % apply_style () self % seen_generation = - 1 end subroutine chain_build !> The chain, colored if the trajectory's colors are drawn. subroutine chain_init ( self ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self call self % chain % init ( self % group , self % chain_kind (), colored = uses_colors ( self )) call self % chain % set_compile ( self % compile ) self % n_colored = 0 end subroutine chain_init !> Whether the trajectory's colors are drawn: wanted, and it has some. logical function uses_colors ( self ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self uses_colors = self % point_colors_ . and . associated ( self % traj ) if ( uses_colors ) uses_colors = self % traj % num_colors () > 0 end function uses_colors !> Forget the render nodes: the chain and the tail (see artist_release). subroutine chain_release ( self ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self call self % chain % release () if ( c_associated ( self % tail )) call vkf_node_delete ( self % tail ) self % tail = c_null_ptr self % group = c_null_ptr self % n_written = 0 self % n_drawn = 0 self % n_colored = 0 self % tail_shown = . false . call artist_release ( self ) end subroutine chain_release !> Write the points added (all of them on a redraw), and draw them all or, !> in trace mode, those passed and the tail to the point at time t. subroutine chain_update ( self , t ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the current time logical :: changed if (. not . write_changed ( self , changed )) return call draw_written ( self , t , changed ) end subroutine chain_update !> The points written as the trajectory changed: the chain made again if !> its colors are drawn now or no longer (its first colors, or the !> setting), then the points new since the last written (and the last one !> again: set_optional; and those whose colors came since), or all of them !> on a redraw (cleared, a new trajectory or data sources). False if the !> chain isn't built. logical function write_changed ( self , changed ) result ( built ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( out ) :: changed !! points written (or the chain emptied) integer :: n , i1 logical :: redraw changed = . false . built = self % chain % is_built () if (. not . built ) return n = self % points () if ( uses_colors ( self ) . neqv . self % chain % is_colored ()) then call self % chain % detach () call self % init_chain () call self % apply_style () self % seen_generation = - 1 end if changed = data_changed ( self , redraw ) if ( redraw . or . . not . associated ( self % traj )) then self % n_written = 0 self % n_colored = 0 end if if ( changed ) then i1 = max ( 1 , min ( self % n_written , n )) ! from the last point written (set_optional) if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) i1 = max ( 1 , min ( i1 , self % n_colored )) ! (and colors added since) call self % chain % reserve ( chain_points_per_point ( self ) * n ) if ( n >= i1 ) call self % write_points ( i1 , n ) self % n_written = n end if end function write_changed !> Draw the points written: all of them (the tail hidden) or, in trace !> mode, those passed by time t (times up to it) and the tail from the !> latest of them to the point at t (unchanged if nothing `changed` and t !> is the time it was drawn for). subroutine draw_written ( self , t , changed ) class ( ChainArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the current time logical , intent ( in ) :: changed !! points were written (write_changed) integer :: m , i1 , i2 , k , k2 m = chain_points_per_point ( self ) if (. not . self % trace ) then self % n_drawn = self % n_written self % first_drawn_ = 1 call self % chain % draw ( m * self % n_drawn ) if ( c_associated ( self % tail )) call check_status ( vkf_line_set_range ( self % tail , 1_c_int , 0_c_int ), 'trajectory artists' ) self % tail_shown = . false . self % tail_time = huge ( 1.0_wp ) return end if if (. not . changed . and . t == self % tail_time ) return i1 = 1 i2 = 0 if ( associated ( self % traj )) call trace_range ( self % traj , t , self % n_written , i1 , i2 ) self % first_drawn_ = i1 self % n_drawn = max ( 0 , i2 - i1 + 1 ) call self % chain % draw_range ( m * ( i1 - 1 ) + 1 , m * i2 ) call tail_ends ( self % traj , self % n_written , i1 , i2 , k , k2 ) call self % draw_tail ( t , k , k2 ) self % tail_time = t end subroutine draw_written ! ================================================================== ! CurveArtist !> A curve artist for `traj` (optional), drawn in color `color` ([r, g, b] !> or [r, g, b, a]; default white) and `width` (window units; default 1). function new_curve_artist ( traj , color , width ) result ( a ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target , optional :: traj real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:), width type ( CurveArtist ) :: a a % sources_ = position_sources ( 3 ) if ( present ( traj )) call a % set_trajectory ( traj ) if ( present ( color )) call a % set_color ( color ) if ( present ( width )) a % width_ = width end function new_curve_artist !> Draw `traj`; with the default data sources, its positions (per its DOF). subroutine curve_set_trajectory ( self , traj ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: traj self % traj => traj if ( self % default_data ) self % sources_ = position_sources ( traj % dof ()) self % seen_generation = - 1 end subroutine curve_set_trajectory !> Where the x (y, z) of the points come from. Returns whether the !> trajectory has those data. logical function set_x_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_curve_source ( self , 1 , src ) end function set_x_data !> Where the y of the points come from (see set_x_data). logical function set_y_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_curve_source ( self , 2 , src ) end function set_y_data !> Where the z of the points come from (see set_x_data). logical function set_z_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_curve_source ( self , 3 , src ) end function set_z_data !> Set data source k (1: x, 2: y, 3: z); returns whether the trajectory has the data. logical function set_curve_source ( self , k , src ) result ( valid ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: k type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src self % sources_ ( k ) = src self % default_data = . false . self % seen_generation = - 1 valid = . true . if ( associated ( self % traj )) valid = self % traj % verify_data ( self % sources_ ) end function set_curve_source !> The x, y and z data sources. pure function data_sources ( self ) result ( s ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( DataSource ) :: s ( 3 ) s = self % sources_ end function data_sources !> The line's color: [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1 !> (with the trajectory's point colors drawn: for points without one). subroutine curve_set_color ( self , color ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) call set_rgba ( self % color_ , color ) call curve_style ( self ) if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) self % seen_generation = - 1 ! (points without colors redrawn) end subroutine curve_set_color !> The line's color [r, g, b, a]. pure function curve_color ( self ) result ( c ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = self % color_ end function curve_color !> The line's width in window units (logical pixels). subroutine curve_set_width ( self , width ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: width self % width_ = width call curve_style ( self ) end subroutine curve_set_width !> The line's width (window units). pure real ( wp ) function curve_width ( self ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self curve_width = self % width_ end function curve_width !> A dash pattern, as OpenGL's line stipple (OpenFrames' setPattern): each !> bit of the 16-bit `pattern` (bit 0 first; z'FFFF', the default, is !> solid) covers `factor` window units, along the whole curve (the dashes !> run on across its points). The dashes' length on screen is kept within !> 0.7 to 1.4 times the pattern's (see shaders/line.vert). subroutine curve_set_pattern ( self , factor , pattern ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: factor , pattern self % pattern_factor = max ( 1 , factor ) self % pattern_ = iand ( pattern , int ( z 'FFFF' )) call curve_style ( self ) end subroutine curve_set_pattern !> Highlight the curve (see the module documentation): `mode` a sum of !> HIGHLIGHT_PULSE and HIGHLIGHT_ARROWS (HIGHLIGHT_NONE: not highlighted), !> in `color` ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]; default white). The other !> settings are kept when not given. subroutine curve_set_highlight ( self , mode , color , arrow_spacing , arrow_speed , band_width , pulse_period ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: mode !! HIGHLIGHT_* (added) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: arrow_spacing !! between arrows (window units; default 40) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: arrow_speed !! (window units per second; default 50) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: band_width !! of the arrows' band (window units; default 12) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: pulse_period !! (s; default 1.5) call update_highlight ( self % highlight_ , mode , color , arrow_spacing , arrow_speed , band_width , pulse_period ) call curve_style ( self ) end subroutine curve_set_highlight !> The curve's highlight: HIGHLIGHT_* (added; HIGHLIGHT_NONE: not highlighted). pure integer function curve_highlight ( self ) result ( mode ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self mode = self % highlight_ % mode end function curve_highlight !> A trail (see the module documentation): only the part within `past` !> before the current time and `future` after it (s, >= 0; 0: none of !> it; huge(1.0_wp): no limit), each fading out over the last `fade` (0 !> to 1, default 0.25) of its window toward its cutoff. Replaces trace !> mode while set. subroutine set_trail ( self , past , future , fade ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: past , future !! s before and after the current time real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: fade !! of each part's window (default 0.25) self % trail_ % on = . true . self % trail_ % past = max ( 0.0_wp , past ) self % trail_ % future = max ( 0.0_wp , future ) if ( present ( fade )) self % trail_ % fade = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , fade )) self % tail_time = huge ( 1.0_wp ) ! (drawn again at the next update) end subroutine set_trail !> How the dash pattern (and a trail's) is laid out: DASH_SCENE (the !> default) anchored to the line: a dash stays put on it as the view !> changes, its size in scene units (one per line and view, from 0.7 to !> 1.4 times the pattern's on screen, changing by doubling as it zooms); !> DASH_SCREEN screen-locked, as OpenGL's line stipple (OpenFrames'): !> every dash the pattern's length in pixels, at any zoom and depth, !> sliding along the line as the view changes; DASH_FIXED a fixed !> length of the line, as paint on it: never changing, so zooming in the !> dashes grow on screen, and out they shrink (under a pixel, blending !> into a fainter solid line); `length` (scene units, for the whole !> pattern: the other patterns, a trail's future's and the arrows', in !> proportion), else the pattern's length on screen where the line is !> first drawn. DASH_SCREEN and DASH_FIXED cost projecting the points !> drawn on the CPU, per view and frame. subroutine curve_set_dash_mode ( self , mode , length ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: mode !! DASH_SCENE, DASH_SCREEN or DASH_FIXED real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: length !! (DASH_FIXED) the pattern's length, scene units real ( wp ) :: l l = 0.0_wp if ( present ( length )) l = max ( 0.0_wp , length ) call self % chain % set_dash_mode ( mode , l ) if ( c_associated ( self % tail )) call self % chain % style_node ( self % tail ) end subroutine curve_set_dash_mode !> The dash pattern's layout: DASH_SCENE, DASH_SCREEN or DASH_FIXED. pure integer function curve_dash_mode ( self ) result ( mode ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self mode = self % chain % dash_mode_of () end function curve_dash_mode !> No trail: the whole curve (or trace mode, if set) again. subroutine remove_trail ( self ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( c_float ) :: none ( 20 ) none = 0.0_c_float ! (direction 0: no trail) self % trail_ % on = . false . call self % chain % set_trail ( none ) self % tail_time = huge ( 1.0_wp ) end subroutine remove_trail !> Whether the curve has a trail (set_trail). pure logical function has_trail ( self ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self has_trail = self % trail_ % on end function has_trail !> The style of a trail's part, `which` TRAIL_PAST or TRAIL_FUTURE: !> `color` ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]: drawn in it instead of the line's !> colors), `opacity` (its alpha multiplied by it: translucency, default !> 1), a dash pattern (`factor` and 16 `pattern` bits, as set_pattern; !> default solid). Settings not given are kept. subroutine set_trail_style ( self , which , color , opacity , factor , pattern ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: which !! TRAIL_PAST or TRAIL_FUTURE real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: opacity !! 0 to 1 integer , intent ( in ), optional :: factor , pattern !! window units per bit (>= 1), 16 bits integer :: k k = merge ( 1 , 2 , which == TRAIL_PAST ) if ( present ( color )) then call set_rgba ( self % trail_ % color (:, k ), color ) self % trail_ % replace ( k ) = . true . end if if ( present ( opacity )) self % trail_ % opacity ( k ) = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , opacity )) if ( present ( factor )) self % trail_ % factor ( k ) = max ( 1 , factor ) if ( present ( pattern )) self % trail_ % pattern ( k ) = iand ( pattern , int ( z 'FFFF' )) self % tail_time = huge ( 1.0_wp ) end subroutine set_trail_style !> Level of detail (default on): seen from far away, the curve is drawn !> from every 2nd, 4th, ... point (and its last), as many as can be !> skipped while staying within half a pixel of all of them, chosen per !> view and per chunk of points. Off: every point is drawn. subroutine set_level_of_detail ( self , enabled ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: enabled self % lod_ = enabled call self % chain % set_lod ( enabled ) end subroutine set_level_of_detail !> Whether level of detail is on. pure logical function level_of_detail ( self ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self level_of_detail = self % lod_ end function level_of_detail !> The error bounds of chunk j of the curve's points (for checks): how far !> the points skipped can be from the segments drawn at stride 2&#94;k, k = 1, !> 2, ... (scene units). function lod_error ( self , j ) result ( error ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: j real ( wp ), allocatable :: error (:) error = real ( self % chain % lod_error ( j ), wp ) end function lod_error !> The color of point i (1 to num_drawn) as drawn: read back from the line !> buffers. function drawn_color ( self , i ) result ( rgba ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ) if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) then rgba = self % chain % point_color ( i ) else rgba = self % color_ end if end function drawn_color !> The dash pattern: its `factor` and 16 pattern `bits`. pure subroutine curve_pattern ( self , factor , bits ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( out ) :: factor , bits factor = self % pattern_factor bits = self % pattern_ end subroutine curve_pattern !> Point i (of the trajectory's: first_drawn to first_drawn + num_drawn - 1 !> drawn) as written: read back from the line buffers. function drawn_point ( self , i ) result ( v ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) v = self % chain % point ( i ) end function drawn_point !> The distance along the curve at point i (1 to num_drawn), as drawn (for !> the dash pattern): read back from the line buffers. function drawn_distance ( self , i ) result ( s ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: s s = self % chain % distance ( i ) end function drawn_distance !> In trace mode, the end of the line (the point at the current time) as !> drawn; false if no tail is drawn. logical function trace_end ( self , v ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: v ( 3 ) !! the tail's end (frame coordinates) real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:,:), pointer :: p v = 0.0_wp trace_end = self % tail_shown if (. not . trace_end ) return call line_buffer ( self % tail , p ) if ( associated ( p )) v = real ( p ( 1 : 3 , 1 , 2 ), wp ) + real ( p ( 1 : 3 , 2 , 2 ), wp ) end function trace_end !> Write the points added (all of them on a redraw), and draw them all, or !> in trace mode those passed and the tail to the point at time t, or with !> a trail the window about time t. subroutine curve_update ( self , t ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the current time logical :: changed if (. not . write_changed ( self , changed )) return if ( self % trail_ % on ) then ! a trail: the window about time t if (. not . changed . and . t == self % tail_time ) return call draw_trail ( self , t ) self % tail_time = t return end if call draw_written ( self , t , changed ) end subroutine curve_update !> The chain (ChainArtist's), with the curve's level of detail. subroutine curve_init_chain ( self ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self call chain_init ( self ) call self % chain % set_lod ( self % lod_ ) end subroutine curve_init_chain !> The chain: a line strip. pure integer function curve_chain_kind ( self ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self curve_chain_kind = CHAIN_STRIP end function curve_chain_kind !> The trace tail: a line of two points (white unless the points' colors are drawn). function curve_new_tail ( self ) result ( node ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( c_ptr ) :: node node = vkf_line_create_colored ( 2_c_int ) end function curve_new_tail !> Number of points to draw (1 if all sources are zero: a point at the origin). integer function curve_points ( self ) result ( n ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self n = source_points ( self % traj , self % sources_ ) if ( all ( self % sources_ % src == SOURCE_ZERO ) . and . n > 0 ) n = min ( 1 , self % traj % num_times ()) end function curve_points !> Write points i1 .. i2 into the chain (and upload the chunks written to). subroutine write_curve ( self , i1 , i2 ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i1 , i2 real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:,:), pointer :: p real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: pos real ( wp ), allocatable :: v (:,:) integer :: j , lo , hi do j = 1 , self % chain % num_chunks () call self % chain % slice ( j , i1 , i2 , lo , hi , p ) if (. not . associated ( p )) cycle if ( is_position_xyz ( self % sources_ )) then ! the usual case: straight from the positions call self % traj % positions ( pos ) call split_points ( pos (:, lo : hi ), p ) else ! other sources: gathered a range at a time allocate ( v ( 3 , hi - lo + 1 )) call self % traj % points ( lo , hi , self % sources_ , v ) call split_points ( v , p ) deallocate ( v ) end if end do if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) call write_colors ( self , i1 , i2 ) if ( is_position_xyz ( self % sources_ )) then ! distances from the positions in double call self % traj % positions ( pos ) call self % chain % written ( i1 , i2 , pos ) else call self % chain % written ( i1 , i2 ) end if end subroutine write_curve !> The colors of points i1 .. i2 into the chain: the trajectory's, and the !> artist's color for points without one yet. subroutine write_colors ( self , i1 , i2 ) type ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i1 , i2 real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: c , col integer :: j , lo , hi , m call self % traj % colors ( col ) m = self % traj % num_colors () do j = 1 , self % chain % num_chunks () call self % chain % color_slice ( j , i1 , i2 , lo , hi , c ) if (. not . associated ( c )) cycle if ( m >= lo ) c (:, 1 : min ( hi , m ) - lo + 1 ) = col (:, lo : min ( hi , m )) if ( hi > m ) c (:, max ( lo , m + 1 ) - lo + 1 :) = spread ( real ( self % color_ , c_float ), 2 , hi - max ( lo , m + 1 ) + 1 ) end do self % n_colored = min ( m , i2 ) end subroutine write_colors !> Color of point i as drawn by a colored chain: the trajectory's, or the !> artist's if it has none yet. function point_rgba ( self , i ) result ( rgba ) type ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ) if ( i <= self % traj % num_colors ()) then rgba = self % traj % color ( i ) else rgba = self % color_ end if end function point_rgba !> A trail at time t: the points within its window (and the one beyond !> each end: the GPU cuts the segments at the cutoffs) drawn, and the !> distances along the curve at t and at the window's edges given to the !> shader (see vkf_line_set_trail), as distances from t's in the !> direction of time; times beyond the trajectory's are extrapolated from !> its end segments. subroutine draw_trail ( self , t ) type ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t real ( wp ), parameter :: unlimited = 0.5_wp * huge ( 1.0_wp ) real ( c_float ), parameter :: far = 1.0e30_c_float real ( c_float ) :: values ( 20 ), hi real ( wp ) :: sgn , lo_key , hi_key , s_now , fade integer :: n , i1 , i2 , k call check_status ( vkf_line_set_range ( self % tail , 1_c_int , 0_c_int ), 'trajectory artists' ) self % tail_shown = . false . n = self % n_written self % n_drawn = 0 self % first_drawn_ = 1 values = 0.0_c_float if (. not . associated ( self % traj ) . or . n < 2 ) then call self % chain % draw_range ( 1 , 0 ) call self % chain % set_trail ( values ) return end if sgn = merge ( - 1.0_wp , 1.0_wp , decreasing_times ( self % traj , n )) ! (keys sgn * time increase with the index) lo_key = sgn * t - merge ( huge ( 1.0_wp ), self % trail_ % past , self % trail_ % past >= unlimited ) hi_key = sgn * t + merge ( huge ( 1.0_wp ), self % trail_ % future , self % trail_ % future >= unlimited ) if ( sgn < 0.0_wp ) then ! (the past is at the larger keys) lo_key = sgn * t - merge ( huge ( 1.0_wp ), self % trail_ % future , self % trail_ % future >= unlimited ) hi_key = sgn * t + merge ( huge ( 1.0_wp ), self % trail_ % past , self % trail_ % past >= unlimited ) end if if ( hi_key < key ( 1 ) . or . lo_key > key ( n )) then ! (the window misses the trajectory) call self % chain % draw_range ( 1 , 0 ) call self % chain % set_trail ( values ) return end if i1 = max ( 1 , keys_up_to ( lo_key , . true .)) ! the last point before the window, or the first i2 = min ( n , keys_up_to ( hi_key , . false .) + 1 ) ! the first after it, or the last self % first_drawn_ = i1 self % n_drawn = i2 - i1 + 1 call self % chain % draw_range ( i1 , i2 ) s_now = s_at ( t ) hi = real ( s_now , c_float ) fade = 1.0_wp - self % trail_ % fade values ( 1 : 4 ) = [ hi , real ( s_now - real ( hi , wp ), c_float ), real ( sgn , c_float ), & real ( merge ( 1 , 0 , self % trail_ % replace ( 1 )) + merge ( 2 , 0 , self % trail_ % replace ( 2 )), c_float )] if ( self % trail_ % past >= unlimited ) then values ( 5 : 6 ) = - far else values ( 5 ) = real ( sgn * ( s_at ( t - self % trail_ % past ) - s_now ), c_float ) values ( 6 ) = real ( sgn * ( s_at ( t - fade * self % trail_ % past ) - s_now ), c_float ) end if if ( self % trail_ % future >= unlimited ) then values ( 7 : 8 ) = far else values ( 7 ) = real ( sgn * ( s_at ( t + fade * self % trail_ % future ) - s_now ), c_float ) values ( 8 ) = real ( sgn * ( s_at ( t + self % trail_ % future ) - s_now ), c_float ) end if do k = 1 , 2 ! each part's color (or the line's: then its alpha only) values ( 9 + 4 * ( k - 1 ): 12 + 4 * ( k - 1 )) = real ( self % trail_ % color (:, k ), c_float ) values ( 12 + 4 * ( k - 1 )) = real ( self % trail_ % opacity ( k ) * merge ( self % trail_ % color ( 4 , k ), 1.0_wp , & self % trail_ % replace ( k )), c_float ) end do values ( 17 : 20 ) = real ([ self % trail_ % pattern ( 1 ), self % trail_ % factor ( 1 ), self % trail_ % pattern ( 2 ), & self % trail_ % factor ( 2 )], c_float ) call self % chain % set_trail ( values ) contains !> Point i's key: its time, increasing with the index. real ( wp ) function key ( i ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i key = sgn * self % traj % time ( i ) end function key !> The number of points with keys below x, or at most x if `inclusive` !> (bisection: the keys increase). integer function keys_up_to ( x , inclusive ) result ( m ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x !! the key logical , intent ( in ) :: inclusive !! keys equal to x counted integer :: low , high , mid low = 0 high = n + 1 do while ( high - low > 1 ) mid = ( low + high ) / 2 if ( key ( mid ) < x . or . ( inclusive . and . key ( mid ) == x )) then low = mid else high = mid end if end do m = low end function keys_up_to !> The distance along the curve at time tt: interpolated between the !> points about it (extrapolated beyond the ends). real ( wp ) function s_at ( tt ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: tt integer :: j real ( wp ) :: t0 , t1 j = max ( 1 , min ( n - 1 , keys_up_to ( sgn * tt , . true .))) t0 = self % traj % time ( j ) t1 = self % traj % time ( j + 1 ) s_at = self % chain % distance ( j ) if ( t1 /= t0 ) s_at = s_at + ( tt - t0 ) / ( t1 - t0 ) * ( self % chain % distance ( j + 1 ) - s_at ) end function s_at end subroutine draw_trail !> The tail: from point k (the latest passed) to the point interpolated at !> time t toward point k2 (the next in time: k + 1, or k - 1 for decreasing !> times); none if either isn't a point written (before the start, or !> everything passed). subroutine update_tail ( self , t , k , k2 ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t integer , intent ( in ) :: k , k2 real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:,:), pointer :: p real ( wp ) :: frac , xyz ( 3 , 2 ), along self % tail_shown = . false . if (. not . c_associated ( self % tail )) return if ( min ( k , k2 ) < 1 . or . max ( k , k2 ) > self % n_written ) then call check_status ( vkf_line_set_range ( self % tail , 1_c_int , 0_c_int ), 'trajectory artists' ) return end if frac = self % traj % time_fraction ( k , k2 , t ) xyz (:, 1 ) = self % traj % point ( k , self % sources_ ) xyz (:, 2 ) = self % traj % point_between ( k , k2 , t , self % sources_ ) call line_buffer ( self % tail , p ) if (. not . associated ( p )) return call split_points ( xyz , p (:, :, 1 : 2 )) along = merge ( 1.0_wp , - 1.0_wp , k2 > k ) * norm2 ( xyz (:, 2 ) - xyz (:, 1 )) ! (the distance along: in point order) call split_distances ( self % chain % distance ( k ) + [ 0.0_wp , along ], p ( 4 , :, 1 : 2 )) self % tail_from = k self % tail_to = k2 call tail_colors ( self , k , k2 , frac ) call check_status ( vkf_line_points_changed ( self % tail , 2_c_int ), 'trajectory artists' ) self % tail_shown = . true . end subroutine update_tail !> The tail's colors: from point k's to the color at frac along to point !> k2's (white, showing the style's color, if the chain has none). subroutine tail_colors ( self , k , k2 , frac ) type ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: k , k2 real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: frac real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: c real ( wp ) :: c0 ( 4 ), c1 ( 4 ) integer ( c_int ) :: capacity type ( c_ptr ) :: data data = vkf_line_colors ( self % tail , capacity ) if (. not . c_associated ( data ) . or . capacity < 2 ) return call c_f_pointer ( data , c , [ 4 , 2 ]) if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) then c0 = point_rgba ( self , k ) c1 = point_rgba ( self , k2 ) c (:, 1 ) = real ( c0 , c_float ) c (:, 2 ) = real ( c0 + frac * ( c1 - c0 ), c_float ) else c = 1.0_c_float end if end subroutine tail_colors !> The style: the artist's color, or white if the points' colors are drawn !> (the shader multiplies them by it). subroutine curve_style ( self ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ) rgba = self % color_ if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) rgba = 1.0_wp call self % chain % set_style ( rgba , self % width_ ) call self % chain % set_pattern ( self % pattern_factor , self % pattern_ ) call apply_highlight ( self % highlight_ , self % chain ) if ( c_associated ( self % tail )) call self % chain % style_node ( self % tail ) end subroutine curve_style !> Change the settings given (see CurveArtist%set_highlight). subroutine update_highlight ( h , mode , color , arrow_spacing , arrow_speed , band_width , pulse_period ) type ( HighlightStyle ), intent ( inout ) :: h integer , intent ( in ) :: mode real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:), arrow_spacing , arrow_speed , band_width , pulse_period h % mode = iand ( mode , HIGHLIGHT_PULSE + HIGHLIGHT_ARROWS ) if ( present ( color )) call set_rgba ( h % color , color ) if ( present ( arrow_spacing )) h % arrow_spacing = max ( arrow_spacing , 1.0_wp ) if ( present ( arrow_speed )) h % arrow_speed = arrow_speed if ( present ( band_width )) h % band_width = max ( band_width , 0.0_wp ) if ( present ( pulse_period )) h % pulse_period = max ( pulse_period , 0.05_wp ) end subroutine update_highlight !> Give the highlight `h` to the line buffers `chain`. subroutine apply_highlight ( h , chain ) type ( HighlightStyle ), intent ( in ) :: h type ( LineChain ), intent ( inout ) :: chain call chain % set_highlight ( h % mode , h % color , h % arrow_spacing , h % arrow_speed , h % band_width , h % pulse_period ) end subroutine apply_highlight ! ================================================================== ! SegmentArtist !> A segment artist for `traj` (optional), drawn in color `color` ([r, g, !> b] or [r, g, b, a]; default white) and `width` (window units; default !> 1), at every `stride`-th point (default 1). function new_segment_artist ( traj , color , width , stride ) result ( a ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target , optional :: traj real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:), width integer , intent ( in ), optional :: stride type ( SegmentArtist ) :: a a % end_ = position_sources ( 3 ) if ( present ( traj )) call a % set_trajectory ( traj ) if ( present ( color )) call a % set_color ( color ) if ( present ( width )) a % width_ = width if ( present ( stride )) call a % set_stride ( stride ) end function new_segment_artist !> Draw `traj`; with the default data sources, from the origin to its !> positions (per its DOF). subroutine segment_set_trajectory ( self , traj ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: traj self % traj => traj if ( self % default_data ) self % end_ = position_sources ( traj % dof ()) self % seen_generation = - 1 end subroutine segment_set_trajectory !> Where the x (y, z) of the segments' start (end) points come from. !> Returns whether the trajectory has the data of all sources. logical function set_start_x_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_segment_source ( self , 1 , 1 , src ) end function set_start_x_data !> Where the y of the segments' start points come from (see set_start_x_data). logical function set_start_y_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_segment_source ( self , 1 , 2 , src ) end function set_start_y_data !> Where the z of the segments' start points come from (see set_start_x_data). logical function set_start_z_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_segment_source ( self , 1 , 3 , src ) end function set_start_z_data !> Where the x of the segments' end points come from (see set_start_x_data). logical function set_end_x_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_segment_source ( self , 2 , 1 , src ) end function set_end_x_data !> Where the y of the segments' end points come from (see set_start_x_data). logical function set_end_y_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_segment_source ( self , 2 , 2 , src ) end function set_end_y_data !> Where the z of the segments' end points come from (see set_start_x_data). logical function set_end_z_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_segment_source ( self , 2 , 3 , src ) end function set_end_z_data !> Set component k of the start (side 1) or end (side 2) sources. logical function set_segment_source ( self , side , k , src ) result ( valid ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: side , k type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src if ( side == 1 ) then self % start_ ( k ) = src else self % end_ ( k ) = src end if self % default_data = . false . self % seen_generation = - 1 valid = . true . if ( associated ( self % traj )) valid = self % traj % verify_data ( self % start_ ) . and . self % traj % verify_data ( self % end_ ) end function set_segment_source !> The x, y and z data sources of the segments' start points. pure function start_data_sources ( self ) result ( s ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( DataSource ) :: s ( 3 ) s = self % start_ end function start_data_sources !> The x, y and z data sources of the segments' end points. pure function end_data_sources ( self ) result ( s ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( DataSource ) :: s ( 3 ) s = self % end_ end function end_data_sources !> All three start (end) sources at once, e.g. position_sources(3) or !> optional_sources(1). Returns whether the trajectory has their data. logical function set_start_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src ( 3 ) integer :: k do k = 1 , 3 valid = set_segment_source ( self , 1 , k , src ( k )) end do end function set_start_data !> All three end sources at once (see set_start_data). logical function set_end_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src ( 3 ) integer :: k do k = 1 , 3 valid = set_segment_source ( self , 2 , k , src ( k )) end do end function set_end_data !> Relative ends (default false): each segment ends at its start plus the !> end sources' values (a vector drawn from each point), not at them. subroutine set_end_relative ( self , relative ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: relative if ( relative . eqv . self % end_relative_ ) return self % end_relative_ = relative self % seen_generation = - 1 ! (all segments written again) end subroutine set_end_relative !> Whether the ends are relative (see set_end_relative). pure logical function end_relative ( self ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self end_relative = self % end_relative_ end function end_relative !> Set the scale of all three end sources (with relative ends: the length !> drawn per unit of the stored vector, e.g. km per newton). Only this !> artist's segments are written again. subroutine set_end_scale ( self , scale ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: scale if ( all ( self % end_ % scale == scale )) return self % end_ % scale = scale self % default_data = . false . self % seen_generation = - 1 end subroutine set_end_scale !> Draw a segment at points 1, 1 + stride, 1 + 2 stride, ... (stride >= 1). subroutine set_stride ( self , stride ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: stride if ( max ( 1 , stride ) == self % stride_ ) return self % stride_ = max ( 1 , stride ) self % seen_generation = - 1 end subroutine set_stride !> The stride: a segment at every stride-th point. pure integer function stride ( self ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self stride = self % stride_ end function stride !> The segments' color: [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1. subroutine segment_set_color ( self , color ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) call set_rgba ( self % color_ , color ) call self % chain % set_style ( self % color_ , self % width_ ) end subroutine segment_set_color !> The segments' color [r, g, b, a]. pure function segment_color ( self ) result ( c ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = self % color_ end function segment_color !> The segments' width in window units (logical pixels). subroutine segment_set_width ( self , width ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: width self % width_ = width call self % chain % set_style ( self % color_ , self % width_ ) end subroutine segment_set_width !> The segments' width (window units). pure real ( wp ) function segment_width ( self ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self segment_width = self % width_ end function segment_width !> A dash pattern (see CurveArtist%set_pattern), starting again at the !> start of each segment. subroutine segment_set_pattern ( self , factor , pattern ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: factor , pattern self % pattern_factor = max ( 1 , factor ) self % pattern_ = iand ( pattern , int ( z 'FFFF' )) call self % chain % set_pattern ( self % pattern_factor , self % pattern_ ) end subroutine segment_set_pattern !> The dash pattern's layout (see CurveArtist%set_dash_mode): screen-locked !> dashes start again at each segment's start, as GL_LINES; DASH_FIXED !> (strips only) is taken as DASH_SCENE. subroutine segment_set_dash_mode ( self , mode ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: mode !! DASH_SCENE or DASH_SCREEN call self % chain % set_dash_mode ( merge ( DASH_SCENE , mode , mode == DASH_FIXED ), 0.0_wp ) end subroutine segment_set_dash_mode !> The dash pattern's layout: DASH_SCENE or DASH_SCREEN. pure integer function segment_dash_mode ( self ) result ( mode ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self mode = self % chain % dash_mode_of () end function segment_dash_mode !> Highlight the segments (see CurveArtist%set_highlight): the arrows run !> along each segment from its start to its end. subroutine segment_set_highlight ( self , mode , color , arrow_spacing , arrow_speed , band_width , pulse_period ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: mode !! HIGHLIGHT_* (added) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: arrow_spacing !! between arrows (window units; default 40) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: arrow_speed !! (window units per second; default 50) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: band_width !! of the arrows' band (window units; default 12) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: pulse_period !! (s; default 1.5) call update_highlight ( self % highlight_ , mode , color , arrow_spacing , arrow_speed , band_width , pulse_period ) call apply_highlight ( self % highlight_ , self % chain ) end subroutine segment_set_highlight !> The segments' highlight: HIGHLIGHT_* (added; HIGHLIGHT_NONE: not highlighted). pure integer function segment_highlight ( self ) result ( mode ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self mode = self % highlight_ % mode end function segment_highlight !> The dash pattern: its `factor` and 16 pattern `bits`. pure subroutine segment_pattern ( self , factor , bits ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( out ) :: factor , bits factor = self % pattern_factor bits = self % pattern_ end subroutine segment_pattern !> Number of line buffers the segments are drawn with (0 until built). pure integer function segment_num_chunks ( self ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self segment_num_chunks = self % chain % num_chunks () end function segment_num_chunks !> Number of segments drawn now (all of them, or in trace mode those at !> the points passed). pure integer function segment_num_drawn ( self ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self segment_num_drawn = self % n_drawn end function segment_num_drawn !> The first segment drawn (1, or in trace mode of decreasing times the !> earliest passed): segments first_drawn .. first_drawn + num_drawn - 1. pure integer function segment_first_drawn ( self ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self segment_first_drawn = self % first_drawn_ end function segment_first_drawn !> Segment s (at point 1 + (s-1) stride; first_drawn to first_drawn + !> num_drawn - 1 drawn) as written: read back from the line buffers. subroutine drawn_segment ( self , s , a , b ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: s real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: a ( 3 ) !! the segment's start (frame coordinates) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: b ( 3 ) !! its end a = self % chain % point ( 2 * s - 1 ) b = self % chain % point ( 2 * s ) end subroutine drawn_segment !> Create the chain of line buffers (sized for the segments now) under `group`. subroutine segment_build ( self , viewer , group ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer , group call self % chain % init ( group , CHAIN_SEGMENTS ) call self % chain % set_style ( self % color_ , self % width_ ) call self % chain % set_pattern ( self % pattern_factor , self % pattern_ ) call self % chain % reserve ( 2 * segment_count ( self )) ! compiled with the group call self % chain % set_compile ( c_associated ( viewer )) self % seen_generation = - 1 end subroutine segment_build !> Forget the render nodes (see artist_release). subroutine segment_release ( self ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self call self % chain % release () self % n_written = 0 self % n_drawn = 0 call artist_release ( self ) end subroutine segment_release !> Write the segments added (all of them on a redraw), and draw them all or, !> in trace mode, those at the points passed at time t. subroutine segment_update ( self , t ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t integer :: m , s1 , s2 , i1 , i2 logical :: changed , redraw if (. not . self % chain % is_built ()) return m = segment_count ( self ) changed = data_changed ( self , redraw ) if ( redraw . or . . not . associated ( self % traj )) self % n_written = 0 if ( changed ) then s1 = max ( 1 , min ( self % n_written , m )) ! from the last segment written (set_optional) call self % chain % reserve ( 2 * m ) if ( m >= s1 ) call write_segments ( self , s1 , m ) self % n_written = m end if self % n_drawn = self % n_written self % first_drawn_ = 1 if ( self % trace . and . associated ( self % traj )) then ! the segments at the points passed (times up to t) call trace_range ( self % traj , t , self % traj % num_times (), i1 , i2 ) s1 = ( i1 - 1 + self % stride_ - 1 ) / self % stride_ + 1 s2 = 0 if ( i2 >= 1 ) s2 = min ( self % n_written , ( i2 - 1 ) / self % stride_ + 1 ) self % first_drawn_ = s1 self % n_drawn = max ( 0 , s2 - s1 + 1 ) end if call self % chain % draw_range ( 2 * self % first_drawn_ - 1 , 2 * ( self % first_drawn_ + self % n_drawn - 1 )) end subroutine segment_update !> Number of segments to draw (none if all sources are zero). integer function segment_count ( self ) result ( m ) type ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer :: n m = 0 if ( all ( self % start_ % src == SOURCE_ZERO ) . and . all ( self % end_ % src == SOURCE_ZERO )) return n = min ( source_points ( self % traj , self % start_ ), source_points ( self % traj , self % end_ )) if ( n > 0 ) m = ( n - 1 ) / self % stride_ + 1 end function segment_count !> Write segments s1 .. s2 into the chain (and upload the chunks written to). subroutine write_segments ( self , s1 , s2 ) type ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: s1 , s2 real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:,:), pointer :: p real ( wp ), allocatable :: v (:,:), w (:,:) integer :: j , lo , hi , sa , sb , ia , ib do j = 1 , self % chain % num_chunks () call self % chain % slice ( j , 2 * s1 - 1 , 2 * s2 , lo , hi , p ) ! chunks hold whole segments if (. not . associated ( p )) cycle ! segments sa .. sb: their start points (odd chain points) and end points (even) sa = ( lo + 1 ) / 2 sb = hi / 2 ia = 1 + ( sa - 1 ) * self % stride_ ib = 1 + ( sb - 1 ) * self % stride_ allocate ( v ( 3 , sb - sa + 1 ), w ( 3 , sb - sa + 1 )) call self % traj % points ( ia , ib , self % start_ , v , self % stride_ ) call split_points ( v , p (:, :, 2 * sa - lo : 2 * sb - lo : 2 )) call self % traj % points ( ia , ib , self % end_ , w , self % stride_ ) if ( self % end_relative_ ) w = v + w ! (no offset: exactly the start, a segment drawn as nothing) call split_points ( w , p (:, :, 2 * sa - lo + 1 : 2 * sb - lo + 1 : 2 )) deallocate ( v , w ) end do call self % chain % written ( 2 * s1 - 1 , 2 * s2 ) end subroutine write_segments ! ================================================================== ! RibbonArtist !> A ribbon artist for `traj` (optional), of color `color` ([r, g, b], alpha !> unchanged, or [r, g, b, a]; default white, alpha 0.25), from the frame's !> origin to the positions (see set_start_x_data, ... for others). function new_ribbon_artist ( traj , color ) result ( a ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target , optional :: traj real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) type ( RibbonArtist ) :: a a % end_ = position_sources ( 3 ) if ( present ( traj )) call a % set_trajectory ( traj ) if ( present ( color )) call set_rgba ( a % color_ , color ) end function new_ribbon_artist !> Draw `traj`; with the default data sources, from the origin to its !> positions (per its DOF). subroutine ribbon_set_trajectory ( self , traj ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: traj self % traj => traj if ( self % default_data ) self % end_ = position_sources ( traj % dof ()) self % seen_generation = - 1 end subroutine ribbon_set_trajectory !> Where the x (y, z) of the surface's start (end) points come from. !> Returns whether the trajectory has the data of all sources. logical function ribbon_set_start_x_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_ribbon_source ( self , 1 , 1 , src ) end function ribbon_set_start_x_data !> Where the y of the surface's start points come from (see set_start_x_data). logical function ribbon_set_start_y_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_ribbon_source ( self , 1 , 2 , src ) end function ribbon_set_start_y_data !> Where the z of the surface's start points come from (see set_start_x_data). logical function ribbon_set_start_z_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_ribbon_source ( self , 1 , 3 , src ) end function ribbon_set_start_z_data !> Where the x of the surface's end points come from (see set_start_x_data). logical function ribbon_set_end_x_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_ribbon_source ( self , 2 , 1 , src ) end function ribbon_set_end_x_data !> Where the y of the surface's end points come from (see set_start_x_data). logical function ribbon_set_end_y_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_ribbon_source ( self , 2 , 2 , src ) end function ribbon_set_end_y_data !> Where the z of the surface's end points come from (see set_start_x_data). logical function ribbon_set_end_z_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_ribbon_source ( self , 2 , 3 , src ) end function ribbon_set_end_z_data !> Set component k of the start (side 1) or end (side 2) sources. logical function set_ribbon_source ( self , side , k , src ) result ( valid ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: side , k type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src if ( side == 1 ) then self % start_ ( k ) = src else self % end_ ( k ) = src end if self % default_data = . false . self % seen_generation = - 1 valid = . true . if ( associated ( self % traj )) valid = self % traj % verify_data ( self % start_ ) . and . self % traj % verify_data ( self % end_ ) end function set_ribbon_source !> The x, y and z data sources of the surface's start points. pure function ribbon_start_data_sources ( self ) result ( s ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( DataSource ) :: s ( 3 ) s = self % start_ end function ribbon_start_data_sources !> The x, y and z data sources of the surface's end points. pure function ribbon_end_data_sources ( self ) result ( s ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( DataSource ) :: s ( 3 ) s = self % end_ end function ribbon_end_data_sources !> The surface's color: [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a]; its !> alpha is the surface's opacity (also with the trajectory's colors). subroutine ribbon_set_color ( self , color ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) call set_rgba ( self % color_ , color ) call ribbon_style ( self ) if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) self % seen_generation = - 1 ! (points without colors redrawn) end subroutine ribbon_set_color !> The surface's color [r, g, b, a]. pure function ribbon_color ( self ) result ( c ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = self % color_ end function ribbon_color !> The pair at trajectory point i (1 to num_drawn) as drawn, its start a !> and end b: read back from the buffers. subroutine drawn_pair ( self , i , a , b ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: a ( 3 ), b ( 3 ) a = self % chain % point ( 2 * i - 1 ) b = self % chain % point ( 2 * i ) end subroutine drawn_pair !> The color of the pair at trajectory point i as drawn (rgba: the !> trajectory's color times the artist's alpha, or the artist's color). function ribbon_drawn_color ( self , i ) result ( rgba ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ) rgba = self % color_ if (. not . self % chain % is_colored ()) return rgba = self % chain % point_color ( 2 * i - 1 ) rgba ( 4 ) = rgba ( 4 ) * self % color_ ( 4 ) end function ribbon_drawn_color !> In trace mode, the pair at the current time (the tail's end) as drawn; !> false if no tail is drawn. logical function ribbon_trace_end ( self , a , b ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: a ( 3 ) !! the pair's start (frame coordinates) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: b ( 3 ) !! its end real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:,:), pointer :: p a = 0.0_wp b = 0.0_wp ribbon_trace_end = self % tail_shown if (. not . ribbon_trace_end ) return call line_buffer ( self % tail , p ) if (. not . associated ( p )) return a = real ( p ( 1 : 3 , 1 , 3 ), wp ) + real ( p ( 1 : 3 , 2 , 3 ), wp ) b = real ( p ( 1 : 3 , 1 , 4 ), wp ) + real ( p ( 1 : 3 , 2 , 4 ), wp ) end function ribbon_trace_end !> Number of trajectory points to draw the surface through (none if all !> sources are zero). integer function ribbon_points ( self ) result ( n ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self n = 0 if ( all ( self % start_ % src == SOURCE_ZERO ) . and . all ( self % end_ % src == SOURCE_ZERO )) return n = min ( source_points ( self % traj , self % start_ ), source_points ( self % traj , self % end_ )) end function ribbon_points !> The chain: a surface (a pair of points per trajectory point). pure integer function ribbon_chain_kind ( self ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self ribbon_chain_kind = CHAIN_RIBBON end function ribbon_chain_kind !> The trace tail: a quad (white unless the points' colors are drawn). function ribbon_new_tail ( self ) result ( node ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( c_ptr ) :: node node = vkf_ribbon_create ( 4_c_int , 1_c_int ) end function ribbon_new_tail !> Write the pairs of trajectory points i1 .. i2 into the chain, with their !> colors (and upload the chunks written to). subroutine write_ribbon ( self , i1 , i2 ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i1 , i2 real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:,:), pointer :: p real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: c , col real ( c_float ) :: own ( 4 ) real ( wp ), allocatable :: v (:,:) integer :: j , lo , hi , ia , ib , m , k do j = 1 , self % chain % num_chunks () call self % chain % slice ( j , 2 * i1 - 1 , 2 * i2 , lo , hi , p ) ! chunks hold whole pairs if (. not . associated ( p )) cycle ia = ( lo + 1 ) / 2 ! the trajectory points of the pairs ib = hi / 2 allocate ( v ( 3 , ib - ia + 1 )) call self % traj % points ( ia , ib , self % start_ , v ) call split_points ( v , p (:, :, 1 : hi - lo + 1 : 2 )) call self % traj % points ( ia , ib , self % end_ , v ) call split_points ( v , p (:, :, 2 : hi - lo + 1 : 2 )) deallocate ( v ) end do if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) then ! each pair in its point's color call self % traj % colors ( col ) m = self % traj % num_colors () own = real ( self % color_ , c_float ) own ( 4 ) = 1.0_c_float ! (the style has the alpha) do j = 1 , self % chain % num_chunks () call self % chain % color_slice ( j , 2 * i1 - 1 , 2 * i2 , lo , hi , c ) if (. not . associated ( c )) cycle do k = ( lo + 1 ) / 2 , hi / 2 if ( k <= m ) then c (:, 2 * k - lo : 2 * k - lo + 1 ) = spread ( col (:, k ), 2 , 2 ) else c (:, 2 * k - lo : 2 * k - lo + 1 ) = spread ( own , 2 , 2 ) end if end do end do self % n_colored = min ( m , i2 ) end if call self % chain % written ( 2 * i1 - 1 , 2 * i2 ) end subroutine write_ribbon !> The tail: the quad from the pair at point k to the pair interpolated at !> time t toward point k2 (as the curve's tail: none if either isn't a !> point written). subroutine update_ribbon_tail ( self , t , k , k2 ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t integer , intent ( in ) :: k , k2 real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:,:), pointer :: p real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: c real ( wp ) :: frac , xyz ( 3 , 4 ), c0 ( 4 ), c1 ( 4 ) integer ( c_int ) :: capacity type ( c_ptr ) :: data self % tail_shown = . false . if (. not . c_associated ( self % tail )) return if ( min ( k , k2 ) < 1 . or . max ( k , k2 ) > self % n_written ) then call check_status ( vkf_line_set_range ( self % tail , 1_c_int , 0_c_int ), 'trajectory artists' ) return end if frac = self % traj % time_fraction ( k , k2 , t ) xyz (:, 1 ) = self % traj % point ( k , self % start_ ) xyz (:, 2 ) = self % traj % point ( k , self % end_ ) xyz (:, 3 ) = self % traj % point_between ( k , k2 , t , self % start_ ) xyz (:, 4 ) = self % traj % point_between ( k , k2 , t , self % end_ ) call line_buffer ( self % tail , p ) if (. not . associated ( p )) return call split_points ( xyz , p (:, :, 1 : 4 )) data = vkf_line_colors ( self % tail , capacity ) if ( c_associated ( data ) . and . capacity >= 4 ) then call c_f_pointer ( data , c , [ 4 , 4 ]) if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) then c0 = ribbon_point_rgba ( self , k ) c1 = ribbon_point_rgba ( self , k2 ) c (:, 1 : 2 ) = spread ( real ( c0 , c_float ), 2 , 2 ) c (:, 3 : 4 ) = spread ( real ( c0 + frac * ( c1 - c0 ), c_float ), 2 , 2 ) else c = 1.0_c_float end if end if call check_status ( vkf_line_points_changed ( self % tail , 4_c_int ), 'trajectory artists' ) self % tail_shown = . true . end subroutine update_ribbon_tail !> Color of point i in a colored chain: the trajectory's, or the artist's !> (opaque: the style has the alpha) if it has none yet. function ribbon_point_rgba ( self , i ) result ( rgba ) type ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ) if ( i <= self % traj % num_colors ()) then rgba = self % traj % color ( i ) else rgba = [ self % color_ ( 1 : 3 ), 1.0_wp ] end if end function ribbon_point_rgba !> The style: the artist's color, or white with its alpha if the points' !> colors are drawn (the shader multiplies them by it). subroutine ribbon_style ( self ) class ( RibbonArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ) rgba = self % color_ if ( self % chain % is_colored ()) rgba ( 1 : 3 ) = 1.0_wp call self % chain % set_style ( rgba , 1.0_wp ) if ( c_associated ( self % tail )) & call check_status ( line_set_style ( self % tail , real ( rgba , c_float ), 1.0_c_float ), 'trajectory artists' ) end subroutine ribbon_style ! ================================================================== ! MarkerArtist !> A marker artist for `traj` (optional; without one, or with all data !> sources zero, a start marker at the origin: in a DrawableTrajectory that !> follows a trajectory, or is a child of a frame that does, it marks the !> current position, as in OpenFrames), drawing `markers` (an ior !> of MARKER_START, MARKER_INTERMEDIATE, MARKER_END; default start and end) !> of `size` window units (default 10) in `color` (all markers; default red !> start and end, white intermediate). function new_marker_artist ( traj , markers , size , color ) result ( a ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target , optional :: traj integer , intent ( in ), optional :: markers real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: size , color (:) type ( MarkerArtist ) :: a a % sources_ = position_sources ( 3 ) a % image_file = '' if ( present ( traj )) call a % set_trajectory ( traj ) if ( present ( markers )) a % markers_ = markers if ( present ( size )) a % size_ = size if ( present ( color )) call a % set_marker_color ( ior ( ior ( MARKER_START , MARKER_INTERMEDIATE ), MARKER_END ), color ) end function new_marker_artist !> Draw `traj`; with the default data sources, its positions (per its DOF). subroutine marker_set_trajectory ( self , traj ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: traj self % traj => traj if ( self % default_data ) self % sources_ = position_sources ( traj % dof ()) self % seen_generation = - 1 end subroutine marker_set_trajectory !> Where the x (y, z) of the markers come from. Returns whether the !> trajectory has those data. logical function marker_set_x_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_marker_source ( self , 1 , src ) end function marker_set_x_data !> Where the y of the markers come from (see set_x_data). logical function marker_set_y_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_marker_source ( self , 2 , src ) end function marker_set_y_data !> Where the z of the markers come from (see set_x_data). logical function marker_set_z_data ( self , src ) result ( valid ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src valid = set_marker_source ( self , 3 , src ) end function marker_set_z_data !> Set data source k (1: x, 2: y, 3: z), redrawing the markers; returns whether !> the trajectory has the data. logical function set_marker_source ( self , k , src ) result ( valid ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: k type ( DataSource ), intent ( in ) :: src self % sources_ ( k ) = src self % default_data = . false . call redraw_markers ( self ) valid = . true . if ( associated ( self % traj )) valid = self % traj % verify_data ( self % sources_ ) end function set_marker_source !> The x, y and z data sources. pure function marker_data_sources ( self ) result ( s ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( DataSource ) :: s ( 3 ) s = self % sources_ end function marker_data_sources !> Which markers to draw: an ior of MARKER_START, MARKER_INTERMEDIATE and !> MARKER_END (0 for none). subroutine set_markers ( self , markers ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: markers if ( markers == self % markers_ ) return self % markers_ = markers call redraw_markers ( self ) end subroutine set_markers !> Which markers are drawn (an ior of MARKER_* flags). pure integer function markers ( self ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self markers = self % markers_ end function markers !> The color of the markers in `which` (an ior of MARKER_* flags): [r, g, !> b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a]. subroutine set_marker_color ( self , which , color ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: which real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) if ( iand ( which , MARKER_START ) /= 0 ) call set_rgba ( self % start_color , color ) if ( iand ( which , MARKER_END ) /= 0 ) call set_rgba ( self % end_color , color ) if ( iand ( which , MARKER_INTERMEDIATE ) /= 0 ) call set_rgba ( self % intermediate_color , color ) call marker_style ( self ) end subroutine set_marker_color !> The color of the start, intermediate or end markers (`which`: one MARKER_* flag). pure function marker_color ( self , which ) result ( c ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: which real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) select case ( which ) case ( MARKER_START ) c = self % start_color case ( MARKER_END ) c = self % end_color case default c = self % intermediate_color end select end function marker_color !> Marker size in window units (logical pixels; > 0). subroutine set_marker_size ( self , size ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: size if ( size <= 0.0_wp ) return self % size_ = size call marker_style ( self ) end subroutine set_marker_size !> Marker size (window units). pure real ( wp ) function marker_size ( self ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self marker_size = self % size_ end function marker_size !> Marker shape: a MARKER_* shape constant (MARKER_DISK to MARKER_SPIRAL; !> MARKER_IMAGE after set_marker_image). These are OpenFrames' disk and its !> marker shaders (Demos/Shaders/Marker_*.frag), built in. subroutine set_marker_shape ( self , shape ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: shape self % shape_ = max ( MARKER_DISK , min ( MARKER_IMAGE , shape )) call marker_style ( self ) end subroutine set_marker_shape !> Marker shape (a MARKER_* shape constant). pure integer function marker_shape ( self ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self marker_shape = self % shape_ end function marker_shape !> Draw the markers as an image file (tinted by the marker color; its !> transparent parts left out), or as a disk again with ''. Returns false !> if the image cannot be read (the markers are then unchanged). logical function set_marker_image ( self , file ) result ( ok ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: file type ( c_ptr ) :: image ok = . true . if ( len_trim ( file ) == 0 ) then image = c_null_ptr self % shape_ = MARKER_DISK else image = vkf_image_read ( trim ( file ), len_trim ( file , kind = c_int )) ok = c_associated ( image ) if (. not . ok ) return self % shape_ = MARKER_IMAGE end if if ( c_associated ( self % image )) call vkf_image_delete ( self % image ) self % image = image self % image_file = trim ( file ) call rebuild_markers ( self ) ! the image is part of the marker nodes end function set_marker_image !> The marker image file ('' for none). function marker_image_file ( self ) result ( file ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: file file = self % image_file end function marker_image_file !> Shrink markers farther from the camera than the trajectory's size !> (OpenFrames' auto-attenuation; see shaders/marker.vert). On by default !> (OpenFrames': off). subroutine set_auto_attenuate ( self , attenuate ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: attenuate self % attenuate = attenuate call marker_style ( self ) end subroutine set_auto_attenuate !> Whether the markers are auto-attenuated. pure logical function auto_attenuate ( self ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self auto_attenuate = self % attenuate end function auto_attenuate !> How intermediate markers are spaced: INTERMEDIATE_TIME, _DISTANCE or _DATA. !> Point colors (default off): with the trajectory's colors (Trajectory% !> add_color, or add's `color`), each marker is drawn in the color at its !> point (intermediate markers between points: blended between theirs, by !> time), points without a color yet in the marker's own color !> (set_marker_color). Off, or without colors: the markers' own colors. subroutine marker_set_point_colors ( self , enabled ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: enabled if ( enabled . eqv . self % point_colors_ ) return self % point_colors_ = enabled call rebuild_markers ( self ) end subroutine marker_set_point_colors !> Whether the trajectory's colors are drawn (set_point_colors). pure logical function marker_point_colors ( self ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self marker_point_colors = self % point_colors_ end function marker_point_colors !> The color marker k of `which` (one MARKER_* flag; k: the intermediate !> marker's number) is drawn in: read back from its buffer with point !> colors, else the marker's own color. function marker_drawn_color ( self , which , k ) result ( rgba ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: which integer , intent ( in ), optional :: k real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ) integer :: i i = 1 if ( present ( k )) i = k select case ( which ) case ( MARKER_START ) rgba = self % start_color if ( self % start_node % is_colored ()) rgba = self % start_node % point_color ( 1 ) case ( MARKER_END ) rgba = self % end_color if ( self % end_node % is_colored ()) rgba = self % end_node % point_color ( 1 ) case default rgba = self % intermediate_color if ( self % inter % is_colored ()) rgba = self % inter % point_color ( i ) end select end function marker_drawn_color !> Whether the markers are drawn in the trajectory's colors: wanted, and it has some. logical function marker_uses_colors ( self ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self marker_uses_colors = self % point_colors_ . and . associated ( self % traj ) if ( marker_uses_colors ) marker_uses_colors = self % traj % num_colors () > 0 end function marker_uses_colors !> The trajectory's color at time t (between points i and i + 1: blended), !> `own` for points without one. function color_at ( self , t , own ) result ( rgba ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t , own ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ), c1 ( 4 ), t0 , t1 integer :: status , i , n n = self % traj % num_times () status = self % traj % time_index ( t , i ) i = max ( 1 , min ( n , i )) rgba = point_rgba_or ( self % traj , i , own ) if ( i >= n ) return t0 = self % traj % time ( i ) t1 = self % traj % time ( i + 1 ) if ( t1 == t0 ) return c1 = point_rgba_or ( self % traj , i + 1 , own ) rgba = rgba + max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , ( t - t0 ) / ( t1 - t0 ))) * ( c1 - rgba ) end function color_at !> Color of point i: the trajectory's, or `own` if it has none yet. pure function point_rgba_or ( traj , i , own ) result ( rgba ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ) :: traj integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: own ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ) rgba = own if ( i >= 1 . and . i <= traj % num_colors ()) rgba = traj % color ( i ) end function point_rgba_or subroutine set_intermediate_type ( self , type ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: type if ( type == self % intermediate_type_ ) return self % intermediate_type_ = type call redraw_markers ( self ) end subroutine set_intermediate_type !> How intermediate markers are spaced (INTERMEDIATE_*). pure integer function intermediate_type ( self ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self intermediate_type = self % intermediate_type_ end function intermediate_type !> Spacing of intermediate markers (> 0): time units, arc length, or a !> number of data points (rounded down, at least 1). subroutine set_intermediate_spacing ( self , spacing ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: spacing if ( spacing <= 0.0_wp . or . spacing == self % spacing_ ) return self % spacing_ = spacing call redraw_markers ( self ) end subroutine set_intermediate_spacing !> Spacing of intermediate markers. pure real ( wp ) function intermediate_spacing ( self ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self intermediate_spacing = self % spacing_ end function intermediate_spacing !> Count intermediate markers from the start (MARKER_START, default) or !> from the end (MARKER_END; recomputed whenever points are added). subroutine set_intermediate_direction ( self , direction ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: direction if ( direction == self % direction_ ) return self % direction_ = merge ( MARKER_END , MARKER_START , direction == MARKER_END ) call redraw_markers ( self ) end subroutine set_intermediate_direction !> Where intermediate markers are counted from (MARKER_START or MARKER_END). pure integer function intermediate_direction ( self ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self intermediate_direction = self % direction_ end function intermediate_direction !> Number of intermediate markers drawn now. pure integer function num_intermediate ( self ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self num_intermediate = self % n_inter_drawn end function num_intermediate !> Where marker `which` (MARKER_START, MARKER_END, or MARKER_INTERMEDIATE !> number i) is drawn, read back from its buffer; false if not drawn. logical function drawn_marker ( self , which , v , i ) result ( shown ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: which real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: v ( 3 ) !! where it is drawn (frame coordinates) integer , intent ( in ), optional :: i !! the intermediate marker's number (1 to num_intermediate) v = 0.0_wp select case ( which ) case ( MARKER_START ) shown = self % start_shown if ( shown ) v = self % start_node % point ( 1 ) case ( MARKER_END ) shown = self % end_shown if ( shown ) v = self % end_node % point ( 1 ) case default shown = . false . if (. not . present ( i )) return shown = i >= self % inter_first . and . i <= self % inter_first + self % n_inter_drawn - 1 if ( shown ) v = self % inter % point ( i ) end select end function drawn_marker !> Create the marker nodes under `group` (see artist_build). subroutine marker_build ( self , viewer , group ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer , group self % group = group self % shown = c_associated ( viewer ) call build_marker_nodes ( self , compile = . false .) end subroutine marker_build !> The start, end and intermediate marker nodes, in the artist's group !> (compiled now if it is already shown). subroutine build_marker_nodes ( self , compile ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: compile logical :: colored colored = marker_uses_colors ( self ) call self % start_node % init ( self % group , CHAIN_MARKERS , self % image , colored = colored ) call self % end_node % init ( self % group , CHAIN_MARKERS , self % image , colored = colored ) call self % inter % init ( self % group , CHAIN_MARKERS , self % image , colored = colored ) call self % start_node % set_compile ( compile . and . self % shown ) call self % end_node % set_compile ( compile . and . self % shown ) call self % inter % set_compile ( compile . and . self % shown ) call self % start_node % reserve ( 1 ) call self % end_node % reserve ( 1 ) call self % inter % reserve ( 1 ) call self % start_node % set_compile ( self % shown ) call self % end_node % set_compile ( self % shown ) call self % inter % set_compile ( self % shown ) call marker_style ( self ) call redraw_markers ( self ) end subroutine build_marker_nodes !> New marker nodes (for a new image), in place of the old ones. subroutine rebuild_markers ( self ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self if (. not . c_associated ( self % group )) return call self % start_node % detach () call self % end_node % detach () call self % inter % detach () call build_marker_nodes ( self , compile = . true .) end subroutine rebuild_markers !> Compute and write everything again at the next update. subroutine redraw_markers ( self ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self self % seen_generation = - 1 self % drawn = . false . end subroutine redraw_markers !> Forget the render nodes (see artist_release). subroutine marker_release ( self ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self call self % start_node % release () call self % end_node % release () call self % inter % release () self % group = c_null_ptr self % start_shown = . false . self % end_shown = . false . self % n_inter_drawn = 0 self % inter_first = 1 call redraw_markers ( self ) call artist_release ( self ) end subroutine marker_release !> Apply the colors, size, shape and attenuation radius (0: off) to the marker nodes. subroutine marker_style ( self ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ) :: r r = 0.0_wp if ( self % attenuate ) r = self % radius call self % start_node % set_marker_style ( style_color ( self % start_node , self % start_color ), self % size_ , self % shape_ , r ) call self % end_node % set_marker_style ( style_color ( self % end_node , self % end_color ), self % size_ , self % shape_ , r ) call self % inter % set_marker_style ( style_color ( self % inter , self % intermediate_color ), self % size_ , self % shape_ , r ) contains !> The style's color: the marker's, or white if each marker has its own (the shader multiplies them). function style_color ( chain , own ) result ( c ) type ( LineChain ), intent ( in ) :: chain real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: own ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = own if ( chain % is_colored ()) c = 1.0_wp end function style_color end subroutine marker_style !> Write the start, end and new intermediate markers if the trajectory changed, !> and draw them all or, in trace mode, those passed at time t. subroutine marker_update ( self , t ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t logical :: changed , redraw , zero , passed_start , passed_end integer :: n if (. not . c_associated ( self % group )) return zero = all ( self % sources_ % src == SOURCE_ZERO ) . or . . not . associated ( self % traj ) ! (a marker at the origin) if ( zero ) then n = 1 ! a marker at the origin else n = source_points ( self % traj , self % sources_ ) end if ! the trajectory's colors drawn or not (its first colors, or the setting, ! changed): the marker nodes made again, with or without colors if ( marker_uses_colors ( self ) . neqv . self % inter % is_colored ()) call rebuild_markers ( self ) changed = data_changed ( self , redraw ) if (. not . self % drawn ) then changed = . true . redraw = . true . self % drawn = . true . end if if ( changed ) then if ( self % inter % is_colored ()) then ! (colors added or changed: all written again) if ( self % traj % num_colors () /= self % n_colors_seen ) redraw = . true . self % n_colors_seen = self % traj % num_colors () end if if ( redraw . or . n < self % n_seen ) call reset_markers ( self ) call update_bounds ( self , n , zero ) if ( n >= 1 ) call write_marker ( self % start_node , marker_point ( self , 1 , zero ), & ! (none: nothing drawn) end_rgba ( self , 1 , self % start_color )) if ( n > 1 ) call write_marker ( self % end_node , marker_point ( self , n , zero ), end_rgba ( self , n , self % end_color )) if ( iand ( self % markers_ , MARKER_INTERMEDIATE ) /= 0 . and . . not . zero . and . n > 2 ) call add_intermediates ( self , n ) end if ! what is drawn: everything, or in trace mode the markers whose times ! have passed (the start and end markers at their points' times) passed_start = . true . passed_end = . true . if ( self % trace . and . . not . zero . and . n >= 1 ) then passed_start = self % traj % time ( 1 ) <= t passed_end = self % traj % time ( n ) <= t end if self % start_shown = iand ( self % markers_ , MARKER_START ) /= 0 . and . n >= 1 . and . passed_start call self % start_node % draw ( merge ( 1 , 0 , self % start_shown )) self % end_shown = iand ( self % markers_ , MARKER_END ) /= 0 . and . n > 1 . and . passed_end call self % end_node % draw ( merge ( 1 , 0 , self % end_shown )) self % inter_first = 1 self % n_inter_drawn = self % n_inter_written if ( self % trace . and . self % n_inter_written > 0 ) call markers_passed ( self , t , self % inter_first , self % n_inter_drawn ) call self % inter % draw_range ( self % inter_first , self % inter_first + self % n_inter_drawn - 1 ) end subroutine marker_update !> The color of point i for a start or end marker: the trajectory's (its !> own if none), with point colors. function end_rgba ( self , i , own ) result ( rgba ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: own ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ) rgba = own if ( self % inter % is_colored ()) rgba = point_rgba_or ( self % traj , i , own ) end function end_rgba !> Point i from the data sources (the origin if `zero`). function marker_point ( self , i , zero ) result ( v ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i logical , intent ( in ) :: zero !! all sources zero, or no trajectory: the origin real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) v = 0.0_wp if (. not . zero ) v = self % traj % point ( i , self % sources_ ) end function marker_point !> A single marker's point (in a chain of one marker), and its color (a !> colored chain), uploaded. subroutine write_marker ( chain , v , rgba ) type ( LineChain ), intent ( inout ) :: chain real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: v ( 3 ), rgba ( 4 ) real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:,:), pointer :: p real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: c integer :: lo , hi if ( chain % num_chunks () < 1 ) return call chain % slice ( 1 , 1 , 1 , lo , hi , p ) if (. not . associated ( p )) return call split_points ( reshape ( v , [ 3 , 1 ]), p ) call chain % color_slice ( 1 , 1 , 1 , lo , hi , c ) if ( associated ( c )) c (:, 1 ) = real ( rgba , c_float ) call chain % written ( 1 , 1 ) end subroutine write_marker !> Start the intermediate markers and the bounds again. subroutine reset_markers ( self ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self self % n_seen = 0 self % n_inter = 0 self % n_inter_written = 0 self % next_index = 0 ! (0: not started) end subroutine reset_markers !> The bounds of the points (for the attenuation radius: OpenFrames uses !> the artist's bounding sphere). subroutine update_bounds ( self , n , zero ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n logical , intent ( in ) :: zero !! all sources zero, or no trajectory: a marker at the origin real ( wp ), allocatable :: v (:,:) real ( wp ) :: r if ( zero ) then self % lo = 0.0_wp self % hi = 0.0_wp else if ( n > self % n_seen ) then ! the new points, a range at a time allocate ( v ( 3 , n - self % n_seen )) call self % traj % points ( self % n_seen + 1 , n , self % sources_ , v ) if ( self % n_seen == 0 ) then self % lo = v (:, 1 ) self % hi = v (:, 1 ) end if self % lo = min ( self % lo , minval ( v , dim = 2 )) self % hi = max ( self % hi , maxval ( v , dim = 2 )) end if self % n_seen = n r = 0.5_wp * norm2 ( self % hi - self % lo ) if ( r < 1.0e-8_wp ) r = 0.0_wp ! too small: no attenuation (as OpenFrames) if ( r /= self % radius ) then self % radius = r if ( self % attenuate ) call marker_style ( self ) end if end subroutine update_bounds !> Compute the intermediate markers not computed yet (all of them when !> counted from the end), and write them. subroutine add_intermediates ( self , n ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n integer :: first if ( self % direction_ == MARKER_END ) then ! everything changes when points are added self % n_inter = 0 self % n_inter_written = 0 self % next_index = 0 end if select case ( self % intermediate_type_ ) case ( INTERMEDIATE_TIME ) call intermediates_by_time ( self , n ) case ( INTERMEDIATE_DISTANCE ) call intermediates_by_distance ( self , n ) case default call intermediates_by_data ( self , n ) end select if ( self % direction_ == MARKER_END ) then ! in trajectory order self % inter_xyz (:, 1 : self % n_inter ) = self % inter_xyz (:, self % n_inter : 1 : - 1 ) self % inter_t ( 1 : self % n_inter ) = self % inter_t ( self % n_inter : 1 : - 1 ) if ( self % inter % is_colored ()) self % inter_rgba (:, 1 : self % n_inter ) = self % inter_rgba (:, self % n_inter : 1 : - 1 ) end if first = self % n_inter_written + 1 if ( self % n_inter >= first ) call write_intermediates ( self , first , self % n_inter ) self % n_inter_written = self % n_inter end subroutine add_intermediates !> Index of the j-th point counted in the intermediate markers' direction. pure integer function counted ( self , j , n ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: j , n counted = merge ( n + 1 - j , j , self % direction_ == MARKER_END ) end function counted !> Every `spacing` time units after the first time, before the last !> (counted from the start or the end). subroutine intermediates_by_time ( self , n ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n real ( wp ) :: t_first , t_last , step , tm integer :: status , index t_first = self % traj % time ( counted ( self , 1 , n )) t_last = self % traj % time ( counted ( self , n , n )) step = sign ( self % spacing_ , t_last - t_first ) if ( self % next_index == 0 ) then self % next_time = t_first + step self % next_index = 1 end if do while ( sign ( 1.0_wp , step ) * ( t_last - self % next_time ) > 0.0_wp ) tm = self % next_time status = self % traj % time_index ( tm , index ) index = max ( 1 , min ( n - 1 , index )) call push_intermediate ( self , self % traj % point_between ( index , index + 1 , tm , self % sources_ ), tm ) self % next_time = self % next_time + step end do end subroutine intermediates_by_time !> Every int(spacing)-th point after the first, before the last. subroutine intermediates_by_data ( self , n ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n integer :: step , i step = max ( 1 , int ( self % spacing_ )) if ( self % next_index == 0 ) self % next_index = 1 + step do while ( self % next_index < n ) i = counted ( self , self % next_index , n ) call push_intermediate ( self , self % traj % point ( i , self % sources_ ), self % traj % time ( i )) self % next_index = self % next_index + step end do end subroutine intermediates_by_data !> Every `spacing` of arc length (the points joined by straight lines). subroutine intermediates_by_distance ( self , n ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ), frac , t0 , t1 integer :: j if ( self % next_index == 0 ) then self % next_index = 2 self % arc = 0.0_wp self % prev_arc = 0.0_wp self % target = self % spacing_ self % prev_point = self % traj % point ( counted ( self , 1 , n ), self % sources_ ) end if do j = self % next_index , n p = self % traj % point ( counted ( self , j , n ), self % sources_ ) self % arc = self % arc + norm2 ( p - self % prev_point ) t0 = self % traj % time ( counted ( self , j - 1 , n )) t1 = self % traj % time ( counted ( self , j , n )) do while ( self % arc >= self % target ) frac = ( self % target - self % prev_arc ) / ( self % arc - self % prev_arc ) call push_intermediate ( self , self % prev_point + frac * ( p - self % prev_point ), t0 + frac * ( t1 - t0 )) self % target = self % target + self % spacing_ end do self % prev_arc = self % arc self % prev_point = p end do self % next_index = n + 1 end subroutine intermediates_by_distance !> Append an intermediate marker at `v`, time `t` (the arrays grown as needed). subroutine push_intermediate ( self , v , t ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: v ( 3 ), t real ( wp ), allocatable :: xyz (:,:), times (:), rgba (:,:) integer :: m if (. not . allocated ( self % inter_xyz )) allocate ( self % inter_xyz ( 3 , 64 ), self % inter_t ( 64 ), self % inter_rgba ( 4 , 64 )) m = size ( self % inter_t ) if ( self % n_inter == m ) then allocate ( xyz ( 3 , 2 * m ), times ( 2 * m ), rgba ( 4 , 2 * m )) xyz (:, 1 : m ) = self % inter_xyz times ( 1 : m ) = self % inter_t rgba (:, 1 : m ) = self % inter_rgba call move_alloc ( xyz , self % inter_xyz ) call move_alloc ( times , self % inter_t ) call move_alloc ( rgba , self % inter_rgba ) end if self % n_inter = self % n_inter + 1 self % inter_xyz (:, self % n_inter ) = v self % inter_t ( self % n_inter ) = t if ( self % inter % is_colored ()) self % inter_rgba (:, self % n_inter ) = color_at ( self , t , self % intermediate_color ) end subroutine push_intermediate !> Write intermediate markers i1 .. i2 into their chain, with their colors !> (with point colors), and upload the chunks written to. subroutine write_intermediates ( self , i1 , i2 ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i1 , i2 real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:,:), pointer :: p real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: c integer :: j , lo , hi call self % inter % reserve ( i2 ) do j = 1 , self % inter % num_chunks () call self % inter % slice ( j , i1 , i2 , lo , hi , p ) if (. not . associated ( p )) cycle call split_points ( self % inter_xyz (:, lo : hi ), p ) call self % inter % color_slice ( j , i1 , i2 , lo , hi , c ) if ( associated ( c )) c = real ( self % inter_rgba (:, lo : hi ), c_float ) end do call self % inter % written ( i1 , i2 ) end subroutine write_intermediates !> The intermediate markers (in trajectory order) whose times are at most !> t: `count` from `first` (the first ones for increasing times, the last !> for decreasing), by bisection. subroutine markers_passed ( self , t , first , count ) type ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t integer , intent ( out ) :: first , count integer :: low , high , mid , m m = self % n_inter_written low = 0 high = m + 1 if (. not . decreasing_times ( self % traj , self % traj % num_times ())) then ! markers 1 .. low passed do while ( high - low > 1 ) mid = ( low + high ) / 2 if ( self % inter_t ( mid ) <= t ) then low = mid else high = mid end if end do first = 1 count = low else ! markers high .. m passed do while ( high - low > 1 ) mid = ( low + high ) / 2 if ( self % inter_t ( mid ) <= t ) then high = mid else low = mid end if end do first = high count = m - high + 1 end if end subroutine markers_passed ! ================================================================== ! DrawableTrajectory !> A drawable trajectory frame named `name` (decorations of color `color`). function new_drawable_trajectory ( name , color ) result ( d ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) type ( DrawableTrajectory ) :: d d % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) end function new_drawable_trajectory !> Add an artist (it must stay alive while added). Artists added after the !> frame is shown are built and compiled at the next update. subroutine add_artist ( self , a ) class ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( in ), target :: a type ( ArtistPointer ), allocatable :: tmp (:) integer :: k do k = 1 , self % n_artists if ( associated ( self % artists ( k )% p , a )) return end do if (. not . allocated ( self % artists )) allocate ( self % artists ( 4 )) if ( self % n_artists == size ( self % artists )) then allocate ( tmp ( 2 * self % n_artists )) tmp ( 1 : self % n_artists ) = self % artists ( 1 : self % n_artists ) call move_alloc ( tmp , self % artists ) end if self % n_artists = self % n_artists + 1 self % artists ( self % n_artists )% p => a self % artists ( self % n_artists )% group = c_null_ptr end subroutine add_artist !> Remove an artist (it stops being drawn; it can be added again, also to !> another frame). subroutine remove_artist ( self , a ) class ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( TrajectoryArtist ), intent ( in ), target :: a integer :: k do k = 1 , self % n_artists if ( associated ( self % artists ( k )% p , a )) then if ( c_associated ( self % artists ( k )% group )) then call check_status ( vkf_node_remove_child ( self % contents_group , self % artists ( k )% group ), 'trajectory artists' ) call vkf_node_delete ( self % artists ( k )% group ) call self % artists ( k )% p % release () end if self % artists ( k : self % n_artists - 1 ) = self % artists ( k + 1 : self % n_artists ) self % n_artists = self % n_artists - 1 return end if end do end subroutine remove_artist !> Remove all the artists. subroutine remove_all_artists ( self ) class ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self do while ( self % n_artists > 0 ) call self % remove_artist ( self % artists ( self % n_artists )% p ) end do end subroutine remove_all_artists !> Number of artists. pure integer function num_artists ( self ) class ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self num_artists = self % n_artists end function num_artists !> Artist i (1 to num_artists). function artist ( self , i ) result ( a ) class ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: i class ( TrajectoryArtist ), pointer :: a a => self % artists ( i )% p end function artist !> Highlight all the frame's curve and segment artists (see !> CurveArtist%set_highlight; HIGHLIGHT_NONE: none of them). subroutine drawable_set_highlight ( self , mode , color , arrow_spacing , arrow_speed , band_width , pulse_period ) class ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: mode !! HIGHLIGHT_* (added) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: arrow_spacing !! between arrows (window units; default 40) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: arrow_speed !! (window units per second; default 50) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: band_width !! of the arrows' band (window units; default 12) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: pulse_period !! (s; default 1.5) integer :: k do k = 1 , self % n_artists select type ( a => self % artists ( k )% p ) class is ( CurveArtist ) call a % set_highlight ( mode , color , arrow_spacing , arrow_speed , band_width , pulse_period ) class is ( SegmentArtist ) call a % set_highlight ( mode , color , arrow_spacing , arrow_speed , band_width , pulse_period ) end select end do end subroutine drawable_set_highlight !> Picks what the artists draw (see the module documentation), then !> the frame's origin (if it shows axes or its name label). subroutine drawable_pick ( self , cam , to_root , hits , n ) class ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: self type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: to_root ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits are added to hits(1:n) integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits integer :: k if ( self % contents_shown ()) then do k = 1 , self % n_artists if (. not . self % artists ( k )% p % pickable_ ) cycle select type ( a => self % artists ( k )% p ) class is ( CurveArtist ) if ( wants ( cam , PICK_CURVE )) call curve_pick ( a , self , cam , to_root , hits , n ) class is ( SegmentArtist ) if ( wants ( cam , PICK_SEGMENT )) call segment_artist_pick ( a , self , cam , to_root , hits , n ) class is ( MarkerArtist ) if ( wants ( cam , PICK_MARKER )) call marker_pick ( a , self , cam , to_root , hits , n ) end select end do end if call self % ReferenceFrame % pick ( cam , to_root , hits , n ) end subroutine drawable_pick !> A candidate closer to the cursor than the best so far (or as close, and nearer). pure logical function better ( pixels , depth , best_pixels , best_depth ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: pixels !! the candidate's distance from the cursor (pixels) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: depth !! its depth real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: best_pixels !! the best hit's so far (pixels) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: best_depth !! the best hit's depth better = pixels < best_pixels - 0.5_wp . or . ( pixels <= best_pixels + 0.5_wp . and . depth < best_depth ) end function better !> A curve's best hit: on the segments drawn (and the trace tail). subroutine curve_pick ( a , frame , cam , m , hits , n ) class ( CurveArtist ), intent ( in ), target :: a class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: frame !! the frame drawing it (for the hit) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits are added to hits(1:n) integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits real ( wp ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: pos real ( wp ) :: extra , lo ( 3 ), hi ( 3 ), c ( 3 ), p0 ( 3 ), p1 ( 3 ), px , s , depth , best_px , best_depth , best_s , t0 , t1 , frac integer :: j , first , count , i1 , i2 , i , best_i , best_j , nd , d1 , d2 logical :: xyz type ( PickHit ) :: h if (. not . associated ( a % traj ) . or . . not . a % chain % is_built ()) return nd = a % n_drawn if ( nd < 1 ) return d1 = a % first_drawn_ ! (the points drawn: d1 .. d2) d2 = d1 + nd - 1 extra = 0.5_wp * a % width_ * cam % pixel_ratio xyz = is_position_xyz ( a % sources_ ) if ( xyz ) call a % traj % positions ( pos ) best_px = huge ( 1.0_wp ) best_depth = huge ( 1.0_wp ) best_i = 0 best_j = 0 ! (the hit is between points best_i and best_j) best_s = 0.0_wp if ( nd == 1 ) then ! (a single point) if ( point_pick ( cam , root_point ( d1 ), px , depth , extra )) then best_px = px best_depth = depth best_i = d1 end if end if do j = 1 , a % chain % num_chunks () ! the segments drawn, chunk by chunk call a % chain % chunk_bounds ( j , first , count , lo , hi ) i1 = max ( first , d1 ) i2 = min ( first + count - 1 , d2 ) if ( count < 2 . or . i2 <= i1 ) cycle c = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), 0.5_wp * ( lo + hi )) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) if (. not . sphere_near ( cam , c , 0.5_wp * norm2 ( hi - lo ), extra )) cycle ! (a chunk far off: skipped) p0 = root_point ( i1 ) do i = i1 , i2 - 1 p1 = root_point ( i + 1 ) if ( segment_pick ( cam , p0 , p1 , px , s , depth , extra )) then if ( better ( px , depth , best_px , best_depth )) then best_px = px best_depth = depth best_i = i best_j = i + 1 best_s = s end if end if p0 = p1 end do end do ! trace mode: the tail from the latest point passed to the point at the time drawn if ( a % trace . and . a % tail_shown ) then t0 = a % traj % time ( a % tail_from ) t1 = a % traj % time ( a % tail_to ) frac = 0.0_wp if ( t1 /= t0 ) frac = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , ( a % tail_time - t0 ) / ( t1 - t0 ))) p0 = root_point ( a % tail_from ) p1 = p0 + frac * ( root_point ( a % tail_to ) - p0 ) if ( segment_pick ( cam , p0 , p1 , px , s , depth , extra )) then if ( better ( px , depth , best_px , best_depth )) then best_px = px best_depth = depth best_i = a % tail_from best_j = a % tail_to best_s = s * frac end if end if end if if ( best_i == 0 ) return h % kind = PICK_CURVE h % frame => frame h % artist => a h % trajectory => a % traj h % index = best_i if ( best_j > 0 ) h % index = min ( best_i , best_j ) ! (the point the hit is after, in point order) h % local = local_point ( best_i ) h % time = a % traj % time ( best_i ) if ( best_j > 0 ) then h % local = h % local + best_s * ( local_point ( best_j ) - h % local ) h % time = h % time + best_s * ( a % traj % time ( best_j ) - h % time ) end if h % position = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), h % local ) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) h % distance = best_depth h % pixels = best_px call add_pick_hit ( hits , n , h ) contains !> Point i in the frame's coordinates (straight from the positions if they are the sources). function local_point ( i ) result ( v ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) if ( xyz ) then v = pos (:, i ) else v = a % traj % point ( i , a % sources_ ) end if end function local_point !> Point i in the root frame. function root_point ( i ) result ( v ) integer , intent ( in ) :: i real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) v = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), local_point ( i )) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) end function root_point end subroutine curve_pick !> A segment artist's best hit: on the segments drawn (as drawn: relative !> ends included; a segment of no length isn't drawn). subroutine segment_artist_pick ( a , frame , cam , m , hits , n ) class ( SegmentArtist ), intent ( in ), target :: a class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: frame !! the frame drawing it (for the hit) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits are added to hits(1:n) integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits real ( wp ) :: extra , a0 ( 3 ), b0 ( 3 ), px , s , depth , best_px , best_depth , best_s integer :: k , best_k type ( PickHit ) :: h if (. not . associated ( a % traj ) . or . a % n_drawn < 1 ) return extra = 0.5_wp * a % width_ * cam % pixel_ratio best_px = huge ( 1.0_wp ) best_depth = huge ( 1.0_wp ) best_k = 0 best_s = 0.0_wp do k = a % first_drawn_ , a % first_drawn_ + a % n_drawn - 1 call a % drawn_segment ( k , a0 , b0 ) if ( all ( a0 == b0 )) cycle if ( segment_pick ( cam , matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), a0 ) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ), matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), b0 ) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ), & px , s , depth , extra )) then if ( better ( px , depth , best_px , best_depth )) then best_px = px best_depth = depth best_k = k best_s = s end if end if end do if ( best_k == 0 ) return call a % drawn_segment ( best_k , a0 , b0 ) h % kind = PICK_SEGMENT h % frame => frame h % artist => a h % trajectory => a % traj h % index = best_k h % time = a % traj % time ( min ( a % traj % num_times (), 1 + ( best_k - 1 ) * a % stride_ )) h % local = a0 + best_s * ( b0 - a0 ) h % position = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), h % local ) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) h % distance = best_depth h % pixels = best_px call add_pick_hit ( hits , n , h ) end subroutine segment_artist_pick !> A marker artist's best hit: its start, end and intermediate markers drawn. subroutine marker_pick ( a , frame , cam , m , hits , n ) class ( MarkerArtist ), intent ( in ), target :: a class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: frame !! the frame drawing it (for the hit) type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits are added to hits(1:n) integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits real ( wp ) :: extra , v ( 3 ), px , depth , best_px , best_depth , best_v ( 3 ) integer :: k , which , best_which , best_k , npts type ( PickHit ) :: h extra = 0.5_wp * a % size_ * cam % pixel_ratio best_px = huge ( 1.0_wp ) best_depth = huge ( 1.0_wp ) best_which = 0 best_k = 0 best_v = 0.0_wp do which = 1 , 3 ! start, end, the intermediate ones select case ( which ) case ( 1 ) if ( a % drawn_marker ( MARKER_START , v )) call consider ( MARKER_START , 0 ) case ( 2 ) if ( a % drawn_marker ( MARKER_END , v )) call consider ( MARKER_END , 0 ) case ( 3 ) do k = a % inter_first , a % inter_first + a % n_inter_drawn - 1 if ( a % drawn_marker ( MARKER_INTERMEDIATE , v , k )) call consider ( MARKER_INTERMEDIATE , k ) end do end select end do if ( best_which == 0 ) return h % kind = PICK_MARKER h % frame => frame h % artist => a h % marker = best_which npts = 0 if ( associated ( a % traj )) then h % trajectory => a % traj npts = source_points ( a % traj , a % sources_ ) end if select case ( best_which ) case ( MARKER_START ) h % index = min ( 1 , npts ) if ( npts > 0 ) h % time = a % traj % time ( 1 ) case ( MARKER_END ) h % index = npts if ( npts > 0 ) h % time = a % traj % time ( npts ) case default h % index = best_k h % time = a % inter_t ( best_k ) end select h % local = best_v h % position = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), best_v ) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) h % distance = best_depth h % pixels = best_px call add_pick_hit ( hits , n , h ) contains !> Take the marker at `v` (`kind`, intermediate number k) as the best hit if picked and better. subroutine consider ( kind , k ) integer , intent ( in ) :: kind , k if (. not . point_pick ( cam , matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), v ) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ), px , depth , extra )) return if (. not . better ( px , depth , best_px , best_depth )) return best_px = px best_depth = depth best_which = kind best_k = k best_v = v end subroutine consider end subroutine marker_pick !> What kind of frame this is: 'DrawableTrajectory'. function drawable_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'DrawableTrajectory' end function drawable_frame_info !> Build the artists' nodes under `group` (`viewer`, may be null: those made !> later are compiled if not null). subroutine drawable_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer , group integer :: k self % shown = c_associated ( viewer ) self % contents_group = group do k = 1 , self % n_artists call build_artist ( self , k , compile = . false .) end do end subroutine drawable_build_contents !> Update the frame (and its descendants), then its artists. recursive subroutine drawable_update ( self , t ) class ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t integer :: k call self % ReferenceFrame % update ( t ) do k = 1 , self % n_artists if (. not . c_associated ( self % artists ( k )% group ) . and . c_associated ( self % contents_group )) & call build_artist ( self , k , compile = . true .) if ( c_associated ( self % artists ( k )% group )) call self % artists ( k )% p % update ( t ) end do end subroutine drawable_update !> Create artist k's node (compiled now if the frame is already shown). subroutine build_artist ( self , k , compile ) type ( DrawableTrajectory ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: k logical , intent ( in ) :: compile type ( c_ptr ) :: group group = vkf_switch_create () if (. not . c_associated ( group )) return ! (built for a window that exists now, if shown; compiled for the windows running) call self % artists ( k )% p % build ( merge ( vkf_viewer_any (), c_null_ptr , self % shown ), group ) if ( compile . and . self % shown ) call check_status ( vkf_compile_node ( group ), 'trajectory artists' ) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % contents_group , group ), 'trajectory artists' ) self % artists ( k )% group = group end subroutine build_artist end module vkf_artists","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_artists.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_line_segments.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_line_segments.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90 vkf_line_segments.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_chain.f90 vkf_line_chain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90->sourcefile~vkf_line_chain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_line_segments.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf