========== ! picking !> What is under point (x, y) of the window (-1 to 1 across it, y up: as !> the event handler's positions), nearest first (see the module !> documentation): none before the first frame. `tolerance`: how close !> lines, markers and frames' origins must be, in window units (logical !> pixels; default 4), beyond half a line's width or a marker's size. !> `kinds`: only hits of these kinds (PICK_*; the others aren't tested). !> `nearest`: only the nearest hit (cheaper: what is deeper than a hit !> found is skipped, e.g. to pick on every mouse move). Frames and !> artists can be left out (`set_pickable(.false.)`). subroutine window_pick ( self , x , y , hits , tolerance , kinds , nearest ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( in ), target :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x , y !! -1 to 1 across the window, y up type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( out ) :: hits (:) !! what is there, nearest first real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: tolerance !! window units (default 4) integer , intent ( in ), optional :: kinds (:) !! PICK_* (default: all) logical , intent ( in ), optional :: nearest !! default false class ( ReferenceFrame ), pointer :: root type ( PickCamera ) :: cam type ( PickHit ) :: h integer :: n , i , j logical :: only_nearest n = 0 only_nearest = . false . if ( present ( nearest )) only_nearest = nearest allocate ( hits ( 8 )) root => null () if ( associated ( self % scene )) root => self % scene % frame () if (. not . associated ( root ) . or . . not . view_camera ( self , x , y , cam )) then hits = hits ( 1 : 0 ) return end if cam % tolerance = 4.0_wp * cam % pixel_ratio if ( present ( tolerance )) cam % tolerance = tolerance * cam % pixel_ratio if ( present ( kinds )) then cam % kinds = 0 do i = 1 , size ( kinds ) if ( kinds ( i ) >= 0 . and . kinds ( i ) < bit_size ( cam % kinds )) cam % kinds = ibset ( cam % kinds , kinds ( i )) end do end if call pick_frame ( root , identity_matrix ()) ! (the root frame's coordinates: the camera's) do i = 2 , n ! nearest first h = hits ( i ) j = i - 1 do while ( j >= 1 ) if ( hits ( j )% distance <= h % distance ) exit hits ( j + 1 ) = hits ( j ) j = j - 1 end do hits ( j + 1 ) = h end do hits = hits ( 1 : n ) contains !> Frame f (at transform m to the root) and its children, under each of !> their parents. recursive subroutine pick_frame ( f , m ) class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: f real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) class ( ReferenceFrame ), pointer :: c integer :: k , best if ( f % pickable ()) call f % pick ( cam , m , hits , n ) if ( only_nearest . and . n > 1 ) then ! (keep the nearest; skip what is deeper) best = minloc ( hits ( 1 : n )% distance , dim = 1 ) hits ( 1 ) = hits ( best ) n = 1 end if if ( only_nearest . and . n == 1 ) cam % max_depth = hits ( 1 )% distance do k = 1 , f % num_children () c => f % child ( k ) call pick_frame ( c , matmul ( m , c % local_matrix ())) end do end subroutine pick_frame end subroutine window_pick !> The window's GUI panels (vkf_gui), made on first use: with `font` (a !> font file name or path, as labels'; default DejaVu Sans) of `size` !> window units (default 15), which apply then. Not valid unless open. function window_gui ( self , font , size ) result ( g ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: font !! file name or path (default DejaVu Sans) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: size !! window units (default 15) type ( Gui ) :: g character ( len = :), allocatable :: path real ( c_double ) :: s if (. not . self % is_open ()) return path = find_font ( default_font ) if ( present ( font )) path = find_font ( font ) s = 1 5.0_c_double if ( present ( size )) s = size g % handle = vkf_viewer_gui ( self % viewer_ , path , len ( path , kind = c_int ), s ) end function window_gui !> Where point `p` (root frame) is in the window, as HUD text positions: !> (x, y) from 0 to 1, left to right and bottom to top (as at the last !> frame). False if it is behind the eye (or before the first frame). !> E.g. to keep HUD text next to a moving object, each frame: a callout. logical function screen_position ( self , p , position ) result ( visible ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p ( 3 ) !! root frame real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: position ( 2 ) !! (x, y), 0 to 1 from the bottom left type ( PickCamera ) :: cam real ( wp ) :: sx , sy , depth visible = . false . position = 0.0_wp if (. not . view_camera ( self , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , cam )) return if (. not . project ( cam , p , sx , sy , depth )) return ! (offsets from the center, in pixels) position = 0.5_wp * ([ sx / cam % half_w , sy / cam % half_h ] + 1.0_wp ) visible = . true . end function screen_position !> The ray from the eye through point (x, y) of the window (-1 to 1 across !> it, y up: as the event handler's positions), in the root frame, as at !> the last frame: its origin (the eye; in an orthographic view, on the !> eye's plane) and its direction (a unit vector). False before the first !> frame. E.g. where the cursor points on a plane: vkf_pick's ray_plane. logical function cursor_ray ( self , x , y , origin , direction ) result ( ok ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x , y !! -1 to 1 across the window, y up real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: origin ( 3 ), direction ( 3 ) !! root frame (direction: a unit vector) type ( PickCamera ) :: cam origin = 0.0_wp direction = [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , - 1.0_wp ] ok = view_camera ( self , x , y , cam ) if ( ok ) call ray ( cam , origin , direction ) end function cursor_ray !> The pick camera of the view shown, with the cursor at (x, y) (-1 to 1, y !> up) and no tolerance. False before the first frame (or closed). logical function view_camera ( self , x , y , cam ) result ( ok ) class ( WindowProxy ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: x , y !! the cursor: -1 to 1 across the window, y up type ( PickCamera ), intent ( out 