he latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> Finding files: data files (e.g. the star catalog data/Stars_HYGv3.txt) by !> name on a search path, as OpenFrames' osgDB::findDataFile. module vkf_files implicit none private public :: find_in_dirs , find_data_file contains !> The path dir/name of the first directory in `dirs` (separated by ';' or !> ':', except a ':' after a drive letter) that has `name`, or ''. function find_in_dirs ( name , dirs ) result ( path ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! file name character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: dirs !! directories, separated by ';' or ':' character ( len = :), allocatable :: path integer :: i , j logical :: exists path = '' i = 1 do while ( i <= len ( dirs )) j = i do while ( j <= len ( dirs )) if ( dirs ( j : j ) == ';' . or . ( dirs ( j : j ) == ':' . and . j > i + 1 )) exit ! ':' not after a drive letter j = j + 1 end do if ( j > i ) then inquire ( file = dirs ( i : j - 1 ) // '/' // name , exist = exists ) if ( exists ) then path = dirs ( i : j - 1 ) // '/' // name return end if end if i = j + 1 end do end function find_in_dirs !> The path of data file `name`: `name` itself if it exists (a path, or a !> file in the current directory), else the first match in the directories !> of the VKFRAMES_DATA_PATH environment variable; '' if not found. function find_data_file ( name ) result ( path ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name character ( len = :), allocatable :: path character ( len = 4096 ) :: env integer :: status logical :: exists path = '' if ( len_trim ( name ) == 0 ) return inquire ( file = trim ( name ), exist = exists ) if ( exists ) then path = trim ( name ) return end if call get_environment_variable ( 'VKFRAMES_DATA_PATH' , env , status = status ) if ( status == 0 ) path = find_in_dirs ( trim ( name ), trim ( env )) end function find_data_file end module vkf_files","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_files.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_handles.f90 – vkframes","text":"Thi