ine_chain.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~vkf_handles.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 vkf_window.f90 sourcefile~vkf_window.f90->sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_handles.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_window.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> Handles (not in OpenFrames): things in the scene the mouse drags, to !> design graphically, e.g. a trajectory's initial position and velocity. !> !> A DragHandle is a frame with a point the mouse can grab (`handle_point`, !> in the frame's coordinates) and move (`move_handle_point`); extensions say !> what the point is and how they are drawn. Windows drive them (WindowProxy, !> see vkf_window): the handle under the cursor is hovered (drawn brighter); a !> left button press on it grabs it (the camera stays where it is: the !> trackball doesn't see the press), the mouse's moves drag it, and the !> release lets it go. The window's event handler is told (`handle_drag`, !> with DRAG_START, DRAG_MOVE and DRAG_END), e.g. to compute a trajectory again !> from the new state while the handle is dragged. Handles can also be moved !> by the program (VectorHandle%set_vector), and dragged by it (`grab`, !> `drag` and `release`, given the cursor's ray). !> !> Where the point goes is where the cursor's ray (WindowProxy%cursor_ray) !> meets the handle's constraint (`set_constraint`), as it was when the !> handle was grabbed, plus the point's offset from the cursor then (so the !> point doesn't jump to the cursor): !> * HANDLE_FREE (the default): the plane through the point facing the camera; !> * HANDLE_PLANE: the plane through the point with the normal given; !> * HANDLE_LINE: the line through the point along the direction given; !> * HANDLE_RADIAL: the line from the frame's origin through the point (e.g. !>   a vector's length only); !> * HANDLE_SPHERE: the sphere about the frame's origin through the point !>   (e.g. a vector's direction only), on the side (near or far, from the !>   camera) where it was grabbed; where the ray misses it, its edge nearest !>   the ray. !> Normals and directions are in the frame's coordinates. A ray parallel to a !> plane or a line doesn't move the point. Positions go through the frames' !> first parents to the root (ReferenceFrame%world_matrix). !> !> Handles on the same spot of the screen (e.g. a trajectory's end marker on !> its state's arrow): the window hovers the one nearest the cursor on the !> screen; within a few pixels of each other, the one of the highest !> priority (`set_priority`; markers, TimeHandle, 1 by default, before !> arrows, 0), then the nearest to the eye. !> !> A VectorHandle is an arrow from its frame's origin to its tip, the tip !> being the handle: a vector (`set_vector`, in the frame's coordinates) !> times a display scale (`set_display_scale`: e.g. 1000 s to draw a velocity !> in km/s as km). Dragging the tip changes the vector. The arrow is in the !> frame's color, lit as frames' axes (by how it faces the viewer); its head !> is `set_head_size` long (scene units; default 0.2 of the arrow, at most !> half of it). It is built once, as a unit shaft and head scaled and turned !> by two transforms: a new vector only sets them (cheap enough for every !> frame of a drag). !> !> A TimeHandle is a marker at a time along a path (a TimePath: a position !> for any time, in the coordinates of the handle's parent frame, e.g. a !> propagator's), dragged along the path to change the time: e.g. a !> trajectory's end, dragged to make it longer or shorter in time. The path !> needn't be drawn where the handle goes (beyond a trajectory's last point, !> the program propagates further). The frame is placed at the path's !> position for the time (`set_time`), so its name label (e.g. the time, !> `set_name`) goes with it; the marker is the size of MarkerArtist's !> markers (window units, not shrinking with distance). A drag takes the time !> within `set_time_range` whose point is nearest the cursor's ray (as seen !> from the eye): among the path's points sampled at the grab, then refined !> between them; where the path passes near itself (orbits), the match !> nearest in time to the handle's time is taken, so it doesn't jump to !> another revolution. A TrajectoryPath follows a Trajectory's points !> (interpolated linearly), within its times. module vkf_handles use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_ptr , c_null_ptr , c_associated , c_int , c_int32_t , c_float , c_double use vkf_math , only : wp , cross , rigid_inverse use vkf_frames , only : ReferenceFrame , PickHit , add_pick_hit , PICK_HANDLE use vkf_pick , only : PickCamera , point_pick , segment_pick , wants , ray_plane , ray_sphere , ray_line use vkf_geometry , only : arrow_size , arrow use vkf_trajectory , only : Trajectory use vkf_artists , only : MARKER_DISK , MARKER_IMAGE use vkf_layer , only : check_status , vkf_mesh_create , mesh_arrays , mesh_set_material , vkf_transform_create , & vkf_transform_set_matrix , vkf_switch_create , vkf_switch_set , vkf_node_add_child , & vkf_marker_create , marker_set_style , line_set_points implicit none private !> A handle's constraint (`set_constraint`; see the module documentation). integer , parameter , public :: HANDLE_FREE = 0 !! the plane facing the camera integer , parameter , public :: HANDLE_PLANE = 1 !! a plane (its normal given) integer , parameter , public :: HANDLE_LINE = 2 !! a line (its direction given) integer , parameter , public :: HANDLE_RADIAL = 3 !! the line from the frame's origin through the point integer , parameter , public :: HANDLE_SPHERE = 4 !! the sphere about the frame's origin through the point !> A handle the mouse drags (see the module documentation): extensions !> give its point and draw it. type , abstract , extends ( ReferenceFrame ), public :: DragHandle private logical :: draggable_ = . true . !! the mouse may grab it logical :: hovered_ = . false . !! under the cursor logical :: dragged_ = . false . !! grabbed, until released integer :: priority_ = 0 !! over other handles on the same spot (higher first) integer :: constraint_ = HANDLE_FREE !! HANDLE_* real ( wp ) :: axis_ ( 3 ) = [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! the plane's normal or the line's direction (frame coordinates) ! the drag, from the grab (frame coordinates) real ( wp ) :: ref_point ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! the point when grabbed real ( wp ) :: ref_axis ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! the plane's normal or the line's direction then real ( wp ) :: radius = 0.0_wp !! (HANDLE_SPHERE) the sphere's radius logical :: far_side = . false . !! (HANDLE_SPHERE) grabbed on the far side real ( wp ) :: offset ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! the point's offset from the cursor's contains procedure :: set_draggable , draggable procedure :: set_constraint , constraint , constraint_axis procedure :: set_hovered , hovered , dragged procedure :: set_priority , priority procedure :: grab , drag , release procedure ( handle_point_interface ), deferred :: handle_point procedure ( move_handle_point_interface ), deferred :: move_handle_point procedure ( show_state_interface ), deferred :: show_state end type DragHandle abstract interface !> The point the mouse grabs (frame coordinates). pure function handle_point_interface ( self ) result ( p ) import :: DragHandle , wp implicit none class ( DragHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) end function handle_point_interface !> Move the point to `p` (frame coordinates), and the drawing with it. subroutine move_handle_point_interface ( self , p ) import :: DragHandle , wp implicit none class ( DragHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p ( 3 ) !! the new point (frame coordinates) end subroutine move_handle_point_interface !> Draw the handle as hovered, dragged or neither (`hovered`, `dragged`). subroutine show_state_interface ( self ) import :: DragHandle implicit none class ( DragHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self end subroutine show_state_interface end interface !> An arrow whose tip the mouse drags (see the module documentation). type , extends ( DragHandle ), public :: VectorHandle private real ( wp ) :: vector_ ( 3 ) = [ 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp ] !! the vector (frame coordinates) real ( wp ) :: scale_ = 1.0_wp !! drawn as scale * vector (scene units) real ( wp ) :: head_size_ = 0.0_wp !! the head's length (scene units; 0: 0.2 of the arrow) type ( c_ptr ) :: switch = c_null_ptr !! shows the arrow (not when the vector is 0) type ( c_ptr ) :: shaft = c_null_ptr , head = c_null_ptr !! the transforms of the unit shaft and head type ( c_ptr ) :: shaft_mesh = c_null_ptr , head_mesh = c_null_ptr !! the unit shaft and head (colored by their materials) contains procedure :: set_vector , vector , tip procedure :: set_display_scale , display_scale procedure :: set_head_size , head_size procedure :: set_color => vector_set_color procedure :: handle_point => vector_handle_point procedure :: move_handle_point => vector_move_handle_point procedure :: show_state => vector_show_state procedure :: frame_info => vector_frame_info procedure :: bound => vector_bound procedure :: pick => vector_pick procedure :: build_contents => vector_build_contents end type VectorHandle !> The VectorHandle constructor: `VectorHandle(...)` makes one (see `new_vector_handle` for its !> arguments). interface VectorHandle module procedure new_vector_handle end interface VectorHandle !> A path for a TimeHandle (see the module documentation): a position for !> any time. type , abstract , public :: TimePath contains procedure ( path_position_interface ), deferred :: position end type TimePath abstract interface !> The position at time `t` (the handle's parent's coordinates). function path_position_interface ( self , t ) result ( p ) import :: TimePath , wp implicit none class ( TimePath ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the time real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) end function path_position_interface end interface !> A TimePath along a Trajectory's points, interpolated linearly (before !> its first time: its first point; after its last: its last). type , extends ( TimePath ), public :: TrajectoryPath type ( Trajectory ), pointer :: trajectory => null () !! the trajectory followed (not owned) contains procedure :: position => trajectory_path_position end type TrajectoryPath !> The TrajectoryPath constructor: `TrajectoryPath(...)` makes one (see `new_trajectory_path` for its !> arguments). interface TrajectoryPath module procedure new_trajectory_path end interface TrajectoryPath !> A marker dragged along a path to change its time (see the module !> documentation). type , extends ( DragHandle ), public :: TimeHandle private class ( TimePath ), pointer :: path_ => null () !! the path (not owned) real ( wp ) :: time_ = 0.0_wp !! the time (its point: the frame's position) real ( wp ) :: t_min = 0.0_wp , t_max = 1.0_wp !! the times a drag may reach real ( wp ) :: size_ = 1 4.0_wp !! the marker's size (window units) integer :: shape_ = MARKER_DISK !! a MARKER_* shape type ( c_ptr ) :: marker = c_null_ptr !! the marker node (at the frame's origin) ! the drag: the path sampled at the grab (times; positions, the parent's coordinates) real ( wp ), allocatable :: sample_t (:), sample_p (:,:) contains procedure :: set_path , set_time , time , set_time_range , time_range procedure :: set_marker_size , marker_size , set_marker_shape , marker_shape procedure :: set_color => time_set_color procedure :: grab => time_grab procedure :: drag => time_drag procedure :: handle_point => time_handle_point procedure :: move_handle_point => time_move_handle_point procedure :: show_state => time_show_state procedure :: frame_info => time_frame_info procedure :: bound => time_bound procedure :: pick => time_pick procedure :: build_contents => time_build_contents end type TimeHandle !> The TimeHandle constructor: `TimeHandle(...)` makes one (see `new_time_handle` for its !> arguments). interface TimeHandle module procedure new_time_handle end interface TimeHandle integer , parameter :: path_samples = 600 !! a TimeHandle's path sampled at a grab public :: handles_shown integer , save :: n_shown = 0 !! handles shown in a window (so far) contains ! ================================================================== ! DragHandle !> Whether the mouse may grab the handle (default true). subroutine set_draggable ( self , draggable ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: draggable !! true: the mouse may grab it self % draggable_ = draggable if (. not . draggable . and . self % hovered_ ) call self % set_hovered (. false .) end subroutine set_draggable !> Whether the mouse may grab the handle. pure logical function draggable ( self ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self draggable = self % draggable_ end function draggable !> Where the handle can be dragged (HANDLE_*; see the module documentation), !> with `axis`: the plane's normal (HANDLE_PLANE) or the line's direction !> (HANDLE_LINE), in the frame's coordinates. Taken when the handle is !> next grabbed. subroutine set_constraint ( self , constraint , axis ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: constraint !! HANDLE_* real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: axis ( 3 ) !! (frame coordinates; any length but 0) if ( constraint < HANDLE_FREE . or . constraint > HANDLE_SPHERE ) return self % constraint_ = constraint if ( present ( axis )) then if ( norm2 ( axis ) > 0.0_wp ) self % axis_ = axis / norm2 ( axis ) end if end subroutine set_constraint !> The handle's constraint (HANDLE_*). pure integer function constraint ( self ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self constraint = self % constraint_ end function constraint !> The constraint's normal or direction (unit vector, frame coordinates). pure function constraint_axis ( self ) result ( axis ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: axis ( 3 ) axis = self % axis_ end function constraint_axis !> The handle's priority over others on the same spot of the screen (higher !> first; default 0, a TimeHandle's 1; see the module documentation). subroutine set_priority ( self , priority ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: priority !! higher: hovered first self % priority_ = priority end subroutine set_priority !> The handle's priority over others on the same spot. pure integer function priority ( self ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self priority = self % priority_ end function priority !> The handle is under the cursor (set by the window), or not. subroutine set_hovered ( self , hovered ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: hovered !! true: under the cursor if ( hovered . eqv . self % hovered_ ) return self % hovered_ = hovered call self % show_state () end subroutine set_hovered !> The handle is under the cursor. pure logical function hovered ( self ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self hovered = self % hovered_ end function hovered !> The handle is grabbed (until released). pure logical function dragged ( self ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self dragged = self % dragged_ end function dragged !> Grab the handle with the cursor's ray (origin, unit dir; root frame): !> its constraint is taken as it is now, and the point's offset from where !> the ray meets it. False if it isn't draggable. logical function grab ( self , origin , dir ) result ( ok ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the cursor's ray (root frame) real ( wp ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ), p ( 3 ), h ( 3 ), near , far , c ( 3 ) ok = . false . if (. not . self % draggable_ ) return m = self % world_matrix () p = self % handle_point () self % ref_point = p self % ref_axis = self % axis_ select case ( self % constraint_ ) case ( HANDLE_FREE ) self % ref_axis = matmul ( transpose ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 )), - dir ) ! (facing the camera, now) case ( HANDLE_RADIAL ) if ( norm2 ( p ) > 0.0_wp ) self % ref_axis = p / norm2 ( p ) case ( HANDLE_SPHERE ) self % radius = norm2 ( p ) self % far_side = . false . c = m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) if ( ray_sphere ( origin , dir , c , self % radius , near , far )) & ! (the side nearer the point) self % far_side = norm2 ( origin + far * dir - ( matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), p ) + c )) < & norm2 ( origin + near * dir - ( matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), p ) + c )) end select self % offset = 0.0_wp if ( constrained ( self , origin , dir , m , h )) self % offset = p - h self % dragged_ = . true . call self % show_state () ok = . true . end function grab !> Drag the grabbed handle to the cursor's ray (origin, unit dir; root !> frame), held to its constraint. False (and not moved) if it isn't !> grabbed or the ray doesn't meet the constraint. logical function drag ( self , origin , dir ) result ( moved ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the cursor's ray (root frame) real ( wp ) :: h ( 3 ), p ( 3 ) moved = . false . if (. not . self % dragged_ ) return if (. not . constrained ( self , origin , dir , self % world_matrix (), h )) return p = h + self % offset if ( self % constraint_ == HANDLE_SPHERE . and . norm2 ( p ) > 0.0_wp ) p = self % radius * p / norm2 ( p ) call self % move_handle_point ( p ) moved = . true . end function drag !> Let the handle go. subroutine release ( self ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self if (. not . self % dragged_ ) return self % dragged_ = . false . call self % show_state () end subroutine release !> Where the ray (origin, unit dir; root frame) meets the constraint taken !> at the grab, the frame at transform `m` to the root: `h`, in the frame's !> coordinates. False if it doesn't. logical function constrained ( self , origin , dir , m , h ) result ( ok ) class ( DragHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ) !! the cursor's ray: its origin (root frame) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: dir ( 3 ) !! its direction (a unit vector) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: h ( 3 ) !! where it meets the constraint (frame coordinates) real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ), a ( 3 ), c ( 3 ), w ( 3 ), q ( 3 ), t , near , far c = m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) p = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), self % ref_point ) + c a = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), self % ref_axis ) h = self % ref_point select case ( self % constraint_ ) case ( HANDLE_FREE , HANDLE_PLANE ) ok = ray_plane ( origin , dir , p , a , t , w ) case ( HANDLE_LINE , HANDLE_RADIAL ) ok = ray_line ( origin , dir , p , a , t , w ) case ( HANDLE_SPHERE ) ok = self % radius > 0.0_wp if (. not . ok ) return if ( ray_sphere ( origin , dir , c , self % radius , near , far )) then t = near if ( self % far_side . or . near < 0.0_wp ) t = far w = origin + t * dir else ! (missed: the edge nearest the ray) q = origin + max ( 0.0_wp , dot_product ( c - origin , dir )) * dir ok = norm2 ( q - c ) > 0.0_wp if (. not . ok ) return w = c + self % radius * ( q - c ) / norm2 ( q - c ) end if case default ok = . false . end select if ( ok ) h = matmul ( transpose ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 )), w - c ) end function constrained ! ================================================================== ! VectorHandle !> A vector handle (see the module documentation): `vector` in its frame's !> coordinates (default [1, 0, 0]), drawn `scale` times as long (default 1), !> in `color` ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]). Its axes and labels are hidden. function new_vector_handle ( name , vector , color , scale ) result ( h ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! the frame's name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: vector ( 3 ) !! frame coordinates real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: scale !! display scale (scene units per vector unit; > 0) type ( VectorHandle ) :: h h % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) call h % show_decorations (. false .) if ( present ( vector )) h % vector_ = vector if ( present ( scale )) then if ( scale > 0.0_wp ) h % scale_ = scale end if end function new_vector_handle !> The vector (frame coordinates); can change at any time. subroutine set_vector ( self , vector ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: vector ( 3 ) !! frame coordinates self % vector_ = vector call update_arrow ( self ) end subroutine set_vector !> The vector (frame coordinates). pure function vector ( self ) result ( v ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ) v = self % vector_ end function vector !> The arrow's tip: the display scale times the vector (frame coordinates). pure function tip ( self ) result ( p ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) p = self % scale_ * self % vector_ end function tip !> Scene units per unit of the vector (> 0; default 1): the arrow is !> `scale` * vector. subroutine set_display_scale ( self , scale ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: scale !! scene units per vector unit (> 0; else ignored) if ( scale <= 0.0_wp ) return self % scale_ = scale call update_arrow ( self ) end subroutine set_display_scale !> The display scale. pure real ( wp ) function display_scale ( self ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self display_scale = self % scale_ end function display_scale !> The head's length (scene units; at most half the arrow); 0 (the !> default): 0.2 of the arrow's length. subroutine set_head_size ( self , size ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: size !! the head's length (scene units; 0: 0.2 of the arrow) self % head_size_ = max ( 0.0_wp , size ) call update_arrow ( self ) end subroutine set_head_size !> The head's length set (0: 0.2 of the arrow's). pure real ( wp ) function head_size ( self ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self head_size = self % head_size_ end function head_size !> The arrow's color; [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]. subroutine vector_set_color ( self , color ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call self % ReferenceFrame % set_color ( color ) call self % show_state () end subroutine vector_set_color !> The point the mouse grabs: the tip. pure function vector_handle_point ( self ) result ( p ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) p = self % tip () end function vector_handle_point !> The tip dragged to `p`: the vector p / the display scale. subroutine vector_move_handle_point ( self , p ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p ( 3 ) !! the tip's new place (frame coordinates) call self % set_vector ( p / self % scale_ ) end subroutine vector_move_handle_point !> The arrow's color, brighter when hovered and more when dragged. subroutine vector_show_state ( self ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( c_float ) :: color ( 4 ), glow ( 4 ) if (. not . c_associated ( self % shaft_mesh )) return color = real ( self % color (), c_float ) glow = 0.0_c_float if ( self % dragged ()) then glow ( 1 : 3 ) = 0.45_c_float else if ( self % hovered ()) then glow ( 1 : 3 ) = 0.25_c_float end if call check_status ( mesh_set_material ( self % shaft_mesh , [ 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], color , & [ 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], glow , 0.0_c_float )) call check_status ( mesh_set_material ( self % head_mesh , [ 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], color , & [ 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], glow , 0.0_c_float )) end subroutine vector_show_state !> What kind of frame this is: 'VectorHandle'. function vector_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'VectorHandle' end function vector_frame_info !> The arrow's bounding sphere (frame coordinates). subroutine vector_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ) !! the bound's center (frame coordinates) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: radius !! its radius (scene units) center = 0.5_wp * self % tip () radius = 0.5_wp * norm2 ( self % tip ()) end subroutine vector_bound !> Picked at its tip and along its head (within the tolerance, plus a few !> pixels), as PICK_HANDLE; else the frame's origin. subroutine vector_pick ( self , cam , to_root , hits , n ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( in ), target :: self type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam !! the camera and cursor of the pick real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: to_root ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits so far, in hits(1:n); added to integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits type ( PickHit ) :: h real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ), base ( 3 ), len , head_len , radius , pixels , depth , s , head_pixels , head_depth logical :: at_tip , on_head call self % ReferenceFrame % pick ( cam , to_root , hits , n ) if (. not . ( self % draggable () . and . self % contents_shown () . and . wants ( cam , PICK_HANDLE ))) return call arrow_sizes ( self , len , head_len , radius ) if ( len <= 0.0_wp ) return p = matmul ( to_root ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), self % tip ()) + to_root ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) base = matmul ( to_root ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), self % tip () * ( 1.0_wp - head_len / len )) + to_root ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) at_tip = point_pick ( cam , p , pixels , depth , extra = 6.0_wp * cam % pixel_ratio ) on_head = segment_pick ( cam , base , p , head_pixels , s , head_depth , extra = 4.0_wp * cam % pixel_ratio ) if (. not . ( at_tip . or . on_head )) return if ( on_head . and . (. not . at_tip . or . head_pixels < pixels )) then pixels = head_pixels depth = head_depth end if h % kind = PICK_HANDLE h % frame => self h % position = p h % local = self % tip () h % distance = depth h % pixels = pixels call add_pick_hit ( hits , n , h ) end subroutine vector_pick !> The arrow: a unit shaft and head under their transforms, in a switch. subroutine vector_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the frame's contents group self % shaft_mesh = unit_part ( 1.0_c_double , 0.0_c_double , 1.0_c_double , 1.0_c_double ) ! (a closed cylinder) self % head_mesh = unit_part ( 0.0_c_double , 1.0_c_double , 0.0_c_double , 1.0_c_double ) ! (a cone on a disk) if (. not . ( c_associated ( self % shaft_mesh ) . and . c_associated ( self % head_mesh ))) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: VectorHandle ' // self % name () // ': could not build its arrow' return end if self % switch = vkf_switch_create () self % shaft = vkf_transform_create () self % head = vkf_transform_create () call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % shaft , self % shaft_mesh )) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % head , self % head_mesh )) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % switch , self % shaft )) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % switch , self % head )) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( group , self % switch )) call self % show_state () call update_arrow ( self ) if ( c_associated ( viewer )) n_shown = n_shown + 1 end subroutine vector_build_contents !> A unit part of an arrow along z from the origin (vkf_geometry's arrow: !> body and head lengths and radii), white (colored by its material), lit !> as frames' axes. Null on failure. function unit_part ( body_length , head_length , body_radius , head_radius ) result ( mesh ) real ( c_double ), intent ( in ) :: body_length !! the shaft's length (0: none) real ( c_double ), intent ( in ) :: head_length !! the head's length (0: a flat top) real ( c_double ), intent ( in ) :: body_radius !! the shaft's radius real ( c_double ), intent ( in ) :: head_radius !! the head's radius at its base type ( c_ptr ) :: mesh integer , parameter :: segments = 24 real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: xyz , normals , uv integer ( c_int32_t ), dimension (:), pointer :: indices integer :: n_vertices , n_indices call arrow_size ( segments , n_vertices , n_indices ) mesh = vkf_mesh_create ( int ( n_vertices , c_int ), int ( n_indices , c_int ), & [ 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], c_null_ptr , c_null_ptr , 2_c_int ) if (. not . c_associated ( mesh )) return call mesh_arrays ( mesh , n_vertices , n_indices , xyz , normals , uv , indices ) call arrow ([ 0.0_c_double , 0.0_c_double , 0.0_c_double ], [ 0.0_c_double , 0.0_c_double , 1.0_c_double ], & body_length , head_length , body_radius , head_radius , segments , xyz , normals , uv , indices ) end function unit_part !> The arrow's length, its head's length and radius (scene units). pure subroutine arrow_sizes ( self , len , head_len , head_radius ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: len !! the arrow's length (the tip's distance) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: head_len !! its head's length real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: head_radius !! its head's radius len = norm2 ( self % tip ()) head_len = 0.2_wp * len if ( self % head_size_ > 0.0_wp ) head_len = min ( self % head_size_ , 0.5_wp * len ) head_radius = 0.35_wp * head_len end subroutine arrow_sizes !> The shaft and head placed for the vector (hidden if it is 0). subroutine update_arrow ( self ) class ( VectorHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ) :: len , head_len , head_radius , u ( 3 ), a ( 3 ), b ( 3 ), m ( 4 , 4 ) if (. not . c_associated ( self % switch )) return call arrow_sizes ( self , len , head_len , head_radius ) call check_status ( vkf_switch_set ( self % switch , merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , len > 0.0_wp ))) if ( len <= 0.0_wp ) return u = self % tip () / len a = cross ( u , [ 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp ]) if ( norm2 ( a ) < 1.0e-6_wp ) a = cross ( u , [ 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp ]) a = a / norm2 ( a ) b = cross ( u , a ) ! (a, b, u right-handed) m = 0.0_wp m ( 4 , 4 ) = 1.0_wp m ( 1 : 3 , 1 ) = 0.4_wp * head_radius * a ! the shaft: 0.4 of the head's radius m ( 1 : 3 , 2 ) = 0.4_wp * head_radius * b m ( 1 : 3 , 3 ) = ( len - head_len ) * u call check_status ( vkf_transform_set_matrix ( self % shaft , m )) m ( 1 : 3 , 1 ) = head_radius * a m ( 1 : 3 , 2 ) = head_radius * b m ( 1 : 3 , 3 ) = head_len * u m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) = ( len - head_len ) * u call check_status ( vkf_transform_set_matrix ( self % head , m )) end subroutine update_arrow ! ================================================================== ! TrajectoryPath !> A path along `traj` (which must stay alive while used). function new_trajectory_path ( traj ) result ( path ) type ( Trajectory ), intent ( in ), target :: traj !! the trajectory followed type ( TrajectoryPath ) :: path path % trajectory => traj end function new_trajectory_path !> The trajectory's position at time `t` (Trajectory%point_at: linear !> between its points, its first or last point outside its times; 0 if !> it has none). function trajectory_path_position ( self , t ) result ( p ) class ( TrajectoryPath ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the time real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) p = 0.0_wp if ( associated ( self % trajectory )) p = self % trajectory % point_at ( t ) end function trajectory_path_position ! ================================================================== ! TimeHandle !> A time handle (see the module documentation) on `path` (which must stay !> alive while used), at time `time` (default 0) within `t_min` to `t_max` !> (default: the time), in `color` ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]). Its axes !> and labels are hidden (its name label can be shown: e.g. the time). function new_time_handle ( name , path , time , t_min , t_max , color ) result ( h ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! the frame's name class ( TimePath ), intent ( in ), target :: path !! the path it moves along real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: time !! its time real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: t_min , t_max !! the times a drag may reach real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) type ( TimeHandle ) :: h h % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) call h % show_decorations (. false .) h % priority_ = 1 ! (a marker over an arrow on the same spot) h % path_ => path if ( present ( time )) h % time_ = time h % t_min = h % time_ h % t_max = h % time_ if ( present ( t_min )) h % t_min = t_min if ( present ( t_max )) h % t_max = t_max call h % set_time ( h % time_ ) end function new_time_handle !> The path the handle moves along (which must stay alive while used); its !> time kept (the frame placed on the new path). subroutine set_path ( self , path ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( TimePath ), intent ( in ), target :: path !! the path self % path_ => path call self % set_time ( self % time_ ) end subroutine set_path !> The handle's time (kept within its time range): the frame placed at the !> path's point for it. subroutine set_time ( self , time ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: time !! the time self % time_ = max ( self % t_min , min ( self % t_max , time )) if ( associated ( self % path_ )) call self % set_position ( self % path_ % position ( self % time_ )) end subroutine set_time !> The handle's time. pure real ( wp ) function time ( self ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self time = self % time_ end function time !> The times a drag may reach (t_min <= t_max; else swapped); the handle's !> time brought within them. Taken at the next grab. subroutine set_time_range ( self , t_min , t_max ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t_min , t_max !! the earliest and latest times self % t_min = min ( t_min , t_max ) self % t_max = max ( t_min , t_max ) call self % set_time ( self % time_ ) end subroutine set_time_range !> The times a drag may reach. pure subroutine time_range ( self , t_min , t_max ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: t_min , t_max !! the earliest and latest times t_min = self % t_min t_max = self % t_max end subroutine time_range !> The marker's size (window units, > 0; default 14). subroutine set_marker_size ( self , size ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: size !! window units if ( size <= 0.0_wp ) return self % size_ = size call self % show_state () end subroutine set_marker_size !> The marker's size (window units). pure real ( wp ) function marker_size ( self ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self marker_size = self % size_ end function marker_size !> The marker's shape (a MARKER_* shape of vkf_artists but MARKER_IMAGE; !> default MARKER_DISK). subroutine set_marker_shape ( self , shape ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: shape !! a MARKER_* shape self % shape_ = max ( MARKER_DISK , min ( MARKER_IMAGE - 1 , shape )) call self % show_state () end subroutine set_marker_shape !> The marker's shape (MARKER_*). pure integer function marker_shape ( self ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self marker_shape = self % shape_ end function marker_shape !> The marker's color; [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]. subroutine time_set_color ( self , color ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call self % ReferenceFrame % set_color ( color ) call self % show_state () end subroutine time_set_color !> Grab the handle with the cursor's ray (origin, unit dir; root frame): !> the path sampled over the time range. False if it isn't draggable or !> has no path. logical function time_grab ( self , origin , dir ) result ( ok ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the cursor's ray (root frame) integer :: k ok = . false . if (. not . ( self % draggable () . and . associated ( self % path_ ))) return if ( allocated ( self % sample_t )) deallocate ( self % sample_t , self % sample_p ) allocate ( self % sample_t ( path_samples ), self % sample_p ( 3 , path_samples )) do k = 1 , path_samples self % sample_t ( k ) = self % t_min + ( self % t_max - self % t_min ) * ( k - 1 ) / ( path_samples - 1 ) self % sample_p (:, k ) = self % path_ % position ( self % sample_t ( k )) end do self % dragged_ = . true . call self % show_state () ok = . true . end function time_grab !> Drag the grabbed handle to the cursor's ray (origin, unit dir; root !> frame): its time where the path is nearest the ray (see the module !> documentation). False (not moved) if it isn't grabbed or the path is !> all behind the eye. logical function time_drag ( self , origin , dir ) result ( moved ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: origin ( 3 ), dir ( 3 ) !! the cursor's ray (root frame) real ( wp ) :: parent ( 4 , 4 ), miss ( path_samples ), best , t_best real ( wp ) :: t_min ( path_samples ), m_min ( path_samples ) !! the local minima refined: their times and misses integer :: k , n_min logical :: found moved = . false . if (. not . ( self % dragged_ . and . allocated ( self % sample_t ) . and . associated ( self % path_ ))) return parent = matmul ( self % world_matrix (), rigid_inverse ( self % local_matrix ())) ! (the path's coordinates to the root) do k = 1 , path_samples miss ( k ) = ray_miss ( self % sample_p (:, k )) end do if ( minval ( miss ) >= huge ( 1.0_wp )) return ! each local minimum of the samples refined; of those nearly as near as ! the nearest (a path passing the same place again: orbits), the one ! nearest in time to the handle's n_min = 0 do k = 1 , path_samples if (. not . is_minimum ( k )) cycle n_min = n_min + 1 call refine ( k , t_min ( n_min ), m_min ( n_min )) end do if ( n_min == 0 ) return best = minval ( m_min ( 1 : n_min )) found = . false . t_best = self % time_ do k = 1 , n_min if ( m_min ( k ) > 1.5_wp * best + 1.0e-4_wp ) cycle if ( found . and . abs ( t_min ( k ) - self % time_ ) >= abs ( t_best - self % time_ )) cycle t_best = t_min ( k ) found = . true . end do if (. not . found ) return call self % set_time ( t_best ) moved = . true . contains !> How far point p (the path's coordinates) is from the ray, as seen !> from its origin (the tangent of the angle; huge() behind it). real ( wp ) function ray_miss ( p ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p ( 3 ) !! the point (the path's coordinates) real ( wp ) :: v ( 3 ), along v = matmul ( parent ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), p ) + parent ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) - origin along = dot_product ( v , dir ) ray_miss = huge ( 1.0_wp ) if ( along > 0.0_wp ) ray_miss = norm2 ( v - along * dir ) / along end function ray_miss !> Sample k is a local minimum of the samples' misses (in front of the eye). logical function is_minimum ( j ) integer , intent ( in ) :: j !! the sample is_minimum = miss ( j ) < huge ( 1.0_wp ) if ( j > 1 ) is_minimum = is_minimum . and . miss ( j - 1 ) >= miss ( j ) if ( j < path_samples ) is_minimum = is_minimum . and . miss ( j + 1 ) > miss ( j ) end function is_minimum !> The time of the least miss between sample j's neighbours (golden-section !> search), and that miss. subroutine refine ( j , t , m ) integer , intent ( in ) :: j !! the sample real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: t !! the time found real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: m !! its miss real ( wp ), parameter :: golden = 0.5_wp * ( sqrt ( 5.0_wp ) - 1.0_wp ) real ( wp ) :: a , b , c , d , fc , fd integer :: it a = self % sample_t ( max ( 1 , j - 1 )) b = self % sample_t ( min ( path_samples , j + 1 )) c = b - golden * ( b - a ) d = a + golden * ( b - a ) fc = ray_miss ( self % path_ % position ( c )) fd = ray_miss ( self % path_ % position ( d )) do it = 1 , 40 if ( fc < fd ) then b = d d = c fd = fc c = b - golden * ( b - a ) fc = ray_miss ( self % path_ % position ( c )) else a = c c = d fc = fd d = a + golden * ( b - a ) fd = ray_miss ( self % path_ % position ( d )) end if end do t = 0.5_wp * ( a + b ) m = min ( fc , fd ) end subroutine refine end function time_drag !> The point the mouse grabs: the marker, at the frame's origin. pure function time_handle_point ( self ) result ( p ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) p = 0.0_wp end function time_handle_point !> The handle moved to the sampled point of the path nearest `p` (frame !> coordinates; after a grab: the path's points are sampled then). subroutine time_move_handle_point ( self , p ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: p ( 3 ) !! the point (frame coordinates) real ( wp ) :: q ( 3 ) integer :: k if (. not . allocated ( self % sample_t )) return q = p + self % position () ! (the parent's coordinates) k = minloc ( norm2 ( self % sample_p - spread ( q , 2 , size ( self % sample_t )), dim = 1 ), dim = 1 ) call self % set_time ( self % sample_t ( k )) end subroutine time_move_handle_point !> The marker's color and size: brighter and larger when hovered, more !> when dragged. subroutine time_show_state ( self ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ) :: rgba ( 4 ), size , light if (. not . c_associated ( self % marker )) return rgba = self % color () size = self % size_ light = 0.0_wp if ( self % dragged ()) then light = 0.6_wp size = 1.4_wp * size else if ( self % hovered ()) then light = 0.35_wp size = 1.2_wp * size end if rgba ( 1 : 3 ) = rgba ( 1 : 3 ) + light * ( 1.0_wp - rgba ( 1 : 3 )) call check_status ( marker_set_style ( self % marker , real ( rgba , c_float ), real ( size , c_float ), self % shape_ , & 0.0_c_float )) end subroutine time_show_state !> What kind of frame this is: 'TimeHandle'. function time_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'TimeHandle' end function time_frame_info !> The marker's bounding sphere: the frame's origin. subroutine time_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ) !! the bound's center (frame coordinates) real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: radius !! its radius (scene units: 0, the marker sized on the screen) center = 0.0_wp radius = 0.0_wp end subroutine time_bound !> Picked at its marker (within the tolerance plus half its size), as !> PICK_HANDLE; else the frame's origin. subroutine time_pick ( self , cam , to_root , hits , n ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( in ), target :: self type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam !! the camera and cursor of the pick real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: to_root ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits so far, in hits(1:n); added to integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits type ( PickHit ) :: h real ( wp ) :: pixels , depth call self % ReferenceFrame % pick ( cam , to_root , hits , n ) if (. not . ( self % draggable () . and . self % contents_shown () . and . wants ( cam , PICK_HANDLE ))) return if (. not . point_pick ( cam , to_root ( 1 : 3 , 4 ), pixels , depth , extra = 0.5_wp * self % size_ * cam % pixel_ratio )) return h % kind = PICK_HANDLE h % frame => self h % position = to_root ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) h % local = 0.0_wp h % time = self % time_ h % distance = depth h % pixels = pixels call add_pick_hit ( hits , n , h ) end subroutine time_pick !> The marker: one point at the frame's origin. subroutine time_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( TimeHandle ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the frame's contents group self % marker = vkf_marker_create ( 1_c_int , c_null_ptr , 0_c_int ) if (. not . c_associated ( self % marker )) then write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: TimeHandle ' // self % name () // ': could not build its marker' return end if call check_status ( line_set_points ( self % marker , reshape ([ 0.0_c_double , 0.0_c_double , 0.0_c_double ], [ 3 , 1 ]))) call self % show_state () call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( group , self % marker )) if ( c_associated ( viewer )) n_shown = n_shown + 1 end subroutine time_build_contents !> Whether any handle has been shown in a window (so windows look for !> handles under the cursor). logical function handles_shown () handles_shown = n_shown > 0 end function handles_shown end module vkf_handles","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_handles.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_model.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_model.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_model.f90 vkf_model.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_model.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~vkf_model.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_model.f90 vkf_model.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_model.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> 3D models: a model file (3ds, obj, glTF, ... through vsgXchange) in a !> frame, as OpenFrames' Model. !> !> The model is placed in its frame by its own transform: !> translate(model_position) * rotate(model_attitude) * scale(model_scale) * !> translate(-model_pivot), so e.g. the pivot can be the model's center !> (`model_bound`) and the scale can size it. module vkf_model use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_ptr , c_null_ptr , c_associated , c_int use vkf_math , only : wp , quat_identity , quat_normalize , frame_matrix , identity_matrix use vkf_frames , only : ReferenceFrame , PickHit , pick_ellipsoid use vkf_pick , only : PickCamera use vkf_layer , only : vkf_model_read , vkf_node_bound , vkf_transform_create , vkf_transform_set_matrix , & vkf_node_add_child implicit none private !> A model (see the module documentation). type , extends ( ReferenceFrame ), public :: Model private character ( len = :), allocatable :: file !! the model file (unallocated: none) type ( c_ptr ) :: model_ = c_null_ptr !! the loaded model's node real ( wp ) :: model_position_ ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! where the pivot is in the frame real ( wp ) :: model_attitude_ ( 4 ) = quat_identity !! attitude in the frame (quaternion [x, y, z, w]) real ( wp ) :: scale_ ( 3 ) = 1.0_wp !! scale along the model's x, y, z real ( wp ) :: pivot_ ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! the model's point at model_position_ (model coordinates) real ( wp ) :: bound_center ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! the model's bounding sphere: center (model coordinates) real ( wp ) :: bound_radius = 0.0_wp !! the model's bounding sphere: radius (0: unknown) type ( c_ptr ) :: model_node = c_null_ptr !! transform of the model within the frame contains procedure :: set_model , share_model , model_file , has_model , model_bound procedure :: set_model_position , model_position procedure :: set_model_attitude , model_attitude procedure :: set_model_scale , model_scale procedure :: set_model_pivot , model_pivot procedure :: frame_info => model_frame_info procedure :: bound => model_frame_bound procedure :: pick => model_pick procedure :: build_contents => model_build_contents end type Model !> The Model constructor: `Model(...)` makes one (see `new_model` for its !> arguments). interface Model module procedure new_model end interface Model contains !> A model frame named `name` (decorations of color `color`), with the !> model file `file` if given (see `set_model`). function new_model ( name , file , color ) result ( m ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: file real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) type ( Model ) :: m logical :: ok m % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) if ( present ( file )) ok = m % set_model ( file ) end function new_model !> Read the model file (now, so its bound is known). Returns false if it !> could not be read. Set it before a window first shows the model. logical function set_model ( self , file ) result ( ok ) class ( Model ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: file type ( c_ptr ) :: node node = vkf_model_read ( file , len ( file , kind = c_int )) ok = c_associated ( node ) if (. not . ok ) return self % file = file self % model_ = node if ( vkf_node_bound ( node , self % bound_center , self % bound_radius ) /= 0 ) then self % bound_center = 0.0_wp self % bound_radius = 0.0_wp end if end function set_model !> Use the model already read by `other` (no second copy in memory). logical function share_model ( self , other ) result ( ok ) class ( Model ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( Model ), intent ( in ) :: other ok = c_associated ( other % model_ ) if (. not . ok ) return self % model_ = other % model_ self % file = other % file self % bound_center = other % bound_center self % bound_radius = other % bound_radius end function share_model !> The model file ('' if none). function model_file ( self ) result ( file ) class ( Model ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: file file = '' if ( allocated ( self % file )) file = self % file end function model_file !> True if a model was read (or shared). pure logical function has_model ( self ) class ( Model ), intent ( in ) :: self has_model = c_associated ( self % model_ ) end function has_model !> The model's bounding sphere, in the model's own coordinates (before its transform). subroutine model_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( Model ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius center = self % bound_center radius = self % bound_radius end subroutine model_bound !> Where the model's pivot is placed in its frame (frame coordinates). subroutine set_model_position ( self , position ) class ( Model ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: position ( 3 ) self % model_position_ = position call update_model_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_model_position !> Where the model's pivot is placed in its frame (frame coordinates). pure function model_position ( self ) result ( p ) class ( Model ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) p = self % model_position_ end function model_position !> Attitude of the model in its frame (quaternion [x, y, z, w]). subroutine set_model_attitude ( self , q ) class ( Model ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q ( 4 ) self % model_attitude_ = quat_normalize ( q ) call update_model_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_model_attitude !> Attitude of the model in its frame (quaternion [x, y, z, w]). pure function model_attitude ( self ) result ( q ) class ( Model ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: q ( 4 ) q = self % model_attitude_ end function model_attitude !> Scale along the model's x, y and z axes. subroutine set_model_scale ( self , scale ) class ( Model ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: scale ( 3 ) self % scale_ = scale call update_model_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_model_scale !> Scale along the model's x, y and z axes. pure function model_scale ( self ) result ( s ) class ( Model ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: s ( 3 ) s = self % scale_ end function model_scale !> The point of the model (in its own coordinates) placed at model_position, !> about which it is rotated and scaled. subroutine set_model_pivot ( self , pivot ) class ( Model ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: pivot ( 3 ) !! (model coordinates) self % pivot_ = pivot call update_model_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_model_pivot !> The model's pivot, in its own coordinates (see `set_model_pivot`). pure function model_pivot ( self ) result ( p ) class ( Model ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) p = self % pivot_ end function model_pivot !> The model's bounding sphere in the frame (through the model transform). subroutine model_frame_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( Model ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius real ( wp ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) m = frame_matrix ( self % model_position_ , self % model_attitude_ , self % scale_ , self % pivot_ ) center = matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), self % bound_center ) + m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) radius = self % bound_radius * maxval ( abs ( self % scale_ )) end subroutine model_frame_bound !> The kind of frame: 'Model'. function model_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( Model ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'Model' end function model_frame_info !> The model under the model transform. subroutine model_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( Model ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer handle (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the group node to build under if (. not . c_associated ( self % model_ )) return self % model_node = vkf_transform_create () call update_model_transform ( self ) if ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % model_node , self % model_ ) /= 0 . or . vkf_node_add_child ( group , self % model_node ) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Model ' // self % name () // ': could not build the scene' end subroutine model_build_contents !> Give the model transform to its node (once built). subroutine update_model_transform ( self ) type ( Model ), intent ( inout ) :: self if (. not . c_associated ( self % model_node )) return if ( vkf_transform_set_matrix ( self % model_node , & frame_matrix ( self % model_position_ , self % model_attitude_ , self % scale_ , self % pivot_ )) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Model ' // self % name () // ': transform failed' end subroutine update_model_transform !> Picked on the model's bounding sphere (not its triangles); else at the !> frame's origin. subroutine model_pick ( self , cam , to_root , hits , n ) class ( Model ), intent ( in ), target :: self type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam !! the cursor's ray and the pick's settings real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: to_root ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits so far (grown as needed) integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits in hits real ( wp ) :: c ( 3 ), r , m ( 4 , 4 ) call self % bound ( c , r ) if ( self % contents_shown () . and . r > 0.0_wp ) then m = identity_matrix () if ( pick_ellipsoid ( self , cam , to_root , c , m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), [ r , r , r ], . false ., hits , n )) return end if call self % ReferenceFrame % pick ( cam , to_root , hits , n ) end subroutine model_pick end module vkf_model","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_model.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_frames.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_frames.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 