pendent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> Math for vkframes: the working precision, quaternions and 4x4 transforms. !> !> Quaternions are `q(4) = [x, y, z, w]` (vector part first, as OpenFrames and !> OpenSceneGraph store them), unit length for rotations. The rotation of q !> takes vectors in a frame to its parent frame: v_parent = rotate(q, v_local). !> Matrices are 4x4, column-major, acting on column vectors. module vkf_math use , intrinsic :: iso_fortran_env , only : real64 implicit none private integer , parameter , public :: wp = real64 !! working precision real ( wp ), parameter , public :: pi = acos ( - 1.0_wp ) !! pi real ( wp ), parameter , public :: quat_identity ( 4 ) = [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! the identity rotation public :: quat_from_axis_angle , quat_multiply , quat_conjugate , quat_normalize public :: quat_rotate , quat_to_matrix , quat_from_matrix , quat_slerp , quat_from_vectors public :: identity_matrix , translation_matrix , frame_matrix , rigid_inverse , cross public :: set_rgba contains !> The rotation by `angle` (radians) about `axis` (need not be unit length). pure function quat_from_axis_angle ( axis , angle ) result ( q ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: axis ( 3 ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! (radians) real ( wp ) :: q ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: n n = norm2 ( axis ) if ( n == 0.0_wp ) then q = quat_identity else q ( 1 : 3 ) = axis / n * sin ( 0.5_wp * angle ) q ( 4 ) = cos ( 0.5_wp * angle ) end if end function quat_from_axis_angle !> The product a*b: rotating by b, then by a. pure function quat_multiply ( a , b ) result ( q ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: a ( 4 ), b ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: q ( 4 ) q ( 1 ) = a ( 4 ) * b ( 1 ) + a ( 1 ) * b ( 4 ) + a ( 2 ) * b ( 3 ) - a ( 3 ) * b ( 2 ) q ( 2 ) = a ( 4 ) * b ( 2 ) - a ( 1 ) * b ( 3 ) + a ( 2 ) * b ( 4 ) + a ( 3 ) * b ( 1 ) q ( 3 ) = a ( 4 ) * b ( 3 ) + a ( 1 ) * b ( 2 ) - a ( 2 ) * b ( 1 ) + a ( 3 ) * b ( 4 ) q ( 4 ) = a ( 4 ) * b ( 4 ) - a ( 1 ) * b ( 1 ) - a ( 2 ) * b ( 2 ) - a ( 3 ) * b ( 3 ) end function quat_multiply !> The conjugate of q: the inverse rotation, for a unit quaternion. pure function quat_conjugate ( q ) result ( c ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) c = [ - q ( 1 : 3 ), q ( 4 )] end function quat_conjugate !> q / |q| (the identity for a zero quaternion). pure function quat_normalize ( q ) result ( u ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: u ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: n n = norm2 ( q ) if ( n == 0.0_wp ) then u = quat_identity else u = q / n end if end function quat_normalize !> The vector v rotated by the unit quaternion q. pure function quat_rotate ( q , v ) result ( r ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q ( 4 ), v ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: r ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: t ( 3 ) ! r = v + 2 w (u x v) + 2 u x (u x v), with u = q(1:3), w = q(4) t = 2.0_wp * cross ( q ( 1 : 3 ), v ) r = v + q ( 4 ) * t + cross ( q ( 1 : 3 ), t ) end function quat_rotate !> The 3x3 rotation matrix of the unit quaternion q (columns: the rotated axes). pure function quat_to_matrix ( q ) result ( m ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: m ( 3 , 3 ) real ( wp ) :: x , y , z , w x = q ( 1 ); y = q ( 2 ); z = q ( 3 ); w = q ( 4 ) m ( 1 , 1 ) = 1.0_wp - 2.0_wp * ( y * y + z * z ) m ( 2 , 1 ) = 2.0_wp * ( x * y + z * w ) m ( 3 , 1 ) = 2.0_wp * ( x * z - y * w ) m ( 1 , 2 ) = 2.0_wp * ( x * y - z * w ) m ( 2 , 2 ) = 1.0_wp - 2.0_wp * ( x * x + z * z ) m ( 3 , 2 ) = 2.0_wp * ( y * z + x * w ) m ( 1 , 3 ) = 2.0_wp * ( x * z + y * w ) m ( 2 , 3 ) = 2.0_wp * ( y * z - x * w ) m ( 3 , 3 ) = 1.0_wp - 2.0_wp * ( x * x + y * y ) end function quat_to_matrix !> The unit quaternion of a 3x3 rotation matrix (columns: the rotated !> axes; the inverse of quat_to_matrix), by Shepperd's method (from the !> largest of w and the vector components, for accuracy). pure function quat_from_matrix ( m ) result ( q ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: m ( 3 , 3 ) real ( wp ) :: q ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: t , s t = m ( 1 , 1 ) + m ( 2 , 2 ) + m ( 3 , 3 ) if ( t >= max ( m ( 1 , 1 ), m ( 2 , 2 ), m ( 3 , 3 ))) then s = 2.0_wp * sqrt ( 1.0_wp + t ) q = [( m ( 3 , 2 ) - m ( 2 , 3 )) / s , ( m ( 1 , 3 ) - m ( 3 , 1 )) / s , ( m ( 2 , 1 ) - m ( 1 , 2 )) / s , 0.25_wp * s ] else if ( m ( 1 , 1 ) >= m ( 2 , 2 ) . and . m ( 1 , 1 ) >= m ( 3 , 3 )) then s = 2.0_wp * sqrt ( 1.0_wp + m ( 1 , 1 ) - m ( 2 , 2 ) - m ( 3 , 3 )) q = [ 0.25_wp * s , ( m ( 1 , 2 ) + m ( 2 , 1 )) / s , ( m ( 1 , 3 ) + m ( 3 , 1 )) / s , ( m ( 3 , 2 ) - m ( 2 , 3 )) / s ] else if ( m ( 2 , 2 ) >= m ( 3 , 3 )) then s = 2.0_wp * sqrt ( 1.0_wp - m ( 1 , 1 ) + m ( 2 , 2 ) - m ( 3 , 3 )) q = [( m ( 1 , 2 ) + m ( 2 , 1 )) / s , 0.25_wp * s , ( m ( 2 , 3 ) + m ( 3 , 2 )) / s , ( m ( 1 , 3 ) - m ( 3 , 1 )) / s ] else s = 2.0_wp * sqrt ( 1.0_wp - m ( 1 , 1 ) - m ( 2 , 2 ) + m ( 3 , 3 )) q = [( m ( 1 , 3 ) + m ( 3 , 1 )) / s , ( m ( 2 , 3 ) + m ( 3 , 2 )) / s , 0.25_wp * s , ( m ( 2 , 1 ) - m ( 1 , 2 )) / s ] end if q = q / norm2 ( q ) end function quat_from_matrix !> Spherical linear interpolation from `a` (t = 0) to `b` (t = 1), along the !> shorter arc; linear when the two are nearly equal. Same as OpenSceneGraph's !> osg::Quat::slerp, which OpenFrames' TrajectoryFollower uses. pure function quat_slerp ( t , a , b ) result ( q ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the fraction of the way (0 to 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: a ( 4 ), b ( 4 ) real ( wp ) :: q ( 4 ) real ( wp ), parameter :: epsilon = 0.00001_wp real ( wp ) :: cos_omega , omega , sin_omega , scale_a , scale_b , to ( 4 ) cos_omega = dot_product ( a , b ) to = b if ( cos_omega < 0.0_wp ) then cos_omega = - cos_omega to = - b end if if ( 1.0_wp - cos_omega > epsilon ) then omega = acos ( cos_omega ) sin_omega = sin ( omega ) scale_a = sin (( 1.0_wp - t ) * omega ) / sin_omega scale_b = sin ( t * omega ) / sin_omega else scale_a = 1.0_wp - t scale_b = t end if q = scale_a * a + scale_b * to end function quat_slerp !> The shortest rotation taking the direction of `from` to that of `to` !> (OpenSceneGraph's osg::Quat::makeRotate(from, to)); a half turn about a !> perpendicular axis if they are opposite, the identity if either is zero. pure function quat_from_vectors ( from , to ) result ( q ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: from ( 3 ), to ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: q ( 4 ) real ( wp ), parameter :: eps = 1.0e-12_wp real ( wp ) :: u ( 3 ), v ( 3 ), d , axis ( 3 ) q = quat_identity if ( norm2 ( from ) == 0.0_wp . or . norm2 ( to ) == 0.0_wp ) return u = from / norm2 ( from ) v = to / norm2 ( to ) d = dot_product ( u , v ) if ( d >= 1.0_wp - eps ) return if ( d <= - 1.0_wp + eps ) then axis = cross ( u , [ 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp ]) if ( norm2 ( axis ) < 1.0e-6_wp ) axis = cross ( u , [ 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp , 0.0_wp ]) q = [ axis / norm2 ( axis ), 0.0_wp ] return end if q = quat_normalize ([ cross ( u , v ), 1.0_wp + d ]) end function quat_from_vectors !> The inverse of a rigid transform (rotation and translation): [R' -R't]. pure function rigid_inverse ( m ) result ( inv ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) real ( wp ) :: inv ( 4 , 4 ) inv = 0.0_wp inv ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ) = transpose ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 )) inv ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) = - matmul ( inv ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), m ( 1 : 3 , 4 )) inv ( 4 , 4 ) = 1.0_wp end function rigid_inverse !> The 4x4 identity matrix. pure function identity_matrix () result ( m ) real ( wp ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) integer :: k m = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , 4 m ( k , k ) = 1.0_wp end do end function identity_matrix !> The 4x4 transform translating by `t`. pure function translation_matrix ( t ) result ( m ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) m = identity_matrix () m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) = t end function translation_matrix !> A frame's local-to-parent transform, as OpenFrames' FrameTransform builds !> it: translate(position) * rotate(attitude) * scale(scale) * translate(-pivot). pure function frame_matrix ( position , attitude , scale , pivot ) result ( m ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: position ( 3 ) !! origin in the parent frame real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: attitude ( 4 ) !! quaternion [x, y, z, w] real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: scale ( 3 ) !! scale along each local axis (default 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: pivot ( 3 ) !! local point placed at `position` (default 0) real ( wp ) :: m ( 4 , 4 ) real ( wp ) :: r ( 3 , 3 ), s ( 3 ), p ( 3 ) integer :: k s = 1.0_wp p = 0.0_wp if ( present ( scale )) s = scale if ( present ( pivot )) p = pivot r = quat_to_matrix ( attitude ) m = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , 3 m ( 1 : 3 , k ) = r (:, k ) * s ( k ) end do m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) = position - matmul ( m ( 1 : 3 , 1 : 3 ), p ) m ( 4 , 4 ) = 1.0_wp end function frame_matrix !> The cross product a x b. pure function cross ( a , b ) result ( c ) real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: a ( 3 ), b ( 3 ) real ( wp ) :: c ( 3 ) c = [ a ( 2 ) * b ( 3 ) - a ( 3 ) * b ( 2 ), a ( 3 ) * b ( 1 ) - a ( 1 ) * b ( 3 ), a ( 1 ) * b ( 2 ) - a ( 2 ) * b ( 1 )] end function cross !> Set `rgba` from `color`: [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a]. pure subroutine set_rgba ( rgba , color ) real ( wp ), intent ( inout ) :: rgba ( 4 ) !! [r, g, b, a] real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) integer :: n n = min ( 4 , size ( color )) rgba ( 1 : n ) = color ( 1 : n ) end subroutine set_rgba end module vkf_math","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_math.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_shadow.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_shadow.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 vkf_shadow.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkf_terrain.f90 vkf_terrain.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vk