this one sourcefile~~vkf_shadow.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 vkf_shadow.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> Shadow cones: the regions of a celestial body's shadow in the light of !> another (e.g. the Earth's or the Moon's shadow in sunlight), drawn as !> transparent cones: !> !> * the umbra (total eclipse: the light hidden), converging behind the body !>   to its apex, at d R / (Rs - R) from the body's center; !> * the antumbra (annular eclipse: the light seen around the body), from the !>   umbra's apex outward, widening at the umbra's angle; !> * the penumbra (partial eclipse), widening behind the body. !> !> (R and Rs: the body's and the light's radii; d: the distance between their !> centers. The edges are the lines tangent to both spheres: the outer !> tangents for the umbra and antumbra, half-angle asin((Rs - R) / d), the !> inner ones for the penumbra, asin((Rs + R) / d).) A body larger than its !> light has no apex: its umbra widens (or is a cylinder), with no antumbra. !> !> A ShadowCones is a frame of its own, made a child of the body (`add_child`) !> for one body's shadow, and shown or hidden with `show_contents`: a scene !> without one does no shadow work at all. It refers to the body and the light !> frames (they must stay alive while set); each scene update, after the whole !> tree has moved (late_update), it moves itself to the body's center and !> turns its +z axis away from the light (its own position and attitude are !> set there, whatever its parent), and reshapes the cones for the distance !> between them: the cones' vertices are rewritten in place and uploaded only !> when the shape changed (not as the body only turns). Hidden, it does !> nothing (and is placed again when shown). !> !> The radii: given (`set_body_radius`, `set_light_radius`), or the frames' !> own: a Sphere's equatorial radius, a TerrainBody's (a light that is a plain !> ReferenceFrame needs its radius given: none, no shadow). The shadow is drawn to !> `set_length` behind the body's center (default: twice the umbra's length; !> a hundred body radii without an apex); the umbra stops there if shorter. !> Each region has a color ([r, g, b, a]; the surfaces are unlit, !> transparent, seen from both sides, as the cones of vkf_shapes) and can be !> drawn or not (`set_regions`). !> !> Bodies in a shadow are not darkened (that needs shadows in the lighting). module vkf_shadow use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_ptr , c_null_ptr , c_associated , c_int , c_int32_t , c_float use vkf_math , only : wp , pi , quat_from_vectors , rigid_inverse use vkf_frames , only : ReferenceFrame , NO_AXES use vkf_sphere , only : Sphere use vkf_terrain , only : TerrainBody use vkf_layer , only : check_status , vkf_mesh_create , vkf_mesh_vertices_changed , vkf_switch_create , vkf_switch_set , & vkf_node_add_child , mesh_arrays , mesh_set_material implicit none private !> The regions (combine with ior). integer , parameter , public :: SHADOW_UMBRA = 1 , SHADOW_PENUMBRA = 2 , SHADOW_ANTUMBRA = 4 integer , parameter , public :: SHADOW_ALL = 7 !! SHADOW_UMBRA + SHADOW_PENUMBRA + SHADOW_ANTUMBRA integer , parameter :: n_regions = 3 !! umbra, penumbra and antumbra integer , parameter :: umbra = 1 , penumbra = 2 , antumbra = 3 !! region indices integer , parameter :: n_around = 128 !! segments around each cone !> A shadow region's surface: a frustum along z from z0 (radius r0) to z1 !> (radius r1), in the shadow frame's coordinates. type :: ShadowRegion logical :: drawn = . false . !! has a surface (and is to be drawn) real ( wp ) :: z0 = 0.0_wp !! start along z (scene units) real ( wp ) :: r0 = 0.0_wp !! radius at z0 (scene units) real ( wp ) :: z1 = 0.0_wp !! end along z (scene units) real ( wp ) :: r1 = 0.0_wp !! radius at z1 (scene units) real ( wp ) :: color ( 4 ) = 1.0_wp !! [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) type ( c_ptr ) :: switch = c_null_ptr !! shows or hides the mesh (null until built) type ( c_ptr ) :: mesh = c_null_ptr !! the surface: rings of vertices at z0 and z1 end type ShadowRegion !> A body's shadow cones (see the module documentation). type , extends ( ReferenceFrame ), public :: ShadowCones private class ( ReferenceFrame ), pointer :: body_ => null () !! the body casting the shadow (not owned) class ( ReferenceFrame ), pointer :: light_ => null () !! the light (not owned) real ( wp ) :: body_radius_ = 0.0_wp , light_radius_ = 0.0_wp !! (0: the frames' own) real ( wp ) :: length_ = 0.0_wp !! (0: automatic) integer :: regions_ = SHADOW_ALL !! an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA, SHADOW_ANTUMBRA type ( ShadowRegion ) :: region ( n_regions ) !! umbra, penumbra and antumbra real ( wp ) :: shaped ( 4 ) = - 1.0_wp !! R, Rs, d and length the cones have now real ( wp ) :: distance_ = 0.0_wp !! body to light at the last update (scene units) real ( wp ) :: drawn_length_ = 0.0_wp !! the length drawn at the last update (scene units) contains procedure :: set_body , body , set_light , light procedure :: set_body_radius , set_light_radius , body_radius , light_radius procedure :: set_length , length , drawn_length , distance procedure :: set_regions , regions procedure :: set_region_color , region_color procedure :: region_extent , umbra_length procedure :: frame_info => shadow_frame_info procedure :: bound => shadow_bound procedure :: build_contents => shadow_build_contents procedure :: late_update => shadow_late_update end type ShadowCones !> The ShadowCones constructor: `ShadowCones(...)` makes one (see `new_shadow_cones` for its !> arguments). interface ShadowCones module procedure new_shadow_cones end interface ShadowCones contains !> The shadow named `name` of `body` in the light of `light` (frames of the !> same tree; optional here, set later with set_body and set_light), with !> their radii if given (else the frames': see the module documentation). !> Its axes and name label are hidden. function new_shadow_cones ( name , body , light , body_radius , light_radius ) result ( s ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target , optional :: body , light real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: body_radius , light_radius !! scene units (default: the frames' own) type ( ShadowCones ) :: s s % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name ) call s % show_axes ( NO_AXES ) call s % show_axes_labels ( NO_AXES ) call s % show_name_label (. false .) if ( present ( body )) s % body_ => body if ( present ( light )) s % light_ => light if ( present ( body_radius )) call s % set_body_radius ( body_radius ) if ( present ( light_radius )) call s % set_light_radius ( light_radius ) s % region ( umbra )% color = [ 0.95_wp , 0.25_wp , 0.2_wp , 0.25_wp ] s % region ( penumbra )% color = [ 0.95_wp , 0.75_wp , 0.25_wp , 0.08_wp ] s % region ( antumbra )% color = [ 0.35_wp , 0.5_wp , 1.0_wp , 0.25_wp ] end function new_shadow_cones !> The body casting the shadow (it must stay alive while set), and its !> radius (optional: see set_body_radius). subroutine set_body ( self , body , radius ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: body real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: radius !! scene units (see set_body_radius) self % body_ => body if ( present ( radius )) call self % set_body_radius ( radius ) end subroutine set_body !> The body casting the shadow (null if not set). function body ( self ) result ( p ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self class ( ReferenceFrame ), pointer :: p p => self % body_ end function body !> The light (e.g. the Sun; it must stay alive while set), and its radius !> (optional: see set_light_radius). subroutine set_light ( self , light , radius ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ), target :: light real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: radius !! scene units (see set_light_radius) self % light_ => light if ( present ( radius )) call self % set_light_radius ( radius ) end subroutine set_light !> The light (null if not set). function light ( self ) result ( p ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self class ( ReferenceFrame ), pointer :: p p => self % light_ end function light !> The body's radius (scene units; 0: the body's own, a Sphere's !> equatorial radius or a TerrainBody's). subroutine set_body_radius ( self , radius ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radius !! scene units (0: the body's own) self % body_radius_ = max ( 0.0_wp , radius ) end subroutine set_body_radius !> The light's radius (scene units; 0: the light's own, if a Sphere). subroutine set_light_radius ( self , radius ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radius !! scene units (0: the light's own) self % light_radius_ = max ( 0.0_wp , radius ) end subroutine set_light_radius !> The body's radius used (0: none known). real ( wp ) function body_radius ( self ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self body_radius = self % body_radius_ if ( body_radius > 0.0_wp . or . . not . associated ( self % body_ )) return body_radius = frame_radius ( self % body_ ) end function body_radius !> The light's radius used (0: none known). real ( wp ) function light_radius ( self ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self light_radius = self % light_radius_ if ( light_radius > 0.0_wp . or . . not . associated ( self % light_ )) return light_radius = frame_radius ( self % light_ ) end function light_radius !> A body's own radius: a Sphere's equatorial one, a TerrainBody's; else 0. real ( wp ) function frame_radius ( frame ) result ( r ) class ( ReferenceFrame ), intent ( in ) :: frame real ( wp ) :: radii ( 3 ) r = 0.0_wp select type ( frame ) class is ( Sphere ) radii = frame % radii () r = max ( radii ( 1 ), radii ( 2 )) class is ( TerrainBody ) r = frame % body_radius () end select end function frame_radius !> How far behind the body's center the shadow is drawn (scene units; 0: !> automatic, twice the umbra's length). subroutine set_length ( self , length ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: length !! scene units (0: automatic) self % length_ = max ( 0.0_wp , length ) end subroutine set_length !> The length set (0: automatic). pure real ( wp ) function length ( self ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self length = self % length_ end function length !> The length drawn at the last update. pure real ( wp ) function drawn_length ( self ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self drawn_length = self % drawn_length_ end function drawn_length !> The distance between the body and the light at the last update. pure real ( wp ) function distance ( self ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self distance = self % distance_ end function distance !> The regions to draw: an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA and !> SHADOW_ANTUMBRA (default SHADOW_ALL). subroutine set_regions ( self , regions ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: regions !! an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA, SHADOW_ANTUMBRA self % regions_ = iand ( regions , SHADOW_ALL ) self % shaped = - 1.0_wp ! (redrawn at the next update) end subroutine set_regions !> The regions drawn: an ior of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA and !> SHADOW_ANTUMBRA. pure integer function regions ( self ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self regions = self % regions_ end function regions !> A region's color (region: one of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA, !> SHADOW_ANTUMBRA; [r, g, b], alpha unchanged, or [r, g, b, a]). subroutine set_region_color ( self , region , color ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: region !! SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA or SHADOW_ANTUMBRA real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] (alpha unchanged) or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1 integer :: k , n k = region_index ( region ) if ( k == 0 ) return n = min ( 4 , size ( color )) self % region ( k )% color ( 1 : n ) = color ( 1 : n ) call apply_color ( self % region ( k )) end subroutine set_region_color !> A region's color [r, g, b, a] (0 for an unknown region). function region_color ( self , region ) result ( c ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: region !! SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA or SHADOW_ANTUMBRA real ( wp ) :: c ( 4 ) integer :: k c = 0.0_wp k = region_index ( region ) if ( k > 0 ) c = self % region ( k )% color end function region_color !> The index in self%region of SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA or !> SHADOW_ANTUMBRA (0 for anything else). pure integer function region_index ( region ) result ( k ) integer , intent ( in ) :: region !! SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA or SHADOW_ANTUMBRA select case ( region ) case ( SHADOW_UMBRA ) k = umbra case ( SHADOW_PENUMBRA ) k = penumbra case ( SHADOW_ANTUMBRA ) k = antumbra case default k = 0 end select end function region_index !> A region's surface at the last update, along the frame's +z axis (away !> from the light; the body's center at the origin): drawn, from z0 !> (radius r0) to z1 (radius r1). subroutine region_extent ( self , region , drawn , z0 , r0 , z1 , r1 ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: region !! SHADOW_UMBRA, SHADOW_PENUMBRA or SHADOW_ANTUMBRA logical , intent ( out ) :: drawn !! it has a surface and is drawn real ( wp ), intent ( out ), optional :: z0 , r0 , z1 , r1 !! scene units type ( ShadowRegion ) :: g integer :: k k = region_index ( region ) if ( k > 0 ) g = self % region ( k ) drawn = k > 0 . and . g % drawn if ( present ( z0 )) z0 = g % z0 if ( present ( r0 )) r0 = g % r0 if ( present ( z1 )) z1 = g % z1 if ( present ( r1 )) r1 = g % r1 end subroutine region_extent !> The distance from the body's center to the umbra's apex at the last !> update (huge() for a body no smaller than its light; 0 before). pure real ( wp ) function umbra_length ( self ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: r , rs , d r = self % shaped ( 1 ) rs = self % shaped ( 2 ) d = self % shaped ( 3 ) umbra_length = 0.0_wp if ( d <= 0.0_wp ) return if ( rs > r ) then umbra_length = d * r / ( rs - r ) else umbra_length = huge ( 1.0_wp ) end if end function umbra_length !> What kind of frame this is: 'ShadowCones'. function shadow_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'ShadowCones' end function shadow_frame_info !> The drawn regions' bounding sphere (frame coordinates). subroutine shadow_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius !! the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) real ( wp ) :: lo , hi , r integer :: k center = 0.0_wp radius = 0.0_wp lo = huge ( 1.0_wp ) hi = - huge ( 1.0_wp ) r = 0.0_wp do k = 1 , n_regions if (. not . self % region ( k )% drawn ) cycle lo = min ( lo , self % region ( k )% z0 ) hi = max ( hi , self % region ( k )% z1 ) r = max ( r , self % region ( k )% r0 , self % region ( k )% r1 ) end do if ( hi < lo ) return center ( 3 ) = 0.5_wp * ( lo + hi ) radius = hypot ( 0.5_wp * ( hi - lo ), r ) end subroutine shadow_bound !> A switch with a mesh for each region (vertices written at each change !> of shape), under `group`. subroutine shadow_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the frame's contents group real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: v , normals , uv integer ( c_int32_t ), dimension (:), pointer :: indices integer :: k , i , j , n n = n_around do k = 1 , n_regions associate ( g => self % region ( k )) g % mesh = vkf_mesh_create ( int ( 2 * n , c_int ), int ( 6 * n , c_int ), [ 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , & 1.0_c_float ], c_null_ptr , c_null_ptr , 5_c_int ) ! unlit, transparent; vertices change if (. not . c_associated ( g % mesh )) cycle call mesh_arrays ( g % mesh , 2 * n , 6 * n , v , normals , uv , indices ) v = 0.0_c_float normals = 0.0_c_float normals ( 3 , :) = 1.0_c_float uv = 0.0_c_float do i = 1 , n ! ring 0: vertices 0..n-1; ring 1: n..2n-1 j = modulo ( i , n ) indices ( 6 * i - 5 : 6 * i ) = int ([ i - 1 , j , n + i - 1 , j , n + j , n + i - 1 ], c_int32_t ) end do call apply_color ( g ) g % switch = vkf_switch_create () call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( g % switch , g % mesh ), 'shadow' ) call check_status ( vkf_switch_set ( g % switch , 0_c_int ), 'shadow' ) ! (until shaped) call check_status ( vkf_node_add_child ( group , g % switch ), 'shadow' ) end associate end do self % shaped = - 1.0_wp ! (shaped at the next update) end subroutine shadow_build_contents !> A region's color, through its mesh's material (the unlit shader !> multiplies the vertex color, white, by the diffuse color). subroutine apply_color ( g ) type ( ShadowRegion ), intent ( in ) :: g real ( c_float ) :: c ( 4 ) if (. not . c_associated ( g % mesh )) return c = real ( g % color , c_float ) call check_status ( mesh_set_material ( g % mesh , c , c , [ 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], & [ 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 0.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], 0.0_c_float ), 'shadow' ) end subroutine apply_color !> After the tree's update for time t: the shadow moved to the body, turned !> away from the light, and reshaped if the distance or a setting changed. recursive subroutine shadow_late_update ( self , t ) class ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the scene time if ( associated ( self % body_ ) . and . associated ( self % light_ ) . and . self % contents_shown ()) call place ( self ) call self % ReferenceFrame % late_update ( t ) end subroutine shadow_late_update !> Move the shadow to the body's center (in the parent's coordinates) with its !> +z axis away from the light, and reshape the cones if the radii, the !> distance or the length set changed. subroutine place ( self ) type ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ) :: to_parent ( 4 , 4 ), m ( 4 , 4 ), b ( 3 ), s ( 3 ), u ( 3 ), d , now ( 4 ) ! the body's and the light's centers in the parent's coordinates to_parent = rigid_inverse ( matmul ( self % world_matrix (), rigid_inverse ( self % local_matrix ()))) m = matmul ( to_parent , self % body_ % world_matrix ()) b = m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) m = matmul ( to_parent , self % light_ % world_matrix ()) s = m ( 1 : 3 , 4 ) u = b - s d = norm2 ( u ) self % distance_ = d call self % set_position ( b ) if ( d > 0.0_wp ) call self % set_attitude ( quat_from_vectors ([ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp ], u / d )) now = [ self % body_radius (), self % light_radius (), d , self % length_ ] if ( all ( now == self % shaped )) return self % shaped = now call shape_regions ( self , now ( 1 ), now ( 2 ), d ) end subroutine place !> The regions' frustums for body radius r, light radius rs and distance d !> (see the module documentation), written to their meshes. subroutine shape_regions ( self , r , rs , d ) type ( ShadowCones ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: r , rs , d !! scene units real ( wp ) :: sa , ca , ta , sb , cb , tb , apex , len integer :: k self % region % drawn = . false . self % drawn_length_ = 0.0_wp if ( r > 0.0_wp . and . rs > 0.0_wp . and . d > r + rs ) then sa = ( rs - r ) / d ! the umbra's half-angle (sine; < 0: widening) ca = sqrt ( 1.0_wp - sa ** 2 ) ta = sa / ca sb = ( rs + r ) / d ! the penumbra's cb = sqrt ( 1.0_wp - sb ** 2 ) tb = sb / cb apex = huge ( 1.0_wp ) if ( sa > 0.0_wp ) apex = r / sa len = self % length_ if ( len <= 0.0_wp ) then len = 10 0.0_wp * r if ( sa > 0.0_wp ) len = 2.0_wp * apex end if self % drawn_length_ = len ! the umbra: from the outer tangents' circle on the body to the apex (or len) associate ( g => self % region ( umbra )) g % z0 = r * sa g % r0 = r * ca g % z1 = min ( apex , len ) g % r1 = max ( 0.0_wp , g % r0 - ( g % z1 - g % z0 ) * ta ) if ( g % z1 >= apex ) g % r1 = 0.0_wp g % drawn = g % z1 > g % z0 end associate ! the antumbra: from the apex to len associate ( g => self % region ( antumbra )) g % z0 = apex g % r0 = 0.0_wp g % z1 = len g % r1 = ( len - apex ) * ta g % drawn = sa > 0.0_wp . and . len > apex end associate ! the penumbra: from the inner tangents' circle (on the light's side) to len associate ( g => self % region ( penumbra )) g % z0 = - r * sb g % r0 = r * cb g % z1 = len g % r1 = g % r0 + ( len - g % z0 ) * tb g % drawn = len > g % z0 end associate end if self % region ( umbra )% drawn = self % region ( umbra )% drawn . and . iand ( self % regions_ , SHADOW_UMBRA ) /= 0 self % region ( penumbra )% drawn = self % region ( penumbra )% drawn . and . iand ( self % regions_ , SHADOW_PENUMBRA ) /= 0 self % region ( antumbra )% drawn = self % region ( antumbra )% drawn . and . iand ( self % regions_ , SHADOW_ANTUMBRA ) /= 0 do k = 1 , n_regions call write_region ( self % region ( k )) end do end subroutine shape_regions !> A region's frustum into its mesh (uploaded), and shown or hidden. subroutine write_region ( g ) type ( ShadowRegion ), intent ( in ) :: g real ( c_float ), dimension (:,:), pointer :: v , normals , uv integer ( c_int32_t ), dimension (:), pointer :: indices real ( wp ) :: a integer :: i , n if (. not . c_associated ( g % mesh )) return n = n_around if ( g % drawn ) then call mesh_arrays ( g % mesh , 2 * n , 6 * n , v , normals , uv , indices ) do i = 1 , n a = 2.0_wp * pi * ( i - 1 ) / n v (:, i ) = real ([ g % r0 * cos ( a ), g % r0 * sin ( a ), g % z0 ], c_float ) v (:, n + i ) = real ([ g % r1 * cos ( a ), g % r1 * sin ( a ), g % z1 ], c_float ) end do call check_status ( vkf_mesh_vertices_changed ( g % mesh ), 'shadow' ) end if call check_status ( vkf_switch_set ( g % switch , merge ( 1_c_int , 0_c_int , g % drawn )), 'shadow' ) end subroutine write_region end module vkf_shadow","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_shadow.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_sphere.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_sphere.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90->sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90->sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90->sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_frames.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_geometry.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_pick.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_follower.f90->sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 sourcefile~vkf_trajectory.f90->sourcefile~vkf_math.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Files dependent on this one sourcefile~~vkf_sphere.f90~~AfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 vkf_shadow.f90 sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90 vkframes.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_sphere.f90 sourcefile~vkframes.f90->sourcefile~vkf_shadow.f90 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Source File Source File This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a file to a file which it depends on. A file\nis dependent upon another if the latter must be compiled before the former\ncan be. Source Code !> Spheres and ellipsoids: a textured celestial body, as OpenFrames' Sphere. !> !> The body is centered on its frame's origin (or at `set_sphere_position`, !> turned by `set_sphere_attitude`, e.g. to orient a texture). Its shape is a !> sphere of `radius`, or an ellipsoid with semi-axes radius * `sphere_scale`; !> the ellipsoid is built directly (exact normals, geodetic texture mapping; see !> vkf_geometry), where OpenFrames scales a sphere. The texture is an !> equirectangular image (longitude -180 to 180, north at the top). The color is !> used when there is no texture. !> !> Lighting: the body is lit by the scene's lights (a frame's light source, !> e.g. the Sun, or the window's light), with a material (`set_material`; !> OpenFrames' default: no specular reflection). The night texture shows where !> the surface is lit weakly (the night side: city lights), as OpenFrames' !> setNightTextureMap: weighted by 1 - the lit color (the material's ambient !> and diffuse colors in the lights' colors and intensities, and its !> emission), per channel and per pixel, so a brighter light narrows the !> band where the day fades into the night, and ambient light dims the night !> texture. The twilight (`set_twilight`; not in OpenFrames; default none: !> the light ends at the terminator) extends the diffuse light past the !> terminator, to where the light is a given angle below the horizon, fading !> out: e.g. sunlight scattered by an atmosphere. !> !> Translucency (not in OpenFrames): `set_opacity` (default 1, opaque) below !> 1 draws the body translucent: lit as usual, blended over what is behind !> it, drawn after the opaque scene (farthest first: VSG's depth-sorted bin) !> without writing depth, front faces only. Whether it is translucent is !> decided when a window first shows it (as the textures); its opacity can !> then change at any time (through the material's alpha). !> !> Texture files are found with find_data_file (a path, or a name on !> VKFRAMES_DATA_PATH, e.g. data/'s 2k_earth_daymap.jpg and !> 2k_earth_nightmap.jpg). The textures and the mesh resolution are read when !> a window first shows the sphere: set them before that. The radius, scale, !> color and material can change at any time: the meshes are built once, then !> scaled by their transform (radii / the built radii), and the color is applied !> through the material (the shaders multiply the vertex color, white here, by !> the diffuse color). !> !> Level of detail (`set_auto_lod`, on by default; OpenFrames' setAutoLOD): the !> body has meshes of 32, 64, ... 1024 segments around (half as many from pole !> to pole), and each view draws the coarsest whose facets stay within half a !> pixel of the true outline (src/vsg/vkf_layer.cpp: SphereLod), so that the !> body isn't faceted however close the view. Meshes are built when a view !> first wants them (the 128-segment one at once), in the sphere's update. !> Off: one mesh of `set_resolution`'s segments (default 128 x 64). module vkf_sphere use , intrinsic :: iso_c_binding , only : c_ptr , c_null_ptr , c_associated , c_int , c_float use vkf_math , only : wp , quat_identity , quat_normalize , frame_matrix , quat_to_matrix use vkf_frames , only : ReferenceFrame , PickHit , pick_ellipsoid use vkf_pick , only : PickCamera use vkf_layer , only : vkf_image_read , vkf_image_delete , vkf_transform_create , vkf_transform_set_matrix , & vkf_node_add_child , vkf_node_delete , mesh_set_material , vkf_mesh_set_twilight , vkf_compile_node , & vkf_sphere_lod_create , vkf_sphere_lod_add , vkf_sphere_lod_requested use vkf_geometry , only : ellipsoid_create use vkf_files , only : find_data_file implicit none private !> The level-of-detail meshes: segments around the equator (half as many !> from pole to pole); the one built at once. integer , parameter :: lod_segments ( 6 ) = [ 32 , 64 , 128 , 256 , 512 , 1024 ] integer , parameter :: lod_first = 3 !! the index of the mesh built at once (128 segments) !> A sphere or ellipsoid (see the module documentation). type , extends ( ReferenceFrame ), public :: Sphere private real ( wp ) :: radius_ = 1.0_wp !! radius (scene units; default 1) real ( wp ) :: scale_ ( 3 ) = 1.0_wp !! scale along x, y and z: semi-axes radius * scale real ( wp ) :: sphere_position_ ( 3 ) = 0.0_wp !! the body's center in the frame (scene units) real ( wp ) :: sphere_attitude_ ( 4 ) = quat_identity !! the body's attitude in the frame ([x, y, z, w]) real ( wp ) :: built_radii ( 3 ) = 1.0_wp !! the mesh's semi-axes logical :: textured = . false . !! (the color is not used) character ( len = :), allocatable :: texture !! texture file (unallocated or '': none) character ( len = :), allocatable :: night_texture !! night texture file (unallocated or '': none) logical :: auto_lod_ = . true . !! level of detail (default on) integer :: n_lon = 128 , n_lat = 64 !! without level of detail ! material (VSG's Phong; OpenGL's default: no specular reflection) real ( wp ) :: ambient_ ( 4 ) = 1.0_wp !! ambient color [r, g, b, a] real ( wp ) :: diffuse_ ( 4 ) = 1.0_wp !! diffuse [r, g, b, a] (times the color if no texture) real ( wp ) :: specular_ ( 4 ) = [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! specular color [r, g, b, a] real ( wp ) :: emission_ ( 4 ) = [ 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 0.0_wp , 1.0_wp ] !! emission color [r, g, b, a] real ( wp ) :: shininess_ = 0.0_wp !! 0 to 128 (0: no specular highlight) real ( wp ) :: twilight_ = 0.0_wp !! radians below the horizon (0: none) real ( wp ) :: opacity_ = 1.0_wp !! 1 opaque; below 1 translucent (see set_opacity) logical :: translucent = . false . !! built translucent (opacity below 1 when first shown) type ( c_ptr ) :: sphere_node = c_null_ptr !! transform of the body within the frame type ( c_ptr ) :: mesh = c_null_ptr !! without level of detail ! level of detail type ( c_ptr ) :: lod_node = c_null_ptr !! chooses among the meshes, per view type ( c_ptr ) :: lod_mesh ( size ( lod_segments )) = c_null_ptr !! the level-of-detail meshes (null: not built yet) type ( c_ptr ) :: image = c_null_ptr , night = c_null_ptr !! the textures, for meshes built later logical :: shown = . false . !! (meshes built later are compiled) contains procedure :: set_radius , radius procedure :: set_color => sphere_set_color procedure :: set_sphere_scale , sphere_scale , radii procedure :: set_sphere_position , sphere_position procedure :: set_sphere_attitude , sphere_attitude procedure :: set_texture_map , texture_map procedure :: set_night_texture_map , night_texture_map procedure :: set_auto_lod , auto_lod procedure :: set_material , material procedure :: set_twilight , twilight procedure :: set_opacity , opacity procedure :: set_resolution procedure :: frame_info => sphere_frame_info procedure :: bound => sphere_bound procedure :: pick => sphere_pick procedure :: build_contents => sphere_build_contents procedure :: update => sphere_update procedure :: num_lod_meshes end type Sphere !> The Sphere constructor: `Sphere(...)` makes one (see `new_sphere` for its !> arguments). interface Sphere module procedure new_sphere end interface Sphere contains !> A sphere named `name`, of radius `radius` (default 1) and color `color` !> ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]; default white, 90% opaque). function new_sphere ( name , radius , color ) result ( s ) character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: radius !! scene units (default 1) real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) type ( Sphere ) :: s s % ReferenceFrame = ReferenceFrame ( name , color ) if ( present ( radius )) s % radius_ = radius end function new_sphere !> The sphere's radius (scene units, > 0; default 1); can change at any time. subroutine set_radius ( self , radius ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: radius !! scene units (<= 0: ignored) if ( radius <= 0.0_wp ) return self % radius_ = radius call update_sphere_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_radius !> The body's color (used without a texture); [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a]. subroutine sphere_set_color ( self , color ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: color (:) !! [r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a] (0 to 1) call self % ReferenceFrame % set_color ( color ) call apply_material ( self ) end subroutine sphere_set_color !> The body's opacity, 0 (invisible) to 1 (opaque, the default): below 1 !> it is drawn translucent (see the module documentation). Set below 1 !> before a window first shows it to make it translucent; then the !> opacity can change at any time (a translucent body stays translucent, !> an opaque one opaque). subroutine set_opacity ( self , opacity ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: opacity !! 0 to 1 self % opacity_ = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.0_wp , opacity )) call apply_material ( self ) end subroutine set_opacity !> The body's opacity (set_opacity). pure real ( wp ) function opacity ( self ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self opacity = self % opacity_ end function opacity !> The sphere's radius (scene units). pure real ( wp ) function radius ( self ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self radius = self % radius_ end function radius !> Scale the sphere along its x, y and z axes (all > 0), making an !> ellipsoid with semi-axes radius * scale. subroutine set_sphere_scale ( self , scale ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: scale ( 3 ) !! along x, y and z (all > 0, else ignored) if ( any ( scale <= 0.0_wp )) return self % scale_ = scale call update_sphere_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_sphere_scale !> The scale along the sphere's x, y and z axes. pure function sphere_scale ( self ) result ( s ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: s ( 3 ) s = self % scale_ end function sphere_scale !> The semi-axes: radius * sphere_scale. pure function radii ( self ) result ( r ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: r ( 3 ) r = self % radius_ * self % scale_ end function radii !> Position of the body's center in its frame. subroutine set_sphere_position ( self , position ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: position ( 3 ) !! scene units self % sphere_position_ = position call update_sphere_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_sphere_position !> Position of the body's center in its frame (scene units). pure function sphere_position ( self ) result ( p ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: p ( 3 ) p = self % sphere_position_ end function sphere_position !> Attitude of the body in its frame (quaternion [x, y, z, w]), e.g. to !> orient its texture. subroutine set_sphere_attitude ( self , q ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: q ( 4 ) !! quaternion [x, y, z, w] (normalized here) self % sphere_attitude_ = quat_normalize ( q ) call update_sphere_transform ( self ) end subroutine set_sphere_attitude !> Attitude of the body in its frame (quaternion [x, y, z, w]). pure function sphere_attitude ( self ) result ( q ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ) :: q ( 4 ) q = self % sphere_attitude_ end function sphere_attitude !> The texture: an equirectangular image file ('' for none). subroutine set_texture_map ( self , file ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: file !! found with find_data_file; '' for none self % texture = file end subroutine set_texture_map !> The texture file ('' for none). function texture_map ( self ) result ( file ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: file file = '' if ( allocated ( self % texture )) file = self % texture end function texture_map !> The texture for the side away from the light (e.g. city lights; an !> equirectangular image file as the texture, '' for none), shown where the !> diffuse light is weak. subroutine set_night_texture_map ( self , file ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: file !! found with find_data_file; '' for none self % night_texture = file end subroutine set_night_texture_map !> The night texture file ('' for none). function night_texture_map ( self ) result ( file ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: file file = '' if ( allocated ( self % night_texture )) file = self % night_texture end function night_texture_map !> The material (OpenFrames' setMaterial; each optional): ambient, diffuse, !> specular and emission colors ([r, g, b] or [r, g, b, a], 0 to 1) and !> shininess (0 to 128: the specular highlight's sharpness; 0 for none). !> The ambient and diffuse colors scale the body's color or texture (VSG's !> Phong); the specular color is reflected from the lights' specular parts. !> Defaults: ambient and diffuse white, no specular reflection or emission. subroutine set_material ( self , ambient , diffuse , specular , emission , shininess ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: ambient (:), diffuse (:), specular (:), emission (:) !! [r, g, b(, a)], 0 to 1 real ( wp ), intent ( in ), optional :: shininess !! 0 to 128 (< 0: 0) if ( present ( ambient )) self % ambient_ ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( ambient ))) = ambient ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( ambient ))) if ( present ( diffuse )) self % diffuse_ ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( diffuse ))) = diffuse ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( diffuse ))) if ( present ( specular )) self % specular_ ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( specular ))) = specular ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( specular ))) if ( present ( emission )) self % emission_ ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( emission ))) = emission ( 1 : min ( 4 , size ( emission ))) if ( present ( shininess )) self % shininess_ = max ( 0.0_wp , shininess ) call apply_material ( self ) end subroutine set_material !> The material (each optional): ambient, diffuse, specular and emission colors !> and shininess. pure subroutine material ( self , ambient , diffuse , specular , emission , shininess ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ), optional :: ambient ( 4 ), diffuse ( 4 ), specular ( 4 ), emission ( 4 ) !! [r, g, b, a] real ( wp ), intent ( out ), optional :: shininess !! 0 to 128 if ( present ( ambient )) ambient = self % ambient_ if ( present ( diffuse )) diffuse = self % diffuse_ if ( present ( specular )) specular = self % specular_ if ( present ( emission )) emission = self % emission_ if ( present ( shininess )) shininess = self % shininess_ end subroutine material !> The twilight: the diffuse light extended past the terminator to where !> the light is `angle` (radians, 0 to 1.5) below the horizon, fading out !> smoothly (where it meets the light on the day side: the same brightness !> and slope, so no line shows), and the night texture fading in across it. !> 0 (the default): none, the light ends at the terminator (an airless !> body). Not in OpenFrames. Can change at any time. subroutine set_twilight ( self , angle ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: angle !! radians below the horizon (clamped to 0 to 1.5) self % twilight_ = max ( 0.0_wp , min ( 1.5_wp , angle )) call apply_material ( self ) end subroutine set_twilight !> The twilight angle (radians below the horizon; 0: none). pure real ( wp ) function twilight ( self ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self twilight = self % twilight_ end function twilight !> The material, with the diffuse color times the body's color (without a !> texture), and the twilight, on every mesh built. subroutine apply_material ( self ) type ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer :: k call apply_material_to ( self , self % mesh ) do k = 1 , size ( self % lod_mesh ) call apply_material_to ( self , self % lod_mesh ( k )) end do end subroutine apply_material !> The material, with the diffuse color times the body's color (without a !> texture), and the twilight, on mesh `mesh` (if not null). subroutine apply_material_to ( self , mesh ) type ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: mesh !! a mesh handle (null: nothing done) real ( wp ) :: diffuse ( 4 ) if (. not . c_associated ( mesh )) return diffuse = self % diffuse_ if (. not . self % textured ) diffuse = diffuse * self % color () if ( self % translucent ) diffuse ( 4 ) = diffuse ( 4 ) * self % opacity_ ! (the shader's alpha: the diffuse color's) if ( mesh_set_material ( mesh , real ( self % ambient_ , c_float ), real ( diffuse , c_float ), & real ( self % specular_ , c_float ), real ( self % emission_ , c_float ), & real ( self % shininess_ , c_float )) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Sphere ' // self % name () // ': could not set the material' if ( vkf_mesh_set_twilight ( mesh , real ( self % twilight_ , c_float )) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Sphere ' // self % name () // ': could not set the twilight' end subroutine apply_material_to !> Level of detail (default on; see the module documentation): meshes of !> several resolutions, the one drawn chosen per view. Off: one mesh of !> `set_resolution`'s segments. Set it before a window shows the sphere. subroutine set_auto_lod ( self , lod ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self logical , intent ( in ) :: lod self % auto_lod_ = lod end subroutine set_auto_lod !> Whether level of detail is on. pure logical function auto_lod ( self ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self auto_lod = self % auto_lod_ end function auto_lod !> The mesh resolution without level of detail: segments in longitude and !> latitude (default 128 x 64). subroutine set_resolution ( self , n_lon , n_lat ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: n_lon !! segments in longitude (at least 3) integer , intent ( in ) :: n_lat !! segments in latitude (at least 2) self % n_lon = max ( 3 , n_lon ) self % n_lat = max ( 2 , n_lat ) end subroutine set_resolution !> The body's bounding sphere: its center, and its largest semi-axis. subroutine sphere_bound ( self , center , radius ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( out ) :: center ( 3 ), radius !! the bounding sphere, frame coordinates (scene units) center = self % sphere_position_ radius = maxval ( self % radii ()) end subroutine sphere_bound !> Picked on the ellipsoid (exact), with the geodetic latitude and longitude !> of the point hit (in the body's axes: sphere_attitude); else the frame's !> origin. subroutine sphere_pick ( self , cam , to_root , hits , n ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ), target :: self type ( PickCamera ), intent ( in ) :: cam !! the camera and cursor of the pick real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: to_root ( 4 , 4 ) !! the frame's transform to the root frame type ( PickHit ), allocatable , intent ( inout ) :: hits (:) !! hits so far, in hits(1:n); added to integer , intent ( inout ) :: n !! number of hits if ( self % contents_shown ()) then if ( pick_ellipsoid ( self , cam , to_root , self % sphere_position_ , quat_to_matrix ( self % sphere_attitude_ ), & self % radii (), . true ., hits , n )) return end if call self % ReferenceFrame % pick ( cam , to_root , hits , n ) end subroutine sphere_pick !> What kind of frame this is: 'Sphere'. function sphere_frame_info ( self ) result ( info ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable :: info info = 'Sphere' end function sphere_frame_info !> The body: an ellipsoid mesh under the sphere's transform. subroutine sphere_build_contents ( self , viewer , group ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: viewer !! a window's viewer (null: headless) type ( c_ptr ), intent ( in ) :: group !! the frame's contents group type ( c_ptr ) :: image , night , body image = read_texture ( self , self % texture ) night = read_texture ( self , self % night_texture ) self % textured = c_associated ( image ) self % built_radii = self % radii () self % translucent = self % opacity_ < 1.0_wp if ( self % auto_lod_ ) then ! meshes chosen per view, built when wanted self % image = image ! (kept for those built later) self % night = night self % shown = c_associated ( viewer ) self % lod_node = vkf_sphere_lod_create ( maxval ( self % built_radii )) call build_lod_mesh ( self , lod_first , compile = . false .) ! (compiled with the scene) if (. not . c_associated ( self % lod_mesh ( lod_first ))) return body = self % lod_node else self % mesh = ellipsoid_create ( self % built_radii , [ 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], image , & self % n_lon , self % n_lat , night , translucent = self % translucent ) if ( c_associated ( image )) call vkf_image_delete ( image ) if ( c_associated ( night )) call vkf_image_delete ( night ) if (. not . c_associated ( self % mesh )) return body = self % mesh end if call apply_material ( self ) self % sphere_node = vkf_transform_create () call update_sphere_transform ( self ) if ( vkf_node_add_child ( self % sphere_node , body ) /= 0 . or . vkf_node_add_child ( group , self % sphere_node ) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Sphere ' // self % name () // ': could not build the scene' end subroutine sphere_build_contents !> Build level-of-detail mesh k (lod_segments(k) segments around) and add it !> to the level-of-detail node (compiled for the windows if `compile`). subroutine build_lod_mesh ( self , k , compile ) type ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer , intent ( in ) :: k !! index into lod_segments logical , intent ( in ) :: compile type ( c_ptr ) :: mesh mesh = ellipsoid_create ( self % built_radii , [ 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float , 1.0_c_float ], self % image , & lod_segments ( k ), lod_segments ( k ) / 2 , self % night , translucent = self % translucent ) if (. not . c_associated ( mesh )) then write ( * , '(a,i0,a)' ) 'vkframes: Sphere ' // self % name () // ': could not build its ' , lod_segments ( k ), '-segment mesh' return end if self % lod_mesh ( k ) = mesh call apply_material_to ( self , mesh ) if ( compile ) then if ( vkf_compile_node ( mesh ) /= 0 ) write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Sphere ' // self % name () // ': could not compile a mesh' end if if ( vkf_sphere_lod_add ( self % lod_node , mesh , int ( lod_segments ( k ), c_int )) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Sphere ' // self % name () // ': could not add a mesh' end subroutine build_lod_mesh !> Update the frame (followed trajectories, children) and, with level of !> detail, build the mesh the views have wanted if it isn't built yet (the !> coarsest with as many segments as wanted, or the finest). recursive subroutine sphere_update ( self , t ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self real ( wp ), intent ( in ) :: t !! the scene time integer :: wanted , k call self % ReferenceFrame % update ( t ) if (. not . c_associated ( self % lod_node )) return wanted = vkf_sphere_lod_requested ( self % lod_node ) if ( wanted <= 0 ) return k = findloc ( lod_segments >= wanted , . true ., 1 ) if ( k == 0 ) k = size ( lod_segments ) if (. not . c_associated ( self % lod_mesh ( k ))) call build_lod_mesh ( self , k , compile = self % shown ) end subroutine sphere_update !> Number of level-of-detail meshes built so far (0 without level of detail). integer function num_lod_meshes ( self ) result ( n ) class ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self integer :: k n = 0 do k = 1 , size ( self % lod_mesh ) if ( c_associated ( self % lod_mesh ( k ))) n = n + 1 end do end function num_lod_meshes !> An image handle for texture file `file` (null if none or unreadable). function read_texture ( self , file ) result ( image ) type ( Sphere ), intent ( in ) :: self character ( len = :), allocatable , intent ( in ) :: file !! found with find_data_file (unallocated or '': none) type ( c_ptr ) :: image character ( len = :), allocatable :: path image = c_null_ptr if (. not . allocated ( file )) return if ( len ( file ) == 0 ) return path = find_data_file ( file ) if ( len ( path ) > 0 ) image = vkf_image_read ( path , len ( path , kind = c_int )) if (. not . c_associated ( image )) write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Sphere ' // self % name () // ': could not read texture ' // file end function read_texture !> The body's transform: its position, attitude and scale (radii / the built !> radii); nothing before it is built. subroutine update_sphere_transform ( self ) type ( Sphere ), intent ( inout ) :: self if (. not . c_associated ( self % sphere_node )) return if ( vkf_transform_set_matrix ( self % sphere_node , frame_matrix ( self % sphere_position_ , self % sphere_attitude_ , & self % radii () / self % built_radii )) /= 0 ) & write ( * , '(a)' ) 'vkframes: Sphere ' // self % name () // ': transform failed' end subroutine update_sphere_transform end module vkf_sphere","tags":"","url":"sourcefile/vkf_sphere.f90.html"},{"title":"vkf_text.f90 – vkframes","text":"This file depends on sourcefile~~vkf_text.f90~~EfferentGraph sourcefile~vkf_text.f90 vkf_text.f90 sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefile~vkf_files.f90 sourcefile~vkf_layer.f90 vkf_layer.f90 sourcefile~vkf_text.f90->sourcefil